window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3101,"title":"Chapter 3101: Against All Odds","paragraphs":["When the Dream Gate was forcefully closed and destroyed, Nephis was hit by a devastating backlash. Her Transcendent form collapsed, and she staggered, a torrent of blood exploded from her mouth. She fell to the ground, trembling, the white flames that burned in her eyes dancing erratically.","Her mind was in tatters, temporarily plunged into a dazed state.","The world was enveloped by darkness once more, flakes of ash swirling in the air. Two of the three remaining tendrils collided with the shattered stones of the devastating district, dissolving into cold currents and crumbling. The third one, however — the one that had destroyed the Gate — still loomed like a towering edifice, damaged and tattered, swaying above Nephis.","Sunny suddenly felt a deathly chill permeating his consciousness.","The situation was critical.","He had not recovered from witnessing the dreadful expanse of the abyssal horror’s true extent yet, and now, he had to think fast again. Nephis was temporarily out of commission, but the enemy still remained — more than that, the enemy was as powerful as an Unholy abomination.","Even if the abyssal horror was severely wounded by the incinerating light of Sun God’s lifeless shell, it was still strong enough to wipe them out. In fact, it would probably do that in just a few short moments.","’What to do?’","Sunny’s thoughts were calm, as if even his ability to panic was too damaged to function.","No matter how he thought about it, there seemed to be no way to turn the situation around.","However, just then...","The Spell whispered something into his ear.","It was a sound so sweet that, if Sunny could, he would have given the Spell a hug.","It said:","[You have slain a Great Titan, Prince of Darkness.]","[Your shadow grows stronger.]","Sunny’s mind settled.","Somewhere far away, in the heart of the ancient city — where the radiance of Godgrave had not reached — hidden in the flowing mist of nothingness, Saint had usurped the darkness of the Jade Titan and destroyed him.","Wrapped around her battered body, Sunny could feel her [Heart of Darkness] straining to contain the ocean of elemental darkness that had poured into it after the Jade Titan perished. He sensed something about Saint changing — the shadow that served as her soul was cracking under immense pressure, balancing on the verge of collapse.","But at the same time, it was expanding.","As it did, a roaring current of true darkness flowed into her.","And at the same time, Saint’s body suddenly began to absorb vast amounts of the white mist that swirled and flowed around her, causing a vast vortex to form.","She was evolving.","But just as it had happened before, she was slowing down and suppressing her evolution, unwilling to leave the battlefield before the battle was over.","This time, however, the process was different. It felt like Saint was not only trying to slow down her evolution, but also guide it, attempting to remain summoned until her rise to the Tyrant Class was complete.","Sunny would have been exhilarated by the fact that his most loyal Shadow would become a Supreme Tyrant soon, but at the moment, he could not afford to feel anything, let alone joy.","He and Nephis were about to be destroyed by the abyssal horror, and despite her efforts, Saint was in no shape to fight that thing — and wouldn’t be any time soon.","However...","That did not really matter. Because her evolution was not the only boon granted to Sunny by her triumph over the Jade Titan... one of the seven princes of the Underworld, the Prince of Darkness.","The Titan himself was a boon, too.","His shade was.","Sunny separated himself from Nephis, landing on the shattered stones between her and the towering tendril of darkness. He stood there, looking up with a dark, defiant expression.","At that moment, he felt the same gaze that had followed him throughout the Underworld expedition again — only, this time, there was nothing subtle about it. Instead, it was focused on him entirely, the power of that harrowing gaze alone dreadful enough to make him groan, streams of blood flowing out of his mouth, nose, and eyes.","Even Blood Weave, which usually prevented him from bleeding, could not stem the flow. In fact, his whole body was going haywire.","Nevertheless, Sunny raised a trembling hand and pointed it at the gargantuan tendril.","His bloodied lips moved, as if he was trying to remember how to form words.","In the end, he managed to force out a few.","\"You... hey, you. What... what are you staring at, bastard?\"","With that, Sunny’s lips twisted into a smile.","The tendril twisted, as if observing him...","And then dove in his direction with shocking speed.","’Oh... crap!’","Before the crushing mass of darkness could swallow Sunny and Nephis, though, there was a rustle.","And then, the blade of a colossal greatsword passed through the tendril, severing it at the base... well, at least at the closest thing to a base the blade could reach. The roots of the tendril were still hidden in the Abyss, after all.","There, behind the gargantuan tendril of darkness, a stone colossus in fearsome black armor, at least two hundred meters high, had appeared a few moments ago.","It was the shadow of the Prince of Darkness — the shade of the Great Titan Saint had slain.","Sunny had summoned it just as he baited the abyssal horror into attacking him.","The last visible tendril of that harrowing being plummeted from its great height, threatening to crush Sunny and Nephis. But instead, it dissolved in Neph’s light, dissipating into the surrounding darkness.","For a moment, dead silence enveloped the devastating district of the ancient city.","In that silence, Sunny let out a shaky breath.","He looked around with a pale, hesitant expression.","\"Are... are we alive?\"","His voice was tentative.","Raising both hands, he briefly touched his chest and shoulders.","Then, his expression changed to that of bewildered surprise.","\"We actually are.\"","Sunny paused for a moment.","\"Well... I’ll be damned!\""]},{"number":3102,"title":"Chapter 3102: Tides of Darkness","paragraphs":["Far away, Saint crouched, lowering herself to the surface of the river, and then leapt into the air. Wreathed in darkness and mist, her towering figure soared above the shattered stalagmite and landed on what remained of the ancient amphitheater’s arena.","She rose slowly, ruby dust spilling down the tattered surface of her black armor. Her eyes burned with crimson flames, regarding the world with cold intensity.","She turned slowly, struggling to contain the furious tempest of devastating forces raging in the depths of her lightless being, and looked south — where, in the distance, the remnants of her silent army were making their last stand against the legion of fallen Stone Saints who defended the city.","Without their commander, the Tainted Saints had lost some of their flawless cohesion. However, they still fought unlike other Nightmare Creatures, maintaining strict discipline and adhering to proper strategy. They still were a deadly threat, eradicating the shades with ruthless swiftness.","Not all of them were, though.","Now that the Jade Titan was dead and they had escaped his authority, some of the Tainted Saints slowed down and fell away from the battle formations. Now, they were all facing the heart of the city... they were facing Saint, looking at her across the vast distance, just like she was looking at them.","And under her gaze, they slowly lowered their weapons and knelt.","In the next moment, Saint turned into a torrent of crushing darkness and rushed south.","Reaching the battlefield, she assumed her tangible form and immediately brandished her tenebrous sword.","The kneeling abominations fell to its sharp edge first, slaughtered without mercy or hesitation. They accepted their depths calmly, stalwart and unflinching until the very last moment. As they perished, a vast field of annulment enveloped the battlefield. Then, Saint plunged into the battle formation of her fallen kin like a whirlwind of darkness, sowing death and devastation everywhere she went.","When she appeared, the remaining shades surged forward with newfound strength, as well. It was as if they regained a spark of their former glory, pushing the enemy back despite being few in number.","The Tainted Saints were still strong and numerous... but Sunny felt a strange confidence that all of them would fall to Saint’s blade.","The defenders of the city were being cut down one after another. The Jade Titan was dead. The abyssal horror...","Shuddering in terror that he could not control, Sunny wiped the blood off his face and threw a fearful look toward the great chasm.","\"It’s not dead.\"","Neph’s voice sounded hoarse.","Having regained a semblance of composure, she rose from the ground, swayed, and then steadied herself by leaning on the Blessing.","The two of them looked into the boundless darkness, still reeling from the harrowing encounter. Sunny hesitated for a few moments, then asked:","\"How do you know? Because the Spell did not announce its death?\"","That could mean something, or it could mean nothing. Creatures of Darkness did not seem to possess shadows, after all — they existed outside the cycle of life and death.","When Sunny and Nephis killed the motes of darkness hiding inside stone shells, the Spell had remained silent. It could have been because they had never been alive, to begin with... or because those pieces of darkness were merely tiny parts of the abyssal horror, not independent beings. In any case, there was no guarantee that the Spell would announce the death of that terrifying thing.","Nephis did not seem to rely on the Spell at the moment, either. She shook her head.","\"Those tendrils were merely its limbs. They extended from the Abyss, but we never saw their source... so even if the tendrils are destroyed, the source still remains.\"","Looking in the direction of the great chasm, Sunny paled.","Not only because the thought of that thing still being alive was chilling, but also because he felt something.","He was drawn to the edge of the chasm.","It was not a mundane feeling, but it was not some kind of outside influence, either. Instead, it was the familiar, vague sensation he had experienced a few times before — the sensation of his very blood being pulled in a certain direction. That only happened when another piece of Weaver’s Lineage was nearby.","So... either Shadow Weave was at the very edge of the city, or Broken Sword had somehow made it into the Abyss. If it was the latter, then the last part of Weaver’s Lineage was either still inside the Abyss or below it.","As the name suggested, the Underworld was located below the world — and below the Underworld, there was the Abyss. And what was below the Abyss?","It was the Shadow Realm, the realm of Death.","Sunny doubted that Shadow Weave was there, though, because he would have sensed something otherwise. Granted, even though he had been on the outer reaches of the Shadow Realm, he had never made his way to the precise area where its dark sky connected to the Abyss. Why would he, if that was where the Dark Drifters came from?","So, chances were that Shadow Weave was much closer.","However...","’If it’s in the Abyss — where that damn thing is, as well... I’ll just give up on completing the Lineage.’","Sunny did not hesitate to make that decision.","He was not going to fight an Unholy being. Before, the abyssal horror had almost killed him by merely looking in his direction — there was no prize in the world valuable enough to voluntarily crawl into that thing’s den.","In fact, the mere fact that Sunny was not running away without looking back at the moment was already the height of foolishness. The smartest thing he could do was abandon the expedition immediately and flee the Underworld.","But, well...","He had brought two incarnations to this dark realm. One of them, currently with Saint, used his gloomy shadow as the avatar. The other used the crazy shadow... and maybe because of that, Sunny felt like he could not leave yet. He had to check, at least.","He hesitated for a moment.","\"Even if it’s not dead, it has to be seriously wounded, right?\"","Neither Sunny nor Nephis were strong enough to wound the abyssal horror. The sky of Godgrave, though? He knew that the terrifying being had sacrificed a lot to banish the merciless light from its dark domain. It destroyed the Dream Gate — something Sunny had not even known was possible — effortlessly, but reaching the Gate had cost it a lot.","So, Sunny and Nephis probably had a bit of time before the terrifying creature sprouted new tendrils to reach for them from the Abyss.","Sunny stared in the direction of the great chasm for a short while, then looked at Nephis.","Saint was still in the throes of evolution. There was Nether’s citadel waiting to be conquered, as well.","\"I want to check the edge of the city. I think... I hope there is time.\"","Nephis studied him for a few moments, then nodded.","\"Then let’s go and see.\""]},{"number":3103,"title":"Chapter 3103: Spark of Light","paragraphs":["Saint was still fighting her fallen kin, while Sunny and Nephis set their sights on the very edge of the ancient city — there, the great river plummeted into the abyssal chasm in the roar of an immense waterfall, and white mist billowed in cold winds.","Before they ventured forward, however, Sunny hesitated for a moment. He looked around, at the ruins of the devastated streets around them, and asked in a low tone:","\"Should I... leave a tether here? Just in case.\"","It was unlikely that they would be able to remain in the Underworld for much longer. But even if they were forced to retreat, a tether could help him return here at will.","Sunny had doubts, though.","Nephis shook her head.","\"You shouldn’t.\"","She wiped the blood off her lips and looked at the scorched expanse of shattered stone where her Dream Gate had stood. Her expression darkened.","\"Now that we are facing Cursed and Unholy beings, we need to rethink a lot of things. In the battle against the Cursed Demon, Abjuration, it was able to use my connection to the Longing Domain to target its subjects... this time, the thing from the Abyss was able to destroy my Dream Gate. Who’s to say that some Unholy horror won’t be able to make use of your tether, as well?\"","Sunny’s expression turned grim.","Nephis was right. The harrowing deities of the Dream Realm were beyond their understanding and wielded powers that defied reason. It would already be bad enough if the abyssal horror could trace the tether back to Sunny and attack his soul... but what if it could follow him to the other end of the tether, as well?","Imagining that thing extending its tendrils into NQSC or Bastion made Sunny shudder.","\"We only have one attempt, then. We’d better not waste it.\"","Sharing an uneasy look, they moved toward the edge of the city. They had to fly again, landing on the rock outcropping above the swirling white mist — Nephis was still reeling from the dire strain of the battle against the dark copy, but she summoned her wings, gritting her teeth as pain and exhaustion washed over her.","Nether’s flying stronghold was now behind and above them, while in front of them, a seemingly boundless expanse of impenetrable darkness stretched as far as they could see — which wasn’t far, considering that Saint was on the other end of the city.","Neph’s radiance, which usually resembled a brilliant star, seemed like a tiny spark in the face of that vast expanse of cold darkness. Her light didn’t reach far, barely illuminating the wisps of mist below.","Beyond that, there was only an endless, inscrutable black void.","The roar of the unseen waterfall enveloped them, the air full of cool vapor. Sunny inhaled deeply, still failing to suppress the instinctual terror that held his heart in an icy grasp. The abyssal horror still hid somewhere in the depths of that black void.","Sunny could not see it, could not sense it... he did not know if a towering tendril would rise the next moment to envelop him and pull him down into the darkness.","However, he still forced himself to look ahead, facing the boundless darkness.","And then, his expression changed.","Sunny’s eyes glinted, and he raised a hand, pointing forward.","\"Neph, do you... see it?\"","She answered in a quiet, reserved tone:","\"Yeah.\"","Sunny let out a quiet sigh.","There, below them, another tiny spark of light was shining in the boundless darkness.","Sunny and Nephis looked at each other. A few moments passed in silence — there was so much each of them had to say, and yet, no words could express the truth of what they felt.","In the end, Sunny raised a hand and lightly gripped Neph’s shoulder. Then, he let go, took a step forward, and spread his dark wings.","They glided across the black void, enveloped by the roaring of the waterfall and the clouds of water vapor, the swirling mass of white mist just a few meters below them.","In the end, they reached the source of the mysterious light. There, a shelf or rugged rock extended from the sheer rock, protruding from the roaring wall of falling water. It tapered to a point, hanging above the abyss like a narrow cliff — the light they had seen shone at the very tip of that cliff, shimmering lightly.","Below, there was nothing but darkness. The stones were slippery, and if one lost their footing, all that awaited them was an endless, harrowing fall.","Sunny walked forward with careful steps. Nephis followed, moving slowly... it was as if she was afraid of what lay ahead, gathering all her courage to face it.","Sunny did not know what to expect, but he knew that they had found what he had been searching for — his blood told him, pulling him forward with subtle but strangely inescapable force.","There, hidden in the mysterious light... Shadow Weave, the last fragment of Weaver’s Lineage, awaited.","And Broken Sword, as well.","Finally, they arrived at the tip of the cliff and discovered where the light was coming from.","On the very edge of boundless darkness, a cracked sword was thrust into the stone at an angle. An enchanted lantern hung from its crossguard, illuminating a small patch of dark stone with brilliant light. Despite the decades that had passed, the lantern still burned brightly, keeping the unfathomable mass of darkness at bay.","And in front of the cracked sword...","Both Sunny and Nephis froze, looking down.","They were looking at different things, though.","Neph’s gaze was aimed at the weathered bones that lay on the edge of the abyss. A white skull, a scattering of broken ribs, a fractured arm extending to the lantern.... it was a skeleton of a human, battered and broken, covered by the tattered remains of a faded military uniform.","It was her father, Broken Sword — the first human to have ever conquered the Third Nightmare, and the Fourth one as well.","What remained of him, hidden in eternal darkness.","Sunny, however, was not looking at the forlorn remains of the great hero of humanity.","Instead, he was looking at the shadow cast by the skeleton.","The shadow was lying on the cold stones — however, it was not broken or battered.","It was not a human shadow, either.","Instead, it was tall and imposing, shrouded in a long mantle. Eight hands extended from the folds of the mantle, and atop the shadow’s head...","Three twisting horns rose like a crown.","It was a shadow of Weaver, the Demon of Fate."]},{"number":3104,"title":"Chapter 3104: Broken Sword","paragraphs":["\"So he was dead, after all.\"","Neph’s even voice sounded like a dull blade.","She remained motionless for a long while, then slowly approached the weathered skeleton.","A soft sigh escaped from her lips.","She stayed silent, then asked in a quiet whisper:","\"Why are you lying here all alone?\"","Sunny kept quiet, as well, still looking at the tall shadow that the remains of Broken Sword cast.","The shadow of Weaver.","Then, he slowly pulled his gaze away and looked at Nephis.","Her pale face was smeared in blood and dust, gaunt from fatigue. The white sparks that usually danced in the depths of her eyes were gone, and her lips were pressed into a line. Her gaze was both intense and distant.","Sunny turned to look at the weathered bones, too.","This was Broken Sword... the legendary, glorious Broken Sword — one of the greatest, if not the greatest, heroes of humanity. A swordsman of sublime skill and talent, as well as an Awakened whose power had paved the way for all humans to follow.","A man who had conquered the Third Nightmare before anyone even knew what a Saint was. A man who had become a Sovereign while humanity was still reaching toward the seemingly insurmountable peak of Transcendence.","...A man who had been betrayed by his comrades and slain in the lightless depths of the Underworld, never to see the light of day again.","Sunny had hoped until the last moment that, somehow, Broken Sword would still be alive. The legendary warrior of the human race was just that kind of person — someone who was larger than life. How could death claim him so easily?","But in the end, Sunny’s hopes had been for naught. No matter how ingenious and powerful Broken Sword had been, death still claimed him, like it claimed everyone else. The betrayal of the Dreamspawn, Anvil of Valor, and Ki Song... Aster, Song, and Vale... had achieved its goal, setting everything that happened since in motion.","Neph’s lonely and nightmarish upbringing, the Forgotten Shore, the clash of Song and Valor forces in Antarctica, the Tomb of Ariel, Godgrave, the return of the Dreamspawn and his eventual fall...","It had all started here, from that man.","From his bitter, lonesome death.","How would history have turned out if he survived?","Sunny did not know.","Would things have been different if Broken Sword had not discovered Shadow Weave while pursuing Apotheosis, thus forcing the hands of his companions?","Sunny did not know that, either. Perhaps the Sovereigns would have betrayed him, anyway. Gods knew, the Dreamspawn certainly had been harboring sinister ideas, and Anvil had not needed a reason to disdain Broken Sword — he had only needed an excuse.","But none of that mattered now, since all of them were gone.","Broken Sword was gone, as well... had been gone for a long, long time.","His death was avenged, and the three traitors who had killed him were slain or sealed by his daughter.","Justice had prevailed, and the Immortal Flame clan still thrived.","And yet...","Looking at the bones of the first Sovereign, Sunny could not help but feel mournful.","That sense of melancholy overpowered even the terror that was squeezing his heart, making him sigh heavily.","Everyone deserved better than what the Age of the Nightmare Spell offered them, but Broken Sword especially did not deserve to have died alone in this dark, desolate, dreadful pit.","’Damn it all.’","Nephis, meanwhile, knelt near the remains of her father and touched his skull gently, as if brushing his cheek.","She did not say anything, looking down with a distant expression.","After a while, though, she spoke:","\"What am I meant to say? Should I tell him that I’ve dealt with the people who killed him?\"","She paused for a few moments, and then smiled bitterly.","\"Or should I ask why he abandoned me, all those years ago? Four years old... did he really have to leave for the next Nightmare so soon?\"","Sighing heavily, Nephis shook her head.","\"Our family was already on the verge of collapse after my mother and grandfather perished. But he did not get to see how everything rotted and collapsed after his disappearance... how our retainers all left one after another or were killed. How our fortune dwindled, until it was entirely gone. How my grandmother grew older and older under the crushing weight of being hunted by his former friends. Until she was gone, as well.\"","Nephis brushed her fingers across Broken Sword’s skull once more, then sighed again.","Her voice sounded wistful.","\"It’s so easy, being dead.\"","Despite the harsh words, her gaze was strangely tender.","After a long pause, she added:","\"But still. He tried... he tried his best. He did it earnestly. It must have been so hard, to do everything he did.\"","She lingered for a moment, then smiled.","\"In my mind, he has always been a giant. But now that I think about it... he must have felt pain the same way I do. He must have felt sorrow and despair the same way I do. He was even younger than I am today when he died. So what can I say to him?\"","Nephis hesitated, and then bowed slightly to the weathered bones.","\"Rest well now, my father. Your nightmare is over.\"","Sunny stayed still for a while, then bowed, as well.","He remained bowed for some time, then straightened and looked at the cracked sword rising from the stone and the lantern hanging from its crossguard.","Why were they here?","The answer... was obvious. Broken Sword had made his way to the edge of the Abyss so that no one could find him. But then, he left a lantern to illuminate his final resting place... so that his shadow remained.","Shadows could not exist without light, after all.","Which meant that, somehow, he had known that someone would come to collect the fragment of Weaver’s Lineage one day — that someone would need it one day. And he had not wanted it to fall into the wrong hands.","What had Broken Sword known that Sunny did not?","And who was it that Broken Sword had wanted to recover his legacy?","There were no answers, and there would probably never be.","Nephis remained silent for a few moments, and then said quietly:","\"We shouldn’t linger, so it would be wise to do what you wanted to do fast. I’ll take... his bones after you’re done. He should be buried with the rest of my family. Actually, most of those graves are empty... but now, there will be one less.\"","Sunny nodded slowly and then approached the towering shadow of Weaver.","Throwing a guarded look into the dark chasm, he hesitated for a moment...","And then reached toward the shadow, drawing it into his soul.","It responded to his call without resistance.","In the next moment, Sunny shuddered."]},{"number":3105,"title":"Chapter 3105: Shadow Weave","paragraphs":["Every time Sunny had inherited a part of Weaver’s lineage, he had to endure harrowing agony. That was because his very being was assimilating something that was forbidden, and turning into something it was not meant to be.","The gods themselves had forbidden daemons from propagating, after all. So, by inheriting the legacy of Weaver, Sunny was going against the will of the gods — against the nature of his existence itself.","However, when a shadow cast by the Demon of Destiny fused with his own, there was no pain. There was no agony, either, and he did not lose consciousness, like he had when accepting Mind Weave.","However, the transformation he was undergoing was so profound and all-encompassing that it made Sunny feel instinctual fear. He was a creature of shadows, after all, so Shadow Weave was bound to alter the very foundation of him — the very depths of his vast, lightless soul.","And being changed so entirely could not be anything but frightening.","In the dark expanse of his Soul Sea, the silent waters surged, growing restless. In the black void of the sky above them, devastating winds rose, slamming into the seven tenebrous Shadow Cores. The Shadow Cores themselves trembled, as if great forces were raging within them.","Then, a weave of golden threads shimmered in the darkness, permeating the world — that was the intricate web of the Soul Weave, which usually remained invisible, helping his soul endure the transformation.","Sunny could feel other parts of his existence reacting, as well. His blood rushed, boiling. His bones seemed to vibrate. His muscles contracted and relaxed uncontrollably, answering an unknown impulse. His state of mind changed subtly, making him feel like he was observing himself from outside himself.","His titanic Will expanded and receded like an ocean — as if affected by the pull of some unfathomable, invisible mass.","Perhaps it was the mass of his Will itself changing, as well.","’What...’","Sunny drew a labored breath.","Then, a quiet groan escaped from his lips.","He swayed and leaned on Nephis to support himself, feeling a profound change overcoming his entire self.","’What is happening to me?’","For a moment, a frightening thought flashed through Sunny’s mind. He was suddenly afraid that by inheriting all fragments of Weaver’s lineage, he was becoming Weaver — that the treacherous daemon had left these seeds for some unfortunate soul to find so that the great and terrible Demon of Fate could be reborn, replacing their foolish, shortsighted heir.","Their epigone.","But no... that was not how Lineages worked. None of those who had inherited the Lineages of the great gods became vessels for the dead gods. More than that, Weaver had willingly and meticulously arranged their own death — if they wanted to escape it, they would not have spared Orphne of the Nine, to begin with.","Weaver had definitely scattered fragments of their Lineage across the Dream Realm for a purpose. But simply being reborn? The treacherous Demon of Fate would have pursued a goal so trivial. They would definitely have had a far more diabolical purpose in mind.","One part of their legacy was the Nightmare Spell.","The other? Sunny was that legacy — at least a part of it — but even he did not fully understand Weaver’s intent.","’I just... have to endure.’","Gritting his teeth, Sunny tried to calm himself and explore the changes his nature was undergoing.","He did not know what inheriting Shadow Weave had done to Broken Sword, or would have done to anyone else for that matter — anyone else except him. Sunny was a Divine Shadow, after all, so he was bound to have a special connection to this part of Weaver’s inheritance.","Shadow Weave fused with his dark existence, producing a powerful and wondrous synergy. Sunny could feel all aspects of him being enhanced and altered, as if a binding substance was added to the sublime alloy of his body and soul.","In fact, there was not one, but two great waves of alteration happening to him.","The first came from Shadow Weave altering his whole being.","The second came from the seventh fragment of Weaver’s legacy fusing with the other six, completing the forbidden lineage.","’What... exactly...’","Even before reading the description of the Spell, Sunny tried to fathom the nature of what was happening to him — of the first wave of alterations, at least.","His powers... were not exactly growing. However, they were changing. It felt as if a whole new facet of the Shadow Slave Aspect was being revealed to him — something he had always been meant to know and control, but failed to understand and master on his own. Perhaps he could never have mastered it, to begin with, not without receiving the lineage of a deity.","Shadow God’s Lineage, which he had been meant to inherit, ended up being swallowed by Blood Weave. But now, he was receiving a tenacious substitute created by the Demon of Fate. It led him on a path different from what the Lineage of Shadow God would have opened for him, but not necessarily inferior.","’So that was what it meant...’","Raising his hand, Sunny peered into the depths of his existence, where shadow essence flowed through invisible veins. He had always known that he was different from other Awakened, who controlled soul essence instead — however, it was only now that he understood the fundamental distinction.","Soul essence was the essence of life, while shadow essence was the essence of death. No wonder he could only grow more powerful by slaying living things... however, shadow essence was far more than mere force of destruction.","Shadows were formless, and so was shadow essence. In fact, it could assume the form of any energy — as Sunny watched, the lightless currents of his essence turned radiant and pure, no different from soul essence, before reverting back. If he wanted to, he could turn it into something else, as well — heat, kinetic force, electricity... he could even turn it into matter.","Or other, more esoteric kinds of things as well.","True darkness? Nothingness? One day, with effort.","Most obviously, though, he could turn his essence into shadows, thus becoming their source, not only their ruler. The shadows he created could then be controlled, called upon to shroud him, or manifested like any other. In fact, Shadow Weave had greatly enhanced the power of Shadow Manifestation.","Before, the shadows he manifested permanently were equivalent to materials roughly two Ranks below his. Now, that gap was reduced to merely one Rank, meaning that at the moment, he could create permanent tools and weapons worthy of a Saint.","More importantly, the shifting nature of his essence could greatly ease his efforts to master Shadow Dance — after all, if he truly wanted to shadow a being, he needed to shadow the shape of their soul, as well.","He had already took a step in that direction by shadowing Neph’s [Soul Flame], but the malleable nature of his essence could greatky accelerate his progress.","Sunny also fathomed how to channel his essence into his shades, granting them far greater power. He even felt a hint of an ability to influence living shadows with his essence — in order to truly discover that ability, however, he would still need to explore and experiment.","And those were not the only boons Shadow Weave granted him, either.","The power granted to those his seven shadows augmented was enhanced, while the seven shadows themselves became more tenacious and difficult to destroy. The range and intricacy of his Shadow Step was increased. The innate affinity of his Will deepened, making it stronger as far as visiting death upon living beings went.","Sunny was the Sovereign of Death, after all, and Death had been created by Shadow. So when he accepted Shadow Weave, the Death aspect of his spirit was greatly enhanced.","The most profound and instantly recognizable transformation, though, happened to his shadow sense, which now encompassed more than just the shape and depths of the shadows that surrounded him.","Now, he could effortlessly communicate with those shadows, learning far more about the things that cast them — from mundane things like color and taste to more metaphysical things like Rank, Class, and nature.","It was as if a colorless, silent world had suddenly become full of vibrant colors and varied sensations, making Sunny feel as if he had been blind all this time. He felt it all — the rough texture of the weathered stone, the coldness of the falling water, the weight of moisture hanging in the air, the beautiful grey painting of Neph’s eyes...","It almost overwhelmed him.","Even then, Sunny felt that this was not the most important thing he had gained, though.","The true expansion of his abilities came from somewhere else.","It was hard to sense, and even harder to fathom. But Sunny felt that a profound change had happened to his very soul, as well as to the nature of his Domain... to the power he wielded over his Shadows, and his shades.","In the past, seven Shadows had come to dwell in his soul. Some of them had been Shadow Creatures, to begin with, while some Sunny had created by fusing shades and Echoes with the help of the Nightmare Spell — with the exception of the Marvelous Mimic, whom he had created on his own by turning a Memory into an Echo, then animating that Echo with the shade of the Mordant Mimic.","But now, Sunny felt that he did not need the transitional medium of the Echo anymore, and neither did he need the assistance of the Spell. The nascent understanding of how to elevate shades to the status of Shadows was already in his mind, and now, all he needed to do was experiment and develop the complete process.","Shades did not possess agency or a sense of self, and therefore, they were not imbued with the Will. More importantly, they were dead things, and therefore static. They could not change, evolve, or grow.","His Shadows, however, were different. Although peculiar creatures, they were beings with their own minds and individuality. They wielded their Will as any other creature would, and were capable of growth. Needless to say, their existence was superior to that of shades who lacked personhood.","Of course, not all shades were fit to become Shadows... but some were. And many of those who weren’t could be helped along the way by Sunny’s power.","There was an even deeper layer of mastery over his Domain that Sunny sensed, but could not quite grasp yet. After all, now, he was already capable of transforming shades — but was this transformation limited to becoming Shadows? Or could he do something else?","Could he consume his shades, for example, to rebuild his cores? Could he destroy them and turn them into soul essence, like Shadow God had been able to? Could he nourish strong shades with the weaker ones, thus making them more powerful?","All these questions needed to be answered, but Sunny suspected that he was now on the threshold of an entirely new horizon of possibilities.","However, there was a contradiction.","Why would he try to consume the shades in order to build new Shadow Cores if he was already a Titan?","And why would he elevate the shades to the status of Shadows if he already ruled seven Shadows, and could not accept more?","And there... there hid the final part of the new power Sunny sensed.","A long time ago, Eurys had said that his Shadows, while powerful, were not complete.","Now, Sunny felt like he stumbled onto a hint of the understanding of how to finally make them whole.","But before he could think on that matter deeply, the Spell suddenly whispered into his ear.","It said:","[You have lost an Attribute.]","[You have lost an Attribute.]","[You have lost an Attribute.]","[You have lost an Attribute.]","[You have lost an Attribute.]","[You have lost an Attribute...]","And then, in a voice that hinted at triumphant satisfaction, the Spell said, its voice echoing in the darkness.","[You have received an Attribute.]","[You... are complete.]","Sunny flinched and stayed motionless for a few long moments.","Then, he inhaled deeply and summoned his runes.","As the shimmering field of them ignited in the darkness, his gaze rushed to the string describing his Attributes. And there, Sunny saw something that he had long expected to see.","The runes read:","Attributes: [Lord of Shadows], [Flame of Divinity], [Jade Shell], [The Curse], [Fated]...","And at the end of it, a new one.","[The Weave]."]},{"number":3106,"title":"Chapter 3106: Third Paradox","paragraphs":["Sunny inhaled deeply, trying to sense what changes had happened to him due to the completion of the Weave.","He remembered how he had started on the path of inheriting the lineage of the mysterious daemon, and all the trials he had to overcome to obtain it.","Back then, on the Forgotten Shore, ignorant of the world and enthralled by the Soul Devourer... why was it that he had decided to climb the branches of that malevolent tree? Sunny barely remembered.","’Oh, right... I wanted to find the most delicious fruit to give it to Nephis and lift her mood.’","Nephis had resisted the enthrallment a bit better than Sunny and Cassie, spending most of her days on the shore of the Ashen Barrow and looking west with longing in her eyes... like Odysseus dreaming of Ithaka on the shore of Ogygia. Even if she could not remember why she had wanted to leave and what she was striving to achieve, she still felt restless and lost in the deceitful bliss of the mind hex.","Sunny, brainwashed as he was, could not understand why she seemed to be so down, so he decided to bring her some delicious soul fruits to cheer her up. That was why he stumbled on the Thieving Bird’s nest, destroyed the Thieving Bird’s egg, and received Blood Weave.","That was what put him on the path of searching for the scattered parts of Weaver’s lineage.","Had it really been a coincidence, or was all of it a part of Weaver’s plan?","To be honest, Sunny did not know if anything having to do with him could be called a coincidence. He was Fated, after all.","He wasn’t sure that anything having to do with Weaver could be called a coincidence, either.","However, now that he had spent more than a decade searching for traces of the nebulous daemon and learning more about that mysterious creature, Sunny thought that he understood the Demon of Fate — and fate itself — at least a little bit better.","As such... he did not think that once, a long time ago, Weaver had imagined a street rat called Sunny finding the first fragment of their lineage and going on to hunt for the rest.","However, Weaver could very well had read the currents of fate and twisted them ever so slightly, making sure that, one day in the future, the world would assume just the right shape for just the right kind of person to end up in the right place at the right time, setting Weaver’s plan in motion — making Weaver’s plan inevitable, even.","So while Weaver might not have known Sunny’s face or name, they would have known what kind of being their heir would be.","A kind of being who would survive an encounter with the Soul Devouring Tree and the Vile Thieving Bird’s Spawn, descend into the depths of the Sky Below and swallow Weaver’s phalanx, reach the estuary of the Great River in the Tomb of Ariel, conquer the illusory world of the Demon of Imagination, lay siege to the Eternal City at the bottom of the Twilight Sea, win Ariel’s Game, and brave the dark depths of the Underworld.","Sunny sighed deeply, looking at the runes with a dark expression.","’I think I already said it... but couldn’t that damn daemon leave the pieces of his lineage in more easily accessible places? They really put me through a whole damn lot!’","Just one of those harrowing adventures was enough to kill the absolute majority of people. Surviving seven in a row? Even for a Fated individual, it was a stretch.","Shaking his head, Sunny felt... relieved.","It was all over now, at least.","All that was left was to claim his prize.","And what a prize it was!","Sunny could already feel it... all parts of him being tempered as all seven fragments of the Weave fused into a single whole, each growing stronger and supporting the rest.","His blood had grown more potent, both making him more durable and greatly enhancing his endurance.","His already unbreakable bones had become nearly indestructible, the marrow within them absorbing great torrents of vitality.","His muscles, tendons, and organs had been reforged and tempered, making him even more resilient and offering him even greater explosive strength.","His spirit had become vaster, the weight of his Will leaving a deeper dent in the fabric of the world.","His soul had become both more malleable and harder to destroy.","His mind expanded, offering him an even greater capacity to fathom countless ideas at the same time.","His shadows swelled with greater power, the potency of his essence increasing as well.","But those... those were merely side effects of [The Weave] being completed.","Before turning his mind to the last and true boon gifted to him by it, Sunny aimed his gaze at the runes and read the description of his new Attribute.","The runes read:","[\"Tell me, oh Demon of Fate,\" said Oblivion. \"How can fate be changed?\"","The Demon of Fate laughed, looking at the great tapestry of fate with wonder and fear.","\"Why would you want to change fate? Fate cannot be changed. Fate cannot be bargained with. Fate cannot be escaped, either, because fate does not know the distinction between the past and the future. Everything that has ever happened, is happening, and will happen is inscribed in the threads of fate, because fate is great, and there is nothing greater than fate.\"","The Demon of Fate looked at Oblivion and said in a nebulous tone, \"Mortal men are powerless in front of fate. We, the daemons, are just as powerless as mortals. Even the great gods bow their heads to fate, and those who dwell in the Void are not above it either. Fate rules all, is above all... it is a force that looms above the Flame and the Void, governing both — encompassing all of existence.\"","The Demon of Fate smiled bitterly.","\"How can the future be changed if time itself is merely a weapon created by the gods, and the gods are powerless against fate? Fate cannot be changed because it doesn’t know time. It exists in the flash of a single moment. Fate is not something that is happening; it is something that has already happened. It is an axiom, immutable and inalienable. How are you going to change something that has already transpired, sister? That is impossible.\"","Hearing the Demon of Fate, Oblivion shook her head. \"It is possible.\"","The Demon of Fate scoffed and said in a tone of amusement, \"What makes you so sure?\"","Oblivion leaned forward then and said, her voice echoing in the darkness, \"The Void is everchanging, and therefore, in its endless permutations, it eventually gave birth to something unchangeable — to the Flame of Desire. That is the paradox of Chaos. Fate is no different. If it truly governs all possible events and encompasses all possible outcomes... then it will give birth to something that cannot be encompassed or governed one day. It will give birth to the paradox that will destroy it. Creating such a paradox — that is how fate can be changed.\"","The Demon of Fate seemed appalled, \"A third paradox? What kind of treacherous being can summon it into existence? That thing would have to possess the power of a great god, the curse of a daemon, and be the avatar of fate itself on top of that. Do you think I can create such an abomination, sister?\"","The Demon of Fate grinned, \"Is that a challenge?\"]","Sunny stared at the runes, dumbfounded.","’Huh?’","The power of a great god, the curse of a demon, an avatar of fate...","What did it mean to be an avatar of fate? Gods had avatars. Lesser beings could sometimes control incarnations, as well — Sunny himself was an example of such a creature. But fate? Fate did not possess personhood. It did not have goals or ambitions, either. It simply existed, and therefore, it could not incarnate its consciousness in a mortal vessel.","So what kind of avatar could fate create?","If Sunny imagined fate as a force as opposed to a being, then maybe its avatar did not have to wield its consciousness. Maybe it simply had to be a manifestation of fate as a force, its personification. A living embodiment of inevitability, a person who enforced fate by the mere fact of their existence... whether they wanted to or not.","And who could these champions of fate have been?","One group came to mind.","’The Nine.’","The Nine, who were all Fated... just like Sunny was.","His eyes widened slightly.","’An avatar of fate... a Fated person?’","Then, his eyes widened a little more.","’Wait! T—then, then... the power of a god, the curse of a daemon, an avatar of fate? That described a person who has the [Fated] Attribute, a Divine Aspect, and the lineage of a daemon! That’s me, goddamnit!’","The paradoxical abomination Weaver had mentioned... was Sunny?","Sunny, who was [Fated], wielded the Shadow Slave Aspect, and obtained [The Weave].","His expression changed","’You’ve got to be kidding me. And who is that damned daemon calling an abomination?!’"]},{"number":3107,"title":"Chapter 3107: Set in Stone","paragraphs":["What right did that creepy daemon have to call anyone an abomination? That eerie thing had eight hands! With seven fingers on each one!","’And it doesn’t even make sense!’","Why eight hands? Because spiders, who wove silk, had eight legs?","What about Weaver’s legs?! The great and terrible Demon of Fate had those too, presumably! Add those to the eight hands, and you get ten limbs!","That would make Weaver more like a crab — or a lobster — not a spider.","Where did that creepy lobster get the nerve to call Sunny an abomination?!","Sunny grimaced and rubbed his face.","’What am I even thinking about?’","He was simply reeling from reading the description of the Weave. That one sounded like a personal message to him more than any other, answering the question he had just asked himself.","However, like all the answers the Spell gave, it only gave birth to a greater swarm of questions.","’There is a lot to ponder on here.’","Sunny closed his eyes for a moment.","First of all — and most importantly — was the identity of who Weaver was talking to, as well as the general content of their conversation. It was a conversation between the Demon of Fate and the Demon of Oblivion — the most mysterious and least known of all the daemons.","More than that, shockingly, the description of the Weave suggested that it was Oblivion who had first broached the subject of changing fate, not Weaver.","’Can I even trust anything Weaver said?’","Weaver was known to be a consummate liar... however, somehow, Sunny felt like the nebulous daemon had been sincere in this conversation.","In fact, the whole tone of the conversation was unlike the Weaver Sunny had come to know. It almost felt like the version of the Demon of Fate shown in this description was much... younger and less burdened than all other versions Sunny had witnessed.","Still, Sunny had always felt that Weaver’s true ambition was to break fate. And how could he not? After all, the Nightmare Spell — Weaver’s greatest masterpiece — had always rewarded its carriers for defying fate as much as they could. The more your actions in the Nightmare changed the fated outcome, the greater its evaluation was.","It was startling to find out that the idea of going against fate — as well as the general blueprint of how to achieve it — had actually come from... ’Wait. Who was it again?’","Sunny frowned and seemed confused for a moment.","Right! From the Demon of Oblivion. It was Oblivion who seemed to have given Weaver the initial motivation to struggle against fate.","Or maybe it was not so simple.","Sunny had to admit that he knew close to nothing about Oblivion. And if he was truly honest, he would have to admit that despite inheriting their Lineage and chasing their ghost for more than a decade, he knew very little about Weaver as well.","What was the relationship between these two daemons? What had Oblivion been scheming, and how had she died?","He didn’t know.","And then, there was a peculiar detail about the description of the Weave — although Sunny was not sure if it carried any meaning. Throughout the entire conversation, the Spell had never once called Weaver by name. It had only described the nebulous daemon as the Demon of Fate. Was that because Weaver had not earned their name yet, back when that conversation happened?","Or was it pure coincidence? The Spell was quite liberal in its descriptions, so it could very well have been.","Or was there a different reason Sunny did not yet understand?","In fact, Sunny failed to understand a lot of things about the mystifying conversation between Weaver and Oblivion.","’Where do I even start?’","There was the way Weaver had described fate. In hindsight, it was sort of obvious, but Sunny had never considered it before — the fact that not only mortals, but even the gods had been powerless in the face of fate... were subject to fate. That alone was not the truly explosive piece of information, though.","What truly stunned him was that, according to Weaver, even the Void Beings — even the eternal Void itself — were subject to fate.","Why wouldn’t they be, though? The gods themselves were Void Beings, so if they were affected by fate, then the rest of their kin would be, too.","Which framed fate as something that existed on a plane of its own — a higher plane than any other. An absolute above the absolute.","There had been a time when Sunny thought of fate as one of the universal laws of existence. These laws, however, were created by the gods. Beyond the framework of laws that composed existence, there was the everlasting Void and the alien, unfathomable undercurrents that ruled it.","And beyond that, apparently, there was fate.","Not only that, but Weaver had also described fate as a force that existed beyond and above time. Therefore...","Sunny felt a headache.","Therefore, from the cosmic perspective of fate, the future could never be changed. Because the future was never a vague expanse of potentials and possibilities — it was not something that was yet to happen. Instead, it had already happened... had always have happened, and was therefore set in stone. It was a fact.","Since fate existed above time and fused the past, the present, and the future into a single, eternal, immutable fact — or maybe a process that was both endless and instantaneous, but irrespectively finished and complete — it naturally couldn’t be changed.","...Only it could.","Weaver... and Oblivion?... had set the scheme to break fate in motion, while Sunny and Cassie completed it. The vast tapestry of fate was in shambles, and the future, which had been set in stone like a fact, was now as unknown and unknowable as it was meant to be. Someone went and broke the whole damn stone.","Which created a paradox.","If fate was truly like a serpent eating its own tail, knowing no distinction between cause and effect, between the past and the future... if it was indeed an absolute law above all absolute laws, axiomatic and immutable, then how the hell could it have become infinitely malleable and incomplete?","’One hell of a paradox, indeed.’","And Sunny was the confluence of endlessly improbable eventualities that had made that paradox possible — a person who had inherited an Aspect of a god, a Lineage of a daemon, and a unique connection to fate.","Sunny was not a stranger to improbable events due to being Fated, but seen in that light, his strange existence really took the cake.","Was that what Oblivion had meant? That only a Fated being could cause the impossible confluence of events capable of changing fate, meaning that only fate could destroy fate — and not only that, that the seeds of its destruction had always been hidden in its very nature?","Sunny was not sure that he was qualified to know the answer to that question. All of it was more than a little bit above his pay grade — even as a demigod, all he felt toward this cosmic kind of understanding was sheer terror.","The universe was already vast enough, and mysteries hidden beyond its veil were not for the likes of him to glean."]},{"number":3108,"title":"Chapter 3108: Chaos, Order, and Fate","paragraphs":["Sunny did want to know one thing, though.","’The third paradox?’","Oblivion had called the birth of the Flame the first paradox — the Paradox of Chaos. Weaver, meanwhile, had called the destruction of fate at the hands of a Fated being — the Paradox of Fate — the third paradox.","Then what was the second paradox?","Once again, that question had no answer. However, Sunny had an inkling of a suspicion.","The paradoxes were numbered, which suggested that they came in order. The first paradox, the Paradox of Chaos, described the inevitability of a forever-changing entity — the Void — eventually creating an unchangeable axiom, the Flame of Desire. Due to their very nature, the Void and the Flame had been destined to clash, which led to the Void being sealed.","Thus, the Void was the source of its own fall.","The third paradox, the Paradox of Fate, described the inevitability of a flawlessly determined force, fate, eventually creating a being who could render it impossible to determine. Was that being Weaver? Or was it Sunny? Or were they one and the same, as far as the eventual paradox went? It did not matter — what mattered was that fate was the source of its own destruction, as well.","So what came between the paradox of the Void and the paradox of fate?","Sunny was inclined to believe that it was the Flame.","The Void, the Flame, and fate — these were three absolute forces, with fate governing the other two. Both fate and the Void had a destructive paradox woven into their very foundation, so why would the Flame be any different?","In fact, Sunny already knew the seed of destruction woven into the very foundation of the Flame — of the existence created by the gods. In fact, there were two strong candidates for what the second paradox, the Paradox of Order, could be.","The first potential seed of destruction was defined by a simple question that Nether, the Demon of Destiny, had once asked the Goddess of the Black Skies... and later expanded on by the Puppeteer Moth, the Spirit of Doubt.","Why did the flame wane?","Sunny found it uncomfortable to think about, but it was true that the Flame that gave life to all of existence waned. Perhaps because it had been cut off from the fuel that was meant to feed it — the Void — or perhaps because that was simply its nature, but the Flame constantly grew weaker.","The Flame was waning, yet at the same time, it was growing stronger — because the lives and aspirations of those the Flame gave life to fueled it. According to the Puppeteer, living beings existed exclusively to feed the Flame with their lives, which was the epitome of cruelty and endless hunger.","Sunny, however, did not really believe the sinister moth. He rather saw the process as a part of natural, symbiotic, and even beautifully poetic order. The Puppeteer insisted that the gods could have made their world flawless, thus sparing all the living things populating it the need to struggle, strive, and aspire — to hurt, fight, and despair.","But Sunny agreed with what Ananke had said once... that a flawless thing was no different from a dead thing, because it could never grow and improve — it could only remain still and unchanging. So, being flawed was the essence of life.","Regardless of whether the Puppeteer had deceived him or not, the Flame waned, but it also fueled itself and grew stronger. It was a wondrous, self-sustaining miracle... but would it always remain the same? Who was to say that the flames of desires burning in the souls of living beings would not become insufficient to fuel the Flame one day, and that it would not be extinguished?","That, in Sunny’s mind, was the first possible explanation of the Paradox of Order.","The second one was far more obvious...","It was the Forgotten God, who was destined to consume the world one day — the literal Flaw of Existence. Or maybe it was daemons, who were born of the Forgotten God.","The daemons... were they the Paradox of Order?","Sunny thought that it was quite probable.","He scratched the tip of his nose.","’Honestly, though, I am not even sure if I should care.’","Cosmic paradoxes and theoretical principles that were so great that even the confines of the vast universe could not contain them... what did any of it have to do with him? Sunny had a bunch of far more practical problems to deal with.","Like eldritch deities who had fallen to Corruption, abyssal horrors that defied understanding, the complicated intricacies of Apotheosis, and the literal damn apocalypse.","Who had time to ponder lofty issues of cosmic proportions when they had to deal with the lowly, mundane issue of the world ending?","Definitely not Sunny.","In fact, Sunny felt that as soon as words like paradoxical, axiomatic, and cosmic entered the conversation, and as soon as he felt the need to invent a word for something more absolute than the absolute... that was his sign to scamper off.","’I should probably follow my own advice and do just that.’","Sunny threw a final look at the runes before dismissing them.","There was one last fact he was yet to address... it was that, apparently, he had the dubious honor of being an avatar of fate.","He had been one in the past, at least, before fate was torn apart.","Much more interesting, though, was that the Nine had been avatars of fate.","That... was bitterly ironic.","After all, one would expect Weaver, the Demon of Fate, to be its champion. Turned out, it was actually the opposite — Weaver had been the enemy of fate, while its nine champions had been born by fate to destroy the nebulous daemon.","In hindsight, it was a miracle that Weaver had survived for so long while going against nine walking manifestations of fate — of an absolute force that both the Void and the Flame bowed to — despite their humble beginning.","Not only that, but Weaver had even defeated the Nine, thwarting their plan to destroy all of existence and enthroning the Nightmare Spell as its new governing force.","The mission of the Nightmare Spell was still shrouded in mystery... one thing about it, however, was clear.","It was that the Spell had not completed its mission yet.","Would it achieve what Weaver had created it to do, in the end?","’I guess it depends on me, Nephis, and Cassie.’","Coincidentally, Sunny was an heir of a daemon, Nephis was an heir of a god, and Cassie was a seer deeply connected to fate.","How would their journey — and therefore Weaver’s design — end?","To answer that question, they would have to wait and see."]},{"number":3109,"title":"Chapter 3109: The Spellweave","paragraphs":["Sunny sighed and looked into the darkness where the runes had shimmered a few moments ago.","It would have been nice if the Spell had explained clearly what the function of [The Weave] truly was. However, in its usual manner, it presented him with a riddle in the form of a conversation between two daemons instead.","Sure, he had learned a lot from the description of the Weave — but nothing about the Weave itself.","That, Sunny would have to discover himself.","He inhaled deeply.","In front of him, Nephis noticed that the shadow cast by the remains of her father was gone. She would have felt the change that had happened to Sunny, as well — in fact, she might have already read his runes. However, at the moment, she was not in a state to pay attention to the esoteric mysteries of cosmic order.","She was fully focused on Broken Sword, instead.","Reaching forward, she touched the weathered bones softly, and then drew them into her Soul Sea. When the remains of her father disappeared, hidden safely in the depths of her soul, Nephis let out a heavy sigh and looked up at the cracked sword rising from the stone and the enchanted lantern hanging from its crossguard.","Somewhere far away, on the other side of the ancient city, Saint and the shades of her fallen kin were still slaughtering the last defenders of the city — there were not a lot of abominations left, while the ranks of her taciturn army were swelling. That battle, too, would be over soon.","However, now that the initial daze of having completed the Weave was gone, Sunny felt an eerie, cold feeling settle in his chest.","He was still overcome with terror.","In fact, his fear had become much more overwhelming — almost palpable.","Sunny frowned and directed his focus inward.","’The Weave... why did that sinister daemon create you? What, exactly, did Weaver want to bequeath to their epigone?’","The Weave granted Sunny many boons, most of which simply made him stronger and more tenacious — especially the latter. But the same could be said about all Divine Lineages. Each of them comprehensively empowered the descendants of the gods, focusing on one aspect of their being in particular.","So what was left if Sunny disregarded the overall tempering he had undergone due to collecting the Weave?","The answer was quite simple. It was almost comically obvious, in fact.","He was left with the ability to weave.","One way or another, each fragment of Weaver’s lineage enhanced his ability to practice Weaver’s sorcery. Blood Weave granted him the ability to perceive spellweaves, Bone Weave allowed him to interact with them, Flesh Weave increased his finesse when handling essence string... and so on.","There was even the Nightmare Spell, which presented him with an endless supply of Memories and Echo to study and learn from.","So, it would not be a reach to say that Weaver had wanted their epigone to master weaving.","But why?","Sunny was a powerful sorcerer, but in the grand scheme of things, his unique way of creating enchantments was not fundamentally greater than other schools of sorcery. He was ahead of most human sorcerers, but that was largely due to his personal talent and power, not the uniqueness of his methods as an enchanter.","He was not the only weaver in existence anymore, either — Ananke was already mastering it, and others would follow.","So what was so important about weaving that the lineage of the Demon of Fate centered around it?","Sunny remained motionless for a moment, searching for something inside himself, and then held his breath.","’Is that?’","The answer he found was frightening in its implications. It was that there was nothing important about weaving in and of itself.","Teaching him how to weave enchantments did not matter — what mattered was what learning how to weave prepared him for.","Sunny had learned how to weave from the Nightmare Spell. He had mastered the foundations of sorcery by observing how it wove Memories and Echoes... so what was the next step?","The next step was to learn from the being who had created the Nightmare Spell. From Weaver. And to do that, Sunny had to observe what Weaver had woven.","Sunny did, in fact, possess something that the Demon of Fate had created personally. It was Weaver’s Mask — one of the two Divine Memories that Weaver had woven and gifted to the High Priest and the High Priestess of the Nightmare Spell.","That was not what Sunny had to observe, though...","There was another creation of Weaver that he had access to.","It was the Nightmare Spell.","The Nightmare Spell, the inner workings of which all Awakened saw in the brief moments between conquering a Nightmare and returning into the harsh embrace of reality — the endless black void illuminated by countless stars, all connected by rays of silver light into a vast and unfathomable pattern.","That starlit void, as well, was a spellweave... it was the Spellweave.","And by observing it, Sunny could learn what Weaver had wanted him to master.","’D—damnation...’","It was right in front of him — in front of everyone — this whole time.","An ugly expression settled on Sunny’s face as he felt the cold claws of fear gripping his heart tighten. He had a feeling that he needed to follow this train of thought to its logical conclusion, fast... or something dreadful was going to happen.","It felt like hours had passed since he absorbed Shadow Weave, but in reality, it was just a handful of seconds. And as another second passed by, Sunny felt a shiver run down his spine.","’The Spellweave?’","There was one glaring, fundamental difference between the weave of the Nightmare Spell and the weaves of Memories and Echoes it and Sunny created. It was that Memories were woven out of essence string, while the Nightmare Spell...","The Nightmare Spell was woven out of Strings of Fate.","Sunny had already gained the ability to touch the Strings of Fate, and he could even glimpse knowledge from them — however, that ability of his was both rudimentary and dangerous.","So, logically, that was what [The Weave] had to have granted him...","A greater capacity to manipulate the Strings of Fate."]},{"number":3110,"title":"Chapter 3110: Gazing into the Abyss","paragraphs":["There was one peculiar trait of Divine Lineages that Sunny had noticed after observing Nephis, as well as heirs of the Great Clans, for a long time. It was that their Divine Lineages did not seem like an overwhelming advantage if the inheritor was weak, but gradually revealed more of their unfathomable potential as the inheritor walked the Path of Ascension and climbed to higher Ranks.","It was as if by drawing closer to the Divine Rank — and to beings who had left behind the Lineages — the heirs of the gods could use more of their inheritance, and only by becoming gods themselves would they unlock its full potential.","Sunny had no reason to believe that Weaver’s lineage was any different. So, even if the purpose of the Weave was to grant him the ability to manipulate the Strings of Fate, he would not be capable of doing so immediately, as a mere Supreme.","However, if he was right... then he would at least be able to see where the path he had been walking was leading, and know which direction to follow.","All Sunny had to do was confirm his suspicion.","And just now, he did.","While peering into the depths of his being, he finally discovered the fundamental change that had happened to him when the Weave was completed — not the quantitative enhancement various aspects of him had undergone, but a qualitative change.","The change had not happened to his body, soul, or mind... or even his shadow.","Instead, it happened to his spirit, building upon the foundation that Spirit Weave had already established.","That alteration had to do with the innate affinity of his Will.","Before, the natural inclination of Sunny’s spirit, and therefore of his Will, was to express the concept of death. However, he had always possessed another, minor affinity — an affinity to fate.","There was nothing minor about it now, though. His lesser affinity had been elevated to a startling height, becoming just as profound as his affinity to shadows and death — in fact, it might have even surpassed them.","As such, for all intents and purposes, Sunny was a unique existence now. He was a Supreme who drew power from two source elements in equal measure... and therefore, in theory, could rule two Domains.","He had no idea what a Fate Domain could look like, or how he was supposed to build it, but he already felt a profound change in his perception of the world.","Somewhere in that change, most likely, hid the key to learning how to manipulate the Strings of Fate. For now, however, Sunny could only tell that he had become greatly attuned to them — no less than Cassie was, perhaps.","That attunement expressed itself as a mystical, miraculous intuition.","Sunny was not even sure that he could call that sense intuition, now — it was a far more expansive and profound form of perception than mere instinct. It not only provided him with seemingly prophetic hints and hunches, but also granted him a profound, subliminal understanding of everything that surrounded him.","As if he was subconsciously drawing knowledge from the Strings of Fate that brushed against him.","Sunny suspected that if the part of the great tapestry of fate that described the future was still intact, he would have been able to sense what would happen in the future, as well.","Since Cassie and he had broken fate, though, all he could sense was the past and present... however, his subconscious grasp of what had transpired and was transpiring around him was now far greater than his conscious understanding, granting him far greater awareness.","His intuition had reached a truly supernatural level.","Sunny finally inhaled, shivering.","Because now that he was aware of how his intuition had changed, he could not help but realize that the eerie fear that had pierced his heart was not rational. It was his subconscious connection to fate telling him that something dreadful was about to happen.","That something terrifying was now imminent.","’What...’","Concentrating on his newfound miraculous intuition, Sunny tried to discern more about the imminent danger.","He couldn’t quite sense what it was, but he managed to determine the direction from which the threat was emanating.","Unsurprisingly, it was the bottomless chasm in front of them.","’It’s time for us to run.’","That was what Sunny wanted to say.","However, as he directed his attention to the dark abyss, a strange compulsion suddenly overcame him. It was as if something vast and invisible enveloped him, effortlessly breaking his formidable defenses — the great fortress wall built around his mind, as well as the deep moat filled to the brim with his titanic Will.","He did not even realize what had happened.","As Saint finished off the last defenders of the city, and as Nephis rose from the ground with a distant look on her face, Sunny fell into a daze. Not quite realizing what he was doing, he walked past her and stopped at the very edge of the cliff, beyond the cracked sword and the shining lantern.","Then, even knowing that he would not see anything in the endless void of elemental darkness, Sunny gazed into the abyss.","And when he did...","The Abyss gazed back at him.","Sunny froze.","Even though he was unable to see, he still perceived what was hidden far below. Perhaps he sensed it through the vibrations of the Strings of Fate, or perhaps the laws of existence were simply twisted and perverted by the being hidden there.","What he saw, drifting there in the abyssal darkness...","Was a giant, weathered skeleton of a humanoid being.","Its bones were broken, the proportions of its body were slightly wrong, and there were three harrowing, empty sockets on its eerie skull.","The being’s flesh was long gone... but it was not dead.","Instead, a universe of appalling Corruption made its nest in the flawlessly white bones, animating them with a profane semblance of life.","No, not profane...","Unholy.","The being gazing at Sunny from the depths of the Abyss was an Unholy Nightmare Creature — a dark god of Corruption. However, it was not the abyssal horror he and Nephis had fought.","Because Sunny could perceive that horror, too.","The abyssal horror was like a web of dark tendrils that had wrapped itself around the giant skeleton, endlessly flowing... binding it.","Restraining it like shackles and imprisoning it in the Abyss.","Or, at least, it had been.","Now that hundreds of the dark tendrils had been incinerated by the flames of Godgrave, its ability to restrain the Unholy abomination was grievously diminished.","In fact, it had become woefully insufficient.","And the prisoner of the Abyss was on the verge of breaking free.","At that moment, Sunny’s shoulders fell.","He realized that it was already too late to escape...","In fact, he had already failed to escape.","Because the moment the Unholy One’s gaze fell on him, and the moment Sunny beheld its harrowing visage, the seeds of Corruption began to bloom in his soul, consuming it — a part of it, at least.","One of his Shadow Cores, the one that belonged to the incarnation standing on the edge of the great chasm, was now overflowing with appalling darkness, being slowly swallowed by it.","Far below, more of the dark tendrils snapped, and the skeleton moved its giant hand slightly.","Pointing a bony finger up.","At that moment, Sunny did two things.","He dismissed Saint.","And he pushed Nephis, who had just pulled the cracked sword out of the stone and picked up her father’s lantern, back — with all the strength he could muster.","Neph’s eyes widened as she was sent flying through the air, breaching hundreds of meters in a single moment.","Almost at the same time, something pierced Sunny’s back.","He looked down, his eyes widening in horror, and saw a strange, needle-like spike of squirming black material protruding from his chest.","He did not even feel any pain.","...A moment later, one of his Shadow Cores exploded.","His incarnation collapsed and was dispelled, his shadow utterly destroyed and vanquished with a single blow.","A wave of blinding pain washed over his consciousness, and somewhere far away, his avatars fell to their knees.","The six of them did.","Because the seventh was no more."]},{"number":3111,"title":"Chapter 3111: Final Heartbeat","paragraphs":["[Your shadow has been destroyed.]","As one of his Shadow Cores exploded, a few others cracking from the aftershock of the devastating blow, Sunny was blinded by pain. He staggered and fell to his knees — all of his remaining incarnations did, some hidden from sight in the dark embrace of shadows, some surrounded by people, some waging war against dreadful abominations on calamitous battlefields.","’N—not good...’","He had lost a Shadow Core, becoming a Terror once again — in an instant. One of his seven shadows, the crazy guy, had also been destroyed. Sunny did not have time to mourn the death of his invaluable helper, though, or think about how easily his incarnation had been killed.","How easily he had been killed.","After all, the disaster was not yet over.","The Unholy abomination was still there, and neither Sunny nor Nephis was out of danger. In fact, Sunny thought that he would be lucky to only lose one incarnation today.","That thing in the Abyss... to say that it scared him would be no different from describing an asteroid impact as bad weather. There were simply no words in the human language to name the feeling it inspired.","Sunny was shaken.","However, he had to act, and he had to act fast.","There had been two of his incarnations in the Underworld. One was gone now, but the other one remained — when Sunny dismissed Saint, he was left alone in utter darkness, suppressed and suffocated by its tenebrous expanse.","He could feel the fractured surface of the ramparts beneath him, as well as the cold wind blowing from the distant abyss. The defenders of the city had been slaughtered, and the shades were gone, having returned into the dark expanse of his soul with their commander. Only the shadow of the Prince of Darkness remained, slowly turning toward the great chasm, far away in the distance.","Nephis flashed past the towering colossus, then landed nimbly on the scorched and fractured surface of the devastated square. She slid back dozens of meters, finally coming to a halt at the very edge of a deep fissure.","By then, the Prince of Darkness was already swinging his enormous sword. The blade of the titanic greatsword, almost two hundred meters in length, was slow to accelerate — however, when it gathered momentum, its edge was heavy enough to cut the world apart.","However, before the colossal shade could deliver the blow, an invisible presence flickered in the darkness in front of it.","In the next moment, the towering figure of the Prince of Darkness was obliterated, disintegrating into a million pieces. The shadow of a Supreme Titan crumpled in the blink of an eye, vanquished without offering any resistance. Torn apart like a paper figurine.","Sunny was covered in cold sweat, gritting his teeth as terror clawed at his heart.","He was surrounded by elemental darkness, utterly devoid of power. There was no time to assume the form of the Jade Saint and channel Neph’s flames, either. He only had a few moments left to act.","So, gathering all his strength, he raised his hand, made it into a fist, and slammed it into the ground with all the strength of a Supreme.","The ground quaked.","In an instant, a dreadful amount of kinetic energy was converted into heat. The surface of the ancient stone shattered beneath his blow, melting and vaporizing in a destructive conflagration.","And therefore, there was a flash of light.","This mundane light was weak and feeble, easily defeated by the endless mass of true darkness — its radiance was dim, and it had only lasted a brief moment.","But that moment was all Sunny needed to dive into the embrace of shadows cast by the fleeting explosion of light and emerge from them many kilometers away, in front of Nephis.","There, the mystical lantern left behind by Broken Sword still glowed, illuminating the ruined streets of the ancient city and summoning countless shadows into existence. Sunny arrived just in time to reach forward and catch Nephis, helping her balance herself and pulling her away from the edge of the deep fissure.","For a moment, they were face to face, pale and terrified.","That terror was not something they could control — it was simply an inevitable consequence of mortal beings finding themselves in the presence of a god... a fallen and corrupted god. That was why even Nephis, who had always shared a distant relationship with fear, could not control it now.","\"Sunny...\"","Her whisper was barely audible.","Unlike Sunny, Nephis was not sensitive to fate, so she had not witnessed the prisoner of the Abyss. However, she had inherited the Knowledge of Corruption, so she must have sensed it in her own way.","Sunny did not answer. There was no time for words — he knew that they only had moments left to live.","Trying to run was meaningless, as well. How could they hope to outrun a god? Speed and distance meant nothing in the face of an Unholy creature. Reality was nothing but a malleable canvas for that being, fragile and brittle. With a thought, it could bring them back.","Sunny raised a hand, feeling like he was suffocating.","He had not felt so weak and powerless — utterly helpless — in a long, long while.","How could a demigod feel that way?","Sunny was standing with his back to the great chasm, while Nephis was facing it. He saw her eyes widen as he looked over his shoulder, trembling uncontrollably.","’Faster, faster...’","He looked down, fearing catching a glimpse of what Nephis saw, reflected in the dark depths of her terrified eyes.","There was an eerie sound... the sound of stone turning to dust, of a waterfall turning to ice, of winds dying as something that had never been meant to exist moved through them.","Perhaps it was a giant, skeletal hand rising above the edge of the boundless black void.","Sunny felt it then...","A clear premonition.","A damning understanding that he only had a single heartbeat left to live.","’Faster!’","And, just then, a Memory finally manifested itself into existence in his hand, woven out of darkness.","It was a small lantern carved from black stone.","Sunny finally remembered how to breathe.","Before the gaze of the Unholy horror fell on them, he turned into a shadow and pulled Nephis into the gate of the Shadow Lantern.","In the next moment, both of them disappeared.","The black lantern fell to the ground, rolled on shattered stone, and vanished without a trace.","A dead silence settled over the Underworld.","Now, once again, only darkness remained, shrouding its vast and dreadful expanse."]},{"number":3112,"title":"Chapter 3112: Shoot for the Moon","paragraphs":["Escaping the shadows, Sunny and Nephis rolled down a tall dune of obsidian dust before coming to a stop at its bottom. Above them, the black sky of the Shadow Realm was illuminated by the pale radiance of a distant essence storm.","Around them, the desolate expanse of the Realm of Death stretched endlessly in all directions, cold winds blowing across its surface. The world was silent.","The two of them remained motionless for a long while, breathing heavily. Their wildly beating hearts were slow to calm down, and the indescribable terror of facing an Unholy One still echoed in their dazed, rattled minds.","Eventually, though, Sunny was able to breathe normally again. He let out a heavy sigh and groaned, finally sensing the dull pain radiating through his soul. Where one of his Soul Cores had been once, there was now nothing but emptiness — the jagged wound dealt to his soul was not fatal, but it was still painful, making him feel like a cripple.","Still...","’We made it out.’","At the end there, all he could think about was summoning the Shadow Lantern and escaping through its gate — once Sunny pulled Nephis with him into the embrace of shadows, he hurriedly dismissed the Divine Memory, leaving the prisoner of the Abyss no chance to follow them.","Perhaps the creature could have twisted the enchantments of a different Memory with its profane Will, but the Shadow Lantern was a relic left behind by Shadow God — so, Sunny had hoped that even an Unholy abomination would not be able to influence it easily.","It seemed like he had been right. After all, neither of them would be alive otherwise.","Thinking about the creature imprisoned in the Abyss made Sunny shiver again, and his instinctual fear swelled once more.","’Damnation.’","He was properly shaken by the encounter with that horrid thing.","After a while, Nephis sat up and brushed the obsidian dust off her hair. Sunny pushed himself off the ground, as well, looking around with a lost expression. Neither of them said anything, trying to recover from the harrowing experience.","Sunny’s thoughts were wild and disjointed, swarming in his head like a cloud of wasps.","A long while later, he looked at Nephis and hesitated for a moment before speaking. In the end, all he could say was:","\"That thing... the Unholy One... it simply pointed at me, Nephis. And I died.\"","Sunny’s voice was grim. He pursed his lips, and then added somberly:","\"No. Even before that, it only had to gaze at me to infect my soul with Corruption. It only had to look my way to destroy me.\"","Sunny was not just anyone, either. He was... he had been a Supreme Titan. He stood at the very pinnacle of power among all humans — people who could compare to him could be counted on the fingers of one hand, and even among them, nobody could claim to surpass him with any measure of confidence. And yet, the prisoner of the Abyss obliterated him so easily.","Neph’s expression was dark. She remained silent for a moment, then said quietly:","\"We knew how powerful the Unholy Nightmare Creatures would be.\"","Then, she inhaled deeply and shook her head.","\"However, knowing and experiencing it are two entirely different things. The power of that dreadful thing was beyond anything I had imagined. It was... sobering.\"","Sunny could only give a grim nod.","Sobering... yes, that was the right word. He had known that Unholy abominations would be terrifying and unfathomably powerful — and yet, he still underestimated just how harrowing they would be.","Sunny and Nephis were in a hurry to challenge the Fifth Nightmare and become Spirits. Before, he had thought that conquering Apotheosis would buy them some time — but now, he was starting to suspect that simply becoming Sacred would not be enough to prepare them for what was about to come.","Sunny could not imagine winning a battle against the prisoner of the Abyss without becoming a Divine being himself first. Even if he and Nephis managed to defeat the horrid creature, somehow, while still being Spirits...","Sunny was suddenly covered in cold sweat.","Even if they defeated that profane creature, there were others like it. Was there a handful of them? A dozen? More?","The thought itself was terrifying.","At the moment, Sunny knew of only a few Unholy Nightmare Creatures. There was the thing in the Abyss. One was theorized to dwell in the skull of the continent-sized skeleton in Godgrave... it was too close to human civilization for him to remain undisturbed by the idea.","And then, there was one hidden on the Moon.","’No wonder Professor Obel warned me to never look at the Moon too closely.’","There was probably an Unholy abomination hidden in the heart of the Burned Forest, another one in the frozen wastelands west of Ravenheart... perhaps the eerie darkness that was swallowing Citadels in the far east was a manifestation of an Unholy One’s power, as well. Who knew how many more there were, and where they were hiding?","But it was the one on the Moon that frightened Sunny the most.","Once the waking world was entirely consumed by the Dream Realm, Earth’s moon would be swallowed, as well. It would shine upon the Dream Realm one day — where the laws of the waking world would not be suppressing the being that dwelled on its surface anymore.","The being would be able to gaze down and abandon its lunar prison then, descending into the world below.","How would humanity survive then?","Sunny’s expression turned darker and darker.","Having become Sacred, would he and Nephis survive if beings like the one they had just barely escaped besieged them on all sides?","That was highly unlikely.","So, if they conquered the Fifth Nightmare, there would be no time at all to collect themselves and prepare for the next one. They would have to reach the Moon and challenge the Sixth Nightmare as well — challenge it almost immediately.","So, entering the Seed of the Fifth Nightmare would be like reaching the finish line. After that, it would be full steam ahead until they either became Divine — became true gods — or died.","Therefore, humanity would either be saved or perish with them.","Sunny grimaced.","’What is it that people say? Dream big?’","Shoot for the moon?","He had never thought that this simple phrase would sound so sinister one day."]},{"number":3113,"title":"Chapter 3113: Post Mortem","paragraphs":["Sunny fell silent again, finally able to think straight.","There was a lot to think about... albeit not much time to do so.","They had escaped the danger momentarily, but he did not feel safe. In fact, Sunny felt more vulnerable than ever, here in the lifeless realm that was supposed to be his natural environment.","Strangely enough, his soul was not being eroded by the Shadow Realm nearly as much as it had been before. That was probably because, this time, he had not come here as a masterless shadow — his connection to Nephis was protecting him to a large degree.","Nephis herself was not affected too much, either. It was unclear whether staying in the Shadow Realm for long would still destroy her, but for now, she seemed fine. In fact, it was as if her entire figure was emanating a subtle, beautiful radiance, illuminating the dark sands around them.","Nevertheless, Sunny was anxious.","The Shadow Realm was connected to the Underworld, after all... it was connected to it by the Abyss. So, the prisoner of the Abyss was not that far, hidden somewhere in the darkness above them.","That thing was not the only danger they could face, either.","There were the Dark Drifters and other Creatures of Darkness that came to the Realm of Death to hunt the shadows. There were far more terrifying creatures here, as well.","Sunny had not forgotten the warning Eurys had given him once — the warning about harrowing beings that dwelled in the heart of the Shadow Realm. However, he understood that warning better now.","The last and most dreadful battle of the Doom War had happened right here, in this desolate land. The Void Gate had been opened here, as well, at its very center.","What did it mean?","It meant that the strongest beings of both the Demon Legion and the Divine Host had been here when Corruption invaded the world. It spread from here across all of existence... which meant that the soldiers who had fought in that calamitous final battle were the first ones to be swallowed by Corruption.","The strongest champions of the Doom War and Corruption... were not a good mix.","Sunny was suddenly very glad that he had listened to Eurys and abandoned his ambitions of exploring the depths of the Shadow Realm.","’That bastard is not entirely useless, after all...’","And speaking of Eurys. Had he not mentioned reaching the Shadow Realm by traversing the Abyss?","Now that Sunny knew what dwelled in that bottomless well of elemental darkness, he could not help but feel a sense of grim astonishment.","’How the hell did he get past both the abyssal horror and that horrid thing?’","No wonder Eurys had been in such a pathetic state when Sunny stumbled on him, with many of his bones shattered, barely able to move.","The fact that there was anything left of him at all was already startling.","Sunny inhaled deeply, thinking back to the dreadful visage of the giant skeleton hidden in the Abyss.","What was that thing?","Was it a nephilim who had succumbed to Corruption? That was not supposed to be possible.","Or was it the corpse of one, reanimated by an endless mass of Corruption that used its bones as a shell?","Or was it the remains of an actual angel?","What about the abyssal horror, then? What was it and why would it keep the Unholy One bound? Was it feeding on it, somehow? Had it been created by Nether instead, tasked with restraining a test subject? Had it been born before or after the Doom War?","Sunny was not sure. What he was certain about, however, was that the metaphor that had come to his mind when he first beheld the prisoner of the Abyss was not entirely figurative. He could only describe the terrifying rot nestling within the ancient bones as a universe of appalling darkness... and he did not know if that was an exaggeration.","Sunny knew that the souls of Divine beings were vast. The entire Shadow Realm had been hidden inside Shadow God once... had been Shadow God. So, how vast was the rotten expanse of an Unholy abomination’s soul?","The world inside Ariel’s Tomb was fashioned from the soul of an Unholy Titan, whom the Demon of Dread had slain. If anything, Sunny now suspected that Ariel had only used a fraction of it to create his masterpiece.","He could not help but shiver.","When he read the story of how Ariel had slain the Stone Titan for the first time, it sounded quite epic. But now, having met an actual Unholy being, Sunny could only think of it as utterly terrifying.","’Damn daemons...’","He inhaled deeply, trying to calm himself, and thought back to the moment of his death.","Only now that some time had passed did Sunny begin to realize how close to complete destruction he had come. It was as he told Nephis — all the prisoner of the Abyss had to do was point at his incarnation to destroy it.","Actually, that might have been a mercy. Although that thing probably did not know it, it had done Sunny a favor. If the Unholy horror had not destroyed his incarnation, all of Sunny would have become a Nightmare Creature by now, all seven of his Shadow Cores consumed by Corruption.","’I should count my blessings, I guess?’","Sunny smiled weakly.","The most terrifying part, however... was that they had gotten impossibly lucky. Sunny was a unique being because he was divided into seven incarnations, so he only lost one of them. If anyone else had happened to be in his place, however, they would have simply been killed in the blink of an eye.","Nephis, Mordret... Cassie, Ananke...","None of them would have survived that blow. The moment the prisoner of the Abyss pointed at them, they would have been erased from existence once and for all.","That, too, put the power of the Unholy Ones into perspective.","And that perspective was so stark that it was difficult not to fall to the ground in utter despair.","Sunny remained motionless for a long while, then grimaced.","’That’s nothing new.’","He had felt the same way when facing the Mountain King for the first time, watching the Spire Messenger fly above the Forgotten Shore, when Solvane tore the heart out of his chest in the Kingdom of Hope, when the Winter Beast wiped out the remains of the First Evacuation Army in the Antarctic Center, when he first witnessed a storm made of rustling swords obscure the sky...","All those threats, and countless others like them, had seemed insurmountable once — and yet, to the Sunny of today, they were nothing but trivial obstacles.","With enough time and effort, the prisoner of the Abyss and other Unholy horrors would be the same.","So, there was no point in wasting time on despair.","...That was what Sunny forced himself to believe, at least.","For now, he had more practical matters to attend to."]},{"number":3114,"title":"Chapter 3114: Missing Core","paragraphs":["Sunny’s soul had been dealt a severe blow, losing one of his Shadow Cores.","There were obvious consequences, like the dull pain he was experiencing and his diminished power. The craziest of his shadows was gone, making him feel sad and a little depressed... as if a part of him was gone. It was, quite literally.","’I’ll miss that guy...’","His feelings regarding the demise of a loyal shadow aside, there was also the fact that he was once again a Terror, meaning that there was less of him out there. He could be in fewer places at the same time, could empower fewer things, and if he wanted to focus all his power in one place, the augmentation would not be as potent as it had been before.","As for the soul wound... it wasn’t as bad as it could have been. Losing a single core was not going to kill a Titan, and especially not Sunny — his soul was especially tenacious, after all, and would slowly recover if even a little piece of it remained intact.","However, there were also less obvious consequences of plummeting to a lesser Class.","Sunny would be unable to summon the full form of the Curse until his seventh Shadow Core was rebuilt, for example.","Much more importantly... one of his Shadows was homeless now.","Each of the Shadows dwelled in one of his Shadow Cores, drawing on its power and retreating into its nurturing dark flames to heal and recover. Now that Sunny was a Terror, he had seven Shadows, but only six cores, meaning that someone could not find shelter within his soul anymore.","That someone was Slayer.","Sunny had been afraid that this strange situation would result in the destruction of the bond between him and the murderous Shadow, but luckily, the situation was not that dire. Slayer was still his Shadow, and he still felt a connection to her... however, she could not be dismissed.","That meant that if Slayer was wounded, she could not be healed by the dark flames of his soul — which presented a problem, since she was in the middle of a vicious war against the Barrow Wraiths right now. Receiving ghastly wounds and being mangled by the enemy was not a rare occurrence, and if these wounds kept accumulating, Slayer would inevitably be destroyed.","Unknown complications could arise in the near future, as well. Sunny did not entirely understand how the connection between him and the Shadows functioned, but he knew that they depended on him. Where did the essence they used to fuel themselves come from? Would its current run dry without the dark cradle of a Shadow Core? Would they wither and fade as time went on?","Sunny did not know. And he would rather not find out.","Luckily for him...","Sunny looked around.","If he wanted to build a new Shadow Core and become a Titan again, he was in the right place. There was nowhere in the Dream Realm where he could accomplish that goal faster. The vast expanse of the Shadow Realm surrounded him, promising a thrilling hunt.","It was just that Sunny was not in the mood to wander the Realm of Death in search of powerful shadows to consume. He did not have the time, and there were all the threats he had just been thinking about, as well.","However...","Sunny’s expression turned pensive.","Maybe he didn’t need to.","After all, he had just attained Shadow Weave. Among various boons it granted him, there was one that could help him solve this particular issue. Perhaps it was time to test his new powers.","Sunny remained motionless for a few moments, then took a deep breath and dove into his Soul Sea.","’Here goes nothing.’","Instantly, the familiar landscape revealed itself to his mind’s eye. The dark waters of his soul were still and silent. The lightless sky above encompassed six tenebrous black spheres, a few of them covered in cracks and healing slowly. The Nameless Temple towered above the water, surrounded by a legion of shades.","There was a vast sea of silent shadows populating his soul now. Some were distinct, while some were vague and elusive — the former were whole, while the latter had been vanquished recently and were now being mended.","Sunny’s gaze shifted to a particular direction, where the newest recruits of the Shadow Legion stood. Unlike the rest of the shades, these ones were assembled into neat battle formations, standing upon the still water like a disciplined army. They were six thousand Shadow Saints, commanded by dozens of Supreme officers...","The colossal shadow of the Prince of Darkness was also there, wreathed in nurturing black flames. The mighty shade had been utterly obliterated by the prisoner of the Abyss, but luckily, the Titan of Tainted Jade was merely vanquished, not destroyed. In a few days, he would be ready to be summoned again, adding his strength to the power of the Shadow Legion.","Beyond them, countless other shades stood, stretching toward the dark horizon — every living being Sunny had slain over the years, except for those who were summoned and fighting his enemies on various battlefields. Hundreds of thousands still remained, all looking at the steps of the Nameless Temple, where their Sovereign stood.","Sunny exhaled and sat down on one of the steps, looking at his shades intently. Slowly, his gaze focused on a particular one — a beast he had once slain on the Chained Isles, an eternity ago.","He could feel a deeper connection to that beast than before. It was as if his authority over the shades had expanded, becoming not necessarily greater, but broader in its implications.","There was no instruction manual to Shadow Weave — unless the cryptic conversation between Weaver and Oblivion could be considered one — but Sunny could vaguely sense a new kind of power slumbering somewhere deep within him.","So, he reached toward that power and explored it carefully, trying to discern its functions. He felt like a blind man trying to guess the nature of an unknown mechanism by tracing its shape with his fingers — it was mysterious, unclear, and covered in darkness.","Eventually, though, his intuition gave him a hint of what he had to do, and how he could do it.","Sunny inhaled deeply and looked at the bestial shade, commanding it to... dissolve.","For a few moments, nothing happened.","Then, the black beast was suddenly enveloped by dark flames, its form slowly melting in their tenebrous embrace.","In a few moments, the shade vanished in a black blaze, disappearing without a trace.","Once the dark flames were dispelled, the Spell whispered in Sunny’s ear:","[Your shadow grows stronger.]","Summoning the runes, Sunny looked at the string he had not paid attention to for a long, long while.","It read:","Shadow Fragments: [0/6000].","He grimaced.","He had clearly felt his soul being reinforced when the black beast was consumed. It was just that it did not offer him as many shadow fragments as a true shadow would — instead, it offered him as many as consuming an Ascended soul shard would grant a Supreme.","A fraction of a single shadow fragment... but not nothing.","Sunny exhaled slowly and looked down.","’That works.’","When he raised his gaze again, his eyes glinted darkly.","And when they did, a vast inferno of dark flames suddenly enveloped the silent expanse of his soul. Thousands of shades burned in the cataclysmic blaze, chosen carefully to become sacrifices.","The runes shimmered and changed.","Shadow Fragments: [3/6000].","Shadow Fragments: [23/6000].","Shadow Fragments: [194/6000].","Shadow Fragments: [447/6000].","Shadow Fragments: [1342/6000]...","The counter continued to climb and climb.","Until, eventually, it reached completion.","’Oh, hell!’","Focused on his new power, Sunny had forgotten what would follow.","A ghastly pain suddenly pierced his entire being...","The pain of a new Shadow Core forming in the depths of his soul."]},{"number":3115,"title":"Chapter 3115: Dark and Sinister","paragraphs":["[Your shadow is complete.]","Sunny hissed, finally feeling that the pain tearing his soul apart was subsiding. His new Shadow Core was fully formed, and he was a Titan again — already. It did not take him long to reclaim his Class at all. Of course, it had also cost him countless shades, weakening his Domain somewhat. But all in all, that loss was one he could easily cope with.","With the kind of battles he was fighting these days, those of his shades that were below the Ascended Rank rarely had an opportunity to do something useful. So, he had consumed many of those, as well as some that were more powerful, but were difficult to integrate into the Shadow Legion. In fact, it felt like he was doing a long-needed cleanup of his soul... it already felt less crowded.","In the future, he would have to explore this newfound ability more. Could he consolidate the Shadow Legion, perhaps, making those of his shades that were truly powerful even more so?","Somehow, Sunny doubted it. Shades were dead, after all, and therefore static. It was against their nature to change and grow.","However, he could turn some of his shades into Shadows, and fuel those with the lesser shades. He would not need to hunt for Memories to feed them anymore — at least up to the Supreme Rank. Beyond that, even he did not know how to help his Shadows conquer Apotheosis, or if it was even possible. The Spell, at least, was either refusing or incapable of offering assistance.","Regardless, at the moment, Sunny could only shelve that idea. He already had seven Shadows, after all, and could not accommodate another.","Sunny felt that he would find a way to do just that sooner or later, though.","For now, he exhaled slowly and looked at Nephis.","She seemed to have recovered somewhat, looking at him silently. Sunny did not have to explain what had happened to him, since Nephis could read his runes just fine — she would know that he had completed the Weave, that he lost a Shadow Core, and that he managed to build a new one by sacrificing thousands of his shades.","A pale smile appeared on Sunny’s lips.","\"See? I’m as good as new. No need to worry.\"","Then, he groaned and spat a bit of blood.","Nephis gave him a long look, then sighed and shook her head.","\"Your shadow is staring at me.\"","Hearing that, Sunny turned his gaze to the shadow his body was casting onto the black sand. It was even darker than the obsidian dust it was lying on, motionless, gazing at Nephis intently instead of obediently copying his movements.","Sunny frowned.","He had not known what to expect from the new shadow, but hoped that it would be like the crazy guy, reborn. However, the newcomer was quite different from his fallen predecessor.","The new shadow just seemed... dark. Far darker than it was supposed to be, and more than a little bit sinister as well.","In fact, Sunny felt a cold chill run down his spine when he looked at it.","He sighed.","\"Welcome to the world of the living, new guy. Well, to the Realm of Death, I guess. I’ll call you... wait, we already have a creepy shadow. Huh, what then?\"","Sunny pondered for a moment, then opened his mouth with a glint in his eyes.","However, before he could speak, Nephis interrupted him:","\"Do not name him Creepy Number Two.\"","The glint in Sunny’s eyes dimmed.","He remained silent for a moment, then scoffed.","\"Whatever. Let’s go with eerie, then. That fits your sinister ambiance, too.\"","The eerie shadow slowly turned its head and stared at him silently.","All shadows were silent, but this shadow’s subtle silence was strangely unsettling. Sunny coughed, took control of his new invaluable helper, and manifested him into an avatar. After doing that, he allowed his other incarnation to turn into a shadow instead.","Looking at Nephis, he sighed.","\"Should we finish our expedition here?\"","It was easy for him to leave the Shadow Realm. All he had to do was use one of his other incarnations to summon the Shadow Lantern, and escape the desolate land through its gate.","Nephis raised an eyebrow.","\"You have a different idea?\"","Sunny hesitated for a moment, then nodded.","\"I think... before we go, we can visit an old friend.\"","Rising from the sand, Nephis nodded.","\"Let’s do that, then. I wanted to meet him for a long time, as well.\"","There was a lot they had to discuss, adjusting their plans in light of this new, harrowing experience. Cassie would have to participate in that discussion, as well... even Mordret, if he was willing, not to mention Ananke.","For example, they had to determine the probability of the prisoner of the Abyss escaping the Underworld. Sunny felt that the creature would not be able to leave, at least for now — the abyssal horror that had kept it bound was not dead, after all, just wounded. It would recover from the damage it had received soon. Most of all, however, there were the white mists that shrouded the Hollow Mountain.","Nothing could keep the Void from seeping into the world. Surely, a single Unholy being — a creature merely tainted by the Void, not born from it — would not be able to break through its flowing cage easily.","But since Sunny and Nephis were already in the Shadow Realm, they could visit Eurys first.","They did not walk to their destination, of course. Instead, Sunny used Shadow Step to carry them both through the desolate wasteland. After the suffocating darkness of the Underworld, being surrounded by the endless expanse of shadows felt like a breath of fresh air — soothing and liberating.","On top of that, he was not being eaten alive by the Shadow Realm... at least not as blatantly as before. So, Sunny actually enjoyed their swift journey across the sea of obsidian dunes.","He was moving with astonishing speed, but it was still going to take them a little time to reach Eurys.","So, not wishing to waste it, Sunny summoned his runes once again.","This time, he ignored the counter showing his shadow fragments and looked directly at a different string of runes.","The ones describing his Shadows... in particular, the one describing Saint.","Saint had almost finished her evolution, after all.","This time, she achieved it much faster than ever before — perhaps because she had already been halfway to reaching a higher Class, perhaps simply because the situation had demanded it.","The runes read:","Shadow: Jade Saint.","Shadow Rank: Supreme.","Shadow Class: Tyrant."]},{"number":3116,"title":"Chapter 3116: Princess of the Underworld","paragraphs":["Shadow: Jade Saint.","Shadow Rank: Supreme.","Shadow Class: Tyrant.","Sunny looked at these runes for a short while, feeling deeply satisfied. Finally, after a long while, Saint had evolved to a new Class once more — this time reaching the coveted title of a Tyrant.","There was a qualitative jump in power between a Devil and a Tyrant, marking the latter as the first of the higher Classes, so he had high expectations for his oldest and most loyal Shadow.","Sunny continued to study the runes.","They read:","Shadow Attributes: [Princess of the Underworld], [Warmaster], [Stalwart], [Flame of Divinity], [Heart of Darkness], [Vessel of Nothing].","Shadow Abilities: [Royal Banner], [Weapon Sage], [Underworld Armament], [Mantle of Darkness], [Blade of Darkness], [Shield of Nothing].","There were two new additions — one Attribute and one Ability. Saint had absorbed a great deal of both true darkness and nothingness, as well, meaning that her elemental Abilities had grown far more potent.","The new Attribute had quite a catchy name. Sunny focused on it, reading the description.","Attribute: [Princess of the Underworld].","Attribute Description: [This Shadow has inherited the crown of the Underworld, and with it, the legacy of endless war.]","Sunny stared at the short description for a while, contemplating it.","’The crown of the Underworld...’","It was not difficult to understand the hidden meaning of these words. A long time ago, Nether had bestowed seven suits of armor to his most flawless creations. However, those suits of armor — the Mantles of the Underworld — were both a gift and a trial.","Sunny suspected that those of Nether’s favorite children who had passed the trial would have been recognized as his heirs, the Princes of the Underworld — like the Titan of Tainted Jade, the Prince of Darkness.","After all, Sunny had completed that trial himself, and that was the name of the enchantment responsible for tallying his victories.","However, all of the Princes were dead now, having either been destroyed in the endless war their creator had started or consumed by Corruption. The last of the seven Princes had been slain by Saint — so, ironically enough, she was the one who proved herself worthy of Nether’s inheritance in the end, not them.","Only Saint was not one of Nether’s favored creations, and neither had she received a suit of armor from him. Instead, she had forged her armor herself and had chosen her own path, walking among the shadows through true darkness and nothingness.","It was quite fitting, actually, for someone created by the Demon of Choice.","Sadly...","The kingdom she was supposed to inherit was long gone. Her people were extinct, the cities of the Underworld lay in ruin, and even Nether himself was dead. So, this crown of his was an empty promise — a symbol of a long-forgotten past that carried great weight, but offered very little to its wearer.","Maybe that Attribute did grant Saint some benefit, like gaining recognition among the creatures of the Underworld or being able to control ancient sorceries left behind by Nether better. But mostly, it must have simply functioned as a symbol of her authority — a spiritual mark that proclaimed her status as a Tyrant.","The Ability she had gained was much more interesting.","Sunny shifted his gaze to the runes that described it.","Ability: [Royal Banner].","Ability Description: [Those who fight under this Shadow’s stalwart banner are connected to her by the bond of loyalty, and are therefore bestowed the boon of her command. They are vessels of her will and conduits of her power, becoming living armaments for their commander to wield.]","Sunny’s gaze grew sharper.","If he was not wrong... then the [Royal Banner] Ability allowed Saint to fulfill the role of a general. Those who followed her command would be connected to her by a mystical bond, and through her to each other. That would allow Saint to command her soldiers directly, and therefore any army she commanded would act with an extreme level of unity, cohesion, and tactical excellence.","She possessed the [Warmaster] Attribute, after all, which expressed her profound knowledge of all kinds of warfare.","That alone was a tremendous boon. However, the description implied much more... it implied that Saint’s soldiers would be enhanced by the connection to their general, sharing in her might.","What did it mean?","It meant that they would be infused with her Will, as well as inherit a measure of her power.","Not all of her power, of course — at least Sunny did not think so. The [Underworld Armament], [Mantle of Darkness], [Blade of Darkness], and [Shield of Nothing] Abilities were too specific, after all, and could only function because of Saint’s [Heart of Darkness] and [Vessel of Nothing] Attributes.","However, that left one Ability... perhaps the most important Ability of them all.","It was [Weapon Sage].","If all soldiers under Saint’s banner inherited a lesser version of her sublime and varied martial skill — while already benefiting from the direct control of a Warmaster on a tactical level — then the army she commanded would be truly terrifying. It would be nearly impossible to defeat unless the enemy forces were utterly, overwhelmingly superior in terms of raw power.","Among soldiers, experience was more valuable than gold, as were ability and talent. Those who dwelled on the battlefield rarely lived long, so experience was difficult to come by — a seasoned veteran was worth ten inexperienced recruits, or maybe more. If that veteran was not only seasoned, but also competent and gifted, though, they were simply priceless.","What the combination of the [Warmaster] Attribute’s influence and the lesser version of the [Weapon Sage] Ability did... was make every soldier under Saint’s command equal to such a priceless veteran.","An army composed of only seasoned, indomitable elites... was an army Sunny never wanted to face on the battlefield.","He would rather be the commander of that army — or rather, the liege lord of that army’s commander.","And now, it seemed that he was.","’Damn.’","In short, Saint was now a force multiplier that could dramatically elevate the power of the entire Shadow Legion.","Sunny had gained a legion of Shadow Saints and the shadow of the Prince of Darkness, as well, not to mention Shadow Weave.","Overall, the expedition to the Underworld had proven to be quite fruitful... despite its disastrous ending.","As Sunny rushed across the desolate expanse of the Shadow Realm, carrying Nephis with him, he could not help but feel a hint of dark exhilaration.","He did not know what the future held, but he knew one thing.","Now that Saint was a Tyrant...","Those damn Barrow Wraiths would learn what sorrow meant very, very soon."]},{"number":3117,"title":"Chapter 3117: Old Bones","paragraphs":["Eventually, they made it to the graveyard of Soul Serpents. Eurys was just where Sunny had left him — a dozen kilometers away, at the bottom of a tall dune.","It seemed that the ancient skeleton had not managed to crest it yet, rolling down its steep slope countless times.","At the moment, he was sprawled on the black sand, staring at the sky. A distant essence storm illuminated his shattered bones, painting an eerie picture — when Sunny and Nephis rose from the shadows, the white skull turned, staring at them with empty eye sockets.","Sunny had to suppress a shudder, remembering the abhorrent skeleton that lay hidden in the Abyss.","Eurys remained silent for a few moments, and then said in a creaky voice:","\"My, oh my. It seems that I have guests. Ah, what to do? Please forgive me, children... the whole place is a mess...\"","From his tone, it was hard to say what place he was talking about — the bottom of the tall dune, the Shadow Realm, or the entire world.","In any case, the description fit all three.","Nephis approached the battered skeleton and looked down at it, expressionless. Eventually, she said:","\"So you are alive, after all.\"","Eurys laughed.","\"Alive? Oh, I wouldn’t go that far... but it’s good to see you too, abomination.\"","Sunny frowned.","\"Hey, bastard. What did I say about using that word?\"","The ancient skull turned slightly, staring at him.","Then, Eurys chuckled.","\"Something about breaking my old bones? Salutations, boy. How many cities did you destroy this time?\"","Sunny scoffed with an indignant expression, offended by that greeting. It was as if Eurys thought him to be some kind of walking calamity hellbent on sawing destruction everywhere he went.","\"What? None! Why would you think...\"","But then, he abruptly closed his mouth and just glared at the ancient skeleton silently for a few moments.","In the end, Sunny had to say through gritted teeth:","\"One... and half.\"","He did... sort of... destroy Weave when he and the Thieving Bird fell from the sky and crashed into it during their battle. And while the nameless city in the heart of the Underworld ultimately survived, a couple of the great stalagmites did end up crumbling and falling into the white mist.","Eurys just stared at him silently. Despite the fact that the old skull could not express any emotions, Sunny could not help but feel that his gaze was mocking.","Eventually, the ancient skeleton cackled.","\"Good job! You’ve been gone for so long, so I really thought that it’d be a bigger number. You have really restrained yourself well, it seems!\"","Sunny let out a heavy sigh and sat down on the sand near Eurys. Nephis followed his example, and a few moments later, the ancient skeleton asked in a curious tone:","\"So, what have you been up to since our last meeting?\"","He seemed... more subdued than usual, somehow. Maybe Neph’s presence made Eurys want to be on his best behavior, or maybe he was simply tired of endlessly trying and failing to scale the steep dune.","Maybe the curse of Shadow God was finally catching up to him, and he was slowly losing himself.","Remembering the appalling end of Azarax, the King of Kings, Sunny felt his gaze turning somber.","He remained silent for a short while, then spoke in a reserved tone:","\"What have I been up to? Well, let’s see...\"","Sunny thought back to everything that had happened since his last conversation with Eurys.","\"I went to Ariel’s Hell and took your old friend, Azarax, off the tree. The curse consumed him eventually, but he helped me get to the old tomb hidden in the heart of that dismal place. I climbed into the Tomb of Ariel, found the loathsome bird who had stolen my fate, and killed it. The vile thing did not stay dead for long, but I managed to reclaim what it had taken from me... even if, in the process, the damn bird absconded with more of my possessions.\"","Sunny grimaced and then continued in a dark tone:","\"After that, I sealed a terrible idea in a deep well to save humanity. Later... the world is ending, so I was quite busy trying to keep it from falling apart. I did go on a mountain trip with my girlfriend — one thing led to another, and we ended up making the sun rise in the Underworld. It was quite a sight.\"","Sunny chuckled joylessly.","\"The view was simply to die for. And I did... and so, here I am, in the Land of Death.\"","Eurys stared at him silently for a long while, not saying anything.","In the end, though, he spoke in a friendly tone:","\"My, oh my! It is good that you took Azarax... that insufferable buffoon... off the tree. Your tale was quite amusing, as well. But, uh... I wasn’t asking you, boy.\"","Sunny blinked a couple of times.","He threw a furtive glance at Nephis.","\"Oh.\"","She smiled faintly.","\"The last time we met, I was still Dormant, wasn’t I?\"","Eurys nodded.","\"And look at you now! Already a mighty Supreme. Well, you nephilim were always an eerie kind.\"","He looked at Sunny and asked:","\"Do you know what that abominable girl said when she found Azarax and me in the middle of hell, boy?\"","Sunny silently shook his head.","Eurys laughed.","\"I don’t need two guides, she said. So, pick among yourselves whom I should free. My, oh my! Can you believe it?\"","He did his best impression of Neph’s dispassionate tone, then laughed again, as if finding the memory infinitely amusing.","Sunny looked at Nephis.","Could he?","\"Actually... I can believe it very easily.\"","She remained unperturbed and just shrugged casually.","\"I picked well in the end, didn’t I?\"","’I’d say.’","No matter what horrible crimes Eurys had committed in the ancient past, he did guide Nephis into the depths of the Underworld, to a Seed of Nightmare. If she had chosen Azarax, he would have lost his mind before they even left the Nightmare Desert — in fact, he might have turned on her immediately after being taken off the tree.","Nephis sighed.","\"Many things have happened since.\"","She remained silent for a few moments, then said quietly:","\"I was broken in one Nightmare and rebuilt myself in another. I swore loyalty to the people who had betrayed and killed my father, then betrayed and killed them in turn. There was war, there were bitter losses... there were brief moments of peace and sweet triumphs, as well. I am still pursuing my goal. I have come so far, but I am still only halfway there.\"","Eurys did not answer immediately.","\"I have come so far, but I am still only halfway there...\"","His voice sounded low and wistful.","He turned his skull to the slope of the dune — in the direction where the heart of the Shadow Realm, and the death he was seeking, lay.","\"Come to think of it, that describes my situation as well.\"","Eurys looked back at them.","\"Unless, of course, that wicked shadow of yours keeps his promise and kills me. How about it, boy? Have you come to try again?\"","Sunny remained motionless for a while, then slowly shook his head.","\"Not today. There is no point. I have grown far more powerful than I used to be, and Nephis is here with me as well. But, still, we are not strong enough to undo what Shadow God did.\"","He paused for a few moments, and then added quietly:","\"We may be gods ourselves soon, though. The next time we meet... if we meet... Nephis and I will be Sacred, at least. Then, I will fulfill my promise.\"","Eurys stared at him with his empty eye sockets.","\"You are going to make use of Weaver’s spell, then?\"","Sunny nodded.","\"Yes. We plan to challenge the Fifth Nightmare soon... as soon as possible.\"","Eurys remained silent for a long while, and then sighed.","\"Go forth and conquer, then. I wish you luck — gods know, you’ll need it.\"","He paused, clacked his jaw, and added in a thoughtful tone:","\"But then again, the gods are dead. So, really, they wouldn’t know anything at all...\"","His voice echoed in the darkness of the Realm of Death, wishing them a safe journey."]},{"number":3118,"title":"Chapter 3118: Dying City","paragraphs":["A dying city sprawled under the dark sky, the sun obscured by billowing clouds of black smoke. The great river that had once flowed through it was gone, the sediment on its bottom littered with corpses and broken weapons. The proud walls of the city were covered in fractures and deep scars, some sections so battered that they seemed ready to crumble.","The streets of the city were like a vision of hell, or maybe a scene from a hideous nightmare. Closer to the wall, countless buildings had burned down, with only their skeletal remains rising from the ash like blackened gravestones. Other areas were still intact, but enveloped by a suffocating atmosphere of fear and desperation.","Here and there, rotting bodies lay on the cobblestones, with no one bothering to gather and burn them anymore. Those people who still clung to life were suffering from hunger, disease, and murderous thirst. Clean water was a rarity, so many resorted to drinking whatever kind they could find, ignoring the risk of sickness and death.","The wails of people dying from the plague had become background noise, with nobody paying them attention anymore.","The bay had become a graveyard of ships, their masts protruding from the waves like twisted branches. By now, it was all but impossible to bypass the complicated maze of shipwrecks to enter the harbor... or leave it.","The soldiers who defended the city were like pale shadows of their former selves. They suffered from the lack of food and drinking water, too. Disease was just as rampant among them as it was among the civilian population.","Most of all, the majority of them had already perished in the endless onslaught of war.","There were very few people left in the city who had not been called upon to become soldiers, in fact, but their number was still greatly diminished. All men had long taken up weapons to defend the wall, and when too many of them died, women took their place. Even children were conscripted, gathering arrows from below the walls and helping with menial tasks.","Worst of all... the sole Supreme of the besieged city, the Mason King, was dying. Countless months of clashing with the tyrannical Will of Azarax, the Plague of Steel, had eroded his spirit and worn out his soul. Now, the old man was slowly fading away.","And yet, the city still stood.","Its battered walls were scarred and fractured, but they refused to crumble.","Its people were being consumed by disease and despair, but they had not given up.","The soldiers, who had sacrificed countless lives to defend the city, were not ready to surrender to death yet.","But everything came to an end, sooner or later.","Looking at the nightmarish vista of the dying city, Effie knew that their days were numbered.","There was simply a limit to what people could do, no matter how deep the well of their resolve was. The city had been besieged for so long... how long had it been, actually?","She frowned, trying to remember.","’Two years? No, not yet. But only a few months shy.’","Almost two years had passed since she and her companions had entered the Nightmare — a little less since the Steel Horde established an encirclement around the city. There had been countless assaults, countless battles, countless losses. Being able to halt the unstoppable expansion of Azarax’s bloody empire for so long was a miraculous feat, but did it matter in the end?","The city was still going to fall. Its people were still going to be slaughtered. No matter how long they had managed to hold out, their valiant defiance was still going to end up being nothing but a short line in the glorious chronicle of the King of Kings... a paragraph, at best, no different from all his previous conquests.","Worst of all, time did not stay still while they were fighting for their lives in the Nightmare. The same number of months had passed in the real world, as well.","Effie’s expression darkened.","Somewhere out there... by now, the world was probably ending. The Dream Realm was devouring the last refuge of mankind. Humanity was besieged on all sides. Sunny and Nephis were desperately trying to stem the endless tide of abominations, and Cassie was probably even busier than them.","Two years...","Her son had not seen her for that long. He was about to turn nine, meeting another birthday without his mother. Was he alright? Was he well?","What about his father?","She sighed heavily.","They probably missed her just as much as she missed them. Were they counting days, both hoping to hear news about her and feeling their hearts sink every time someone knocked on the door?","’Two years, damn it.’","Effie had known that the Fourth Nightmare might take them a long time to conquer. But she had not expected it to take years, with no end in sight.","No, actually, the end was already near... it was just not the kind of end they wanted.","The Mason was dying. The old man was still keeping Azarax at bay despite his broken spirit, but the spark of his life was growing feebler with each day. Once he was gone, no amount of valor would prevent the Plague of Steel from conquering the city — Effie and her companions would not be able to stop him, either.","She gazed at the nightmarish vista of the city one more time and then looked down at her calloused hand.","In the dim torchlight, her hand was trembling uncontrollably.","Effie stared at it for a while, and then slowly made a fist, willing it to settle. Finally, the tremors subsided.","She inhaled deeply.","’The end... let’s end it, then. Little Ling’s birthday is in December — I should wrap up everything quickly and return just in time to light the candles on his birthday cake.’","Effie smiled wistfully.","’Ah, cake... I haven’t had cake in a while...’","With that, she turned around and descended the wall of the Stone Castle.","In the next few days, she was going to break the Steel Horde’s back, win the war, and write the final line in the chronicle of the great and terrible Azarax, the King of Kings."]},{"number":3119,"title":"Chapter 3119: Drawbridge","paragraphs":["Dawn was approaching, so the Stone Castle was slowly waking up. This beautiful stronghold had been the Mason’s original creation once — the city grew around it, eventually becoming what it was today. Or had been, at least.","The castle was a small city in and of itself. It couldn’t compare to Bastion, of course, but countless people could find shelter behind its walls, still. The inner stronghold of the besieged city had its own walls, its own moat, its own layered defenses, all isolated from the greater urban sprawl beyond — as long as the drawbridge was raised, getting inside was as difficult as breaching the city wall.","More so, even, since building a highly defensible fortress was far easier than ensuring the safety of a thriving metropolis.","It used to be that the Stone Castle was sparsely populated, with only the royal family, their servants, and their closest retainer inhabiting its courtyards and walls. Now, however, the situation had changed.","As Effie descended from the wall and made her way to the drawbridge, she had to carefully wade through a mass of people. The castle was overcrowded, with each courtyard and corridor becoming a makeshift shelter — the citizens were in the throes of nightmares, sleeping restlessly with nothing but flimsy straw mats between them and the ground.","They were mostly those who were too old to fight, too young to be of use, or already maimed and unable to wield a weapon. Most able-bodied people had already been conscripted to help defend the city, so there were few of them here, behind the last line of defense.","Some of these people slept, but most were awake, pressing themselves against the walls or hugging each other, covered with threadbare blankets and staring into the distance tiredly. The mass of them was like a furnace, generating almost palpable waves of heat — when Effie walked by, something ignited in their eyes, and for a short while, they seemed like proper humans again.","This was a recent arrangement. Before, the remains of the civilian population stayed in the city, scattered across its safer areas. It was better to keep them apart, since that made it harder for disease to spread. But now that the Mason was about to fall, there were no safe areas anymore. So, everyone... everyone who was still alive... was brought to the inner stronghold over the last few nights.","Despite how crowded the castle was, seeing it like that was sobering. Before, it would have never been able to accommodate the entire population of the city — but the population had shrunk so much that now, it was enough. So many people had died. More people had died than survived, really.","That made Effie question if the accomplishment of holding the city for all this time was even worth a damn.","’Well, there were certainly benefits.’","All of them, those who had challenged the Nightmare, were far more powerful than they were at the start. How could they not be?","Close to two years of constant battles, almost always against an overwhelmingly powerful foe, had tempered them. They had already been the best and most seasoned warriors of humanity, and with the accumulating weight of experience, their skill and tenacity only grew.","Their skill was improving by leaps and bounds. Their soul arsenals were expanding. They were learning to wield their Aspects better and discovering new facets of their power... there were other, less conspicuous improvements, as well.","Tactics, strategy, logistics, civil engineering, leadership — and so much more. The task of running an embattled city, wringing every drop of usefulness out of the limited resources at their disposal, was teaching them things beyond martial excellence and personal valor.","A few of them were close to unlocking their Aspect Legacies, as well.","The Nightmares were always catalysts of explosive growth, and this one was no different. In fact, it was far greater in scope and intensity than all the previous Nightmares Effie had survived.","The problem, of course, was that she and the others would only get to enjoy the benefits of their growth if they survived this one, as well. And that was looking harder and harder to achieve with each passing day.","What was the point of all that improvement if all it ultimately granted them was a slower death?","Finally making her way through the crowded paths of the castle, Effie reached the drawbridge. It was lowered, and the last batches of people were crossing it to escape the vast desolation of the devastated city. Soldiers were showing them the way, explaining their new temporary arrangements. A young man in a luxurious tunic was overseeing the process.","The tunic was embroidered with golden thread, shimmering beautifully in the torchlight. It had seen better days, though, just like the people walking across the drawbridge and the city itself.","The young man was the prince of the dying city, the youngest son of the Mason. His older siblings had perished centuries ago, having failed to outlive their Supreme father... their great-grandchildren were long gone, as well. The family trees of powerful Awakened were a complete mess.","Effie glanced at the prince, wondering how her own family tree would look one day, if she survived the Nightmare and the apocalypse both.","’Supremacy... it’s a bit messed up, as far as human connections are concerned.’","That was the price of becoming a demigod, as well.","When the young prince noticed Effie, a pale smile illuminated his face. He left his post and headed her way.","The prince was a pleasant enough fellow. He was diligent, polite, and competent — even if his talents did not lie on the battlefield, just like his father’s. He had also been able to maintain his optimism and decorum for a long while, helping Effie rally the citizens and keep them from losing hope.","It was just that now, there was a shadow of melancholy in his eyes. The plague had not spared the royal family, either, taking the lives of two of his three children. The smile never reached his eyes since then.","But just like the walls of the city, the prince had not crumbled.","Approaching Effie, he bowed.","\"May the heavens smile upon you, Priestess.\"","Effie looked at him for a moment, then nodded.","\"And you as well.\"","He hesitated, studying her, as if unsure what to say. So, Effie spoke instead.","\"This should be the last of them, right? You only have a few hours left. Make sure that everyone is inside the castle.\"","The prince turned to the stream of gaunt, battered people entering through the gate.","\"Yes... this is the last of them.\"","His voice was distant.","Effie sighed.","\"How is your father? He didn’t look too well yesterday.\"","The prince remained silent for a moment, then smiled wistfully.","\"He is fading away. I think the era of the Mason will end soon — maybe in a few days, maybe in a few weeks.\"","He paused, then added in a soft tone:","\"My father... among the great and terrible Supremes, he might not have been the most glorious, or one whose thrilling feats are sung about across the mortal realms. But, still... long centuries of peace, long centuries of prosperity. If I wanted to leave behind a legacy, I would have wanted to leave a legacy like his.\"","The prince looked at Effie and chuckled.","\"I am sorry, my lady. As a priestess of War, you must find my talk of peace distasteful.\"","Effie looked into the distance.","\"Actually, I am quite fond of peace.\"","She hesitated for a moment, then turned to the prince and smiled.","\"It is just that my fondness for peace is purely theoretical, since I’ve never known it. I don’t think I’ll recognize peace even if it hit me in the face.\"","As long as Effie could remember herself, she had been fighting for her life. And by the time she grew powerful enough to survive, she was fighting for the lives of others.","So, what was peace?","She did not know.","Effie sighed, then shook her head.","\"The legacy of your father is not long centuries of peace and prosperity, though. It is you, your family — and all these people. So, as long as his people continue to live and remember him, his era will continue.\"","The prince remained silent for a long while, then nodded.","\"As long as we continue to live. As long as we remember.\"","With that, he looked across the drawbridge, at the desolate city.","\"Stone breaks, but people endure. Thank you, Priestess.\"","He turned to her then and looked at her solemnly.","After a long stretch of silence, the prince said, his tone laden with meaning.","\"We will remember you as well, my lady.\"","Effie inhaled deeply, then smiled and turned away.","Stepping onto the drawbridge to leave the castle, she left the prince behind.","This was most likely the last time they saw each other.","If so...","Effie wished for the young prince and his people to find peace and prosperity once more, one day."]},{"number":3120,"title":"Chapter 3120: Desolate Streets","paragraphs":["On the other side of the drawbridge, a crowd of people — the last of the citizens to be led into the inner keep — were waiting for their turn to cross. The elderly were holding the smallest of children, while those who were old enough to stand on their own were hugging their legs, looking around with curious eyes.","These kids had grown up while looking at the distant, magnificent palace of the Mason King, but few had ever been inside. The adults were broken by the horrors of war, but children were far more resilient — since they barely remembered anything else, this was simply how the world was for them.","So, the light in their eyes had not been extinguished yet, and they were excited to see the castle up close.","To the side of the bridge, a crowd of children surrounded an unlikely babysitter, clamoring for his attention.","\"Uncle, uncle! Tell us about the living ship!\"","\"Is it true that you fought a god once?\"","\"Uncle... what does stardust taste like? Is it sweet?\"","Nightwalker chuckled, looking around with a helpless expression.","\"Why are you guys pestering me? I am supposed to keep watch! Go, shoo. Find your grandmas... and for the record, I can never fight a god. After all, Storm God is my grandma. How can I disrespect my elders?\"","Effie shook her head.","Nightwalker had been in charge of an important task before — he had been the only one who could bypass the blockade, so he often sailed away and returned with supplies to feed the people of the besieged city.","Even with how the harbor was now, littered with shipwrecks and utterly impossible to navigate, he could still do it. The problem was that all the ships of his fleet had sunk, so there was nothing for him to sail on. Now that Nightwalker was grounded, all he could do was join the defenders of the city on the wall.","His strength was greatly appreciated there, but without his perilous voyages, the city had no food source anymore. So, people had been slowly starving for a long while.","Effie knew a thing or two about starvation, so she felt their pain.","Noticing her, Nightwalker shooed the giggling children away and rose to greet her.","’It’s a nice morning, isn’t it?\"","Effie looked up.","The sky was still dark, barely painted pale lilac in the east.","\"I’d say it’s still the middle of the night.\"","She spared him a look.","\"Are you ready?\"","Nightwalker chuckled.","\"Me? I should be asking you instead.\"","He fell silent, mirth draining from his face. A few moments later, he said quietly:","\"You can still change your mind, you know. You don’t have to do it yourself.\"","Effie smiled.","\"It’s a little bit too late for that, I think.\"","There was already no way back. There had not been for some time.","She chuckled.","\"Ah, but don’t get me wrong. I’d gladly trade places with you. Sadly, you’re not the one Azarax has developed an unhealthy fixation on.\"","She paused for a moment.","\"What can I say? I guess you are not charming enough.\"","Nightwalker stared at her, aghast.","\"What are you talking about? My charm has never failed me. That bastard just didn’t have the chance to get to know me, since I was busy hunting for supplies most of the time. Otherwise, he wouldn’t even look your way.\"","Effie grinned.","\"Whatever you say, grandpa.\"","Nightwalker’s expression was quite amusing.","She looked back to the bridge, then asked:","\"Everything has been prepared?\"","He hesitated for a moment, then nodded.","\"The castle is secured. Kai and Morgan finished the preparations in the city, as well. Seishan... well, you’d know best. As for Soul Reaper, we won’t know until it’s done.\"","Effie sighed.","\"I’ll leave the civilians to you, then. Once the bridge rises... make sure that the keep stays safe.\"","Nightwalker remained silent for a short while.","Eventually, he nodded.","\"The castle won’t fall. I guarantee it.\"","Effie left him behind, as well.","She passed through the crowd of civilians and reached the empty, desolate streets of the city. Since most of its inhabitants had been taken away to the stronghold, there were only soldiers left here, rushing as they made the last preparations before retreating into the keep, as well.","They stopped and bowed deeply when they saw Effie, an indescribable emotion hidden in the depths of their sunken, haunted eyes. Their expressions were solemn, and only grew more so when she greeted them with an easy smile.","At some point, however, her smile faltered.","’What is that I’m seeing?’","Out there in front of her... were Morgan and Seishan.","The Princess of Valor and the Princess of Song were sitting on the ground among the rubble, having completely forgotten their sense of decorum.","They were... playing cards.","Effie blinked and rubbed her eyes, wondering if she was imagining things. But no, her eyes weren’t lying to her. Morgan and Seishan were indeed sitting on the dusty cobblestones and playing cards, discussing something quietly amongst each other.","She could hear bits and pieces of their conversation.","\"Another ace? How can this be?\"","\"That is called skill, Your Highness.\"","\"Don’t your highess me, wench. You’re cheating!\"","\"How would I cheat? That doesn’t even make sense.\"","\"Five aces in a deck of cards is what doesn’t make sense.\"","\"Oh, so you have a pair of aces? Hmm... unfortunate.\"","\"Of course I do. Or do I only want you to believe that I do?\"","\"I will believe anything you say, Your Highness. I wouldn’t dare doubt your honesty.\"","\"How are you so good at being infuriating?\"","\"It comes with practice.\"","\"Stop practicing on me, then!\"","Effie stared at them, dumbfounded.","\"What are you doing, fools?\"","Morgan and Seishan put away their cards and looked at her. Morgan shrugged.","\"Waiting for you, obviously.\"","Seishan nodded.","\"What, did you expect that we’ll leave you all alone on this fine morning?\"","Morgan threw one last glance at her cards, then grimaced and stood up.","\"Let’s go. We’ll see you off to the gate.\"","Effie gave her a long look, then smiled.","\"It’s an honor... Your Highness.\"","Morgan’s eye twitched, and she forced out a smile.","\"Why, of course. Anything for our esteemed Steward of the East.\"","Seishan rose, then stretched and spoke in her husky, tantalizing voice.","\"By the way, I always wanted to ask... in your case, wouldn’t it be the Stewardess of the East? That would make more sense.\"","Effie could only stare at her blankly.","\"Did the plague rot your brain?\"","Seishan shrugged.","\"Someone would have to split my skull open to find out.\"","Hearing that, Morgan livened up.","\"If you want to, that can be arranged. I’ll volunteer.\"","Ignoring them, Effie walked past.","\"Fine, let’s go. I appreciate it. Goodness gracious, it’s still dark outside! A fine young lady like me shouldn’t be walking the streets alone in the dark... who knows what terrible things might happen!\"","To whoever was foolish enough to bother her, that was.","The three of them made their way to the city gate, sharing a lighthearted conversation. The mood was carefree and laidback, as if they were not passing through burned ruins and stepping over the blackened bones, circling around rotting corpses from time to time.","It was so carefree, in fact, that for a short while, Effie was distracted from the truth.","From the fact that today, her life could very well come to an end."]},{"number":3121,"title":"Chapter 3121: They Will Open the Gate","paragraphs":["The city was dead and quiet as they walked toward the distant wall. The streets were empty, with not a soul around. An eerie silence suffused the world, as if they had taken a wrong turn somewhere and somehow ended up in hell... if hell did exist, then Effie imagined it looking similar to this.","She had seen all kinds of horrors in her life, and the blackened ruins — collapsed buildings, bodies scattered in the dust, the smell of rot and ash permeating the air — were nothing new to her. The devastation itself was not hell... the knowledge of all the human pain, despair, and broken dreams that lay hidden under the rubble was.","Effie was glad that Morgan and Seishan had chosen to accompany her on this dreary walk. Otherwise, it would have felt too lonesome.","As they approached the city gate, however, the situation changed.","She had ordered most of her soldiers to pull back, but somehow, a grand welcome was waiting for her. Countless soldiers — all gaunt and battered — had assembled to see their commander off, forming two human walls on both sides of the road.","They did not cheer, and neither did they say anything. However, as Effie approached, she could see everything they wished to say in their eyes.","The soldiers saluted her silently as she walked past, their reserved expressions betraying a storm of turbulent emotions. Sorrow, reverence, pain, courage — she could see all of it, and more.","But most of all, what she saw was strength.","These people were all wounded, hungry, exhausted, sick, and losing hope. But none of them had broken — none of them was entertaining the thought of giving up.","So, she thought she’d give them a good show.","Straightening her spine, Effie met the gazes of her soldiers and smiled. It was a confident, easy smile — one that betrayed no hint of fear or hesitation. The same smile they had seen countless times.","If the young prince of the dying city had been honest when he said that they would remember her, Effie wanted them to remember her like this.","It was a strange wish, considering that all of them were mere phantoms conjured by the Spell, and would be gone once the Nightmare was over.","What meaning was there in being remembered by forgotten phantoms?","Finally, they reached the gates of the city. There, a lone figure was waiting for them, standing in the middle of the road — barring their way.","It was Kai, of course.","Morgan and Seishan slowed down, allowing Effie to approach him alone.","As she did, she whistled quietly.","’Uh-oh. Kai is not happy...’","Indeed, it was as clear as day. The others had tried to hide their emotions, but he did not bother to — his face was dark and somber... desperate, even. There were black circles under his eyes, and his gaze was scathing.","Bruised eyes, sunken cheeks, chapped lips...","’Goodness.’","Kai had really let himself go. The world had to be ending.","\"Effie...\"","Stopping in front of him, Effie smiled.","\"Why the long face?\"","He stared at her for a moment, then frowned.","\"There has to be another way. You don’t have to... you must not. We can come up with another plan. Please, reconsider.\"","Effie studied him silently for a short while, then chuckled.","\"You know me, buddy. I am not a very considerate person. It took me a lot of effort to consider this one plan... now, you expect me to reconsider the whole thing? Gods have mercy, I cannot.\"","He refused to be placated by her lighthearted tone, looking at her with dark intensity.","Effie sighed.","\"It’s a good plan, Kai... it’s the only way. You know it. Each of us just needs to do their part. My part is a bit flashy, but it’s not the most difficult. In fact, I might be getting off easier than the rest of you.\"","Kai gritted his teeth.","\"He’ll kill you!\"","Effie remained silent for a moment, then shook her head and laughed.","\"He might. But he won’t kill me immediately — and that’s good enough. So, step aside.\"","Kai glared at her for a while longer, then looked down.","Eventually, he moved to the side, allowing her to pass.","Effie lingered for a moment, then patted him on the shoulder and walked past him.","Now, only the gates loomed above her.","She hesitated a little, then took a deep breath.","\"Hey, Kai. Can you do me a favor?\"","He did not answer, prompting Effie to turn and glance at him.","\"Once I am out there... don’t look.\"","She did not say anything else, and he did not respond, either.","In the end, however, Kai nodded slowly.","Effie smiled and nodded, as well.","\"I have an image to maintain, that’s all. Well, you used to be an idol, so you should understand.\"","With that, everything that needed to be said had been said. Effie looked ahead once more and raised her voice:","\"Open the gate!\"","The towering main gate of the city, which had stayed shut since the beginning of the siege, refusing to be breached or broken, finally groaned and moved.","Opening that enormous gate was a complicated affair, since the Mason had constructed it himself. It weighed too much to be pushed by people or Awakened — even Ascended and Saints would struggle to force it open. So, a complex mechanism was involved, operated by a team of engineers.","Now, that mechanism had been activated, pushing two titanic slabs of mystical stone apart.","The sun was already rising by then, chasing away the night — a new day had arrived, bringing with it a promise of a brighter tomorrow.","Or a darker one, maybe.","Effie was not sure which, but she knew that tomorrow would be entirely different from all the days before.","Once the gate was open wide enough for a person to pass through, she inhaled deeply and stepped forward.","Behind her, countless soldiers struck their fists against their armor, solemnly shouting her name. The sound of their voices rose to the sky like a deafening roar, making the heavens quake.","Effie smiled faintly.","’Damn it.’","She was a little touched.","The irony of the situation, though, was that she was playing the role of the War Maiden in this Nightmare, so they weren’t even shouting her real name.","’Those fools...’","Passing through the gate, Effie entered the vast, dreadful killing field that stretched from the wall of the city to the horizon. If the city only resembled hell, then this was its true face. Corpses piled like mountains here, with fat crows waddling between broken weapons and remains of towering siege engines. The ground had turned into black sludge, soaked with blood and ash. The stench was unbearable, pillars of smoke rising into the pale sky.","She walked forward without looking back.","Out there, on the horizon, a dark line contoured the world. That line was the vast, seemingly endless camp of the Steel Horde — at night, the fires its soldiers made looked like a boundless sea.","That was where Effie was headed...","Today, after a long and bitter siege, she was going to admit defeat and surrender the city to the King of Kings."]},{"number":3122,"title":"Chapter 3122: Field of Dishonor","paragraphs":["It took Effie a while to cross the killing field. Behind her, the gates of the city stayed open, as if inviting the conquerors to come and claim their prize. The soldiers of the Steel Horde, of course, noticed the unusual movement.","They saw a lone figure walking across the black expanse of blood-soaked mud, as well.","By the time Effie reached the encampment of the conquering army, there was already a welcoming committee waiting for her.","Hiding her emotions behind a composed expression, she looked around.","The Steel Horde was doing much better than the defenders of the city, who looked like walking corpses by now. However... its warriors didn’t look too good, either.","It did not matter how numerous they were or how fearsome the power of the conquering horde was. These people had been stuck here, below the walls of the once-peaceful city, for almost two years now. The casualties they had suffered were far greater than the losses among its defenders — a truly terrifying amount, to the point that it was impossible to count how many had died.","And so, they had learned terror. Even with Azarax instilling them with confidence, their eventual victory assured, the warriors of the Steel Plague could not help but feel a deep and penetrating fear when looking at the distant walls of the city.","The casualties were not their only problem, either.","The empire of Azarax the Mighty was vast and powerful, but it was also young and vulnerable. His endless conquest left him with no time to consolidate his rulership and properly integrate the conquered lands, establishing a shared foundation of culture, laws, and economic interest that held empires together.","So, the longer his conquest stalled, and the longer he failed to deliver new spoils to feed his empire, the more internal tension there was.","Two fruitless years spent under the walls of a single, weak city-state... various regions of the Steel Empire were already sliding into turmoil and unrest. His generals, meanwhile, were growing uneasy about the fate of their families and noble houses back home.","As a result, not only were the soldiers becoming restless, but the supply chains that sustained the great and insatiable horde were also growing strained. It took an unfathomable amount of provisions to feed the endless ocean of soldiers — with an unstable situation in the rear, satiating their daily needs had long become a problem.","The warriors of the Steel Horde were not starving like the defenders of the city, but they weren’t unfamiliar with hunger either. That was what Effie saw when she looked at the soldiers who left the encampment to meet her — gaunt faces, worn equipment, haunted looks. The long siege had been cruel to them, too.","Those were only the ordinary soldiers, of course. The Dread Warriors, Azarax’s elites, were as hale and full of vigor as ever. Their tables never seemed to lack food, while their weapons and equipment were meticulously maintained.","Effie struggled to keep her expression steady as the familiar aura of dread they exerted washed over her. Nothing could compare to the crushing, suffocating presence of the man who stood in front of the soldiers, though, watching her approach with a dark grin.","Azarax looked like he always did. Years of bitter battles, countless lives lost, rivers of blood that spilled into the ground, all the hopes he had crushed and all the dreams he had broken — none of it seemed to matter to him. He was still just as confident as ever, just as indomitable as ever, just as amused and full of dark glee as he had always been.","Under his dark gaze, Effie walked the last of the distance between them and stopped in front of the King of Kings, looking at him calmly.","The Dread Warriors watched her. The ordinary soldiers of the Steel Horde watched, as well. Far away on the walls of the city... if Kai had stayed true to his promise, he would not see, at least.","No one that mattered would witness her indignity.","\"Ah, what a surprise. If it isn’t the Priestess of War herself... welcome to my camp, War Maiden. To what do I owe the pleasure?\"","Azarax sounded relaxed, as if he had already known what would happen — as if this outcome was all but inevitable, and the only thing he had not guessed was its timing.","Effie inhaled deeply, gathering her courage.","It was funny... she had not needed to be brave while walking alone toward the war camp of a murderous Sovereign, even knowing that he could easily kill her if he wished. Speaking the words she had prepared to say, however, was as difficult as raising a mountain into the air.","She remained silent for a short while, then briefly glanced over her shoulder, at the distant city.","Finally, Effie was able to speak:","\"You told me once that you would spare the women and the children if I surrendered to you of my own free will.\"","Azarax’s smile widened a little.","\"Did I? I don’t really remember... but I must have if you are reminding me, priestess. What of it?\"","Effie inhaled once more, forcing the air into her lungs, and lowered her head.","\"I...\"","Saying the words hurt her more than any physical wound ever had.","\"I...\"","She grimaced, and then pushed the whole sentence out of her mouth, feeling like each word was a razor that cut her throat and lips.","\"I surrender.\"","Her voice was quiet.","Azarax studied her for a while, then laughed.","\"What? I didn’t quite hear it. My soldiers did not hear you, either.\"","Effie closed her eyes for a moment.","Then, raising her head, she looked at Azarax and said in a loud, clear voice.","\"I surrender! The city... surrenders. I ask you to give its citizens three days to bury their dead. After that, my soldiers will lay down their arms, and allow the Steel Horde... the victorious Steel Horde... to enter the city unopposed.\"","Azarax stared at her for a few moments, his smile slowly turning darker.","Eventually, he spoke in an even tone:","\"I guess the old man is done for, then. A pity. I wanted to rip off his head with my own hands... but as long as he dies, that is fine. However...\"","His fearsome, suffocating gaze pierced Effie like a blade.","\"You don’t look like someone who has come to surrender and beg, War Maiden.\"","For a moment, Effie’s expression turned ugly.","Then, she exhaled slowly and composed herself.","Well... he wasn’t wrong.","She had come to admit her defeat and surrender herself to the mercy of the victor. It was not a negotiation — she was begging. She was begging him to give the city time to bury the dead, and she was also begging him to keep his promise and spare the women and the children.","Pride was not something that beggars could afford.","Dignity wasn’t a privilege afforded to losers, either.","Effie remained motionless for a few moments.","Her hands began to tremble again.","In the end, she looked down, at the wet mud between them...","And slowly lowered herself to her knees.","Her hands sank into the cold mud, and a few moments later, her forehead touched it, as well.","\"I... surrender.\"","There she was, kneeling in the mud, having abandoned her pride, her dignity, and all hope.","Seeing her lowering herself before him, Azarax laughed.","\"Good. Now that... that is humility. I guess your endless pride was not unbreakable after all, priestess.\"","He looked over her, at the distant city — at its gate, which was wide open.","Then, he spared a glance to his Dread Warriors.","\"I am a man of my word, after all. So, I’ll keep the women and the children alive... spare them, though? Well, there will be some of that. They’ll survive, at least.\"","As he spoke those words, his elite soldiers were already assembling, dark glint shimmering in their eyes, and the camp behind him was boiling with movement.","\"However, as for waiting three days... there has already been enough waiting.\"","His smile turned into a dark, hungry grin.","\"It’s time for this damn siege to end. Will you watch with me as your city falls, priestess? I’d appreciate it very much.\"","With that, Azarax laughed and pointed forward.","\"Go, my warriors! Go forth and plunder! Destroy that city... leave no stone unturned!\""]},{"number":3123,"title":"Chapter 3123: Greater Power","paragraphs":["As the Dread Warriors rushed forward like a river of hungry steel, Effie felt the ground tremble. She was still kneeling in the mud with her head lowered, an indescribable bitterness squeezing her heart. A moment later, someone’s hand grabbed her by the hair and violently jerked her head upward.","In terms of physical might, Effie was stronger than a dozen Saints... but all her strength suddenly felt meaningless under the weight of the iron hand that was pulling her upward.","Grabbed by Azarax, all she could do was grit her teeth and suppress a pained groan.","Suddenly, he was very close.","\"You are facing the wrong way, priestess. Come, let us watch your city fall.\"","He threw her down as two soldiers grabbed her hands, binding them with enchanted shackles. A complicated weave of runes ignited on their steel surface, and she felt her essence draining quickly — soon enough, it would be completely exhausted, leaving her weak and vulnerable.","Too easy to kill.","Only...","Effie knew that Azarax was not going to kill her. Not today, at least.","As more soldiers arrived, carrying a fur-covered seat for their Sovereign, the King of Kings sat down and leaned back with an easy smile. Effie, who was sprawled in the mud at his feet, slowly picked herself up. She looked away, in the direction of the battered city.","The Dread Warriors and other elite legions of the Steel Horde were already halfway to its gates. The ordinary soldiers stayed back, though.","\"Tell me, priestess, now that you betrayed your god, what should I call you? Then again, maybe I’ll ordain you as the priestess... of me. Should I establish a temple of my own?\"","Azarax was grinning, but his eyes remained cold, peering at her with a dark, murderous hunger.","Effie looked down, avoiding his gaze.","’Betrayed War God, huh?’","War Maidens gave an oath to never surrender without a fight. If Effie were truly one of them, she would have been breaking the covenant with War God by lowering herself in front of Azarax.","And that was precisely the reason why Azarax was not going to kill her just yet. Because he saw the act of breaking her as proof of being greater than the gods.","Far away, the Dread Warriors were nearing the open city gate.","Everything was...","Everything was going according to plan.","Effie sighed quietly and raised a hand, trying to wipe the grime off her face.","\"Breaking things is far easier than building them, King Azarax. Building a temple would be no different.\"","She had not spent these two years idly.","Effie had fought countless battles against the Steel Horde, true, but she was also learning her enemy patiently. The structure of Azarax’s army, the customs of his people, the history of how his father had come to power, and how Azarax killed him to claim the throne.","And not only the Steel Horde. She had learned about other realms and other Domains of this ancient time, as well.","Most of all, however, she learned about Azarax.","What motivated him, what moved him. What his virtues were, and what his vices were as well.","And at the end of it all, she had to admit that Azarax... was not that complicated at all.","He was a genius warrior, yes. His Aspect was frighteningly powerful. He was a tyrant with a natural talent for leadership, as well — he was not the kind of enlightened and benevolent leader that people of her time usually imagined when thinking about an ideal ruler, but rather a king fit for his time.","Someone who could crush people with his authority and keep them in line with an unshakeable fist until the very thought of defiance and disobedience was eradicated from their minds.","And he was quite charismatic, too.","But beneath it all, his character was a collection of vile and banal cliches, only unique because Azarax took them to an absolute, inhuman extreme.","Azarax was absolutely prideful, egomaniacal, conceited, and sadistic — but most of all, he was entirely overcome by insatiable lust for power. All of his other traits stemmed from this one overwhelming obsession, and everything he did only pursued two goals. It was all either to gain more power or affirm the power he already possessed, lest it weaken and disappear.","His cruelty, his greed, his ruthless tyranny — it was all a means of obtaining power. So was his narcissistic self-assurance, since in the world Azarax inhabited, no one could be above him, and no one had a greater claim to power than he.","Naturally, that belief clashed with the existence of the gods, who were above all, above everyone. No matter how deftly Azarax refused to admit, even to himself, that there were those out there greater than him, he was not unaware of reality. The gods were like a thorn in his side.","Of course, he was not entirely unfounded in his confidence, even if it bordered on insanity. After all, Azarax had been Transcendent before becoming Supreme, and before that, he was Ascended, Awakened... Dormant. The path he walked was littered with the corpses of those who had been more powerful than him, and yet ended up dying by his hand.","Those who had survived, meanwhile, had all become his thralls.","Why would the gods be any different?","That was why Azarax was fixated on Effie. She was a conduit for his hatred of the gods, a way of diminishing them that was in his power to conquer.","And that was how she had known that he would not kill her immediately.","There were only two possible outcomes to her surrender. One was that Azarax would viciously beat her until she was on the threshold of death, and then make her his thrall. The other was that she would keep her free of the enthrallment, resorting to mental torture instead — to break her and make her surrender to him fully of her own free will.","Both outcomes were acceptable to Effie, since that was what she had planned for.","Unless something completely unexpected happened, there was no way for her to lose... at this stage, at least.","She just had to redefine what losing meant.","This was the first component of the plan.","The second one had come from diligent study of this era, as well.","It had to do with what victory meant for the triumphant army."]},{"number":3124,"title":"Chapter 3124 Meaning of Victory","paragraphs":["What did victory mean?","To Effie, victory had always meant getting to live another day — it meant staying alive and not having to starve. Later, that also included her family, and all of humanity as well.","But these were ancient times, and there was no Nightmare Spell here. There were no Nightmares, and no Dream Realm slowly devouring the world. So what were these people fighting for?","There were numerous reasons for war, but at its most fundamental level, wars were fought over resources. That was what Morgan had said, and she would know best.","In the case of Azarax and his Steel Horde, the purpose of war was rather simple. They were here to conquer land and plunder its riches. The land itself was a resource... the people that populated it were as well, meant to be sold as slaves. Their possessions, meanwhile — gold, fabrics, artworks, and various items of luxury — would change hands and become the property of the conquerors.","That was how militant empires, and their most privileged class — the soldiers — thrived.","Azarax knew it as well, and he also knew that his empire was only as strong as its army. As the commander of the Steel Horde, he would get the largest share of the spoils, but if he wanted his soldiers to stay content and loyal, he had to share his prize.","So, for the Steel Horde, victory meant plunder.","After an adversary stronghold fell, the soldiers were given time — usually a few days — to freely take whatever they wanted. These days were often the most harrowing and heartbreaking for the defeated people, and at the end of it, the soldiers of the Steel Horde were satiated and enriched.","Even if there was no legal text postulating the rules of plunder, it was a silent law. It was a quiet agreement between Azarax and his soldiers, and he would not break it easily — or at all.","There was a process to the slaughter, as well. Not all of the soldiers would get to share in the spoils of the war equally.","The elite forces, such as the Dread Warriors, would be allowed to enter the fallen city and take their pick first. Some time later, less prestigious legions would follow, taking whatever was left. And finally, the dregs of the Steel Horde would be sent forward, hoping to find something that their betters had missed.","By the end of it all, the city would be utterly ravaged, its population slaughtered, those who survived victimized and enslaved. The larger haul would be presented to Azarax, who would take his share and distribute the rest as rewards to his champions.","It was a barbaric, but highly efficient and motivating system...","And now, Effie was forced to watch that efficiency at work.","“How does it feel, watching everything you cherish become dust?\"","Azarax's voice was not malicious or mocking, just... curious.","He chuckled, then let out a sigh.","\"I am asking because I don't know.\"","His words were ambiguous, making Effie wonder if he meant that he had never been defeated, and therefore never had to experience something like this, or if he meant that he had never cherished anything, and was unfamiliar with the feeling of loss as a result.","In any case, he was being too presumptuous.","Turning her head, Effie glanced up at the King of Kings for a few seconds. Eventually, she said evenly:","\"I think you have the wrong idea about me.\"","Azarax raised an eyebrow.","\"Do I?\"","She hesitated, then nodded.","\"Have you forgotten how I ended up here? I'm a mercenary. I was paid to defend this city, so I did. The things I cherish are not here.\"","Azarax stared at her for a bit, his smile turning a little sinister.","\"Really. Well... let's put that to the test.\"","In the distance, the Dread Warriors entered the city gate, with other elites following. No one stopped them. There was no hail of arrows falling from the imposing wall, no devastation of thousands of Awakened Abilities unleashed at the same time. In fact, there was no movement on the wall at all. That was because the soldiers who had defended it retreated. They had only remained at the gate in the early morning to say farewell to their commander — as soon as Effie left, Kai led them toward the inner keep.","Now, the warriors of the Steel Horde were entering the city and spreading through its streets. They rushed past the burned districts, knowing that there was not much plunder there — the areas near the gate had not been affluent, to begin with.","Their true goal was the districts closer to the castle, and the castle itself. That was where true riches were... that was where the noblest people of the fallen city were supposed to be, as well.","Noble slaves were far more valuable, naturally.","If there was one peculiar thing about their advance, it was that the city was too empty — the soldiers of the Steel Horde knew that starvation, lack of water, and the plague had culled the population direly, but they were still surprised to see just how desolate the city looked.","Azarax, however, smiled. His eyes glinted with a vicious glee.","If Effie had to guess, she would say that it was because he felt his Domain expanding. The Mason was still alive, but he could not resist the Will of the King of Kings anymore — so, at Effie's request, he limited his influence to just the castle, surrendering the rest of the city to his foe.","Now that the Dread Warriors were advancing into the city unopposed, Azarax's Will was advancing, as well.","Most of them continued to move toward the castle. Some got distracted after reaching more affluent neighborhoods, breaking into abandoned homes to ransack them. The elites who were not a part of the Dread Warriors did not hope to get their hands on the treasures of the Stone Castle, so they did not even aim for it, making their way to the residential districts where the nobility had lived.","By then, the last of the soldiers of this first, most elite batch of plunderers had already entered the city. There was an ocean of the Steel Horde fighters inside the wall, moving like ants, all drunk on greed and dark desires.","Azarax frowned faintly.","“Isn't it too quiet, priestess? I would have expected to hear wails and begging by now.\"","Still sitting in the mud, suffering from the early symptoms of essence exhaustion, Effie let out a sigh.","“Yeah... about that...\"","As she glanced ahead, her lips twisted into a faint, dark smile.","“You'll hear it soon.\"","At that moment, a deep, reverberating sound resounded above the killing field. Then, the titanic stone gate of the city suddenly moved...","And closed shut."]},{"number":3125,"title":"Chapter 3125 Walls of the Trap","paragraphs":["As the gate of the city closed behind the elite forces of the Steel Horde, Azarax raised an eyebrow and glanced at Effie with a hint of cold displeasure in his eyes.","“Pristess... it seems that you weren't entirely honest with me. Or is it that your soldiers are not as obedient as you believed, and decided to disregard your orders?\"","He meant her promise that the defenders of the city would lay down their arms and surrender their lives without a fight. Azarax's tone was deceptively calm, but dangerous... however, he did not seem concerned. And why would he be? After all, the greatest obstacle in his path was the walls of the city. Now that his soldiers were inside, the hardest part of the siege was over.","Even if the remaining defenders tried to mount a resistance, they would be easily slaughtered by the elites of the Steel Horde. Plus, he was here as well. Even if Azarax had not joined the Dread Warriors in plundering the city, he could reach them quite rapidly if he wanted to — so, even if something unexpected happened, he would have plenty of time to react.","Or so he believed.","Effie, however, had her own thoughts on the matter.","It was all premeditated. She had known that the Dread Warriors and other elites of the Steel Horde would enter the city first. She had also known that Azarax would not kill her... more than that, she had known that he would not follow his soldiers inside.","That was because Azarax would not be able to resist the temptation of staying with Effie as she watched the city fall. He would find a good vantage point and force her to watch, doing his best to break her spirit... reveling in her dishonor.","His cruelty, too, had been accounted for. Effie had come up with the general form of the plan. Morgan, their tactician, worked out its every detail, including innumerable branching contingencies to account for unexpected variables and make the plan flexible enough to survive colliding with reality. Seishan was the one who had made it all possible, while Kai, Nightwalker, and Jet were meant to play key roles in what was about to happen.","Effie smiled faintly, feeling her fear dissipate.","She knew very well that she might die here... in fact, her eventual death was highly probable. Before that, she was bound to experience things that would make her wish she was dead.","But that was alright, as well. Because the possibility of her eventual death had been accounted for, too. It was one of the variables, and not one of the important ones at that.","Because her own task would be completed whether she lived or not.","\"They should be following my orders just fine, Plague of Steel. Ah, but I have to admit — I might have been a little bit dishonest. I am not the most honest person in the world, you see. Let alone in two worlds.\"","Azarax frowned, scrutinizing her with a displeased expression. Then, he turned to look at the distant city gate.","But it was already too late.","Effie and Morgan had known that it would not take Azarax long to reach the city and scale its walls. So, whatever they were going to visit upon the plunderers had to happen rapidly... it had to happen instantly.","And now, Effie was going to enjoy the show — even if it could be the last thing she would see in her life.","In fact, she had to thank Azarax for choosing such a wonderful vantage point.","‘I hope he appreciates my showmanship, as well...'","Far away, in the city, the Dread Warriors and numerous of the best soldiers of the Steel Horde were busy ransacking the affluent houses or advancing toward the castle.","None of them noticed that the city gate had closed yet — and, of course, none of them had learned that the complicated mechanism which moved the titanic slabs of stone was destroyed immediately after the gate shut close. This time, forever.","The people responsible for activating the mechanism one last time before sabotaging it were volunteers — those without families, slowly dying from the plague. They knew that this would be their last mission, but they also knew that their lives would be used as fuel to cause the Steel Horde great harm.","And since everyone in the city had lost friends and loved ones to the horrors of the siege, they were willing to trade their faltering lives for those of Azarax's best.","As they completed their mission, Kai was far away, standing on a tall bastion of the inner keep's wall. The Stone Castle had been built near the sea, so almost all of the city sprawled before him — countless streets, myriad homes. And dark rivers of the Steel Horde warriors spreading through the tangle of streets like poison.","There were several people behind him — Morgan, Seishan, Nightwalker, and the prince of the city. However, due to the distance, only he could see that the gate had already been closed, and that its mechanism had already been destroyed.","Kai inhaled deeply and then spoke in a low, emotionless tone:","\"It's time.\"","Nightwalker sighed and nodded.","\"That's my cue, then. I will go and prepare the Stone Castle for battle.\"","As he walked away, the prince looked ahead with a pale face, a storm of emotions raging in his eyes. However, he did not say anything — just clenched his fist, enduring the turmoil silently.","Morgan and Seishan were matter-of-factly preparing for battle, their expressions as mundane and business-like as on any other day.","Kai closed his eyes for a moment.","He knew what he was about to do.","He knew what the price of his actions would be, as well.","Just like the prince, his heart was bleeding... even if it was for a different reason.","He was worried about Effie. He was frightened for her.","But he also knew that she was right, and that this was the only way. If they were stronger, smarter, or luckier, there might have been a different path to conquering the Nightmare — but they weren't. They were weak, and in this cursed world, weakness was a sin.","But it was also the fuel that allowed those like them to grow and overcome impossible obstacles.","And so, Kai opened his eyes.","Looking at the dying city sprawled below him, he called upon his Aspect and spoke a single word:","\"Burn.\"","And, responding to his command...","The city was swallowed by flames."]},{"number":3126,"title":"Chapter 3126 Inferno","paragraphs":["Effie and her companions had been preparing for this day for a long while — in truth, she realized that the siege could only end in their defeat on the day the great river ran dry, and the Steel Horde entered the city by walking across its riverbed.","There had been more battles after that, and while they managed to repel Azarax and his army time after time, cementing the newly built barricades with blood, it was a losing game.","So, Effie had decided to change the rules. Since then, Seishan had been developing a secret weapon, while Morgan had been developing another. To achieve the goal, she conscripted the help of the Mason King and his family — who were not only the rulers of the city, but also knew all there was to know about stonework, mining, construction, and alchemy as well.","Additionally, she gathered all the sorcerers left in the city, most of whom were either disciples of the Mason King or descendants of his former students.","Their task was both simple and difficult to complete — under her guidance, they had to develop a highly incendiary concoction that blended alchemy and sorcery, produce great quantities of it, and hide it in secretly arranged underground caches throughout the city.","With Morgan's extensive knowledge of history, warfare, and weapons manufacturing, creating a superior analogue of the Greek fire was not a problem. The only problem was to source enough ingredients to produce it in the needed quantity in the harsh realities of a besieged city, with a naval blockade cutting it off from the world.","Still, they managed to achieve their goal in the end. They also created a limited supply of an explosive agent meant to serve as the detonator and delivery vehicle for the sorcerous inferno.","Now, thousands upon thousands of barrels full of highly flammable, unstable liquid were hidden in the tunnels beneath the city. Some were placed in the sewer junctions that had already existed before the siege, while some were placed in the secretly excavated chambers Morgan had created.","A vast runic array connected all the caches, meant to cause the detonators to activate simultaneously.","And so, when Kai ordered the world to burn, that array came alive.","Somewhere in the city, countless items followed his command and caught fire. Among them were the barrels of the flammable liquid and their detonators, as well — and when one of them produced a spark, the heat was transferred to all the rest, causing them all to detonate at the same time.","The result was both immediate and catastrophic.","Throughout the dying city, the earth opened in a deafening roar, spewing towering pillars of fire into the sky. These pillars then turned into swiftly expanding clouds, swallowing the entire expanse of streets between the outer wall and the castle. Fire was literally raining down upon the warriors of the Steel Horde caught in the middle... and it wasn't mundane fire, either.","Instead, it was a burning liquid that stuck to any surface it touched and could not be doused with water. The temperature at which it burned was utterly terrifying, as well, chewing through stone and steel in mere seconds.","There was no need to say what happened when it touched human flesh.","Instantly, the city was swallowed by a harrowing inferno, its vast expanse disappearing into a raging blaze. Countless streets, countless homes... all of it either burned or collapsed into the deep fissures that opened in the ground, the thunderous roar of utter devastation washing over Kai like a requiem.","The screams of the Steel Horde elites caught in the fire, however, were a far sweeter song.","In an instant, all those who had rushed into the city to plunder it were either swallowed or surrounded by flames. The whole city burned, melting and turning to ash like a great funeral pyre for the countless people who had died to defend it — even if there were pockets of safety among the intense flames, the fire was spreading, and they would not remain safe for long.","And if the invaders attempted to escape the inferno by retreating... the gate was already closed, its mechanism destroyed, turning the city into an inescapable trap.","In the face of such vast, callous destruction, the faces of every soldier manning the walls of the Stone Castle turned pale.","But even if they were watching their city being reduced to ash, they felt sorrow and joy in equal measure. Because their enemies were burning with it.","However...","It was not enough.","The Awakened warriors would perish. The Ascended officers might burn to death, as well. But the strongest of them, the Transcendent powerhouses, could potentially find their way out of the inferno. They could stay alive until their Sovereign arrived, at least.","Kai could not allow that to happen.","\"I'm going.\"","His face was grim, the flames reflecting in his eyes.","Leaving Morgan, Seishan, and the pale-faced prince behind, he rose into the air... and then dove into the flames.","‘Slaughter...’","This trap had been set by paying such a high price. An unthinkable price.","So, he had to make sure that it was all worth it... as close to being worth it as he could.","‘I'll slaughter them all.'","The flames roared as they took him in their immolating embrace.","...Far away, across the vast inferno of the burning city and the great expanse of the killing field, Effie smiled as she watched flames rise above the towering wall, and heard the wind carry over screams of chilling agony.","She looked at Azarax, whose expression was contorted in rage.","Effie's faint smile widened a little, turning into a grin.","“Did you say that you were going to destroy my city, Azarax? Look — you failed. You will never be able to destroy it now. It was never yours to destroy.\"","A mad glint appeared in her eyes.","\"I destroyed it. It was I who burned it, not you. All the time you wasted, and for what? To be outdone by a Transcendent mercenary?\"","As Azarax's expression turned dark and dangerous, Effie could not help but laugh.","“What do you think the chronicles will say now? Azarax the Mighty, the King of Kings, wasted two years trying his hardest to conquer a peaceful city. But in the end, he could not.\"","She was still laughing when his fist connected with her head.","Effie was thrown to the ground. The pain was blinding, and she could feel something inside her head cracking as she fell.","But even then...","She still thought that it was pretty funny."]},{"number":3127,"title":"Chapter 3127 Second Part","paragraphs":["Effie had been drained of essence, and now, she received a blow from a Supreme. Although Azarax had not meant to kill her, she was still dazed.","Even without her Aspect, Effie was quite hardy — more so than most Saints... unless they were of a Divine Lineage, naturally. However, getting smacked by the King of Kings was not something she could escape unscathed in her powerless state. Her eardrum had ruptured, and she was pretty sure that her skull had cracked.","Lying in the mud and tasting blood on her tongue, some flowing down her face as well, Effie watched flames dance above the wall of the city.","It was a pretty sight.","There were three parts to their plan of conquering the Nightmare. The first one was right in front of her: the most elite warriors of the Steel Horde being burned alive in an inescapable trap. She had sacrificed the city to kill them. All of the city except for the Stone Castle, at least, which now sheltered the remaining population — so their distant screams were like music to her ears.","However, this trap of hers was not good enough in and of itself.","The Dread Warriors would not be able to open the gate, and all ways to ascend the wall from the city had either been destroyed or walled off, with traps waiting for those who did scale it. So, those of them who survived the initial detonation had only one way left to go — toward the last remaining safe area, the castle.","It was Nightwalker's job to defend it. Kai, Morgan, and Seishan, meanwhile, were meant to hunt down the Dread Generals in the immolating inferno, making sure that these powerful Transcendent champions perished in the flame.","But there was no guarantee that they would succeed. The Steel Horde had already sustained calamitous losses, but how many more elites Azarax would lose depended on how soon he intervened personally.","Even with his power and speed, he would not be able to save all of his warriors... but he could save some.","And indeed, as Effie turned her head, she saw Azarax preparing to rush toward the burning city.","And that was where the second part of the plan came into play.","As Azarax took a step forward, there was the sound of hooves, and the soldiers crowding behind him, watching the distant blaze with stunned and frightened expressions, parted like a sea. A horse with foam on its bloodied lips galloped through their mass, and an exhausted rider jumped off its back, landing into the mud near Azarax and Effie.","He was in such a hurry that drops of mud splattered on the King of Kings, which would usually get the messenger killed. At the moment, however, Azarax did not seem in the mood to pay it any attention.","\"M—my... my lord!\"","The messenger's voice trembled, and his eyes were full of fear.","Azarax scowled.","“What is it?\"","The man, still kneeling on the ground, drew a hoarse breath and then spoke in a tone of urgency:","\"The... the supply caravan, my lord! It was attacked! So many are dead... the wraith took them!\"","The King of Kings' expression changed, and he threw a furious look at Effie.","‘Here it comes.'","She prepared herself, but when his kick arrived, sending her flying like a rag doll, it still hurt like hell. As Effie rolled on the ground, failing to suppress a suffocated groan, she heard Azarax hissing a curse.","Jet was responsible for the second part of the plan. Several days ago, she had secretly left the city and journeyed behind the enemy lines, making her way to the road that the caravans supplying the Steel Horde with equipment and provisions traveled. These caravans arrived daily, with an especially large one coming once a month. These caravans were heavily protected, and the monthly one was especially so. In fact, it was no different from a legion in and of itself, defended by countless Awakened soldiers, Ascended officers, and Transcendent commanders.","Today was the day it was supposed to arrive — and it was not a coincidence that Effie had chosen the same day to act, naturally. The immense size of the Steel Horde was its main advantage, but it was also its weakness. It consumed an unfathomable amount of food and demanded a constant influx of weapons, garments, medicine, and other equipment.","Usually, a part of that burden would be alleviated by scavenging and plundering the conquered lands. However, ever since the Steel Horde had gotten stranded under the walls of the Mason's city, there were no new conquered lands — only the surrounding areas, which had long turned into a desolate wasteland. So, the great army of the King of Kings relied heavily on the supply caravans. Which was why Jet had attacked it at the same time as Effie surrendered herself, facing all its defenders alone.","Her task was not to eradicate the entire guard legion — it was to destroy the supplies. Without them, the Steel Horde would learn what starvation meant, as well... they would feel the same hunger that the people of the besieged city felt. Even if the next caravan could alleviate their hunger somewhat, the supply situation was already unstable because of the unrest in the neglected empire.","These provisions had not appeared out of thin air, either. They were the result of a heavy war tax that the farmers and artisans of the empire paid, often while not having enough to eat themselves. These people had just surrendered their grain and cattle to send off the great caravan... so what would happen if the authorities demanded the same amount of tax to be paid again only weeks later?","Nobody knew.","So, Azarax had a choice now.","A choice Effie had graciously given him.","He could rush toward the city and save as many of his Dread Warriors as he could, or rush toward where the supply caravan had been ambushed and save as many provisions as possible.","Spitting a mouthful of blood, Effie looked up at Azarax from the ground.","The King of Kings... looked blurry.","She was really not feeling well.","Still, she thought she saw his hesitation. Azarax treasured the Dread Warriors, and especially the Dread Generals — they were the greatest trophies of his conquest, after all, the prideful warriors who had once defied him, but who were now his obedient thralls.","However, he also understood that the Dread Warriors were merely one legion of his vast army. And without the supplies... his grasp on the entire Steel Horde might weaken. After all, what was the worth of a warlord who could not even feed his warriors? Azarax could not allow his soldiers to begin asking themselves that question — he refused to, rather.","And so, gritting his teeth, he turned his back to the burning city and disappeared, rushing in the direction of the ambushed caravan. Effie was finally able to draw air into her damaged lungs, drawing a hoarse breath.","‘Good... that's for the best. It's up to you now, Kai...’"]},{"number":3128,"title":"Chapter 3128 Song of Fire","paragraphs":["The dying city that had resembled hell was now in its final death throes, having truly become one. Fire was everywhere, greedily devouring the collapsing buildings. Thick smoke enveloped everything around, plunging the burning streets into an acrid darkness.","Most of the city had been built from stone, but the blaze consuming it was not of mundane nature. The liquid fire Morgan had developed with the help of the local sorcerers burned hot enough to melt stone, and it fed on it too. The flames swallowed one building after another, turning the corpses of those who had fallen to the plague into ash.","The flames were devouring the living, as well.","Everywhere in the burning city, the soldiers of the Steel Horde were screaming in harrowing agony, thrashing as their flesh was melting off their bones. Neither steel armor nor Awakened powers could protect them, and their tortured, terrified voices fused into a hellish litany.","But not all of them were burning... yet.","No matter how many barrels of the Stone Fire Morgan and her subordinates had created, it was not enough to cover every centimeter of the vast city. The fire was spreading, but it was not spreading fast enough.","Those who survived the initial explosion had the chance to save themselves, still. Some tried to save themselves by launching an assault on the Stone Castle, which was protected from the blaze both by Morgan's careful arrangements and by the withering Will of the Mason. The rest tried to flee through the city gate, and once they discovered that it had been sealed shut, turned their gazes to the wall.","All paths to the ramparts had been blocked or destroyed in advance, but humans, and especially Awakened, were resourceful. They would find a way to scale the city wall, overcome the traps waiting for them, and some — those of them who survived — would ultimately escape.","The rest might try to seek shelter in the harbor, instead. The Stone Fire burned atop the water, having turned it into a sea of flame, but if one could hold their breath long enough, they might reach salvation after all.","Kai could not allow that to happen. Nightwalker was holding the Stone Castle. Morgan and Seishan were meant to block off the harbor. So, it was his task to make sure that those who retreated to the city wall died — all of them, without exception. He rushed through the fire and smoke like a dark shadow.","The flames could not harm him today — he had earned the right to move through them by bathing in the scorching blood of a dragon. As he traversed the inferno with terrifying speed, he encountered pockets of surviving soldiers among the shadows.","The soldiers died before realizing what kind of monster lunged at them from the billowing flames. Awakened, Ascended... Kai did not pay them enough attention to determine their Rank. All he knew was that they were not the prey he was hunting for — they were not the Dread Generals, who had to die today at all costs.","Jet was somewhere behind enemy lines, destroying the supply lines of the Steel Horde all alone. Kai did not know what Azarax would choose — would he go after the elusive wraith that threatened to starve his army, or would he plunge into the flames devouring his best soldiers — so he had to hurry.","He slaughtered more soldiers on the way to the wall. At first, he killed them with his sword and his arrows. Then, judging it too slow, he assumed his draconic form, emerging from the fiery clouds of black smoke like a terrifying, towering visage of destruction and death.","Wreathed in fire and smoke, his midnight-blue scales looked almost entirely black.","Then, even that seemed like a waste of time. So, he simply commanded the flames to devour the soldiers of the Steel Horde in his place, using his Aspect to make the blaze move.","He felt it then, in the violent embrace of merciless slaughter...","The heartbeat of fire.","The blaze was like a living being — a giant, insatiable beast that longed to devour all of existence, to use all of existence as fuel for its fleeting radiance. It moved, it twisted, it churned... it grew, it withered. It wanted to be, it wanted to shine...","It wanted to burn.","Kai reached the city wall by then, and clashed with those two Dread Generals who had chosen it as their path to salvation. He burned their soldiers first, and then called upon the flames to attack the Transcendent thralls as well.","The champions of the Steel Horde could endure the flame... but they couldn't endure the fierce black dragon that emerged from the billowing sea of black smoke, wreathed in cinders and fire.","The three of them fought in the middle of hell, the dire force of their battle fueling the spreading inferno.","The Dread Generals were strong. They were heroic. They were seasoned and experienced, having survived innumerable campaigns.","But Kai was strong, heroic, and seasoned as well. In fact, he had survived far more horrifying things than these fallen heroes of annihilated kingdoms could ever imagine. So, he fought them fiercely.","He fought them earnestly.","And somewhere in the middle of that...","The Spell whispered in his ear.","It said:","[You have received an Aspect Legacy...]","At that moment, Kai felt something deep and profound take root in his mind — something that was as old as the world, or possibly even predated it. He recognized its form, as well. It was something that he had tried to master himself, but failed to fathom innumerable times.","It was the True Name of Fire.","There were those who were born with a talent for Shaping, and those who were born without it. Kai's case, however, was unique — his Transcendent form gave him a unique resonance with Shaping, making him believe that if he could invoke the Names, the result would be much more destructive than for any other sorcerer.","However, perhaps for that very reason, his mind had not been able to accommodate any Names. It was as if there was a powerful force blocking him from learning them. He did not merely lack the talent for Shaping... he was the opposite of talented, completely inept.","Until now.","Now, the Name of Fire — and a few more — lived in his mind, having fused with his very spirit, making it feel like invoking them was the most natural thing in the world... like it had been his power all along.","They were like songs, making him feel a familiar longing.","And so, Kai invoked it.","He invoked the Song of Fire.","In the next moment, a vast, roaring pillar of radiant silver flame escaped from his maw, swallowing the Dread Generals in an instant.","Enveloped by that beautiful flame, they only survived for a second.","Then, their figures dissolved into the silver radiance, turning to ash.","And then, the ash was annihilated as well. The pillar of silver flame crashed into the city and exploded, turning into a radiant sea of immolating fire, drowning the world in obliterating heat.","Kai was not done, though...","His hunt was only beginning.","No one was going to escape the burning city today."]},{"number":3129,"title":"Chapter 3129 Lack of Fear","paragraphs":["In the end, very few of the Dread Warriors had managed to escape the inferno. Most of them perished in the fire, while the rest were either slaughtered by Kai, Morgan, and Seishan or died while trying to storm the Stone Castle.","The castle itself, as well as the survivors of the city sheltered behind its walls, remained safe.","The Dread Generals were all gone, slain in the devastating chaos.","The city was no more.","From the outer wall to the moat of the inner keep, it was now an ashen wasteland. Piles of blackened rubble protruded from the ash like twisted gravestones, and clouds of smoke obscured the sky, making the day as dark as the night.","Years of calamitous siege had not managed to destroy the peaceful city of the Mason King, but the actions of Effie and her companions did.","It was not that great of a loss, though. After everything was over and done, Kai had a brief conversation with the young prince. The prince told him in a distant tone that the city was its people, not its buildings and walls. The people were still alive... some of them were... so the city was alive, as well.","Far away, Azarax had managed to secure the remains of the supply caravan. The army of soldiers tasked with protecting it had been decimated by Jet, their Transcendent commanders slaughtered, and most of the provisions were ruined. Only a small portion was still intact.","Soul Reaper herself had disappeared before Azarax arrived. He did not know how she knew when to flee... perhaps the vast swarms of crows circling the camp of the Steel Horde had warned her. She was known to communicate with them from time to time, after all.","Overall, it had been a devastating day for the King of Kings and his horde.","Needless to say, Azarax was in a foul mood by the time he returned to the vast encampment of the besieging army with the battered remains of the supply caravan. The Dread Warriors and other elite units of the Steel Horde had been wiped out. Most of his thralls were gone. His soldiers were going to starve for a while, and their morale had been dealt a severe blow.","And what had he gained in return?","His gaze landed on the beautiful, prideful woman chained to the post of his personal tent. The priestess of War God... the War Maiden.","That was his prize.","Now that she was covered in mud, bloodied and beaten, she did not look so arrogant anymore. However, he could still see it, there in the depths of her eyes — defiance. An infuriating lack of fear. An absence of submission.","The priestess was still unbroken.","That sight made Azarax's blood boil.","For a moment, he entertained the thought of turning her into a thrall. The idea was certainly alluring. Having a woman like that following his every command, wasn't it a tantalizing prospect? Plus, it would please him a great deal to send her into battle against her former comrades, watch them die by her hand, and see the city she had so desperately defended fall to her own blade. See the War Maiden witnessing her comrades die by her hand and her city fall to her blade, most of all.","But no... there was no sport in that.","Now that Azarax had grown truly powerful — far more powerful than any of the enemies he could allow himself to keep alive — he did not enjoy turning them into thralls that much anymore. The fight was over in an instant, and their resistance was as well. They did not really break, they were simply shattered.","This one, though...","This one, he wanted to break thoroughly. He wanted to see her submit to him of her own free will.","Looking at the priestess, who sat on the lush carpet and stared at him with a lack of emotion, Azarax sighed.","\"What was the point of this stunt, priestess?\"","Leaning down, he grabbed her chin and jerked her head upward.","“You managed to kill some of my men, and destroyed one supply caravan. And for what?\"","Azarax scoffed, then shook his head.","\"The walls of the city have still fallen. The last of your soldiers may have retreated to the old man’s castle, but how long can they hold out? Even without the Dread Warriors, my horde is still vast and unrivaled. Now that my soldiers can enter the city, they will conquer that last stronghold soon. Even before that, your people will probably fall to starvation. They are completely isolated in that castle, after all.\"","He smiled darkly.","\"That is if the old man does not crumble entirely before that. So... nothing has changed. All you achieved is buying your people a bit of time and inconveniencing me slightly. And at what cost? It cost you the only shred of mercy I was willing to afford that pathetic city. Foolish priestess... don't blame me for being merciless now.\"","The War Maiden stared at him apathetically for a few long moments, and then moved her hands slightly, the chains rattling as she pushed against the shackles.","“What was it for?\"","Her voice was weak, making Azarax wonder if he had struck her too forcefully before. She looked at him silently, and then twisted her bloodied lips into a smile.","“It was to kill you.\"","Her smile widened, and was then erased by his slap.","The priestess toppled, falling back to the ground. More blood flowed down her face, looking almost black in the dim light of the tent.","Azarax exhaled slowly and then looked at her with displeasure.","He remained silent for a while, then shook her head.","“Well, in that case, you failed. You did manage to spite me quite a bit, though, so... prepare to atone for that.\"","Effie had a feeling that she would not enjoy what was coming next, but she could only steel her heart and prepare.","She had not lied to Azarax, after all.","The first part of the plan was to trap and destroy the elite forces of the Steel Horde inside the city, spearheaded by Kai and Morgan.","The second part of the plan was to ambush the great supply caravan and leave Azarax's warriors stranded without food, achieved by Jet alone.","The third and final part of the plan...","Was to destroy the Steel Horde and kill Azarax.","That one was all up to Effie."]},{"number":3130,"title":"Chapter 3130 Bleak Days","paragraphs":["The next few days were as ghastly as Effie had expected them to be. Azarax was boiling with rage, and he had myriad ways to take it out on her. Of course, he never really lost control — she'd be dead in a moment if he did — and while he wanted her to believe that his mind was overcome by rage, she could see that all his gruesome feats of cruelty were meticulously calculated.","Azarax never truly lost control. Hidden behind his arrogance and outwardly unabashed savagery was a cold, calculating mind. He was always shrewd, knowing exactly how much unrestrained wickedness he could allow himself.","Azarax's true goal was to break Effie's spirit. And to do that, he had wisely decided to break her physically first — the body and the spirit were inseparably connected, after all. But even then, Azarax was careful not to damage her too badly... not to ruin her altogether, since he wanted her to become a thrall after all of it was over and the Steel Horde moved on to its next conquest.","In fact, Effie had a feeling that he wanted her to become his second-in-command. He wanted her to lead the Steel Horde as he conquered the rest of the mortal realms — to become the first of the new Dread Generals, no less.","So, no matter how ghastly his torture was, she could still endure it... somewhat. It was monstrous and gruesome, but not nearly as terrifying as what she had experienced at the hands of the Dreamspawn. Azarax was not starving her, at least — he did not know what her Flaw was, after all — and he was not using her husband to turn the whole ordeal into a morbid nightmare.","In fact, he was not doing anything that would leave a permanent mark on her... after a good healer tended to her wounds, that was. There were plenty of powerful healers in the Steel Horde, sadly, so that allowed Azarax to do quite a lot.","His methods were both simple and effective. There were the utterly mundane forms of abuse and torture, such as beating, cutting, burning, breaking, and drowning. There were more esoteric ones, as well, such as twisting the channels through which soul essence flowed through her body and wreaking havoc in her soul.","The ancients knew far more about the fine art of torturing Awakened than her own people. In that regard, at least, Effie had to give credit where credit was due.","She thought that she was holding up well... at least as well as anyone could be expected to hold up while being tortured and maimed. But, at the same time, she found herself slowly being reduced to a bloodied, scared beast who shivered when it heard the footsteps of its captor.","Effie was still a person, after all. She was not immune to pain, nor was she immune to the fear of pain. So, Azarax's methods, while crude, could not be called ineffective.","Effie still refused to obey him, though. She remained steadfast in her defiant refusal... even if, after a while, he did manage to make her beg for mercy.","On that day, Azarax finally smiled. He was standing there, covered in her blood from head to toe, looking at her with an expression of content and satisfaction.","\"There is progress after all, huh, priestess?\"","Leaning closer, he studied her pale face and grinned.","“Good! To be honest, I was growing quite bored with this arrangement. Shall we come up with something new, then? There's a crowd of people outside this tent clamoring to get to know you better, priestess. Do help me bolster their morale.\"","Effie wanted to protest and say that she would actually prefer if he tortured her some more. But even if she didn't want to admit it, these past few days had taught her caution... fear, even. So, she held her tongue.","'Well... he's bored now. Nothing I could do about it, is there?'","Azarax was a very busy man, after all. He had already dedicated a lot of his time to her — a dubious honor, but an honor nonetheless. So, it was no surprise that he wanted to outsource tormenting her to someone else.","His soldiers were starting to feel the lack of provisions by now, and the ghastly fates of their comrades were still fresh in their minds. They also knew that Effie was to blame for all their woes, which probably motivated them to tear her apart a great deal.","For a moment, Effie thought that Azarax had finally decided to kill her. Dying did not seem like such a bad idea, after everything she had to experience as of late... but no, she still wanted to live. She wanted to live desperately. After all, there were people waiting for her to return. Her husband, her son — she couldn't die so easily, at least for their sake.","Plus, she doubted that Azarax would really allow her to die. Why would he do something like that after spending so much effort carefully keeping her alive?","And, in a sense, getting access to his soldiers was beneficial to her. So, she did not mind.","In the end, Effie ended up chained to a post in front of Azarax's tent, this time wearing a collar around her neck. She spent her time sitting in the mud, her back leaning against the post, observing the movements of the soldiers with bleak eyes. The tendons in her feet had been severed, so she couldn't stand up even if she wanted to. Her body was void of essence, making her as weak as a kitten. Well... a Transcendent kitten, at least.","The soldiers of the Steel Horde were free to do whatever they wished with her. However, they mostly stayed away, only glaring at her with hatred from afar.","That was because there were a dozen corpses lying in the mud around her, about as far as the length of the chain allowed her to move.","These were the corpses of the soldiers who had tried to lay their hands on the chained priestess of War, but ended up being killed by her instead."]},{"number":3131,"title":"Chapter 3131 Secret Weapon","paragraphs":["At first, Effie had believed that Azarax would order his soldiers to nail her to a cross and install it in front of the camp, in view of the city. That would have been quite ironic, considering his eventual fate. The ancients seemed to love crucifying people, as well — it was their favorite form of execution, by far, at least in this era.","However, in hindsight, that wouldn't be very fun for the warriors of the Steel Horde, since there was little they could do to her on a cross. Having their nemesis nailed to a pair of wooden planks would limit their actions, and she wouldn't be able to offer any resistance either — which was the most amusing part, as far as Azarax was concerned.","So, he had gone with a wooden post and a dog collar instead.","Wounded and shackled as she was, Effie couldn't do much. But when the first batch of soldiers rushed forward to get her, she still managed to kill them.","Did she need to be able to stand to kill these vermin? Did she need her essence? Did she need a weapon?","The answer was no, which the warriors of the Steel Horde learned very soon.","Effie used her legs to topple the warriors, crack their skulls, and break their necks. Those who managed to reach her, after all, learned how sharp her teeth were. One even bled to death as a result, crawling back and clutching his torn throat in horror.","Effie spat in disgust and glanced at the wary observers with a grin.","“Who's next?\"","Actually, she would have preferred if the last soldier survived. He was of more use to her alive.","There were some who survived after that, but eventually, the soldiers ceased their attempts to punish her, frightened by the fates of their predecessors.","So, Effie enjoyed a few days of relative peace.","She was not sure how much time had passed since her surrender, having lost track of it during the torture, but the world was still in motion.","Judging by the movements of the Steel Horde, they were preparing for another assault. There had been rain recently, so even the most stubborn fires that still burned in the city would be all but extinguished by now — so, nothing prevented Azarax and his warriors from attacking the Stone Castle.","In fact, there were far fewer soldiers in the encampment than there used to be. That meant that many of them had already scaled the walls of the city and established forward bases there, clearing out the way for the main force to pass through.","Effie did not know if this would be the first major assault on the Stone Castle after the defending forces surrendered the city, or if her friends had been fighting for their lives all this time. She did, however, know that they had not been defeated yet — Azarax would not have missed the chance to throw their bodies to her feet otherwise.","Another mystery that Effie could not solve was what had happened to Jet. Her friend seemed to have escaped Azarax's rage on the day of the ambush, but there had been no news of her since. The soldiers of the horde seemed both hungry and frightened, though, hinting that Jet was still a threat.","In fact, Effie had surmised why they were so wary of Jet by hearing bits and pieces of conversations happening in the encampment. The cause of their fear was not the ambush on the supply caravan itself — rather, they were afraid that the eerie and elusive wraith would continue decimating their supply lines. But most of all, the soldiers were afraid that she would aim her dreadful gaze elsewhere.","They were afraid that Jet would leave the city and journey into the heart of the Steel Empire instead.","Why attack the supply caravans, after all, when she could attack the settlements producing the supplies?","With Azarax locked by the siege and the Dread Generals dead, there were few warriors in the empire who could kill that demon. If she decided to rain terror on its heartland, it was very possible that nobody would be able to prevent her from razing entire cities to the ground.","And while the soldiers of the Steel Horde were safe on the frontline, under Azarax's watchful gaze, their families back home weren't. All of that added to the tense and anxious atmosphere in the vast encampment. Ironically enough, Jet's absence was doing more damage to the morale of Azarax's army than her blade had ever done.","The Stone Castle still stood. The Mason was still clinging to life. Kai and the other members of the cohort were still holding the Steel Horde off, buying Effie time to complete her mission.","Her mission...","Throughout the days of abuse at the hands of Azarax, Effie had not made a good showing of her resilience and indomitable will. It was partially because of how skilled he was at visiting pain upon living things, and partially because she was weakened and drained of essence, stealing her powers away.","But in truth, there was another reason why Effie had ended up in such a pathetic state — and most of her efforts during the torture went into hiding that reason from Azarax. It was that she was being weakened by a far more sinister affliction than essence exhaustion.","Sitting in the mud and chained to a pole, her hands shackled behind her, Effie could feel them trembling uncontrollably. Acting as if nothing was the matter, she looked at her side, where a fresh wound had just scabbed over. A bit of blood was still seeping from the cut, mixing with the grime covering her skin.","Her blood had been turning darker and darker over these past few days. Soon enough, she won't be able to hide her condition anymore...","She would not be able to hide the fact that she was carrying the plague.","Back when Azarax had diverted the river and invaded the city for the first time, Effie realized that they would be defeated eventually. So, she gave Seishan a morbid task — she told her to make the plague stronger instead of learning how to destroy it.","The sorcerers of the Steel Horde had created the plague, so they surely knew how to combat it as well. Effie could not just toss diseased corpses over the wall and hope that the adversary soldiers would be consumed by the same curse that had been unleashed upon the peaceful city.","But she had something that Azarax did not possess... she had Seishan, the descendant of Beast God — the God of Blood. So, she told Seishan to take the plague that the Steel Horde had created and turn it into a much more dire, much more virulent, much more dreadful curse. A curse that Azarax and his sorcerers had no cure for.","After that, Effie and her companions had been patiently waiting for Seishan to nurture the superior strain of the mystical plague within herself. The daughter of Ki Song had almost perished while attempting it, but in the end, she succeeded.","What she created was a profane masterpiece of curses, a mystical pestilence so ghastly and grotesque that even a Supreme would not be able to escape its jaws.","The only obstacle in their path was actually delivering it to Azarax's doorstep. He was not a fool, after all, and he was especially ruthless. So, if they weren't cautious, the King of Kings could detect and destroy their carefully engineered plague before it could really spread among his soldiers.","Luckily, Effie had a perfect delivery system in mind.","It was her own body.","Azarax had a fixation on the War Maiden, after all. She was the only one whom he would not kill immediately and keep close to himself, trying to break her spirit down slowly. Effie herself was the tantalizing lure that Azarax could not resist, and therefore, she was the flawless trap to destroy him.","She had come to the camp of the Steel Horde to surrender, which turned out to be a distraction to lure its elites into a trap. But, in fact, Effie herself was the true trap. Even if she seemed like a human, what she truly was... was a guided warhead carrying a heavy load of a lethal, virulent bioweapon. She was a weapon of mass destruction disguised as a person, engaged in the ghastly act of biological warfare.","And with each day that Effie stayed alive, the plague she had brought with her was spreading wider and wider through the vast encampment of the Steel Horde.","Azarax had been exposed to it the most, since he had spent a lot of time with her alone and came into contact with her blood on countless occasions. The soldiers who had touched her, had been close to her, or survived trying to accost her were next. Everyone whom they had interacted with since were most likely infected by now, as well. All the people the secondary carriers of the plague had talked to must have caught it, too. It must have spread far and wide in the camp of the Steel Horde, claiming innumerable hosts.","The plague was in its incubation period, for now... but it would begin to reveal itself soon. If even Effie, a Saint, was starting to show symptoms, then mundane and Awakened soldiers would follow at any moment now.","Then...","Then, the third part of her plan would finally be complete."]},{"number":3132,"title":"Chapter 3132 Poisoned Chalice","paragraphs":["It began slowly.","Effie was still chained in the mud, with more dead soldiers scattered around her now. Azarax did not seem inclined to remove the corpses, perhaps as a way of making her already morbid existence even more oppressive, perhaps to instill a sense of competition into other warriors of the Steel Horde.","As if seeing their dead comrades would motivate them to try harder and succeed where others had failed. That was a questionable tactic, at best, but considering that a handful of fools inevitably attempted to attack Effie every day, it seemed to be working.","In the meantime, her wounds had healed, somewhat. When they did, Azarax personally arrived to disable her all over again. That was one of the only two times he had bothered to tend to her personally after expelling her from his tent — the second time was immediately after the first major assault on the Stone Castle had failed.","That time, Effie really thought that she would die.","But, in the end, she didn't.","The severity of the beating she received, however, helped mask her worsening condition. She had kept the plague under control for as long as he could, but by now, her body was finally beginning to surrender.","Effie was being consumed by persistent, harrowing pain. It was as if all her organs were devouring themselves. Her blood was turning thick and dark, almost black — luckily, when it dried, it was almost indistinguishable from the mud, and her condition had only worsened after the last visit from the King of Kings. So, no one had noticed the strange detail yet.","The soldiers simply attributed Effie's groans and weakened state to the consequences of the beating she had received from Azarax. It gave more of them the courage to try attacking her in a group... hence the increased number of corpses.","‘How the hell did Seishan endure it for so long...'","Effie had known that the daughter of Ki Song was not to be trifled with from their days on the Forgotten Shore. Still, experiencing the gruesome torment of the plague put things into perspective. Now, she could understand better how Seishan had survived a decade in that harrowing place... longer than any other Sleeper who escaped the Forgotten Shore in the end.","Effie's body... was slowly rotting from the inside. At the moment, her Transcendent physique was struggling to heal it faster than the plague was destroying it, locking her in a vicious cycle. For now, she was able to overcome the terrifying rate of virulent decay — but soon enough, the situation could change.","By the time gruesome sores opened on her body and blood began to seep from her pores, even a blind man would know that something was wrong with the captured War Maiden.","Effie knew that Azarax would know the truth far sooner, though.","That was because while she was still able to hide the symptoms, the soldiers of the Steel Horde could not.","Seishan had engineered her plague to have a long incubation period, so that it could spread wider before being detected. Now, that period was coming to an end.","Azarax himself would have been the first of the infected, but he probably had not felt the changes happening deep within his body yet. He was a Supreme, after all, and an especially powerful one at that. His body possessed an almost inexhaustible amount of vitality. So, even if he had been infected by the plague earlier, it would take longer for it to conquer him.","His soldiers, however, were much weaker. In fact, they were weaker now than ever, because many of them were subsisting on pitiful rations. Hunger, exhaustion, and the burdens of a long siege had made them look gaunt and diminished, which allowed the plague to remain hidden longer.","Its first symptoms were easy to miss, after all. The overall fatigue, the hand tremors... all of it was easy to attribute to exhaustion and starvation. Only Effie knew that there was a different, far more alarming reason why many of the soldiers around the camp seemed like they were on the verge of collapsing as of late.","Observing how widely the plague had already spread, she could not help but feel both horrified and full of dark, merciless joy.","She wondered if the people of the First Generation had felt the same eerie confusion when the Nightmare Spell descended into the world. It had been all but ignored for a long while, and by the time humanity began to pay attention, there was already no time to react.","The same happened with the plague Effie had brought to the encampment of the Steel Horde.","Some of the soldiers looked tired at first. But who wouldn't be, when they had to lay siege to an impregnable castle on an empty stomach?","Their hands were shaking. But whose wouldn't, when countless soldiers had already perished in this grueling campaign, and many more would die before it was over?","It was only when one of them bent over and vomited a torrent of viscous, black blood that the officers of the Steel Horde finally realized that something was wrong.","Sadly, Effie had not witnessed that incident, but she quickly learned of it from the frightened whispers of the soldiers.","Even then, though...","The Steel Horde was slow to react.","The plague had originated from its sorcerers, after all. So, when one soldier was discovered to be a carrier, Azarax wasn't too alarmed.","He might have expected it, even, considering that his soldiers were fighting inside the infected city now. Perhaps the inferno Effie and her cohort had unleashed did not destroy all pockets of the plague — so, he simply ordered his sorcerers to begin administering the cure.","It was only in the process of searching for all the infected soldiers that the healers of the Steel Horde began to feel alarmed. There were simply too many people showing the symptoms of the plague — and while it had not progressed to truly harrowing stages yet, it wasn't in its early days either.","That went against the notion that these first cases were the result of random soldiers being infected while traversing the burned city. So, the healers and the sorcerers began to treat them with uneasy hearts."]},{"number":3133,"title":"Chapter 3133 Spreading Fear","paragraphs":["A few more days passed just like that. The atmosphere in the encampment of the Steel Horde was turning more and more tense. It was as if dark clouds were gathering above it. The supply situation was growing more dire as the old provisions were consumed, while the new ones never arrived.","There were rumors that the War Maiden's wraith continued to attack the smaller supply caravans, but Effie had no way of knowing if Jet was truly continuing her sabotage campaign or if the soldiers were simply frightened and telling tall tales. Azarax was steadily preparing to launch another assault on the Stone Castle — this one, he meant to make the final one.","He was unhappy with the supply shortage as well, and, feeling the plummeting mood of the soldiers, knew that the best way to turn the situation around and keep his fearsome reputation as spotless as possible was to end the siege sooner rather than later.","The Mason had to be taking his last breaths by now... if Azarax truly pushed an assault, the Stone Castle could very well fall quickly. Consumed by pain and drowning in her own blood, chained in the mud in front of the King of King’s tent, Effie could feel the Steel Horde stirring like a hungry beast.","Now that the soldiers knew that they could taste victory soon, their compromised morale soared once more. Even if there was not a lot left to plunder in the burned city, simply leaving this cursed place was a blessed reward.","However... that last fateful assault was not destined to happen. Not in the way Azarax imagined, at least.","Because by the time Azarax was ready to lead his warriors into battle once more, the sorcerers finally realized that the cure they had developed to heal their own plague was not working.","That was when Effie saw the camp of the Steel Horde really descend into panic. Perhaps at any other time, the warriors of the conquering horde would have endured the harrowing fear of the plague. But now, after months of a bitter siege, having suffered incalculable casualties, with the elite core of the entire army having been completely wiped out only weeks earlier, hungry, and with the rumors of an eerie wraith haunting the empire...","Even those soldiers who were not infected by the plague — the majority of them — could not help but feel suffocated by fear and anxiety.","Effie laughed as she watched them squirm. Well, she tried to, at least, before bending over in a fit of wet coughing.","‘Serves you right, bastards... die here, under the walls of the city you wanted to destroy. Let your bones nourish the land you turned into a desert...’","Naturally, her hatred might have been misplaced. After all, these soldiers were mundane people. She doubted that when Azarax the Mighty ordered them to be conscripted into the Steel Horde, they could have said no... in fact, many of them, possibly even most of them, hailed from the lands the King of Kings had conquered in the past.","Having been conquered, they had no choice but to become cogs in the insatiable machine of the militant empire. Choice was not a luxury afforded to those who had been subjugated.","But this was the ancient past. Morality was different and far more primal here... so, Effie did not care about the difficult lives of these people. They were the conquering horde that had come to plunder and burn a peaceful city, so as far as she was concerned, they could all go to hell.","She only hoped that they would die sooner than she did.","That, however... could very well prove impossible.","Azarax and the remaining generals were not going to allow the Steel Horde to descend into a panic, after all. If the soldiers were terrified of the plague, they just needed to be reminded that their king was far more frightening.","It did not take Azarax a long time to restore discipline. After a round of vicious punishments and public executions, as well as a timely delivered, fearsome speech, order was restored — a semblance of it, at least. Indeed, the wrathful below of a Supreme was more frightening than a mystical plague.","And why wouldn't it be? If Azarax wanted to, he could wipe out every soldier of his army far faster than any plague could.","After he reminded his soldiers who they served, though, their fear had no choice but to turn into anger, and that anger had to be directed at someone.","So, while Azarax was busy conversing with his sorcerers to understand why the plague he had created was suddenly killing his own soldiers, the rank and file of the Steel Horde found a perfect target to pour their fear and anger on...","Naturally, it was Effie.","The witch who had brought the plague to their camp.","At that moment, no one had proof that it had indeed been her doing. However, an angry mob did not need proof to make someone its target... ironically enough, the warriors of the Steel Horde had stumbled onto truth in their blind search for a scapegoat.","Effie moved slowly as she saw a large crowd surrounding the circle of mud that had become her home in these past few... however long it had been. The soldiers were glaring at her with murderous hatred, murmuring something in perilous voices, their hands resting on the hilts of their swords. They were staying outside the range her chain allowed her to move... for now. But she could see that, today, they were serious about rending her to shreds.","When the soldiers tried to attack her before, they had never been that many of them. Usually, there was a handful... a dozen at most. That had already been the limit of what she could handle in her weakened state.","Now, though, there were hundreds of them. And their expressions were far darker and full of far greater malice than before.","Effie inhaled deeply.","‘Oops... it seems I'm in trouble.'"]},{"number":3134,"title":"Chapter 3134 Angry Mob","paragraphs":["Effie sighed and then pushed herself off the ground, where she had been lying in a fetal position. Her entire body was a sea of torment, and as she moved, a few of the sores hidden under the layer of mud broke, black blood seeping from them.","Leaning on the wooden post tiredly, she stretched her legs and stared at the crowd of soldiers expressionlessly.","‘They are really here to kill me, huh?’","But she wasn't ready to die yet. Despite everything, she still wanted to live... she wanted to live desperately, possibly more than even before.","Effie remained motionless for a few seconds, watching the soldiers working up the courage to lunge at her, and then smiled.","\"What, are you waiting for an invitation?\"","Her voice was creaky and weak, but they still heard her. Their eyes ignited with murderous fury.","But Effie only laughed.","“Bastards... you don't seem to understand the situation.\"","She leaned sideways and spat a mouthful of black blood into the mud.","“See that? That means that I am infected by the plague. I'll kill some of you... many of you... before the lucky ones manage to land a blow. But guess what? Even those who get lucky won't live long enough to enjoy their fortune, because they'll be infected by the plague, as well. Crowding around a carrier of a virulent disease is not the brightest idea, don't you think?\"","The soldiers paled. Those who stood in the front row tried to step back, but failed, pushed forward by those behind them instead.","Looking at their struggles, Effie grinned.","“But that is not even your real problem. Do you want to know what your real problem is, fools?\"","She fell silent for a few seconds, breathing laboriously, then offered in a hoarse voice:","“There must be three hundred of you in that crowd, at least. You morons. How many of the three hundred of you are already infected, do you think? How many will be infected by the time you are done dealing with me? Catching the plague from me is not even the real danger. Who you should really be afraid of... is the person standing next to you...\"","That made the warriors of the Steel Horde shudder. Before, they had been looking at her with murderous malice... but now, they were suddenly looking at the soldiers around them, distrust and deep, dreadful fear written on their faces. Effie could not help but chuckle.","That was what she wanted to see... that was what she was aiming for even above the deaths caused by the plague. Mutual distrust, fear, doubt, hesitation — this was the true pestilence that could destroy the Steel Horde.","After all, if Azarax's soldiers feared their fellow warriors more than they feared the adversary, how could they ever win a war? This was the rot that had to consume the Steel Horde from within.","That was why Effie smiled even as awful pain consumed her insides.","‘That's right. Look at each other. See? That one doesn't look so good. Why is he so pale? The one behind him is suspicious, as well. Is that dirt on his clothes, or blood? And the one staring at him from afar, doesn't he seem too gaunt all of a sudden?'","Her smile widened.","She was still smiling when a javelin shot from the crowd, ripping through the air at astonishing speed.","‘Uh-oh...’","At that moment, Effie realized that she might have committed a tactical error. She had missed the fact that scaring the soldiers by saying that those who approached her could become infected... might give them the bright idea of killing from a distance.","It seems these idiots were not as idiotic as she had assumed.","Effie's hands were shackled behind her back, and she couldn't really stand up because her tendons had been cut. She dealt with the previous attacks by using her legs and teeth, but dodging a javelin was a problem — especially because the person who had thrown it was obviously an Awakened, or possibly even a Master...","Or possibly even a Saint. There were plenty of them left in the Steel Horde, and while most weren't as powerful as the Dread Generals had been, that didn't mean that they were foolish or incompetent. Azarax wanted to keep Effie alive, but these officers might have had other ideas.","If someone here wasn't blinded by the same kind of unhinged lust for power as Azarax, they would see her clearly for what she was... a threat.","They wouldn't dare to kill her openly, but a large crown of angry and scared soldiers was a great cover for a bit of murder... as well as a perfect tool for it, if the unseen assailant used their cards right.","It would be quite difficult for Effie to dodge the javelin...","She still tried, though, awkwardly pushing her aching body to the side.","The javelin failed to deal her a deadly wound, but she had not been quick enough, either — it left a jagged wound on her side, dark blood soaking the dirty rags her red garments had turned into.","‘Argh...'","More pain... honestly, she couldn't even be bothered to register this source of it, by now.","The worst part was that whoever had thrown the javelin was not done yet — and their actions might have given the rest of the soldiers an idea.","Effie had successfully infected them with doubt and fear, but while the warriors of the Steel Horde were indecisive and fearful, they realized that they could allow themselves to feel these emotions after killing their source.","She could practically see the gears turning in their heads, their wary gazes turning more and more perilous.","An angry crowd was a scary thing.","‘If only I had my essence.'","Chained and surrounded by hundreds of angry men, all of them thirsting for her blood, Effie glanced at the warriors of the Steel Horde tiredly.","If she had essence, she could have snapped her chains and ripped off her collar. She could have called upon her powers and decimated these cowards. Hell, she could have assumed her Transcendent form and squished them like bugs under her feet. Sure, her insides were being consumed by the rotting plague, and she was alone... but she still could have killed them all and avenged herself on the Steel Horde.","But, well.","Dreams didn't always come true.","More often than not, only nightmares did."]},{"number":3135,"title":"Chapter 3135 Final Straw","paragraphs":["Effie sighed deeply, waiting for the brief moment of stillness to end. Once it did, she would probably turn into a pincushion... surviving that would be a challenge.","She could almost see when the hesitation in the eyes of the soldiers was replaced by malice and willingness to act. Even their fear of the plague was drowned out by bloodlust at that moment.","But just before the soldiers could snap, a low voice reverberated above the crowd:","\"Who the hell gave you mongrels the audacity to block the entrance to my tent?\"","And almost immediately, that bloodlust was replaced by terror.","The crowd of soldiers parted, revealing the imposing figure of Azarax, the King of Kings. He wore a dark, perilous expression, and his eyes were seething with barely contained rage.","When he noticed the javelin sticking from the mud near Effie, that scathing gaze turned even more terrifying.","In a voice that sounded almost like a growl, Azarax asked his soldiers:","\"Since when do I lead an army of cowards?\"","The soldiers had already been tense and wary, and his visible fury made them pale. Seeing this, all Effie could do was suppress a dark smile.","What was Azarax trying to say? That he encouraged them to try and kill her, but only in an honest and aboveboard way? Like attacking a bound and wounded woman with their hands, not ranged weapons.","In all honesty, he was being hypocritical. He had chained her in the middle of the camp precisely because he wanted his soldiers to attempt killing her — or hurting her, at least. However, he had only done that because he didn't really believe that they would be able to. What he wanted was to humiliate and torment his prisoner, grounding her spirit down, not lose his priceless trophy entirely.","But, ironically enough, at that moment, it was the spirits of his soldiers that seemed to crack. The hypocrisy of their tyrannical commander was the last drop that defeated their resolve, turning them from a crowd of seasoned murderers into a crowd of frightened, tired, starving men.","“Disperse! We are taking that damn castle today, so prepare to march!\"","As Azarax bellowed, the soldiers glanced at each other, hesitated for a moment, and then followed his command.","That brief moment of hesitation, however, would have never happened before. He noticed it, as well, his face darkening even further.","As the soldiers dispersed, he made his way toward Effie and silently jerked her upright. The radiant priestess of War was gone at that moment. Instead of her, a gaunt woman covered in dirt and dried blood was in front of him, her hair like a dirty rag, her face pale and sunken.","Her eyes, however, were still the same, even if they were clouded by pain.","Azarax snarled, then snapped her shackles with his bare hands and dragged her toward his tent.","“Unsightly... pathetic. At this rate, they will really kill you, priestess. We can't have that, though... no, that wouldn't be fun at all. Everything will be over too soon...\"","Inside the tent, he threw her roughly to the floor and took off a leather cord from his belt, tying her hands tightly. Effie thought that a piece of leather was much better than enchanted shackles, but her joy was short-lived — a moment later, the cord moved like a living being and tightened around her wrist, betraying its mystical nature.","At least her hands were bound in front of her, this time.","Azarax studied her for a few moments, then snarled.","\"Stay still if you want to live. I'll deal with you later.\"","With that, he stormed off from the tent. Effie was left alone.","And once she was left alone, resting on the lush carpet instead of cold mud, she finally had time to realize it...","That today, one way or another, it would all be over.","The siege might not end just yet. The fight her friends were fighting could continue for a while... but the ending of the Nightmare was going to be decided before the night fell.","And her part in all this would most likely be over, too.","When Azarax promised to deal with her later, he had not sounded too menacing... as far as a sadist whose hobby as of late had been torturing her could sound that way. However, it was only because he still failed to realize the magnitude of what she had done.","By the time he returned to the camp, numerous things would change.","Kai and the rest of her cohort only had to push a little bit more to make the defeat of the Steel Horde inevitable. Hopefully, they knew that as well. The Stone Castle had to withstand the assault — that way, the morale of the Steel Horde would be completely broken.","It would be even better if news of Jet attacking another convoy arrived at the same time. Hunger was quite a frightening thing as well, after all.","Hunger, disease, death, and war... the Steel Horde would soon learn to fear all four. Then, Azarax would not be able to deny the fact that salvaging the situation had become all but impossible.","He would soon find out that he was being consumed by the plague, as well. It would probably not kill him, but it would make killing him far easier. And when he realized all that... his anger would only have one way to escape. He could only vent it on Effie.","Lying on the opulent carpet covering the floor of his tent — plundered from some fallen palace, no doubt — she smiled weakly.","It would be quite ironic if he had saved her from a lynch mob, only to kill her with his own two hands on the same day.","There was a silver lining to all of it, though.","‘He'll only kill me if he completely loses control.'","And if he lost control, it would mean that his days were truly and utterly numbered. So, Effie's quiet smile turned into a grin.","‘Come back sooner, Azarax... come back quick. I am bored with this arrangement, as well...'"]},{"number":3136,"title":"Chapter 3136 Raised by Wolves","paragraphs":["Lying there without motion, Effie extended her senses inward and explored her body.","The mystical cord bound her hands tightly, and she felt like she wouldn't be able to rend it even if her strength returned. However, it was not enchanted to drain her, so her essence was trickling back little by little.","She was still in the negative, suffering from the symptoms of essence exhaustion, but that would change soon. Then, she would be able to use her Aspect again. Much more importantly, even before that, her flesh would be infused with essence once more, becoming stronger and more resilient.","That meant that she would be able to resist the plague better. That also meant that she would be able to recover from the wounds Azarax had dealt her, both internal and external, faster.","Effie's goal was to be able to stand by the time the Steel Horde returned from its assault on the Stone Castle. Then, even if she died, she would not have to die on her knees, at least.","Something so simple seemed like an insurmountable challenge now.","She sighed and concentrated on guiding her essence.","Time flowed, permeated by pain and anticipation.","After a while, drifting in the haze of half-consciousness, Effie heard screams and chilling wails rising like a wave from somewhere in the camp. She wondered what was happening, but couldn't quite bring herself to care.","Some time later, she thought she heard an echo of a distant, deafening roar penetrating the walls of the tent. She also heard the sounds of powerful explosions, and could smell a hint of smoke.","The air tasted like ash.","She didn't know the source of that smell, either.","Then, she was suddenly terribly cold.","By then, she still didn't have enough essence to summon even a single Memory. Her body was greedily drinking her essence, absorbing more and more of it — it was still far from being saturated, though. On the bright side, as a result, her wounds were healing faster.","Effie concentrated on controlling the flow of her essence, guiding it through the mangled channels permeating her body to the areas she wanted to be mended first. The essence veins themselves were being healed and straightened at the same time, too.","‘A little bit more... just a little bit more...’","She was still healing by the time the dim twilight of dusk swallowed the world, and Azarax entered the tent, smelling of blood and ash.","As he did, Effie caught a glimpse of the battered, shell-shocked soldiers. She heard a bit of their conversations, as well.","She had to suppress a laugh.","‘So that's why...’","Kai had indeed realized the importance of today's assault. Under his lead, the defenders of the Stone Castle — Nightwalker, Morgan, Seishan, and the rest of them — showed the Steel Horde hell.","Even better, Jet had not missed the chance to act. She was probably observing the situation with the help of her crow Echo, after all... only, this time, she did not choose to attack a supply caravan.","She wasn't somewhere far away, terrorizing the Steel Empire, either.","Instead, once Azarax and his warriors engaged the defenders of the castle inside the city, she infiltrated the encampment of the Steel Horde and attacked its supply stores directly, destroying what little provisions there were left.","So, now, the Steel Horde had failed to take the Stone Castle, was without food, and suffering from a swiftly spreading plague on top of that.","Azarax's expression was ugly.","He stared at Effie with a terrifying gaze, then reached down and pulled her roughly to her feet.","She could see it then, in his eyes, hidden behind murderous rage.","Azarax the Mighty, the Plague of Steel, the King of Kings... was rattled for the first time since she met him.","Staring at her furiously, he shook her violently and hissed:","“Was that your plan all along?!\"","Powerless in his iron grip, all Effie could do was smile.","“It was a good plan, wasn't it?\"","For a moment, there was astonishment in his eyes.","Then, he responded the only way he knew how — by slapping her with ferocious might.","Effie saw stars, her mind buzzing dazedly. However, Azarax was dazed more than she was.","Because, as she reeled from the blow, he was staring at his hand in shock.","His hand, which had struck her so roughly, was trembling.","Black blood was seeping from under his fingernails.","Slowly raising his gaze, Azarax looked at Effie and hissed:","“What did you do? What did you do, witch?!\"","Effie felt that a few of her teeth were dislodged, and her tongue was cut by the sharp shards.","Nevertheless, she tried to give him as brilliant a smile as she could muster.","Her answer was simple.","\"I killed you.\"","Azara looked utterly stunned for a moment. Then, something in his eyes unraveled, and he seemed to be completely consumed by fury.","He lowered his trembling hand, unsheathed a long dagger from his belt, and drove it into Effie's abdomen in one swift motion. As dark blood washed over his hand, she doubled over, blinded by pain.","A strange whine escaped from her lips, then gradually grew louder.","It seemed like she was groaning at first, but as Effie raised her head again, it became clear that she was laughing.","She was laughing out loud, her whole weak, mangled body trembling from laughter. Hearing her laugh seemed to daze Azarax all over again. He froze for a moment, then growled and stabbed her again, and again, and again...","He stabbed her until the sound of her laughter grew quiet.","Finally dropping the priestess to the floor, Azarax turned and staggered out of the tent.","Out there, in front of him, his warriors were returning to the camp, falling to the ground to rest after a strenuous, bitter assault. They looked tired, weak, hungry, sick...","Defeated.","Azarax's face paled.","Behind him, meanwhile...","The bound hands of the priestess moved, rising slowly and wrapping around the hilt of the dagger still protruding from her chest.","She pulled it out of her body slowly and then turned its blade around, bringing its sharp edge to rest against the leather cord that bound her wrists."]},{"number":3137,"title":"Chapter 3137 Plains of Elysium","paragraphs":["Effie did not feel too good.","But, at least, she was free.","A terrifying plague was devouring her from within, and a river of black blood was flowing from the brutal wounds delivered to her by Azarax. Effie felt like she was at the end of her rope.","But the rope that had bound her hands was now cut, and she managed to escape. Azarax had made a mistake when he left his dagger in her body. At first, Effie entertained the thought of turning its blade against him — the mighty King of Kings was distracted, after all, and had turned his back to her. One strike, and the Nightmare would be over...","Her mind was dim, and her thoughts moved slowly, but even in that foggy state, her sharp survival instinct told her that trying to kill Azarax was a fool's errand. She would never manage to bring him down — not in one strike, and not in her current state. Maybe when the plague had ravaged him more thoroughly, but not now.","So, Effie chose to escape instead.","Using the fact that Azarax was dazed and distracted, she crawled to the back of his palatial tent and used the dagger to cut its fabric.","Outside, the camp of the Steel Horde was like a disturbed anthill. The warriors returning from the city were pale and covered in soot. Those who had remained in camp were either dead or rattled. A whole swath of the encampment was completely destroyed and on fire, flames consuming what little was left of the Steel Horde's provisions.","That had to be Jet's doing.","The soldiers were running around trying to put out the flames, while some simply slumped on the ground in exhaustion. There were many wounded... and many of the wounded looked at their trembling hands in horror, dark blood seeping from beneath their bandages.","The air was thick with smoke and ash.","Effie used the chaos to make her way out of the camp.","In truth, she did not quite remember how she had managed to escape it. She seemed to have killed a few soldiers on the way, since the blade of the dagger she was still clutching in her hand was smeared with blood — red blood, not black, which meant that it wasn't her own.","But even if she had killed a few, the rest did not seem to have noticed her escape. Not immediately, at least... by now, they definitely had. Effie knew it because she was being pursued.","With her mind foggy, she couldn't quite understand where she was. She had found herself in a forest, surrounded by countless dead trees. The ground was barren, and the sun was setting, plunging the world into twilight. Effie leaned on a tree, breathing heavily, pressing one hand against her mangled torso.","But it was like trying to stem the flow of a river with a single stone. Azarax had not been miserly when stabbing her, so she received more wounds than what could be covered with one hand — the blood was still flowing, heavy drops falling into the black soil.","That wasn't ideal, since leaving a blood trail while being pursued seemed like a bad idea. And there was something weird going on, as well...","In the places where Effie's blood fell onto the barren soil, it seemed to bloom. Green grass, vines, and flowers sprouted from the earth, growing with astonishing speed. Even the dead trees nearby seemed to come to life, young buds swelling on their branches.","‘What... the hell is...'","Thoughts churned slowly in her head. She didn't understand what was happening, but was vaguely dismayed by it. A blood trail was already bad enough, and now there was an even more conspicuous trail of thriving greenery left in her wake. The forest was coming back to life wherever she passed, so one only had to follow the vivid green to find her.","And the pursuers, whoever they were, were already catching up. She could hear the sounds of movement in the distance.","Effie doubted that Azarax had chosen to pursue her personally — after all, he would have reached her in mere moments if he had. The King of Kings had to be busy trying to salvage the situation at the moment, reigning in the rattled Steel Horde.","Plus, he must have believed her to be as good as dead — if Effie was honest with herself, she would admit it, too — so the soldiers pursuing her were probably experienced trackers, seasoned veterans, and a Saint or two to make sure she would not escape.","Usually, she would have turned the situation around and made these hunters into her prey, but at the moment, Effie was not even sure that she could survive a few more minutes. Fighting seasoned warriors of the Steel Plague was out of the question.","And she still wanted to live... she was desperately resolved to survive, even if common sense dictated that she was too weak and compromised by the plague to survive her fatal wounds.","Who cared about common sense, anyway? Sense never survived collisions with reality when powerful Awakened were concerned, so Effie decided to ignore the glaring truth of her impending and inevitable death as well.","She groaned and pushed herself away from the tree, dropping the dagger and leaving a bloody handprint on it.","Step, step, another step...","With each one, more blood flowed from her wounds, and she felt a little weaker.","But she still took the next one, and the one after that, and the one after that, stumbling forward as the sounds of the pursuit grew louder behind her.","Something strange was happening to her faltering body, and to her tired soul as well. But Effie ignored it and focused only on what lay ahead, willing herself to keep walking even when all she could feel was the insurmountable imperative to fall and grow still.","Maybe the green saplings bursting from the ground were the result of her burning, overwhelming desire to live.","So, Effie continued to stumble forward, one agonizing step at a time.","Until there was nowhere left to go.","The forest disappeared abruptly, opening into a vast expanse of water. In the crimson glow of the blazing sunset, the water was painted vibrant red, glistening like a placid sea of freshly spilled blood.","Effie froze, a stifled laugh escaping from her lips.","‘...End of the road, I guess.'","She could not walk on water, and with the sounds of the pursuit right behind her, it seemed that her journey was coming to an end.","She still took a few steps forward, reaching the edge of the water, and stepped into it. The waves reached her knees soon, and she stumbled, falling.","‘Doesn't even make sense...’","Why was there a sea in front of her? It was supposed to be in the opposite direction, behind the burned city. Effie couldn't have gone that way, because that was where most of the Steel Horde had been returning from during her escape. So, she fled away from the city.","She pushed herself upright and sat in the cool water, staring numbly as her dark blood mixed with it. A belated realization arrived. This had to be the artificial lake Azarax had created to divert the river. It was quite scenic, considering its purpose.","Effie inhaled deeply and looked up, at the crimson sky.","Behind her, she could hear the sound of heavy boots striking the soil, as well as the sound of countless bowstrings being drawn. Her mind was empty, and somewhere beneath that emptiness, the cold and undeniable knowledge that she was about to die floated in the darkness.","The warriors of the Steel Horde let their arrows loose.","Effie was pretty tired. She was hurting horribly. Cold water washed her burning body, soothing her pain... so, for a moment, she thought that maybe it was alright, to lie down in the cold darkness and rest. Instead, she used what little essence she had regained and activated her Awakened Ability, turning her skin as hard as steel. The arrows bounced off it, some shattering into splinters. A couple managed to sink in, but even then, their tips didn't penetrate too deeply.","‘Penetrate too deeply, huh...’","Suddenly, Effie's lips twisted into a crooked smile.","‘To hell with this.'","Lying down to rest in the soothing cold darkness?","Who had time for that?","Effie had no patience for the peace offered by death. She did not need its solace.","So even while the plague was eating her from the inside and sharp arrows pierced her flesh, she decided to struggle a little more.","She was going to see how many of her pursuers she would be able to kill before they brought her down... no, why consider that? She was going to kill them all, so there was no need to count.","Suddenly, Effie remembered her Second Nightmare. She remembered the Temple of the Chalice, and the children she had trained side by side with, enduring the harsh cruelty of the War Maidens and the subtle insanity of the Kingdom of Hope together... until all of them were gone, and she alone remained.","Still struggling.","That was the path of War God, wasn't it? The eternal struggle of all living things — the struggle to stay alive, to live.","To thrive.","‘Oh, War...'","Effie groaned.","‘...rot forever in your grave, you damn god.’","She tried to push herself to her feet, but there was too little strength left in her body, so she barely managed to move.","She kept trying.","And as she did...","Something inside her seemed to reach critical mass.","Something seemed to have reached completion.","It rose, suffusing her entire being, overflowing like a wellspring.","And then, the Spell whispered into her ear.","[You have received an Aspect Legacy, Blessing of War.]","As Effie gasped, clutching her bleeding abdomen, the Spell continued to speak.","[You have received a fragment of Life's Domain.]","[Your soul has given birth to a lesser domain, Garden of Prosperity.]","[You have become the master of a Soul Garden.]","‘W—what?'","Flowing from beneath Effie's hand, her black blood suddenly grew brighter, gradually turning red.","And she finally felt the change that had been happening to her reaching its culmination.","Even if Effie could not see it at the moment, a profound transformation was happening within her soul. If she were to enter her Soul Sea, she would have witnessed the sea that rested under a clear blue sky, illuminated by the warm radiance of a brilliant sun, seething and roiling.","Then, something vast slowly rose from beneath the undulating waves — it was a great island, with tall mountains rising to the sky and clear rivers running along its plains and valleys. Green saplings sprouted from the rich soil, and the barren island was swiftly covered by forests, meadows, groves, and grasslands. Flowers bloomed, and the branches of the trees bent under the weight of ripening fruit.","The thriving abundance of this elysian island was brimming with exuberant and inexhaustible vitality, and that vitality infused Effie's entire being, clashing with the plague that consumed her in a vicious war.","'What... kind of nonsense is this?'","Effie wanted to laugh, but she couldn't because at that moment, more arrows fell on her, more than a few managing to pierce her skin.","She swayed, feeling more blood flowing down her body.","If only she could stand up... then...","Her essence was almost consumed now, and even if her newly unsealed Aspect Legacy had strengthened her, she would still lose the ability to use her Aspect soon.","Once that happened, those arrows would kill her all the same.","But before Effie could run out of essence, she suddenly felt terribly cold.","An icy mist obscured the shore of the lake, hiding her from the eyes of the archers. Terrified screams resounded from the mist, muffled by its cold embrace.","Effie exhaled slowly and finally allowed herself to fall.","Just before she plunged into the water, though, someone caught her.","She looked up, at the icy blue eyes looking down at her from the darkness.","Effie sighed.","\"Big Sister... I feel like crap.\"","Jet, who was holding her, nodded silently.","“You look like crap.\"","Effie tried to chuckle and grimaced instead.","“There's a garden... blooming in my soul... a soul garden...\"","Jet frowned.","\"You appear to be delirious. That's fine, but do try to get a grip. At least until we get out of here.\"","Cradled in her arms, Effie looked up and grinned.","\"Get a grip, huh? What do you want me to grip, exactly?\"","Tracing her gaze, Jet scoffed.","\"Looks like she's doing alright, after all. Good... now, let's run...\""]},{"number":3138,"title":"Chapter 3138 A Moveable Feast","paragraphs":["Time flowed, its slow and steady current eroding both hope and sorrow in equal measure.","The sky was bright, then dark, then bright again.","Its distant veil was blackened by smoke, then cleansed by the purifying fury of rolling stormclouds.","Inside the destroyed city, only the most stubborn cinders still glowed, hidden deep below the ruins.","Outside the city, a vast encampment of the conquering army rested under the ashen sky, drowned by a suffocating atmosphere of suffering, confusion, and fear.","When there was sun, there was dust. When there was rain, there was mud. The tents were dirty, damp, and battered. The people were covered in grime and soot, their grim eyes slowly turning lifeless.","The soldiers were hungry. Hunger was a nightmare that haunted their waking days, stalking them persistently wherever they went, whatever they did. It sunk its fangs into their flesh, sapping them of strength and tormenting them. It also gnawed on their minds, eroding their willpower. Hunger was not the only nightmare haunting the Steel Horde, either.","A vicious plague was preying on the soldiers, stealing their lives away. It was like an invisible monster that walked among them, unseen and silent, marking its victims and feasting on their flesh. There was no way to ward off the man-eating monster and no way to fight it. Once you were marked, all you could do was die.","The agony of those infected by the plague was gruesome. Their deaths were hideous. Long before they could experience the torment of being eaten alive by the plague, however, most perished to cold steel — the King of Kings had commanded to cull the infected, so countless were executed as soon as they started showing symptoms, their bodies burned in communal pyres.","The stench of burned flesh was inescapable. Even worse than the plague, however, was the fear of the plague. The fear was far more virulent than the disease itself, and often just as deadly. The plague only affected some of the soldiers, but the terror of infection affected all of them. A gnawing paranoia made the warriors of the Steel Horde wary of each other, turning their already bleak reality into an oppressive purgatory of suspicion and mistrust.","And on top of the hunger, the plague, the fear...","Was the mounting pressure of a long and brutal siege.","The Steel Horde had already been bruised and battered by the countless assaults on the stalwart city. Then, the Dread Warriors — the most fearsome legion of the horde — were entirely wiped out. And even now that hunger and disease were ravaging the remaining soldiers, the King of Kings was still throwing them at the walls of the Stone Castle over and over again.","To burn in the flames of the fearsome dragon protecting the ruins of the fallen city.","To drown in the river of severing steel that encircled the castle like a moat.","To vanish forever in the billowing clouds of chilling mist, their very souls devoured by the sinister wraith that haunted the ruins.","To see rivers of blood flowing from every little cut they received, sapping them of life in a matter of moments.","To be torn apart when space itself twisted and rippled around them.","Despite the fury of the King of Kings, his soldiers had failed to take the Stone Castle time after time.","So, now, all they could do was crawl tiredly into their dirty tents, enduring the hunger and shivering from the cold, praying that these shivers were not a symptom of the encroaching plague.","Waiting for the next battle to claim their lives.","The camp of the Steel Horde was consumed by fear, fatigue, and exhaustion. It was grey and silent, permeated by the stench of burning corpses.","At the same time, an entirely different scene was taking place not too far away, across the blackened expanse of the burned city.","A radiant island sprawled under an azure sky. Warm wind caressed the leaves of tall trees, making them sway and rustle. Clear brooks murmured as they flowed toward the gentle sea, permeating the air with a refreshing coolness. Everywhere one could look, the world was vibrant and full of life. The branches brimmed with fruit, the bushes were full of sweet berries.","Flowers bloomed on green meadows, emanating a soothing fragrance...","And among it all, the clear ringing of children laughing could be heard, spreading far and wide.","There were people populating the island. Most of them were either old or very young. They looked gaunt, but color was already returning to their faces. The elderly gathered to talk, rest, and prepare simple meals from the gifts of the island. The children ran around, played, or splashed in the clear brooks.","The island was entirely safe. There were no predators here, and no enemies either. Food was delicious and plentiful, and clean water was abundant.","This was the Garden of Prosperity, and the people it sheltered were the remaining population of the city — all of them except for the warriors who defended the Stone Castle from the faltering Steel Horde. However, the warriors benefited from the gifts of the Soul Garden, as well, since both the fruit and the water could be harvested and carried out into the outer world.","‘Feels weird.'","Sprawled on a soft bed in the Stone Castle, still too weak to fight and recovering from her grievous wounds, Effie stared at the ceiling.","It was a strange thing, to know that there were thousands of people currently residing inside of her — and yet, that was precisely the case.","The Garden of Prosperity — her lesser domain — could be described concisely with just a couple of sentences. It was a physical space residing within her soul. Her Soul Sea had become a miniature mortal realm.","That realm was the size of a large island at the moment, but if she became Supreme, it would most likely expand to the size of a continent.","Additionally, the fragment of the Life Domain she had inherited fused into that land, infusing it with boundless vitality. Effie could visit her Soul Garden and enjoy its gifts. She could also admit people inside or summon them back.","It was a miniature paradise she carried within herself."]},{"number":3139,"title":"Chapter 3139 Effie is Coming, Shut the Gates!","paragraphs":["The reality of the situation was not entirely unfamiliar to Effie, since it resembled how her Supreme Memory, the Black Beast Locket, functioned — albeit on a far grander scale. The space within the locket was artificial, but the Soul Garden was entirely real... it just existed inside her soul.","What did it mean for Effie?","In the future, it meant that she would be able to shelter an entire nation inside herself.","‘Would that make me... like, a Great Citadel?’","There would be Bastion, Ravenheart, the Night Garden, NQSC... and Effie?","‘I do have some outstanding Components, if I do say so myself...'","She suppressed a giggle, knowing that it would hurt like hell.","On top of everything, residing in her Soul Garden would be much safer than living anywhere else in the Dream Realm, since no ordinary Nightmare Creature could get in.","‘So, what? One day, some guy would be asked where he's from, and he'll say — oh, I'm from Effie!'","Her expression became strange.","Effie remained silent for a few moments, then shook her head and sent a succulent grape into her mouth.","Alternatively, she would be able to carry an entire army, no different from the Steel Horde, within herself, and deploy it anywhere at a moment's notice.","So, people would scream:","\"There, on the horizon! Effie is coming, shut the gates!\"","She grimaced.","In any case, that was for the future.","At present, the reality of the Soul Garden served a far clearer purpose. It was basically a cheat in the time of a siege, supplying both the population of the Stone Castle and its defenders with an inexhaustible source of food and water. Even the royal family, which had forgotten the taste of luxury over the long siege, was enjoying abundance once more — and the people were, as well.","To be honest, Effie's plan had already been based on outlasting the Steel Horde. It was just that, initially, she had expected a bitter contest of endurance, with both sides suffering from thirst and starvation. The defenders were supposed to come out victorious in that contest due to possessing a vital advantage — due to the fact that Seishan of Clan Song, the heir of Beast God, was on their side.","In the end, however, it had turned out that the survivors of the fallen city possessed two vital advantages instead of one. They also had Effie and her Soul Garden, which solved all of their remaining problems except for one — the fighting itself.","But even then, a starving soldier could not compare to a soldier who fought on a full stomach. So their advantage shone during the battles for the walls of the Stone Castle, as well.","The strongest elites of the Steel Horde were gone, while Azarax himself was weakened by the plague. Additionally, with the number of his warriors diminishing day after day and the confidence in the King of Kings plummeting, his Domain was growing weaker as well. Even the great Steel Empire behind him was stirring in unrest, his authority over it slowly becoming tenuous.","If Azarax was less prideful, he would have retreated from the walls of the city, returned to his empire, and consolidated his rule. Then, he could return with fresh forces in a few years, finishing what he had started. In fact, that was what most of his remaining generals, who had families and things to lose back home, wanted.","But Azarax was the epitome of a Supreme — an individual so determined and obstinate that the world itself had no choice but to bend to his will. And he was an especially tyrannical one, at that, so his pride was absolute. He refused to admit defeat, or even tolerate a temporary setback that could be perceived as such... so, the Steel Horde remained locked in a bloody siege. Effie had a feeling that it would not last much longer, though.","Soon enough, one of the sides would reach its breaking point. There was a chance that it would be the Mason King and his people... but if Effie had to bet, she would bet against the Steel Horde.","Not that it mattered to her, at the moment, because she was on medical leave.","She might have survived the weeks of torture, the brutal burden of the plague, and being stabbed by an enraged Supreme. But it was not like she had miraculously recovered to full strength. Her body was still a wreck, and even with the Garden of Prosperity blooming in her soul, it was recovering slowly. The damage that had been dealt to it was simply too severe.","So, all there was to do was relax on a soft bed and savor delicious fruit.","The fruit was delicious...","‘But I sort of miss meat.'","She would have to go about getting some animals into her soul once she got out of the Nightmare. Did it sound weird? Probably, but Effie didn't care.","‘Some fish, as well.’","Actually, was there already fish in her Soul Garden? She hadn't explored it that much, so she wasn't sure. She seemed to see bees and other small critters there already, and she thought she had heard birds. Where had they come from? Effie had no idea.","Maybe they had come as a part of Life's Domain, or at least were born from it.","‘Isn't Earth War God's realm, though?’","She was a little confused.","As Effie enjoyed another grape, the door to her spacious chamber opened, and Kai walked in, bringing with him the smell of soot and ash. His face was grim and cold, but when he saw Effie, it was illuminated by a smile.","\"You look better already. How do you feel?\"","Not long after Kai arrived, Morgan stopped by as well. Seishan brought a deck of cards. Jet appeared, as if attracted by the smell of fruit.","Well, and when that many beautiful women gathered in one place, Nightwalker was bound to show up.","Effie's bed resting session had somehow devolved into a war council. She sighed.","‘Well... it isn't bad.'","Not too long ago, their meetings had been permeated by the suffocating atmosphere of anxiety and grim anticipation. Now, the mood felt almost... light. There were even chuckles and an occasional bout of laughter.","Observing her friends, Effie sighed again and ate another grape.","‘Well, that's food for you.'","The world seemed like a brighter place on a full stomach...","A few days later, a different war council took place across the ruined city, in the camp of the Steel Horde. Only this one was not graced by the sounds of laughter — instead, it was somber and tense, full of unspoken truths and boiling resentment.","That meeting was destined to decide the outcome of the long siege."]},{"number":3140,"title":"Chapter 3140 Dangerous Tools","paragraphs":["In the heart of the vast encampment, a grand tent stood, surrounded by an open space. Tall mounds of human skulls, which had once belonged to the enemy soldiers, surrounded it like morbid decorations. Inside, the tent was adorned with horns and antlers of terrifying beasts the King of Kings had slain, and a grave silence suffused the air.","Azarax the Mighty, the Plague of Steel, was seated on an imposing throne cut from rough stone. Below him were the commanders of the numerous legions of the Steel Horde — those who still lived, at least. Dozens of Transcendent champions and a scattering of Ascended stood along the walls of the tent, their expressions grim and reserved.","Usually, there would scarcely be any Ascended invited to the war council, but with so many generals having died in the siege or contracted the plague, those who were below them had to assume command over the battered troops.","The positions closest to the King of Kings, where the seven Dread Generals had usually stood, were conspicuously empty.","In fact, this gathering was different from the previous ones, because there was a wide open space between Azarax and his officers, isolating him like a hollow moat.","That space was there because Azarax, too, was infected by the plague.","The merciless conqueror was still fearsome and mighty, his imposing figure instilling terror in the hearts of his subordinates, but he was also diminished. His posture was crooked, his complexion was deathly pale, and there were traces of black blood left in the corners of his mouth, under his fingernails, and below his nostrils.","In fact, blood continued to seep, filling the tent with the smell of iron.","The Plague of Steel, being consumed by the plague of blood... there was something both frightening and ironically poetic about that, making the gathered commanders feel a hint of sacred fear. It was as if the gods themselves were punishing their king. There were whispers across the camp, in fact, saying that the King of Kings had angered one god in particular — War God, the god of life, as well as of victory and conquest.","That was why a seemingly insignificant city had managed to resist Azarax for so long, and that was why the unstoppable conquest of the Steel Horde had come to a crushing halt.","That was why the soldiers of the horde had been punished by a deadly plague, and so many of them had perished in the jaws of war.","Of course, no one dared to say these things loudly, since doing so would get them killed. However, the fact that people dared to whisper was already telling. Before, the soldiers would have never been bold enough to voice their discontent, knowing to keep it to themselves.","But how could they remain silent now?","The Stone Castle still stood, the King of Kings was stricken by the plague, and more and more of them were dying every day. More than that, those most loyal to Azarax — his thralls — were all dead. The Dread Generals were gone, and their legion was gone with them. Other core forces of the Steel Horde had been wiped out or were severely diminished, as well.","Although their numbers had not been great enough to put a dent in the endless ranks of the Steel Horde, the horde itself was changed in their absence. That was because the Dread Warriors and other elite legions that had perished the day the city burned represented the core of the Steel Empire — the lands Azarax inherited from the father he had killed, and which therefore were his first conquest.","Most of the soldiers that remained hailed from the realms he had conquered later. Some realms had been a part of the Steel Empire for a few generations, while some had been swallowed by it only recently. The greatest champions of the fallen kingdoms had been chosen by the King of Kings, defeated by him in personal combat, and became his thralls... they were all dead now.","But not all talented warriors had been enthralled. Some had been judged too weak to receive the recognition of the King of Kings, while some had been born or risen to prominence after the conquest. Some simply did not strike his fancy due to their background or character.","They were the ones who eventually came to lead the lesser legions of the Steel Horde, and they were the ones who stood today in the great tent, having outlived their supposed betters.","Needless to say, their loyalty to Azarax was not as indomitable as that of the thralls and those elites who hailed from the core of the Steel Empire.","For many, it was simply predicated on the fact that his power was insurmountable, and going against him meant death for them, their families, and their people. Many were loyal due to a sense of honor and the weight of given oaths, but their devotion was not absolute.","And just like everything else about the Steel Horde, that devotion had been slowly eroding under the weight of mounting casualties, the plague, and their king's wrathful folly.","\"My king...\"","One of the generals spoke, his voice low and full of resigned caution.","“The soldiers are tired. The provisions delivered by the minor caravans are not enough to feed everyone... our people are hungry, and hunger has stolen their strength away. Many have perished to the plague, and more still are dying in battle.\"","He paused for a moment and threw a brief glance at a tall Transcendent man who stood silently among the generals, leaning on a spear. That man was younger than most people in the tent, with a reserved expression and a calm, heavy gaze. He was one of the strongest warriors left in the Steel Horde, as well as a descendant of a royal family from one of the conquered realms.","While not known for his martial feats, the man was steady and astute, famous among the lesser legions for having the lowest number of casualties among his soldiers. He spoke rarely, but his words were always measured. Therefore, they carried weight. The general sighed and added, turning his gaze back to the bent figure of Azarax.","\"This cannot continue, my king. It must not. We must return home and replenish our forces. Most of all, we must find a cure for the plague... the siege cannot continue until we do.\"","Azarax, who was leaning on the handrest of his throne, threw a dark gaze at him and remained silent for a while. The force of his oppressive presence grew even more unbearable, making the Transcendent generals pale and those who were Ascended struggle to breathe.","Eventually, Azarax spoke in a low, chilling tone:","“Since when do I rule cowards?\"","The general pursed his lips, hiding all traces of dismay from his eyes.","Azarax shifted slightly, forcing a sore that had scabbed over to tear and spill blood. His already grim expression turned a shade darker, making the generals shiver.","\"Since when do my officers think that they can give me commands?\"","He leaned forward a little, looking at the general who had spoken with dark intensity.","“Are you trying to challenge my authority, worm?\"","The general flinched and shook his head.","\"No! No, my king. It was not a command... it was council.\"","Azarax grinned and then grimaced, spitting a mouthful of blood. His voice sounded hoarse and menacing when he spoke:","\"Council? I see... so you feel qualified to give me council now. I assume others share this coward's opinion?\"","The generals glanced at each other, trying to hide their tension. In truth, they did — almost all of them were reluctant to continue the siege. Some were frightened by the plague, some were incensed after seeing their soldiers dying in senseless assaults. Some wanted to return home, where growing unrest threatened their families, status, and lands.","Some merely saw no reason to continue fighting, since the city had already been burned, and there was little left to plunder there even if they won. With only the castle still standing, most of them were not going to see a reward after taking it.","So, they all wanted the same thing. They wanted to convince Azarax to abandon the siege... it was just that none of them dared to speak. The one who had was already a brave enough fool, since their king was not known for patience. He was not known for being merciful to those who defied him, either, so the courageous messenger risked being killed on the spot.","Azarax let out a chuckle.","\"Listen to me, wretches. I am Azarax the Mighty, the Plague of Steel, the King of Kings! I have never been defeated, and I have never failed to take what is rightfully mine, either. This city won't be any different. The siege will continue. The blood will continue to flow.\"","A frightening smile split his dark, pale face apart.","“It will continue to flow until the Stone Castle is taken apart stone by stone, all the people sheltered behind its walls are burned alive, and the Mason King dies by my hand! I will sever his head, fashion it into a cup, and use it to drink wine at the countless feasts to come. Then, people will laugh and say — look! This was a fool who had dared to defy Azarax, the King.\"","He took a laborious breath.","“This is my will! You... all of you... are nothing but tools I use to carry it out. So think long and think hard about what you say next. What use do I have for tools that fail to serve their purpose?\"","An uneasy silence settled among the generals as they glanced at him.","In front of them, the mighty figure of Azarax was just as menacing as ever... but also changed. He sat crookedly on his stone throne, leaning on the handrest. Although his eyes burned with frightening intensity, his face was pale and gaunt. Black blood trickled from his mouth, dampening his beard, and there was a feverish, sickly glint to his skin.","His breathing was ragged.","So many people had died from the plague... but Azarax didn't. He wasn't going to, either. Mere mortals might be devoured by the ghastly disease, but his mighty body would eventually devour it instead. Days would pass, or maybe weeks, and he would return to his former glory. Many of them would be dead by then, or perhaps all of them.","But the King of Kings would persist. He would be alive when their grandchildren grew frail from old age, and when time turned their bones to dust, as well. That was the nature of a demigod — and not just any demigod, at that. Because Azarax was a Supreme who had defeated and slain countless others like him.","How could a creature like that understand them?","How could they persuade him to understand?","Shivering, full of dismay and resentment, the generals glanced at each other.","What could they say? What arguments could they conjure up? What words could they use to make their terrifying king listen?","Eventually, the gazes of many settled on the quiet Saint who stood among them, leaning on a spear. He was known for being insightful, calm under pressure, and using his words wisely, after all. So, they hoped that he would show them the way.","And he did.","The quiet general studied Azarax with a concerned, heavy gaze for a while, as if weighing something in his mind. Then, he seemed to come to a decision and stepped forward. He didn't use words, however.","He used his spear instead."]},{"number":3141,"title":"Chapter 3141 Fate of a Tyrant","paragraphs":["A morning came when Effie was called back to the wall.","This time, however, it was not to defend it. Using a crutch, she limped her way across the castle with Jet. The halls and courtyards weren't crowded anymore, at least — the citizens who had found shelter inside were now safely protected in her Soul Garden, enjoying all its gifts. So, she did not have to carefully make her way through the mass of people.","Still, Effie could not help but grumble.","“Ugh... who made this crutch? It's so shoddy. Feels like it is disintegrating a little with each step.\"","Jet gave her a look.","“Be thankful, fool. Do you think it's easy to make a crutch in a besieged castle? There are no trees around, in case you didn't notice. Plus, people of your height are not exactly common.\"","She paused for a moment and then added:","\"The royals offered to make one from stone, while Morgan had the bright idea of making one from steel. In the end, Nightwalker disassembled a bunch of priceless antique furniture to fashion this thing. In the real world, you could buy a city block with that.\"","Effie gave her crutch another look.","“A whole city block?\"","Jet smiled faintly.","“Well, the world is ending. So real estate prices are suddenly very affordable.\"","Chuckling, they ascended the wall and pushed their way through the crowd of soldiers standing on the battlements in silence. Everyone was here — even those who had ended their shifts and were supposed to be resting.","All of them were looking across the burned city in a strange, transfixed silence.","The castle stood on elevated ground, so they could see past the city wall from here. As Effie and Jet made their way to where Kai, Morgan, Seishan, and Nightwalker stood, they looked into the distance too. Laughter died on their lips, and they found themselves drawn into the silence.","‘Ah...’","The sun was rising, its rays spilling over the horizon. They illuminated the blackened ruins of the city, the crumbling wall, the terrifying killing field below it... and there, beyond the killing field, in the distance, the vast encampment of the Steel Horde.","At this time, it would usually look like an ocean of shimmering light, with countless fires burning in the dim twilight of the early dawn. However, today, the siege camp was dark and quiet, with only pillars of smoke rising above it here and there.","Mundane people could not see, but Saints like Effie were able to discern more. Kai, meanwhile, saw it all.","Even without his magical eyes, though, she could tell at once glance what had happened.","Effie felt her breath turning slow and haggard. A sudden weakness permeated her body.","The Steel Horde... was gone.","Sometime during the night, the warriors of the King of Kings had abandoned the camp, retreating the way they came. They took what they could with them, but left countless tents and weapons behind. Many of them were dead, after all, and those who survived had a long and arduous march in front of them.","If they truly did retreat, of course.","Effie slowly turned to Morgan, struggling to find words.","In the end, she just asked in a hesitant tone:","“We won't find a big horse statue there, will we?\"","Morgan lingered for a moment, then shrugged.","\"There's only one way to find out.\"","The other members of the cohort nodded solemnly.","It took some time to organize a sortie. Only the strongest of the defenders were allowed to go, since the encampment of the Steel Horde was still infested by the plague. Seishan was with them, but it was better to be safe than sorry — so, nobody below the Ascended Rank left the castle.","Effie went, too, hoping that her precious crutch would survive the journey.","They passed the blackened streets of the destroyed city. As they traveled, Effie remembered various scenes from her time here. There was the restaurant she had often gone to, back when the city still had supplies. There, a square where she had once watched children enjoy a puppet show, missing her family. There, a street she had often used to travel from the castle to the wall.","All of it was gone now, turned into ash and cinders.","As they neared the wall, there were more memories. Rushing soldiers, endless battles, the joy of those who survived, the sorrow of those who had outlived their loved ones... countless scars, countless wounds.","The wounds had healed, and the scars had disappeared as well. But the memories remained.","The wall remained as well, even if it was crumbling. Effie felt that the only thing keeping it upright was the will of its builder, the Mason. But the old man was dying now... once he was gone, the wall would probably succumb as well. Then, the city she had come to know would be truly and utterly gone.","Finally, they crossed the killing field.","The last time Effie had walked across it, she had been on her way to surrender to Azarax. That had probably been the darkest day of her tumultuous time in this Nightmare. Only a few weeks had passed, and she was coming back... however, the circumstances were entirely different now.","Soon, Effie and the rest of the scouring force entered the eerily empty camp.","The tents still stood, but the soldiers were gone. Winds blew as they scattered smoke across the desolate expanse of the abandoned camp. Weapons and equipment lay discarded in the dirt, piles of rubbish littering the mud. Here and there, an unbearable stench emanated from the tents.","Lifting the fold of one of them, Effie grimaced and covered her nose. There, a decomposing corpse lay, wrapped in a blanket, bearing the familiar and ghastly signs of having died from the plague.","No one seemed to have bothered with collecting and burning the dead. The retreating soldiers had enough mercy to kill those infected who were still alive, at least, instead of leaving them to the slow and agonizing death from the plague.","It didn't make sense.","Why would the Steel Horde just leave? Had Azarax truly decided to retreat to save his remaining forces? Effie could not quite imagine him admitting defeat. She had always expected to fight one final, decisive battle against him... even if they did not manage to slay the King of Kings himself, they could at least destroy his army, ending the Nightmare that way.","But the Steel Horde was simply gone. There was no sign of Azarax, either. All that remained was silence and desolation, which made Effie feel a sense of eerie, confused unease.","The scouts spread throughout the camp, investigating the mysterious absence of people. Effie wandered it for a while, as well, looking around in confusion. The eerie sense of incongruity grew, but she also felt a powerful, overwhelming sense of relief.","Her enemy was gone, after all. The terrifying army that had been besieging the city for two years had retreated. It was almost unfamiliar not to feel the weight of the Steel Horde pressing down on her... but it was not unwelcome. Quite the opposite.","Finally, they found the answer to the question that had been plaguing their minds ever since they entered the camp. It was hidden in the great tent at the heart of the encampment, where Azarax and his generals used to hold council.","The tent was empty, as well, but the stench of blood was far more powerful here. There were puddles of it on the floor, which had almost, but not quite, dried — as if many people had died here recently.","There were no corpses... except one.","There, on the throne that towered above the vast expanse of the tent, a plague-ridden corpse sat, staring down at the uninvited guests with glassy eyes. Azarax was nearly unrecognizable.","The plague had changed him, somewhat, but it was more so because of the traumatic damage done to his body.","He was impaled through the chest with a spear, pinned to the backrest of the stone throne, with dozens of arrows and javelins striking out of his flesh. Every part of his body that had not been pierced had been hacked and torn apart by sharp blades, as if hundreds upon hundreds of blows descended upon him in quick succession, delivered by scores of hands.","All of him was painted black by the plague-ridden blood, making him look like a ghastly effigy of a human made from tar and mangled flesh.","He must have resisted fiercely after being struck for the first time... it had taken hundreds of blows to bring the fearsome Azarax down, and even then, Effie was not sure how many of his attackers had survived their mutinous ambush.","But in the end, he still died. Azarax the Mighty, the Plague of Steel, the King of Kings... had been weakened by the plague of his own making and slain by his own generals, becoming the greatest and final victim of the Steel Horde.","It was a fitting end for a bloody tyrant like him.","In fact, Effie thought that it was better than he had deserved.","‘I hope you die a thousand deaths, bastard.'","She inhaled deeply, remembering all the pain and humiliation she had endured at his hand.","The years of a bitter siege and all the soldiers she had lost to his ambition, as well. All the civilians who had perished because of him.","Reality was far more cruel than Effie, though.","Instead of dying a thousand deaths, Azarax had been robbed of the right to die, spending thousands of years nailed to a tree in a godforsaken desert before succumbing to the curse of Shadow God.","She used to think that such a fate was a bit too gruesome...","But now, Effie was glad for it. That much torment... was enough to make up for one-tenth of the sorrow he had caused, perhaps.","Looking at the imposing, monstrous corpse that sat on a bloodied throne, she inhaled deeply, and then let out a long sigh.","‘Goodbye, Azarax. You called yourself the King of Kings... but you died like a dog. A fate most fitting.'","Their Nightmare seemed to be coming to an end."]},{"number":3142,"title":"Chapter 3142 Far Away","paragraphs":["A few days later, Effie found herself standing on the shore of the sea. In front of her, the people of the fallen city, who had left the safe harbor of her Soul Garden, were busy working. Some were clearing the bay, some were salvaging the wrecked ship that had been pulled from its depths.","Their work was hard, but they seemed cheerful enough. Haunted and unnaturally quiet, yes, but nevertheless full of vitality. And, most of all, undeniably alive.","The gaunt bodies had filled up somewhat, and they did not look like walking corpses anymore. The quiet despair had also disappeared from their eyes, replaced by tranquility... hope, even.","With anticipation of a brighter future.","Effie quite liked the sight.","There was activity boiling throughout the city, as well. However, it did not look like the citizens were trying to clear away the rubble. Instead, they were simply searching for anything that had survived the fire and could be of use.","Soon enough, the other members of the cohort joined her to observe them.","Effie raised an eyebrow.","\"Where's the prince?\"","The prince had called them out here to discuss something, but now, he was nowhere to be seen.","Kai remained silent for a moment, then sighed.","“His father had taken a turn for the worse. So, the prince is with him.\"","Effie lingered a bit before nodding. She turned back to the sea.","Despite everything that had happened in the past two years, the sea was clear and beautiful beyond the harbor. It stretched toward the horizon, glistening in the sun, its waves murmuring steadily, like they always did.","She let out a heavy breath.","\"Did he mention what their plans are? Are they going to rebuild the city?\"","Jet, who had approached quietly, shook her head.","“The prince said that the city — what remains of it — is a place of death and sorrow now. To them, it is a graveyard. So, they are planning to build ships and sail somewhere else... somewhere far from conquest and war, somewhere far away. To start anew.\"","Looking at the sea, Effie smiled.","\"Well, I can't say I blame them. It must feel nice to have somewhere else to go.”","Back in the real world, there was nowhere far away from war. War was everywhere. That didn't mean that humanity couldn't start anew, though.","Turning to her friends and companions, Effie studied them for a few moments.","\"I guess this is it, then. We won.\"","The others nodded in confirmation, even if their expression betrayed a hint of bewilderment.","Nightwalker shook his head.","“It's astonishing, really. I thought at least half of you would die... if any of us survived at all.”","Seishan smiled.","\"Unlike you, most of us have no experience dying over and over again, so we thought we'd pass.\"","Morgan simply shrugged.","\"I don't know what you are talking about, either. Look at us. Great Clan Valor, Great Clan Song, Great Clan Night... the best and the brightest of the Forgotten Shore, the most fearsome soldier of the government — if the six of us couldn't conquer the Nightmare, then who could?\"","She paused for a moment, then looked to the sea and sighed.","“Although... I feel that this is it. There probably won't be new Supremes for a long, long while after us.\"","This one Nightmare had already gathered the best of what humanity had to offer. The next generations, if they would get to be born, were not going to experience a world as terrifying as the one the six of them had been raised and tempered by. New champions might rise from among the descendants of humanity eventually, but it would take a long time.","Jet studied them for a moment, then smiled.","\"Still. We did well, didn't we?\"","Effie could not help but agree. Leaning on her crutch, she grinned.","“I'd say.\"","With that, they fell into a relaxed, exhausted, peaceful silence.","There was not going to be a lot of peace after they returned to the real world, so they had to enjoy this precious moment as much as they could.","Soon, a strange, imperceptible change rippled through the world. It was as if the weight of the sky had changed, and the scent of the air had become a little colder. As if something old had come to an end, and something new was beginning.","A few moments later, a deafening, roaring crash resounded from the distance. Turning to look across the blackened ruin of the burned city, Effie and her companions saw the impregnable wall they had defended bitterly for two years crumbling into a cloud of dust. It collapsed entirely across its length, pulled down by its own battered weight and erased from existence. They all knew what that meant. Somewhere nearby, within the walls of the Stone Castle, its creator had finally breathed his last breath.","The Mason King had endured long enough to see his people to safety... but now, he was dead.","Effie looked at the beautiful walls of the distant castle, considering.","They had met two Supremes in this Nightmare, which couldn't have been more different from each other. In many senses, the Mason and Azarax were opposites of each other, both representing distinct extremes.","Azarax was powerful and ambitious, proud, and impossible to ignore. An epitome of a tyrant.","The Mason, on the contrary, was quiet and unassuming, so much so that his presence was almost imperceptible at times. He had not been a powerful warrior, but created beauty and prosperity wherever he went.","Effie was not sure which of them would have fared better in the Age of the Nightmare Spell, where abominations and dreadful perils besieged humanity on all sides... but she knew that she wanted to be a Supreme like the Mason. She wanted to inspire and protect her people instead of using them as fuel for her own benefit.","She smiled.","‘Rest well, old man.‘","With that, the beautiful view of the Stone Castle, contrasted sharply against the blackened ruins behind it, suddenly grew vague and indistinct.","Effie inhaled deeply, breathing in the bitter air of this forgotten city for the final time.","Their Nightmare had come to an end."]},{"number":3143,"title":"Chapter 3143 Coronation","paragraphs":["Sunny had survived the expedition to the Underworld... and even if it was just barely, he had not returned from the journey empty-handed. The Weave was finally complete, Saint was a Supreme Tyrant now, the shadow of the Prince of Darkness rested in his soul, and a legion of fearsome shades joined the Shadow Legion.","However, the spoils of the expedition were overshadowed by its heavy implications. Sunny and Nephis had always known that they were no match for the fallen gods of the Dream Realm — the Unholy Nightmare Creatures who were its true masters. At least not yet. But facing one in battle, if their brief encounter with the Abyssal Prisoner could even be called that, put just how inadequate they were into perspective. There was only one conclusion — they had even less time to augment their strength than they had thought. That lit a fire under them, forcing them to accelerate their preparations for the Nightmare even further.","The plan had been to wait until Jet, Kai, Effie, and the rest attained Supremacy before departing, so that humanity could persist in their care. Now, however, Sunny and Nephis could not help but consider an earlier, and therefore much more dire, date. There were still many things they had to do before leaving in search of the Fifth Seed. Their plans of finding a place to harvest mystical stone in the Underworld had failed, for example, which meant that an alternative source had to be discovered. The apocalypse had not stopped on account of their busy schedule, either.","Humanity was besieged on all sides. In the Dream Realm, countless Citadels were struggling under an onslaught of abominations, while some had already been lost. The waking world, meanwhile, was slowly descending into a global crisis. All lands controlled by humanity were under threat.","Still... the next few months felt almost peaceful. Knowing that challenging the Fifth Nightmare would mean nearing the end of this terrifying race, Sunny felt like he needed to enjoy these last days of humanity.","Not of mankind, but rather, of the humanity he himself possessed. He was not sure how Apotheosis would change him, after all, but knew that he would not be the same after becoming a deity.","It was a strange thing, to know that he would not be human for much longer.","In truth, it was more than a little scary... almost as scary as death. More so, perhaps, since Sunny had died on several occasions and still remained himself. A transformation so profound that your previous self would seem a stranger felt far more frightening.","Would he still enjoy drinking coffee? Would he be able to become engrossed in a novel? Would he know how to treasure the touch of soft fabric and the refreshing feeling of a warm bath?","...Would he have any kind of human emotions left at all? Would he still experience the joy of spending time with friends, the tender attachment to his sister?","Sunny did not know, and the unknown frightened him.","It terrified him, really.","And yet, there was no other path but the path forward. None of these things would be there much longer if he failed to conquer Apotheosis, anyway... so, there was no point in hesitating.","The apocalypse continued.","Even as Sunny and Nephis frenetically prepared for the Nightmare, alarming news arrived from all corners of the world.","On the Forgotten Shore, the Shadow Legion was pushing back the Barrow Wraith under Saint's command... however, something was stirring in the depths of the Burning Forest, and even the primeval hunters seemed ill at ease now.","In the east, the eerie darkness continued to spread, swallowing more and more land. In the west, calamitous snowstorms were rolling from the frigid wasteland, bringing with them swarms of Nightmare Creatures. In the south, leviathans who had spent thousands of years in the lightless depths were now rising to the surface, as if chased by something.","On Earth, Nightmare Gates were opening almost every day now, and the abominations escaping from them were stronger. The mystical interference caused by the Call was wreaking havoc across all three remaining Quadrants, disrupting industry and infrastructure. More pieces of the waking world were being swallowed by the Dream Realm, allowing Nightmare Creatures to bypass the Gates.","Resettlement wasn't progressing fast enough.","Even with how strong humanity had become — with the Fire Keepers, the Blood Sisters, the River People — it was slowly losing ground.","Sunny knew that he and Nephis had no choice but to challenge the Nightmare. But, at the same time...","He didn't know if anything would be left by the time they returned.","The fact made him feel indignant.","It was already unfair to be born into a world like this one. But to strain against it for so long, achieving one unlikely victory after another, to accomplish so much and come so far... only to end up losing everything, after all?","That left a bitter taste in his mouth.","Just like that, in the blink of an eye — but also an eternity — time passed. The winter solstice was swiftly approaching, which meant that Effie, Kai, Jet, Morgan, Seishan, and Nightwalker had been gone for almost two years now.","The memories they had left behind were still intact, but there was no news of their fate.","Sunny and Nephis had almost steeled themselves for departing without learning what had happened to their friends...","But then, one day, the world shuddered.","It was as if an invisible ripple spread through the fabric of reality, changing it forever.","There was a remote monitoring station left in Antarctica, keeping watch over the three colossal Nightmare Gates towering above the vast battlefield. The signal barely reached the relays, though, so it was not very reliable. In theory, if one of the Gates disappeared, they were meant to learn about it almost immediately...","In practice, however, Sunny and Nephis knew that something had happened because the Longing Domain suddenly and inexplicably weakened.","The six Saints who had challenged the Fourth Nightmare had released control of the Citadels before delving into the Seed, but they were still widely renowned and venerated figures. So, their simultaneous rise to Supremacy had taken a big bite out of Neph's Domain.","At first, she and Sunny assumed that something terrible had happened — an unexpected calamity that had wiped out a great number of people in an instant, maybe, or some other emergency.","They scrambled to react, but before they could even leave the Ivory Tower, Cassie's voice resounded in their heads, informing them of the real reason the world seemed to have shaken.","The truth, for once, was not alarming.","It was astonishingly joyous, instead.","On that day, six of the greatest champions of humanity had conquered the Fourth Nightmare and became Supreme.","The world welcomed new Sovereigns — and this time, their arrival was met with exhilaration instead of bloodshed and fear."]},{"number":3144,"title":"Chapter 3144 The Gathering of Demigods","paragraphs":["On a day unlike any other in the history of mankind, the Ivory Island descended from the sky and landed on the misty waters of the Stormsea. It had traveled far from its usual place above the Mirror Lake, moving halfway between Bastion and the rapidly growing city in the delta of the River of Tears.","Silver Web, the city of the River People, was not too far either. So was the Night Garden, moving among the waves like a towering wall on the horizon.","Two smaller ships could be seen, as well, sailing across the sky — they were the Chain Breaker and the Time Slayer, the storied vessels capable of braving the heavens. These ships were bringing exalted guests to the Tower of Hope. Today, the great pagoda was meant to serve as a meeting place for the demigods of humanity, so no mere mortal would find themselves under its roof.","The meeting had taken some time to arrange, but it was happening mere days after the new Sovereigns conquered their Nightmare. They had received time to reunite with their families and explore their new powers, albeit just barely.","Now, the demigods had to make arrangements among themselves, deciding which lands would be ruled by whom, how they would share the burdens of protecting humanity, how they would divide it among themselves so that their authorities did not clash.","How they would stave off the apocalypse until true deities were born from their ranks.","The vast meeting chamber was bathed in light, with a large wooden table occupying most of its great width.","The host of the meeting, the current ruler of humanity, entered first. With her alabaster skin and silver hair, sparks of white flame dancing in her eyes, she looked like a radiant spirit of light — a messenger sent by the heavens down to the mortal world. Her gaze was steadfast and heavy, though, giving her radiance a stark and awe-inspiring edge.","She was Changing Star, Nephis of Immortal Flame.","Next was her companion, a being so fearsome that even his existence was a forbidden secret. An exquisitely beautiful man with porcelain skin, raven-black hair, and eyes that were like onyx jewels rose from her shadow. It was as if a sea of darkness was given form. There was something serpentine about his elegant movements, and the shadows across the chamber grew deeper as he appeared.","He was Sunless, Lost from Light — the Lord of Shadows.","The third to arrive was the dreaded King of Nothing, Mordret of Nowhere. He came out of reflections, gazing upon the world with his strange, mirror-like eyes. The world reflected in them was the perfect copy of itself, and yet eerily different. Wearing an aloof expression, the King of Nothing spared his peers a curt nod in greeting and took a seat in silence.","A petite woman wearing a white tunic and a seawave cloak entered next, her delicate beauty so stunningly breathtaking that it escaped description. Her hair was like a waterfall of pale gold, and her eyes were hidden behind a blindfold. There was an air of solemn mystery about her, and her presence was easily forgotten.","She was Cassia, Song of the Fallen, the blind prophet who had broken fate.","Next came a young woman with tantalizing features, wearing a nebulous black mantle. She had an elegant figure and glistening ebony hair, her skin dusky, her eyes piercing blue. Illuminating the world with a captivating smile, she bowed gracefully to the others and took her seat, greeting them in a melodious voice.","She was Ananke, the Silk Weaver, the sorceress who ruled the River People and the Twilight Sea.","Not long after Ananke took her seat, finally, the new Supremes arrived.","The first to enter was a fetching man who looked younger than the others gathered in the chamber, but was actually older than all of them instead. He had strange, nebulous silver eyes that seemed to gleam with distant starlight, flawless dark skin, and a dashing smile.","When he appeared, a cold breeze seemed to blow from the sea, bringing with it the smell of salt, distant lands, and wanderlust.","He was Nightwalker, the last legend of the First Generation, and the founder of the House of Night. As for a regal title... he had only been Supreme for a few days, so people had not had the chance to come up with one yet.","Following Nightwalker, a woman of exotic and riveting beauty entered, her dress a darkly crimson hue. Her supple skin was grey like stormy clouds, smooth like silk, and devoid of any imperfections. That gave her an exotic and tantalizing, but outwardly inhuman look.","She was poised, reserved, graceful, and exquisite, like the embodiment of nobility and regal elegance. Her inhuman beauty was of the kind that put both longing and fear in a person's heart, and when she entered, everyone who looked at her felt soothed and at ease.","That ease, however, hid a darker side — it was the ease of prey bewitched into lowering its guard by a predator.","She was Seishan, the Lost Princess of Song, the most tenacious daughter of the Queen of Worms.","Following the princess of fallen Song, the princess of fallen Valor arrived. She was a striking woman with dark wavy hair and alabaster skin, her eyes as cold as the sharpest of swords. More arresting than their sharpness, however, was their vibrant color — they were as red as freshly spilled blood, the same as her scarlet lips.","With her pale skin, raven-black hair, and austere elegance, she looked both beautiful and daunting. When she entered, the world was suddenly permeated by a lethal sense of clarity and sharpness... unlike before, however, that sharpness did not radiate outward. Instead, it was reserved and focused inward, making it seem that she could cut the world with one graceful movement of her finger.","She was Morgan of Valor, the Princess of War... although now that she had become Supreme, calling her a queen would likely be more appropriate.","A man so handsome that his beauty could become a deadly weapon entered next, following Morgan closely. With auburn hair and sparks glinting in his green eyes, he greeted everyone with a radiant smile. Even demigods could not resist the devastating force of that smile — some responded with their own before knowing what they were doing, some looked away with strained expressions.","His presence was light and effervescent, but also carried a hint of melancholy, making every emotion seem more poignant and precious. His voice was pleasant and impossible to ignore, as well, making them want to listen to it forever.","He was Kai, also known as Nightingale — the Dragonslayer.","Soon after his radiant smile seemed to warm the world, a sense of chill permeated the air. A woman of ravishing beauty entered the chamber, her icy blue eyes glowing with cold light in the shadows of the doorway. Her figure was riveting, her flawless skin was smooth and white as snow, and her raven-black hair was cut short.","She carried herself with a relaxed grace, and her subtle presence filled the chamber with the feeling of otherworldly cold. Despite its subtlety, however, she was impossible to look away from.","She was Jet, the Soul Reaper — a woman who was neither dead nor alive, and who inspired fear and reverence in equal measure.","Finally, a tall woman with a stunning, alluring figure entered the chamber. She was tall and athletic, with perfectly defined, lean muscles rolling under her dewy olive skin and an air of infectious vitality about her. Everything about her screamed of strength and vigor, and it was hard not to feel your blood flowing faster in her presence.","That alluring presence filled the air with liveliness and energy, causing a certain primal intensity to permeate her surroundings, infusing them with stimulating, spirited force. Now that she was Supreme, that energy had only become stronger, threatening to feel overwhelming. She was Athena, Raised by Wolves, known by many as War Beast.","Since the others were already seated, Effie looked around with a confused expression, lingered for a few moments, and then asked:","“What? There are no snacks?\"","Sunny sighed deeply and covered his face with a palm.","There was not one, not two, not three, but eleven — eleven! — Supremes in the room. More than there had ever been, and for once, they were not at each other's throats. Instead, by some miracle, they had all gathered together to discuss how they were going to coexist peacefully.","Sunny groaned inwardly and mumbled:","“Still, it's too many Sovereigns, damn it...\"","Then, he looked at Effie, glared at her for a couple of moments, and said:","“Of course there will be snacks! Who do you take me for?\""]},{"number":3145,"title":"Chapter 3145 New Supremes","paragraphs":["There were a lot of things to discuss, so the meeting was going to take a long time. It could even stretch over several days, considering that Sunny, Nephis, and the other three Supremes who had stayed behind did not even know the details of the Nightmare the rest conquered.","Those who returned were not fully familiar with their new powers, either. A lot of the decisions that needed to be made depended on that knowledge, so Sunny expected to spend some time helping the new Sovereigns make sense of their Supremacy.","‘What a novel idea.’","Sunny and Nephis had to figure out the powers of a Supreme all on their own, relying only on each other in exploring the nuances of the Will and Domain powers. Well, naturally they had — after all, they had ascended to Supremacy by killing their predecessors. So, there had been no one left to teach them.","These new Supremes, however, could enjoy the benefit of having more experienced comrades show them the way. They would have to do a lot of work on their own, naturally, but it was still a starkly different situation.","‘Must be nice.'","Sunny was not bitter at all.","Just as he expected, the meeting ended up consuming several days, and in the process, all of them learned more about what the new demigods could do. Needless to say, their Supreme powers were both extremely potent and, in several cases, exceedingly peculiar.","There was also a lot of confusion because to them, those born in the Age of the Nightmare Spell, the power of a Domain carried an innate duality.","There were two ways a Supreme could build a Domain — one natural, one provided by the Spell, with the latter overshadowing the former in most cases. So, finding the true mechanism of spreading one's authority far and wide wasn't even important for some of the new Supremes.","Still, it couldn't hurt to know.","The most straightforward power among the six new Supremes belonged to Nightwalker, and even that one was weird as hell. His Aspect Abilities had been enhanced across the board, with a couple standing out among the rest. His already fearsome Transcendent form, that of a cosmic starbeast, had grown numerous times greater — as if that giant creature had been merely a whelp before.","He had also become capable of manipulating space at a greater scale — and, more importantly, of twisting it permanently. That alone was a tremendous boon, since it allowed many others to enjoy the benefits of Nightwalker's Aspect freely. He could make a road that allowed people to traverse a week's worth of distance in just a day or two, for example — with some effort, but forever.","What else could he do with that versatile power? Only time could tell. Sunny could not help but imagine a network of teleportation platforms that would connect distant corners of the immensely vast Dream Realm one day in the future, though. Instant teleportation seemed like an unreachable goal, but then again, the Demon of Repose had been able to create the Night Garden.","Who was to say that, given time, Nightwalker would not be able to accomplish something similar?","His Domain would have to grow quite powerful for that, probably. And speaking of his Domain, the natural path to expanding it was somewhat unexpected — at least to Sunny, whose view of Supremes was twisted by the few examples he had.","Apart from conquering Citadels, Ki Song had expanded her Domain by creating puppets. Anvil expanded his by forging swords and bestowing them upon loyal warriors — Sunny was still unsure if the swords had been the core of the Domain, or the people wielding them.","Cassie's Domain consisted of those she remembered, while his own consisted of shadows of those he had killed. Neph's Longing Domain, meanwhile, consisted of people she had inspired to strive for something they longed to achieve.","Nightwalker's Domain had nothing to do with people, though, or any kind of living beings. It was land. He could expand his Domain by laying claim to land... but only land that had not been claimed before.","In other words, without the Spell, he would have had to dedicate his life to journeying and exploration, always striving to find the next frontier. Only that would allow his Domain to grow, and his people to flourish... the problem, naturally, was that all easily conquered lands in the Dream Realm had already been claimed, and all that remained was a collection of unexplored, increasingly harrowing hells.","Still, knowing Nightwalker, Sunny could imagine him having a swell time traveling to exotic, distant hells and meeting exciting, unusual eldritch horrors one day in the future.","What mattered now, however, was that he would be able to use the Components of the Night Garden better as a Supreme. With Nightwalker at the helm, the living ship would be able to serve as a connection between various cities of humanity even if it ceased to be a part of the Longing Domain.","Seishan's new powers were also quite straightforward. Just like the rest of the Supremes, all her Aspect Abilities had grown more potent or evolved. The core of her Supreme power, however, was founded in her unique Transcendent Ability, which allowed her to transform others instead of herself.","The surviving Handmaidens of the Bright Castle had been infused with her blood, thus undergoing the empowering transformation and becoming known as the Blood Sisters. Now, however, the power granted to them by Seishan's augmentation had grown tremendously, and they also gained access to lesser versions of her other Aspect Abilities — especially the ability to grow even stronger by spilling blood.","That was not all there was to it, though. The most far-reaching change in Seishan's powers was that the people she had granted the Blood Blessing could, in turn, bestow it upon others now. There was a hierarchical structure to the spread of her power, with each next generation of those chosen receiving a weaker version of it, but seemingly no limit.","None they had discovered yet, at least. For all Sunny knew, there could be seven possible degrees of separation to this Blood Blessing — or even some random number of them, like sixteen.","Naturally, Seishan could expand her Domain naturally by bestowing her Blood Blessing to chosen champions, and having those champions spread it further. The more people they took into the fold, the more spirit essence she would draw from them, and the more fearsome her Will would become. Blessing someone took a toll on Seishan, though, so she couldn't transform crowds of people...","But that was where the Spell could help. She could also expand her Domain greatly by controlling Citadels — in fact, that was a far easier and more efficient path. Nothing prevented her from doing both at the same time, either.","Everything seemed great on paper... it was just that those who received Seishan's blessing did not only inherit a lesser version of her powers, but also, seemingly, a fraction of her Flaw. In the grand scheme of things, though, that wasn't a big problem. Sunny was sure that nothing awful would come of it.","Next was Morgan, whose Supreme power had turned out to be the most versatile. Apart from her Aspect Abilities receiving an overall enhancement, she gained a deep affinity to runes and runic sorcery.","Her Ascended Ability had evolved in an astonishing way, as well.","Before, Morgan had been able to copy a number of enchantments and store them in her body, making her capable of adapting to almost any situation. Now, not only had this Ability become more expansive, but it had also transformed in quite an astounding manner.","Simply put, it allowed her to copy the enchantments stored in her body onto other living beings. There was a limit to how many enchantments a person could accommodate, and of what power — but if she wanted, she could greatly enhance the power of any human below the Supreme Rank.","A mundane person could accommodate an enchantment of the Dormant Rank, an Awakened person could accommodate two enchantments — one of the Dormant Rank, one of the Awakened Rank — and so on. Which meant that she could make mundane humans almost strong enough to contend with Awakened, and make Awakened capable of facing Fallen abominations on somewhat equal footing. The only limit was her imagination, the enchantments available to her, and the competence of the charmed person.","Those carrying her enchantments willingly would become members of her Domain, so she could only enchant beings below the Supreme Rank...","She could place her enchantments on her enemies as well, though, making her Supreme power a bit more sinister. And while doing so, if her Will was sharp enough, she could carve her sorcery into Nightmare Creatures of any Rank, not just those weaker than her. That would not make them her subjects, but could certainly help her kill them.","That was a potent and versatile power that could both assist Morgan in battle and benefit innumerable humans greatly. The only thing Sunny was not entirely clear on was what, exactly, Morgan's source element was. In the end, they tentatively theorized that it was... swordsmanship. Or rather, any kind of martial craft taken to an extreme.","That made a peculiar kind of sense. Morgan had been meant to become a weapon for her father to wield, but in her defiance, she became a sword that wielded herself instead. A sword sharp enough to cut the world.","So, while anyone could receive her enchantments, those who dedicated themselves to overcoming their nature and striving for the heights of martial arts answered to them better. They could draw more power out of them, and Morgan received more spirit essence in response as well.","Sunny could imagine her being called the Sword Queen in the future... which sounded almost like the title of her father, but was actually the opposite. Anvil had looked down on all people, chillingly regarding them as weapons to be used. Morgan, however, had the power to arm her subjects and help them pursue their lives with greater passion, reaching greater heights.","...Sunny found it a bit weird, though, that there were two Supremes who had come from the Valor family.","As far as he was concerned, Anvil was the epitome of an awful father. But both of his children had become Supreme, so if anyone unfamiliar with the King of Swords heard about the dynamic sibling duo — the King of Nothing and the Sword Queen — they'd probably assume that Anvil had been the greatest dad in history, setting the golden standard of parenting goals for all eternity.","That was a concerning thought.","But not as concerning as the fact that there was now a whole continent inside of Effie..."]},{"number":3146,"title":"Chapter 3146 Great and Wondrous Powers","paragraphs":["Effie's Aspect Legacy had granted her a fragment of Life's Domain — which was not a fragment of Earth, interestingly enough — and helped her soul give birth to a lesser domain of her own, the Soul Garden, which was a domain of thriving and prosperity. Then, the fragment of the Divine Domain fused with her Soul Garden, imbuing it with exuberant, mystical vitality.","And when Effie attained Supremacy, her Aspect Abilities growing more potent or evolving, her lesser domain evolved as well. Now, there was nothing lesser about it anymore — it expanded, becoming the size of a continent. It was just that her Domain was located in her Soul Sea, not in the Dream Realm or the waking world.","As for her Supreme power, it was rather straightforward. It shared the augmentation of her Dormant and Awakened Abilities with all her subjects, albeit in a diminished capacity — similar to how her Ascended Ability functioned before for those of her warriors who saw her during a battle.","Now, however, the effect of her Ascended Ability was greatly enhanced for members of her Domain, making it far more profound and potent.","Those who resided and thrived in her Domain would naturally become its subjects. That actually was a great boon for the Human Domain as a whole, since far more people would be able to abandon the dying Earth now — it was as if humanity had suddenly gained a new Great Citadel. It was unclear just how large a population Effie's Domain could sustain yet, but it had to be substantial.","Effie was in a strange position, though, because her Aspect Legacy had suddenly interfered in the natural progression of her Aspect. It was quite possible that there would not have been a Soul Garden without it, and therefore, Effie would have possessed a different source element and would be able to naturally expand her Domain in a different manner.","In fact, it was quite possible that she still could, which would mean that she possessed a dual source element. They suspected that one of them was nurture and prosperity, while the other was warfare — the kind of warfare meant to protect what her Domain nurtured, that was.","So, it could very well be that those warriors who were inspired by her on the battlefield could also become a part of her Domain, even if they did not make their home in her Soul Garden.","That inner realm needed a name better than \"the Soul Garden\", by the way... and everyone unanimously agreed to forbid Effie from naming it herself. Otherwise, one of the most vital sanctuaries of humanity would have ended up being called something like \"the Big Pantry\", \"Effie's Huge Soul Food Vault\", or \"Snack Quadrant\", which would not be great for morale.","...Sunny thought that Effie's Huge Soul Food Vault was a pretty good name, actually, but for some reason, everyone had ignored his opinion.","Then there were Kai and Jet, whose Supreme powers were the strangest — which was not to say that they were weak. On the contrary, they were quite fearsome. Especially Jet's, whose power was probably the strangest and most frightening of them all.","Kai's source elements seemed to be... songs. Which was a bit confusing, considering that his Domain could not really be called the Song Domain, for obvious reasons. In any case, his Supreme power was a word. Kai was able to leave that word on a living being's soul as a mark... or a brand... thus making them a member of his Domain.","That could be done voluntarily or involuntarily, although Kai, of course, would never resort to the latter — even if it made it easier for him to bend those affected to his will, therefore opening an easier path to great power. The former, meanwhile, was more difficult to accomplish, since it demanded a certain quality from the person being infused with his Word.","Perhaps it was a natural affinity, or maybe simply talent. The point was, different people could draw different benefits from becoming a member of Kai's Domain.","The fundamental benefit they received was being able to share in Kai's Ascended Ability, which allowed him to reshape the world with his voice. Most people were incapable of achieving anything with that power, though — only those with the right predisposition could achieve more, even if it could not compare to the frightening extent of Kai's own Ability.","However, for whatever reason... that only worked when they sang. Simply speaking had no effect whatsoever, and coincidentally, people with musical and artistic inclinations had a better chance of being receptive to the Word and becoming powerful chanters.","Those especially talented could receive other boons, as well. Some chanters inherited enhanced vision from Kai's Awakened Ability. Some could even gain the ability to fly, although there were very few of those.","And to make things even weirder, the statement that most people could not achieve anything while chanting was only partially true. Yes, an average person would not be able to do much after becoming a member of Kai's Domain. But... for whatever reason... that was only true if they chanted alone.","If a large group of people did it together, though, their ineffective efforts fused, producing a powerful effect — the larger the choir, the more pronounced the changes. Sunny could not even find words to describe how bizarre that Domain and that Supreme power were.","He could somewhat accept an image of a talented singer augmenting their cohort with a good song, or disturbing the minds of their enemies with a terrible one.","However, imagining a whole army singing as they went into battle, and becoming stronger for it — that was a bit too much for him. Why couldn't people just get augmentations in the normal, natural way? Like being wrapped in living shadows, wreathed in radiant flames of someone's soul, or staring at the lavish figure of a hundred-meter-tall woman?","Actually, now that Effie was a Supreme, her Transcendent form would probably be taller than a hundred meters. Nightwalker's, Morgan's, and Kai's forms had become far greater, after all. Seishan's ability to transform people had grown more potent, while Jet could now turn into a far more voluminous wraith if she so wished. So, Effie would not be an exception either.","And speaking of Jet...","Her Supreme power was one all of them were still struggling to wrap their heads around. In fact, it remained largely unexplored, since it could only be truly uncovered in battle.","A few things were already clear, though. The most startling of them... was that Jet could not generate spirit essence. And, therefore, she did not really possess a Domain, either.","Instead, her titanic, shattered Soul Core served as a substitute for a Domain, its sheer size adding incredible weight to the tyranny of her Will. The larger it grew, the more potent her spirit became — and it had grown tremendously already.","Jet's Aspect Abilities must have grown more potent or evolved in some ways, as well. But without an army of Nightmare Creatures on the Ivory Island to test them, there was no way to truly find out how.","The only exception was her Transformation Ability, the change in which was evident enough, and her Awakened Ability — the one responsible for her being known as Soul Reaper, since it allowed her to attack the souls of living beings directly.","Now, however, it seemed to have changed in a mysterious way, allowing Jet to attack the spirit of her enemy, as well. Not only was she able to directly weaken the Will of her opponents, but she had become generally resistant to its effects, all but ignoring them at times.","Needless to say, that made her a harrowing enemy for those who had attained a high Rank and relied on the Will to defend themselves and destroy their foes. Just like even Saints were wary of Jet in the era when Supremes were merely a rumor, now, those of the Supreme and Great Ranks... as well as those above... had a reason to be scared of her, as well.","Jet was neither dead nor alive, but she was certainly a natural killer.","As for her source element, it was soul. There was no surprise there, albeit quite a lot of irony.","Observing the six new Sovereigns, Sunny could not help but sigh.","Such great and wondrous powers... but was it going to be enough?","He had a feeling that even if it were, it would be just barely."]},{"number":3147,"title":"Chapter 3147 Three Tasks","paragraphs":["Having more or less determined the general scope of everyone's powers, albeit not in a detailed fashion, the eleven demigods could finally discuss the grave matter of humanity's survival from an informed position.","There were countless minute decisions they had to make — minute only in the grand scope of the apocalypse, of course. In truth, each of these issues could decide the fate of thousands, if not millions of people. Put all together, these minor choices could decide the fate of all humanity, as well.","Luckily, the eleven Supremes did not have to figure out every little detail — like the precise deployment of troops, the timing of each resettlement effort, the resource allocation for the refugees, and so on — themselves. They simply had to decide the general direction in which they wanted to move and entrust the rest to their subordinates, who were far more competent in the infinitely complex task of managing the day-to-day function of humanity.","There was also the fact that planning anything in too much detail was simply meaningless, since the situation across both worlds was highly unstable and changing unpredictably every day. So, the best anyone could do was prepare for the highest possible number of eventualities and pray that the worst projected scenarios would not come to pass.","Even if, deep down, that was pretty much exactly what everyone was expecting to happen.","If one disregarded this infinite number of minor decisions, though, it all boiled down to three profound choices.","The Supremes of humanity had to accomplish three global tasks.","Someone had to conquer the Fifth Nightmare. Someone had to keep the Dream Realm from being consumed by an endless tide of Nightmare Creatures. And, finally, someone had to make sure that billions of people did not perish while the waking world was falling apart.","So, the most important decision facing them was just that — they had to decide who would undertake each of the three tasks.","It was obvious that Sunny and Nephis would challenge the Nightmare. They were the most experienced Supremes among the rulers of humanity, after all, as well as the strongest. However, it was unclear if they would enter the Seed alone or in the company of trustworthy allies.","Sunny had somewhat expected Mordret to volunteer — he had mentioned considering doing just that, after all. In addition, although the Mordret of today was not the same as the Mordret of yesterday, he still wielded a Divine Aspect. Among the Sovereigns, only he could claim to be as powerful as Sunny and Nephis were.","The guy avoided committing to an answer, though, either still hesitating or preferring not to share his decision. This new Mordret was a strange guy... Sunny received an impression that he did not care whether humanity survived too much, extending his help only out of courtesy. Mordret had isolated himself from the rest of the world, maintaining contact with just a few select people, like Morgan, Rain, or Cassie.","He wasn't as invested in the apocalypse as the rest of them. However, it was precisely because Mordret still seemed to care about at least one person — his sister — that Sunny felt like he could very well choose the Nightmare, in the end.","While Mordret abstained from voicing an opinion, someone else surprised them, though.","It was Cassie, expressing her intent to challenge the Fifth Nightmare with them. She spoke the words in a steadfast tone, as if having made the decision a long time ago.","Sunny had a feeling that she might want to follow them into the Seed, but then again, Cassie had an established role in the vast machine of humanity. Many things depended on her, so her absence would be felt almost as much as that of Nephis.","For that reason, he had assumed that she would choose to stay.","Sunny was not sure how he felt about being proven wrong. On one hand, there was a sense of joy in his heart... relief, even. Cassie was their closest friend and confidant, after all — a companion unlike any other. Many years ago, it had all started with the three of them enduring the dire trials of the Forgotten Shore.","There was no need to mention how powerful and useful to have around Cassie was, either. In a battle, she might not have been the most fearsome of the Supremes, but her profound affinity to revelations had saved them almost as many times as cold steel. Her Aspect and Domain were also exceedingly unique, making her a priceless ally.","But it was precisely because of how deep the bond between them ran that Sunny felt uneasy and reluctant at the thought of Cassie joining them in the Nightmare. All Nightmares were deadly, after all, and the Fifth one promised to be more harrowing than the rest of them. Sunny knew that he might never return from it... but the thought of Cassie perishing in the depths of a Nightmare cut him deeper.","It was easy to risk your own life, after all. Putting the lives of those you cherished at risk, though? That was a far more bitter pill to swallow.","In the end, however, there was nothing he could do — not that he would, anyway. Cassie was a Supreme now, same as Sunny, so he could not dictate her decisions. He had no ground to stand on, and no desire to refuse her help either.","So, on that day, it was decided that the three of them — Changing Star, Lost from Light, and Song of the Fallen — would enter the Seed of a Fifth Nightmare and attempt to become the new deities of humanity. With the decision made, many plans had to be adjusted. The other Sovereigns had already come to terms with the thought that Sunny and Nephis would be absent for a long time — years, most likely, and judging by how long the others had spent in the Fourth Nightmare, it might not be only a couple of years either. Now, they had to contend with the fact that Cassie would be gone as well.","Without her, a lot of things would change. At any other time, the news that Song of the Fallen would disappear for an unknown number of years would have caused a shockwave among the people who depended on her knowledge, insight, and mental communication to survive. However, today, it was almost a footnote — because a far more staggering change was about to occur.","The Longing Domain, which had served as the supporting pillar of humanity in the dire years of the early apocalypse, would soon cease to exist."]},{"number":3148,"title":"Chapter 3148 Division of Power","paragraphs":["There was no way to avoid it, since Nephis had to make space to allow other Supremes to establish their Domains. More importantly, it was almost a given that she would not be able to assist her subjects from the depths of the Nightmare — so, clinging to her throne served no purpose. And lastly, there was the simple fact that no matter how their attempt to conquer the Fifth Nightmare ended, the Longing Domain would disappear anyway.","If Nephis perished in the Nightmare, there would be no more Changing Star to govern the sea of frail flames burning in the hearts of humanity. If she succeeded, though, she would not be a Sovereign anymore — she would be a Spirit. And Spirits did not govern Domains... not in the same way Supremes did, at least.","As a matter of fact, neither Sunny nor Nephis knew what exactly would happen to their Domains after the Apotheosis. However, they knew that a deity was meant to be one with his or her source element, not merely controlling a construct made with the help of it.","Perhaps they would still be able to exert influence over their Domains — or over what had once been their Domains, rather. Perhaps the scope of their influence would even increase. However, its nature would definitely change, and neither of them knew how.","They knew, however, that Spirits existed on a plane above the Supremes, and were not concerned with expressing their authority. Although Sunny and Nephis did not know what Apotheosis would mean for them, they did know what their absence, as well as the absence of the Longing Domain, would mean for the warriors of humanity. There would be no miraculous flames to heal their wounds and save their lives anymore. There would be no radiance to shine from beneath their skin and make them stronger. Some of them had grown accustomed to the caring support of their goddess, but now that support would be gone.","Apart from that, the nature of the relationship between mundane people and the Nightmare Spell would change, as well. At the moment, humans who resided in the Dream Realm had two ways of challenging the First Nightmare — they could either leave the confines of the Longing Domain or relay their desire to become Awakened to Nephis, thus prompting her to withdraw her protection and allow the seeds of Corruption hidden in their hearts to bloom.","The latter was an unreliable method, since Nephis could not pay attention to each of the billions of sparks composing her Domain at all times. The former, meanwhile, was somewhat difficult to accomplish — simply because the Longing Domain was so vast, encompassing all settled regions of the Dream Realm.","The swiftest and most reliable way to challenge the Nightmare, therefore, was to leave the Dream Realm altogether and return to Earth, either with the help of a Saint or through Neph's Dream Gate. Everything about that process was about to change.","First of all, Dream Gates were meant to be a one-way passage — they only allowed people to enter the Dream Realm from the waking world, not the other way around. It was because of Neph's [Dreamspawn] Attribute that her Gate was unique, functioning as a Nightmare Gate as well and allowing people to return. Without her, though, leaving Earth would carry the weight of finality for most settlers.","Leaving their Domain in the confines of the Dream Realm, on the contrary, would become easier — simply because the Human Domain would become a coalition of smaller Domains in the future instead of being synonymous with just one.","At the same time, people would have to learn how to petition their Sovereigns in order to escape from the protection of their Domains... instead of praying to Nephis. Sunny could not quite imagine any of the new Supremes being treated with the same type of religious reverence — not yet, at least — so the meditation halls and barely disguised prayers would probably have to be replaced by something new.","The transition would not be a swift or easy process... however, considering how desperately humanity needed more Awakened, Sunny imagined that accelerating it would become a priority. There were other matters to address, as well.","The remaining Supremes all had unique advantages and disadvantages when it came to building Domains. Some could do without the assistance of the Nightmare Spell, while some would be able to support humanity better if they controlled a large amount of Citadels... some, like Jet, would find no use in ruling a Citadel at all.","All of that had to be considered when deciding how to divide the Longing Domain, so that humanity attained as much strength as possible while it was being split between its Supreme protectors.","Sunny felt a bit of incongruity as he watched the ruler of the most powerful and expansive Domain in existence calmly discussing how to divide it among other Supremes. Godgrave had not been that long ago... after that bloody civil war, who would have thought that something this peaceful would be possible one day?","‘I'm almost speechless.'","The eleven demigods deliberated for a long time, eventually coming to a tentative outline of a decision.","According to their plan, out of the seven Sovereigns that were certain to stay behind, four would stand guard over Dream Realm, while three would defend the waking world and oversee the resettlement of its population.","If there was one unexpected benefit to the great number of Sovereigns War Realm had given birth to, it was that its inhospitable laws could not keep all of them away. Even if the waking world was actively pushing those who had attained Supreme power out, they could remain on Earth for several hours before truly feeling the strain.","That meant that they could take turns overseeing its expanse and make sure that at least one Supreme was always present in the waking world in case some kind of unexpected calamity befell it.","The three Sovereigns who took responsibility for the dying cradle of humanity were Jet, Kai, and Effie.","Neither of them particularly needed the assistance of the Spell to build their Domain. Jet would draw no benefit from ruling Citadels, Effie carried one within herself, making it easy to gain new subjects, while Kai was limited in whom he could effectively convert. So, by process of elimination, they were the best choice.","Additionally, Effie had to be present on Earth to hasten the evacuation of its people. Her Soul Garden would greatly boost the rate of resettlement, moving the whole timetable of the great exodus forward by a few years. That alone was reason enough to assign her the task of guarding the waking world.","While these three focused their attention on the waking world, the other four would have to stand their ground and defend the Dream Realm to the last drop of blood. They were Ananke, Morgan, and Seishan, with Nightwalker serving as the link between them.","Ananke would remain in Silver Web, overseeing the Stormsea and protecting the lands of humanity from things that hid in its depths.","Seishan would claim Ravenheart and the Citadel Cities located in the basin of the River of Tears... ironically enough, that meant that she would regain the lands that had been meant to be her birthright, assuming reign over the former territories of the Song Clan.","The same held true for Morgan, who would claim Bastion and the vast expanse of the former Sword Domain. She would return home, as well.","Nightwalker, meanwhile, would take the helm of the Night Garden and turn it into a wandering stronghold of humanity, responsible for keeping the three parts of the Human Domain connected and capable of supporting each other.","Once the plan was finalized, Sunny leaned back in his chair, looking around with a strange expression.","A scion of the Song family would once again rule Ravenheart. The Princess of Valor would return to Bastion. The Night Garden, meanwhile, would fall into the hands of the House of Night once more...","Almost as if it had been meant to be. Sunny was not sure if that was poetic... or upsetting.","‘How come after everything we did to destroy the Great Clans, nothing seems to have changed?'","But, of course... in truth, everything had changed. This peaceful meeting was the best proof that the world had been irrevocably altered.","All the blood they had spilled was to make this moment possible.","Sunny sighed.","‘At least no one laid claim to the Forgotten Shore...'","A troubled smile appeared on his lips. That, too, was a headache he would have to solve... but not today.","Today, they had to draft the speech announcing the tectonic changes awaiting humanity in the upcoming weeks."]},{"number":3149,"title":"Chapter 3149 Loose Ends","paragraphs":["A few days later, Sunny stared into the distance, a contemplative expression on his face.","He remained silent for a long while, then sighed.","“Things... do not look great.\"","He hesitated a little, then shook his head.","“It used to be that humanity was conquering new lands every day. There was so much energy when Nephis first ascended to the throne, so much momentum... we were achieving one victory after another. Those times are behind us now. The world just had to go and end on us without a warning. We were so busy preparing for the end of days that it arrived without anyone noticing. One day, we simply looked around and found ourselves in the middle of the apocalypse.\"","Sunny smiled bitterly.","\"These days, we are not conquering new lands. In fact, we can't even seem to hold onto the ones that were already conquered. It's a controlled retreat, for now... but the Human Domain is shrinking, little by little, every day instead. And do you know what really grinds my gears?\"","His smile turned contemptuous.","\"It is that because of that bastard, the Dreamspawn, most people don't even remember the good times that well. The Longing Domain is about to disappear, and its glory days are all but gone from everyone's memory. That seems quite unfair, don't you think?\"","Sunny cursed.","“And don't even get me started on the waking world. That whole place is a mess — Nightmare Gates opening everywhere, chunks of it being swallowed by the Dream Realm, swarms of abominations besieging all three Quadrants. The Barrow Wraiths, the Black Millipedes, and every other kind of horror imaginable... gods, I really hate those.\"","He inhaled slowly.","\"Well, at least things are looking up now because of Effie, Kai, Jet, Seishan, Morgan, and Nightwalker. South America has been evacuated, and the coastal areas are next. Ananke and the cities in the Stormsea have been a real lifeline for us in the past couple of years, and now that Effie and her Soul Garden are ready to enter the fray... I think we can get ahead of the apocalypse for once. At least for a little while.\"","Leaning back, he shook his head.","“Who knows? The world might still be in one piece by the time I become a god. I sure hope it will be. After all, it would be quite unfortunate to become a god at the same time as all of existence crumbles. There won't be anyone left for me to boast to... what even is the point of godhood if one cannot be smug about it in someone else's face?\"","In response, there was a long stretch of silence.","Then, a heavy sigh dispelled it.","“Has not being a god ever stopped you from being smug?\"","Sunny raised an eyebrow, then frowned in indignation.","The voice, meanwhile, added:","\"And for the love of gods, why are you monologuing in my room? Listen, there is a legion of dead shadows in your soul. Can't you use one of them — any of them! — to ramble at instead?!\"","Sunny was, of course, in Revel's room. The room was just as messy as ever, but at least the great and terrible Lightslayer was in a more presentable shape than her usual reclusive self — if being covered in sweat, grime, and blood could be considered an improvement. She had just returned from the battlefield, and had yet to shake off her fearsome image.","‘No, what am I talking about? Of course, it's an improvement!’","Anything was an improvement compared to her usual sloppy look.","Sunny did not have to be ashamed of how unprofessional his supposed top minion... that was to say, the esteemed elder of his Shadow Clan... looked.","He stared at Revel in confusion.","\"Of course, I can. But where is the fun in that?\"","Groaning, Revel threw an exasperated look his way.","“Why are you hiding in my room, anyway? Did you make Aiko angry again?\"","Sunny coughed.","“Of course not. Why would I make her angry? I don't know what you mean.\"","She seemed unconvinced.","\"Why are you here, then?\"","Sunny cleared his throat.","“By the way, do you remember that time I mentioned hiring Aiko as my assistant, then disappearing for a few years, leaving her in charge of a crumbling business in the absence of its main asset?\"","Revel nodded slowly.","Sunny stared at her with a vague smile for a few moments.","“Well, I am leaving for a few years! And I am leaving you in charge of the Shadow Clan! Congratulations, I guess!\"","His smile was flawlessly innocent.","\"That is why I am here. To deliver the news — and the congratulations — in person. Oh, and I also had a question...\"","Revel looked around her room with a strange expression.","What was that emotion?","Sunny couldn't quite recognize, but thought that it looked strangely similar to... melancholy.","‘What is that about? I just handed her a promotion! Of sorts...’","Why were people so ungrateful?","She sighed.","\"Can't say I didn't see it coming.”","Sunny raised an eyebrow.","“Oh, you did? Well, that simplifies things.\"","Revel nodded.","“You didn't make a secret of your intention to challenge the Nightmare, after all. Our people can only enter the Forgotten Shore with the help of your Dream Gate. The expedition to the Underworld did not produce a safe and reliable path connecting us to the rest of the Dream Realm under the Hollow Mountains, either. So... once you're gone, we will be either stuck here or forced to retreat. I was expecting this conversation for a while.\"","She remained silent for a few moments, then glared at Sunny.","“I just didn't expect it to happen in my private quarters, immediately after I returned from a battle against one of those damn Barrow Lords.\"","Revel's scowl deepened.","“And speaking of my private quarters — do you know what 'private' means, damn it?!\"","Sunny was surprised by the question.","\"Who do you take me for? Of course, I do!\"","He let out a derisive scoff.","“It means that I have to enter through the shadows instead of opening the door!\"","A book Revel had nearby flew in the direction of his head, and Sunny elegantly caught it in the air.","Turning it around to look at the cover, he blinked a few times.","\"What? There's a sequel? But how... how does she keep accidentally seducing all these men...\"","Revel growled.","\"Focus! Anyway, you had a question?!\"","Sunny tore his gaze away from the book, put it aside, and surreptitiously wiped his hand on his tunic.","“Oh, yes.\"","He leaned forward and asked in a friendly tone:","\"Say... how do you feel about pets?\"","Then, he leaned back and sighed.","\"You see, I have this snake. It is a sweet little fellow — about a kilometer long, house-trained, loves eating people... uhm, did I say eating people? I mean people, it loves people!\"","He paused for a moment.","“Anyway, I was hoping you could look after it while I'm gone, just for a little while...\""]},{"number":3150,"title":"Chapter 3150 Final Preparations","paragraphs":["Sunny wanted to use the Grace of Shadows Ability of Soul Serpent to bestow it upon Revel.","There were two reasons why he had chosen to make that decision, each of equal importance.","The first one was pretty obvious, and had already been touched upon by Revel. He had to make arrangements for the Shadow Clan before leaving, the main of which was the fate of the Forgotten Shore.","Sunny and his forces were entrenched there, holding their own against the Barrow Wraiths. With Saint becoming Supreme, he was able to push the abominations back to the border of the Burning Forest — but if Sunny went away, the line of defense would collapse. In fact, if he did not take some kind of measures, the line of defense would simply cease to exist.","The members of the Shadow Clan would find it difficult to travel between the Forgotten Shore and other lands of the Dream Realm, as well, not to mention between the Dream Realm and Earth. Since establishing a safe route through the Underworld seemed impossible at the moment, all they would be able to rely on were Revel and the Nameless Temple.","In any case, the simplest decision seemed to be to give up on the Forgotten Shore and relocate his forces somewhere else. Sunny was tempted to do just that, as well... but ultimately, he felt compelled to fight for his lightless demesne. He had invested too much effort into making it his stronghold, as well as a secret sanctuary for humanity. More than that, giving it up felt like the first domino in a vicious chain of defeat.","The Forgotten Shore was not just any region of the Dream Realm, after all — it was the entire northern frontline of humanity's fight against the encroaching Nightmare. If it fell, all other human lands would feel the pressure eventually, if not soon enough.","Both on a strategic and personal level, the Forgotten Shore was important to Sunny. So, he had chosen to make sure that it remained in human hands... which meant that he had to come up with a way for humans to defend it even in his absence. The question of how to go about that, however, was innately connected to the second reason he was leaving Serpent in Revel's hands.","It was the Fifth Nightmare itself.","No person of the waking world had ever conquered it, and even in history, there were few examples. Sunny only knew of one — of Ketzelkan and other rulers of Mictlan, who had managed to become deities, but seemed to have lost themselves in the process of Apotheosis and ended up destroying their own people.","He knew that people of the Storm Realm, the Twilight Sea, had never produced a Spirit. It was unknown how the scions of the Beast Realm and Heart Realm had fared, but none of them managed to survive the spreading Nightmare, so it was safe to say that their achievements had been ultimately proven insufficient.","In short, there was scarcely any information about what the Fifth Nightmare entailed. The only pieces of knowledge they did possess came from Eurys and, to a larger degree, from the Dreamspawn — and gods knew where he had unearthed that information.","According to the Dreamspawn, Sunny's very own Domain — as well as all his powers and tools — would be turned against him in the Fifth Nightmare. They would, or at least could, become an obstacle instead of helping him pass the trial.","So, even if it felt counterintuitive, Sunny's intuition was telling him that unburdening himself from as much power as possible would aid him in achieving Apotheosis, as well as maintaining a measure of control over who he would become as a result of it.","Apart from that, doing so felt oddly fitting. The Fifth Nightmare would most likely become the most dire trial of his entire perilous life. Stripping all superfluous advantages and facing it as close to his pure self as possible felt like the kind of resolve he needed in order to survive it.","That meant that Sunny had to leave some, if not all, of his Shadows behind. If it was possible, he also had to reduce the number of shades populating his soul.","As much as he hated the idea of parting with his loyal followers, that also lay in line with his overall goals. Sunny's true goal was not to conquer the Fifth Nightmare or become a deity, after all — those were merely measures he had to take in order to achieve it. What he really wanted was to make sure that humanity survived the apocalypse.","There was no point in becoming a god if all of mankind was gone by the time he did, and leaving his Shadows to guard the strongholds of humanity would diminish the possibility of all humans perishing. Those Supremes who were staying behind could certainly use all the help they could get — and Sunny’s powerful Shadows could be of immense help.","The question, however, was... would Sunny even be able to leave them in the real world? When his body, spirit, and soul entered the Seed of Nightmare, would the Spell graciously allow the inhabitants of his soul to stay?","Sunny did not know, but he suspected that it would. Others were able to leave their Memories behind, after all — so why couldn't he do the same with Shadows? The problem was that his Shadows could not exist without him. They drew their power from him, returned to the nurturing embrace of his soul to recover and heal from the wounds they received, and in some cases relied on him for sustenance.","So even if Sunny did leave them behind, their usefulness to the effort of preserving humanity would be limited, and there was a real possibility that they would be destroyed.","Because his Shadows were not independent beings. As Eurys had said once, they were not yet complete.","Sunny had not known how to make them complete before, but after venturing into the Underworld and recovering Shadow Weave, he had come up with a theory.","That theory had been developed further and tested in the month following that dreadful expedition, and now, finally, Sunny was ready to put it into practice.","On the eve of departing for a dreadful Nightmare...","He was preparing to grant his Shadows freedom."]},{"number":3151,"title":"Chapter 3151 Graduation","paragraphs":["It was night on the Forgotten Shore.","Well, of course it was. It was always night here, with no stars and no moon in the perfectly black sky. Still, Sunny liked the idea that, at the moment, it was really nighttime — just like when he had encountered Saint for the first time.","The location was the same, as well. It was the vast square in the depths of the Dark City, not too far from the ruined cathedral... only the cathedral was not so ruined anymore.","In fact, it had been restored to flawless condition. The whole city had been over the years, with Sunny and his shades, as well as members of the Shadow Clan, working tirelessly to make it suitable for humans to live in.","Now, the Dark City stood pristine and empty. The wide streets had been cleared of rubble, the buildings either repaired or demolished and built anew. It was just that there were no citizens here, not really... at least not yet.","Now that Sunny was planning to entrust the Shadow Clan to Revel, that could change. At the moment, however, he had to make sure that the Forgotten Shore remained under human control first.","That was why he had come to the familiar square where Saint had once fought the Iron Spiders, was slain by Sunny, and became his Shadow. At the moment, the square was empty, with not a soul in sight — and not a shade, either.","Except for Sunny and his Shadows.","Saint towered above the square like a magnificent monument carved from flawlessly black jade. Nearby, Fiend stood like a hill of jagged swords. Nightmare was here as well, having risen from the shadows. Slayer stood motionlessly, her graceful figure like that of a dancer. Vile had assumed the form of Sunny, sitting on the ground with a bored, but alarmingly mischievous expression.","The shape of the Dark Castle could be seen in the distance, looming above the city. And finally, Serpent had assumed its titanic Soul Beast form and coiled around the entire square, its head resting on the stones a few dozen meters away from Sunny.","These were his Shadows, his most powerful and loyal followers. Some had been with him for many years, some had joined the Shadow Cohort only recently. All in all, Sunny had really had a blast wandering the harrowing expanse of the Dream Realm in their company. He could not have wished for better companions...","He scratched the back of his head.","‘No, what am I talking about? Of course I could have!'","Sunny looked at his Shadows with a scowl. Nightmare, Fiend, Mimic, Slayer, and Vile... those wretches had truly put him through the depths of hell before becoming his Shadows! Encountering them had been among the absolute worst times in his impossibly appalling collection of terrible experiences.","So while it was true that they were wonderful companions, there could have been Shadows just as fearsome and loyal, but who had not left him with permanent mental scars.","Like Saint and Serpent. Why couldn't every Shadow be like these two?","“Come to think of it... you're actually a bunch of wretched bastards!\"","Sunny shook his head in dismay.","The Shadows ignored his outburst, as they usually did. Only Vile seemed to liven up and turned to him with a grin.","\"Bastard!\"","Sunny sighed and covered his face with a palm.","“Yeah, yeah...”","Hearing the youngest curse, Fiend shifted and looked at Vile with a hint of approval. Then, he turned to Sunny and breathed out a puff of infernal flame.","His grating voice resounded from above.","“Wretch.\"","Sunny laughed.","\"Well, I'll admit it. You have all come around, eventually. Thank you all for tolerating me for these long years of excitement and adventure... I wouldn't have made it without you, guys. Truly.\"","He sighed.","“But everything must come to an end sometime. So... this is it. It's time for all of you to graduate. Well — most of you, at least. Was I a good master or a terrible one? I am not sure. But I did my best.\"","Sunny smiled wistfully, remembering the good old times.","Which, really, had been the absolute worst. But still, he missed those days a little.","All in all, his Shadows really had nothing to complain about. He had nurtured all of them, helping them walk the Path of Ascension in his wake. So, he hoped that they would remember him fondly one day, even if he wasn't there anymore... at least not in the same way.","Sunny inhaled deeply and then looked at Saint.","His voice was quiet.","“Alright, then. It's time to get this show on the road.\"","At the end, his voice shook slightly.","‘Ah... this is going to hurt terribly, won't it?’","As Saint walked forward at his command, her size changing to that of a human, Sunny's shadow split into six, surrounding him like an honor guard. When Saint approached, standing before him, Sunny offered her a pale smile.","\"We... have been through a lot together, haven't we?\"","Fighting Sovereigns and Titans, conquering impossible Nightmares, delving into the darkest corners of the Dream Realm...","Hell, Saint had even been his therapist for a short while.","Hearing his question, she tilted her head a little, and then nodded slowly.","Sunny chuckled.","\"As taciturn as ever...\"","With that, he exhaled and then raised his hand.","Then, using the same motion he used when weaving a soul shard into a Memory, he reached into his own soul and grasped one of his Shadow Cores — his very first one, which had served as Saint's cradle for almost fifteen years.","And feeling his soul tremble, he pulled.","He tore it out.","‘Aargh!’","It hurt like hell.","But also, strangely, it wasn't that bad — no worse than the pain of a new Shadow Core being born, at least.","Sunny had seen Mordret doing something similar to create his Reflections or purge cores that were tainted by Corruption, but had never been able to do it himself — until Shadow Weave, that was.","Of course, there was more to the process than simply tearing the Shadow Core out of his soul. Sunny possessed an instinctual understanding of how to proceed now, and the foundation of his being had become far more capable and malleable, thus allowing the whole thing.","Still, it had taken him months of torturous experimentation to figure out how to remove a Shadow Core from his soul without destroying it. His soul, meanwhile, was not damaged terribly due to being enhanced by Soul Weave.","But removing a Shadow Core was only half of the process. Now, he had to embed it into Saint's soul — or rather, into the shadow that served her as one.","That, Sunny had never attempted before. This was the moment of truth.","Grimacing slightly, he reached forward and drew on his vast experience as a sorcerer to carefully embed the Shadow Core into Saint's chest.","However...","He did not have to worry. Once his core entered the dark depths of her being, it was as if something within Saint responded to its presence.","And then, a wondrous transformation took place in front of his eyes.","As it did, the Spell whispered into his ear...","[You have lost a Shadow.]"]},{"number":3152,"title":"Chapter 3152 First of Her Kind","paragraphs":["Within the vast and boundless shadow hiding inside Saint's mortal shell, five dark embers burned with lightlessness among the sea of darkness. Those embers were jagged and uneven, utterly lifeless — they functioned as a facsimile of true Shadow Cores, but weren't at all equal to one.","Now, however, that was changing.","As Sunny watched, his Shadow Core entered Saint's shadowy soul like a wandering comet. The moment it did, the depths of the vast shadow seemed to respond, and a dark whirlwind surrounded the nebulous sphere. Within the darkness, the edges of the Shadow Core seemed to blur. And then, a conflagration of black flame ignited in the shadow, blooming at the very heart of Saint's being like a tenebrous flower.","The flower had five petals, and those petals were drawn to each of the dark embers, nourishing and reforging them.","Making them complete.","The embers were being reborn in the nurturing dark flames. Their jagged edges slowly became smooth, and their lifeless coldness was replaced with flawless transparency.","Soon, they came to resemble perfect spheres, as well. Five oceans of dark flame burned inside them, making them look like lightless stars — no different from Sunny's own Shadow Cores. In fact, that was what they were now. And, infused with the power of these cores, a subtle change rippled through Saint's soul.","[You have lost a Shadow.]","The Spell announced the loss of a Shadow, but Saint was not destroyed. On the contrary, she was alive and well... as far as a Shadow Creature could be considered alive, of course.","‘A Shadow Creature...’","After following Sunny for nearly fifteen years as a Shadow, Saint had finally become a Shadow Creature. The difference between the two was subtle, but profound.","It was independence.","A Shadow was a subordinate being serving a master — it was a part of its master's soul, and therefore lacked true agency. A Shadow Creature, however, was a complete, self-sufficient individual. It had agency, free will, and the ability to choose its own path... whom to serve, whom to defy. Which battles to fight, and the reason to fight them.","Sunny was not sure which way of being was better. Being a Shadow or a Shadow Creature simply offered different things, as well as had different demands.","He did know one thing, though.","Being a Shadow, while beneficial in many ways, ultimately created a ceiling for one's growth.","There was a limit to how much one could grow while relying entirely on others, after all. To truly come into your power and become a person, you had to stand on your own two feet.","Well... or four, in the case of Nightmare. Or however many feet Mimic had.","Sunny looked at Saint, who seemed to be engrossed by her transformation. Most of the changes happening to her were invisible, transpiring on the mental and spiritual planes. The connection between them had been severed, and Sunny was not sure what Saint was experiencing... he suddenly felt lonely, as if a part of him had gone missing.","It did, quite literally.","Not only was Saint not a part of him anymore, but one of his shadows had disappeared, as well, becoming her shadow instead.","Now, finally, Saint was a complete being... a Shadow Creature in her own right. Sunny wondered what the future held for her. It used to be that humans coexisted with all kinds of creatures once, back when that word was not associated only with the Corrupted — but those noble creatures were long gone.","But now, there was Saint. She was the first and, for the moment, only Noble Creature in this dire era. As such, she was a natural ally of humanity — both humans and creatures were threatened by the spreading Nightmare, after all, and had to fight it together to survive.","But what would happen if the apocalypse was over one day, and the world still existed? Would people and creatures like Saint coexist once more?","Sunny truly hoped that they would.","Because if some bastard decided to bother Saint in the future... he wasn't going to hold back.","‘Just try it, bastards...’","But that was a matter for the far, vaguely possible future. For now, Sunny was more interested in the changes happening to Saint right here and now.","The most obvious one, of course, was that she did not depend on him anymore and had no need of his powers to continue existing. Sunny was also certain that Saint would become more powerful, since true independence and agency were bound to cause her Will to grow.","She might become more... personable, as well. Although Sunny had a feeling that being aloof and taciturn was simply in her nature.","There was one additional benefit, as well. Since Saint's shadow had once belonged to Sunny, she inherited some of his innate traits, such as the ability to augment herself and use the shadow as a scout. In short, she had her own invaluable helper now.","And more than that, since Saint was a Supreme Tyrant, her shadow had the capacity to contain shades. She could not create them, but she could command them — even if it was to a limited degree.","That limit was enough for Sunny to bestow the shades of Shadow Saints upon her, still. He did so without regret, knowing that Saint would make better use of them. She was the one who had slain most of them, anyway.","“Think of it as a bit of inheritance... a legacy, if you will...\"","He smiled as Saint peered at him with her ruby eyes.","Then, his Shadow... his former Shadow... bent down, bowing deeply.","Startled, Sunny waved a hand.","“N—no, no! What are you doing? There's no need for that...\"","He fell silent for a few moments, then grinned.","\"You know it will go to my head.\"","Although Sunny was smiling, and felt greatly satisfied seeing Saint become a true living being, he also felt a bit of melancholy.","Saint was her own person now. One of his shadows was now her companion, not his. It was as if his children had left for the Awakened Academy... he could not help but feel both proud of them and worried for their future.","In truth, however, there was no reason to worry. It was Saint, after all — if he could trust that someone would do well, it was her.","The rest of them, though...","Sunny turned to look at his remaining Shadows.","He was planning to grant independence to Nightmare and Fiend, as well. The former was needed in Bastion to guard the Dreamscape — Sunny would entrust him to Morgan, and Morgan to him. Fiend, meanwhile, was uniquely suited to defend Ravenheart and its surrounding territories from the snow wraiths of the western wastelands. So, Sunny intended to make him Seishan's headache.","The Marvelous Mimic was the headquarters of the Shadow Clan, so Sunny was planning to leave it to Revel.","The same went for Serpent — however, Serpent was unique. Due to his [Grace of Shadows] Ability, it did not have to become independent, and neither was it in Serpent's nature.","That was why Sunny would only lend it to Revel, not part with it forever.","He wasn't going to grant independence to Slayer, either. The two of them had formed a working relationship after a while, but she was simply too dangerous to be unleashed upon the world... at least for now.","As for Vile...","Sunny had special plans for that brat."]},{"number":3153,"title":"Chapter 3153 An Army, a Fortress, and a General","paragraphs":["Sunny had granted independence to Saint. Then, he did the same with the other Shadows.","Once everything was done, he consumed a great number of his shades to restore the Shadow Cores he had lost in the process. A great number of them vanished, diminishing the power of his Domain... but innumerable shades remained, still.","Finally, dazed by the pain and with his vast soul in a pitiful state, he made his way to Revel's chamber.","And here he was, explaining to her what he intended to do.","\"So, that's about it... quite a genius plan, isn't it? As expected of me, the Lord of Shadows!\"","Sunny grinned.","Revel let out a heavy sigh and covered her face with a palm.","She remained silent for a long time, then said evenly:","“Well, I'll give it to you. Sending Lord Nightmare to Morgan is a good idea... with a Sovereign and a Supreme Terror protecting Bastion together, people there will be much safer. The same is true for Seishan and the Shadow Fiend. Thank you for that, by the way. I don't even care about how immensely powerful he is — his unbelievable luck alone is a great asset.”","She paused and then mumbled quietly:","“Plus, he will finally have a chance to learn a thing or two from someone sane... thank the gods, that poor Devil really needs another role model...\"","Sunny blinked a couple of times.","“Huh? What was that?\"","Revel threw a dark look at him.","“Never mind that. That is your plan for the Forgotten Shore? Have you completely lost your mind?\"","Sunny chuckled.","“Oh... a long time ago.\"","Then, he shook his head with a smile.","\"But my plan is very reasonable. Just think about it for a moment.\"","Indeed, what Sunny had in mind for the Forgotten Shore was the product of a long and careful consideration. There was some risk involved, but he had a feeling that it would work out well in the end.","He raised a finger.","“Let's go over it one by one. First... the Soul Serpent.\"","Due to the [Grace of Shadows] Ability of Serpent, Sunny could transfer it to someone else's shadow. He had already done so with Rain, back when she was facing the possibility of becoming infected by the Nightmare Spell. She had been a mundane person at that time, though, and because of that, she had not received any real benefits from Serpent's companionship.","Revel, however, was a Saint — and an immensely powerful one at that, one of the most fearsome Transcendent people in the world even. So, if Sunny left Serpent with her, they would be able to form a true partnership. Needless to say, that was going to be a great boon both for Revel and for the Shadow Clan as a whole.","First of all, Serpent was quite possibly the strongest Shadow Sunny possessed... had possessed... at least on a technical level. It was a Supreme Titan, after all. Granted, Revel did not have a legion of shades resting in her soul, so Serpent would not be able to assume innumerable shapes as her companion — but even its natural Soul Beast form was already a harrowing force on the battlefield.","That was not the real reason why Sunny wanted to leave Serpent with Revel, though. The real reason was the Shadow Clan.","The members of the Shadow Clan had become who they were by receiving the Mark of Shadows. They were part of Sunny's Doman... but only because Serpent was a part of Sunny. If it became someone else's companion, though, they would become connected to that person instead.","Revel would be able to command members of the Shadow Clan more effectively, as well as support them with her strength. More importantly, she would be able to initiate new members into the Shadow Clan, expanding it as needed. Even if Sunny was gone for many years, the hidden force he had created would not cease to exist.","On the contrary, it would receive a chance to flourish under a new leadership. He doubted that the existence of the Shadow Clan would ever be revealed to the masses, since secrecy was required for the important work they were doing on behalf of humanity. But it would not need to remain so utterly clandestine either.","And if Sunny returned and wanted to take Serpent back, Revel could simply continue to act as the front of the whole operation. He would be more than satisfied to quietly support her from the shadows... in fact, that was only fitting for a force calling itself the Shadow Clan.","\"So, you see, it all makes perfect sense.\"","Revel stared at him for a few moments, then glanced at her forearm, where an intricate tattoo of a graceful snake was etched into her alabaster skin. That was her own Mark of Shadows — the strongest among Serpent's offspring — and if needed, it could become a deadly weapon as well.","She sighed.","“Well, what the hell. I guess I'll need to dust off my dual-wielding technique.\"","Then, she shook her head in dismay.","\"Still, the Soul Serpent alone would not be enough to defend the Forgotten Shore. It was the other part of your plan that bothers me.\"","Sunny shrugged.","“The other part is what is so genius about it! You need a fortress, an army, and a fearsome general. And look at that — miraculously, I can grant you all three...\"","Saint might not have been Sunny's servant anymore, but that did not mean that she ceased to exist. The bond of trust and camaraderie between them had not vanished, either. By losing a Shadow, Sunny had gained an ally... a loyal comrade, even. And as far as allies went, one could hardly do better than Saint.","She also commanded the legion of her fallen kin. So, he had requested that she remain on the Forgotten Shore and help Revel defend it as the field commander of the human forces here. The members of the Shadow Clan had been trained by her, after all — so who was better to lead them into battle?","The general was taken care of. She was a Supreme Tyrant, as well. With Serpent and Saint, Revel was already in charge of a greater force than any other Saint in history.","Except for Sunny himself, of course, and perhaps Mordret.","That left the issue of a fortress.","Naturally, there was Mimic to fill that role."]},{"number":3154,"title":"Chapter 3154 New Boss in Town","paragraphs":["Saint was Sunny's companion and ally, so convincing her to come to the Shadow Clan's aid had not been difficult. Mimic, however, was not quite that receptive to earnest communication... and yet, achieving an understanding with it had been even simpler.","After all, the Marvellous Mimic and the Shadow Clan existed in a state of symbiosis. The Mimic sheltered humans and produced soul coins for them, while humans made sure that it never went hungry by feeding it a steady stream of delicious abominations. So, it was in Mimic's own interest to keep the relationship going. Out there in the wild, he would have to risk its safety and work laboriously to deceive and hunt powerful prey.","Being domesticated, though, offered it a far more stable and leisurely existence.","Plus... Sunny had a feeling that the Marvelous Mimic had gotten used to being a home. It almost felt as if it liked being a shelter for countless people, and was quite fond of its current form — that of living, magnificent, carnivorous castle.","Sunny had significantly enhanced the Dark Castle, as well. Even if Mimic was a living being, that did not mean that he couldn't enchant it the same way he and Cassie had enchanted the key Citadels of humanity. So, although Mimic's Rank and Class had not increased, it was far more deadly and impregnable now.","Even if Sunny was absent, it would serve the Shadow Clan well.","Sunny grinned.","\"See? Aren't I brilliant?\"","Revel gave him a long look.","\"Don't you think that if a man calling himself the Lord of Shadows was brilliant, that would be a problem?\"","She scoffed and shook her head.","“Anyway, that is not what I am talking about. Your replacement! Do you really think that leaving that thing here won't cause any problems? If so... think again!\"","Sunny coughed.","Admittedly, the last element of his plan was the most questionable. However, after considering it carefully, Sunny tended to believe that it would work.","That element was Vile.","Yes, Sunny was leaving many powerful tools to Revel. She would become Serpent's host, gain Saint's support, and control a fearsome moving stronghold. However, even that was not enough to make sure that the Forgotten Shore withstood the dreadful peril of the apocalypse.","And so... Sunny was leaving Vile behind, too. To be precise, he was leaving it behind as his replacement. Before entrusting the devilish creature to Saint and Revel, he convinced it to take a particular form — Sunny's own form, that was.","Vile could copy the powers of most beings whose essence it stole, and Sunny had been one of its victims. It had already showcased the ability to contain and command shades in the Tomb of Ariel, and beyond that... if it wanted to, it could create Dream Gates as well. Especially now that one of Sunny's shadows had become its own.","With its transformation into a fully fledged Shadow Creature complete, Vile was not a devil child anymore — it was a mischievous... and more than a little sinister... teenage Devil. So while Sunny indeed felt a bit hesitant to set that Devil free, he was not too worried.","That was because Saint would stay behind to keep an eye on Vile and make sure that it did not do anything too dreadful. Additionally...","Vile would spend almost all of its time on the Forgotten Shore. Sunny would have hesitated setting it loose in a place like Bastion or Ravenheart, but here? There were deadly frozen wastelands to the west, the even deadlier Nightmare Desert to the east, the Hollow Mountains and the Underworld to the south, and the haunted tangle of the Burned Forest to the north.","What was the worst Vile could do?","‘No, no... let's not think those words aloud...'","If it had been immediately after the Tomb of Ariel, Sunny might have hesitated more. But the vile spawn had lost a lot of its savage wildness over the few years it had spent in the embrace of human civilization, learning how to be more cautious.","So, Sunny had transferred half of his remaining shades to the brat, warned him sternly to be a good boy... girl... or whatever it was, and then had Saint give it a look.","For some unexplainable reason, the little wretch all but ignored his warnings, but suddenly grew demure and obedient as soon as Saint glanced at it with her cold, indifferent ruby eyes.","It was like a kid who knew that he could get away with a lot of things when dealing with his parents, but became the picture of good upbringing when staying at his strict, cool aunt's house.","‘I'm cool too, damn it...'","No, what was Sunny thinking? He wasn't and had never been that little devil's parent! He was just its temporary master!","In any case, Sunny had managed to both ensure the safety of the Forgotten Shore and further weaken his Domain with Vile's help. There were still thousands upon thousands of shades resting in his soul, many of them immensely powerful, but at least their number was not overwhelming anymore.","So...","There was only one thing left to do.","Sunny studied Revel for a bit, then smiled.","“Well? Are you ready?\"","She sighed and nodded somberly.","\"As ready as I'll ever be, I guess.\"","Sunny stood up and offered her his hand.","\"Let's shake on it, then.\"","Revel stared at his hand for a while, then rose and took it.","As they shared a handshake, Sunny's serpent tattoo slivered down his arm and slowly slipped under Revel's sleeve. She shivered, her dark eyes widening slightly. And just like that, the bestowal was complete.","Sunny took a deep breath.","Revel would do well... he was sure she would. Saint would serve as her strength and command the legion of shades, both those hidden in her shadow and taken by Vile. Aiko, meanwhile, would handle the administrative side of running the Shadow Clan — and gods knew how capable she was.","The Forgotten Shore would endure the tides of apocalypse.","In fact, Sunny felt that even if the rest of humanity were to fall, this dark land would remain standing.","He felt a little wistful, but also content with his decisions.","‘It's for the best.'","His smile faltered a little, becoming faint.","\"Hey...\"","Revel's voice sounded full of some unknown, poignant emotion.","Turning his gaze back to her, Sunny raised an eyebrow in surprise.","\"Yes?\"","She stared at him silently for a second, then asked in the same deadpan tone:","“Can you perhaps let go now? We've been shaking hands for like half a minute...\"","Sunny looked down, blinked a few times, and unhurriedly let go of Revel's hand.","His smile widened a little.","“Sure. Oh, and congratulations. I will leave these lands in your care... Lady of Shadows.\""]},{"number":3155,"title":"Chapter 3155 Time to Say Goodbye","paragraphs":["Saint and her legion had settled in the area of the Dark City where the solemn square and the Dark Cathedral were located.","Vile made a home... a nest?... in the hidden chamber of the cathedral where Sunny had once lived for a few months.","Fiend was sent to Ravenheart, where he had built a lair in the furnace-like depths of the great volcano.","Nightmare had gone to Bastion to haunt its dreams.","Finally, Serpent coiled around the hill where the Bright Castle had once stood, its scales like a wall of black onyx. The Bright Castle was long gone, of course, and the Marvelous Mimic towered above the Dark City instead. On the vast platform in front of it, the Nameless Temple rested in the darkness. Its tall pillars and magnificent edifice were as black as the starless sky of the Forgotten Shore, and silence shrouded its spacious halls.","Things were a little different in the inner sanctum, though.","There, the sound of butter sizzling on a hot pan crackled loudly, and a dancing fire of a stove threw warm shadows on the stone walls. Someone was humming a lively melody.","Sunny was cooking.","His kitchen was quite a marvel of magical engineering by now, created with the help of three different kinds of sorcery. It had everything a person would need on the road to culinary perfection — which, as those enlightened knew, was no less perilous and insurmountable than the Path of Ascension itself.","Some of the items in the kitchen of the Nameless Temple had been forged by the King of Swords — his shadow, at least — enchanted by the Sovereign of Death, and burned with the radiant flames donated by the Star of Ruin.","Needless to say, there had only ever been a handful of mortals fortunate enough to taste the sublime food prepared by the owner of the Nameless Temple, the Lord of Shadows, Lost From Light. Rumors were that it was the most delicious thing one could taste in their lifetime... and after their death, as well.","Of course, the Lord of Shadows had spread that rumor himself.","Sadly, there were few people in the world who knew of his existence, so the rumor did not spread far.","\"You know... I spent countless years searching for the ultimate truth. Pancakes or waffles? The question had haunted my dreams since before you Awakened.\"","Rain, who was sprawled comfortably on the cushions, gave him a lazy look.","\"Oh, really?\"","Sunny nodded.","\"Indeed. But at the end of this calamitous search, having reached the very limits of comprehension, I finally attained enlightenment and understood that my question had been erroneous all along.\"","Flipping a piece of bread sizzling in the pan, Sunny smiled with the content tranquility of a living sage.","“French toast! French toast is the best. It is the undisputed king of breakfast foods. So, the competition between waffles and pancakes is entirely moot, to begin with.\"","He glanced at Rain and asked in a pleased tone:","“And do you know what the secret of a flawless French toast is? Be wary — the answer might shake the very foundation of what you know about the world.\"","Looking back at the pan, Sunny sighed.","\"Stale bread. The bread has to be a little stale... that's the ultimate truth.\"","Rain, observing him from behind, said languidly:","\"I sort of miss your pancakes, though.\"","Sunny froze.","His hand trembled, and his sagely smile cracked a little.","He remained silent for a few moments, and then asked in a forced tone:","\"Well, why didn't you say so right away? No, no! It's fine... it's absolutely fine. I can make pancakes, as well!\"","Soon, the two of them ascended to the ground floor of the Nameless Temple and entered its courtyard. There, beneath the branches of a towering tree, Sunny laid out an improvised picnic and set up a lantern.","A feast of a breakfast lay in front of Rain, with pancakes and French toast serving as the centerpiece. The delicious aroma permeated the air, and steam rose from a cup of fragrant tea, adding a refreshing note to it. She couldn't help but drool a little and wasted no time assaulting the generous spread with the ferocity of a starving abomination.","She had not forgotten her manners, of course.","“Thank you for the food!\"","Sunny sat down on a cushion and watched her eat with a smile. This one wasn't sagely, but it was sincere.","When Rain was about done, he asked:","\"How are Tamar and your friends doing?\"","Rain leaned back in satisfaction, throwing a regretful look at the empty plates in front of her.","Her face was a little rosy.","\"Shouldn't you know? Same as ever, I guess, only more so. Now that some time has passed since we all became Masters, the initial euphoria of having gained great power is mostly gone. The world is ending, though, and a Master is never idle. The work we do for the Shadow Clan keeps us busy.\"","Sunny was aware, since he had paid attention to all his mortal agents. Tamar and her cohort were not the only Masters in the Shadow Clan — there were quite a few now, actually — but they were his most elite team. So, the missions they received were all especially colorful.","Each one was worthy of being turned into a movie... a horror movie, possibly... but sadly, they were meant to remain unknown and hidden, so the public would never hear of their deeds.","Rain took a sip of tea and leaned on the trunk of the tree, looking up at its branches.","“Ah... that was nice. But you haven't cooked for me in a while. Is something the matter?\"","Sunny remained silent, choosing his words. But before he could answer, she gave him a long look and sighed.","Looking away, Rain asked in a distant tone:","\"You are leaving again, aren't you?\"","Sunny hesitated for a moment, then nodded.","\"Yes.\"","It was time to say goodbye."]},{"number":3156,"title":"Chapter 3156 Strong Roots","paragraphs":["There was a long bout of silence. Then, Rain exhaled lightly and smiled.","Turning to Sunny, she shrugged.","\"Well, it isn't the first time. You left to challenge the Second Nightmare, then to fight the Chain of Nightmares. You always return, though, don't you?\"","Rain paused for a moment, and then added sullenly:","“Even if, sometimes, you do stuff like erasing yourself from everyone's memory and getting into my good graces again by pretending to be an eccentric immortal... who just happened to decide to become my teacher because of a fortuitous encounter...\"","Her teasing was meant to lighten the mood, but Sunny did not respond.","Instead, he simply looked at her for a few long moments.","\"I do tend to return. But, Rain... this time is different.\"","Her smile faltered.","Sunny looked down, brushing his fingers against the warm cup, then looked at the mighty tree Rain was leaning on. Finally, he spoke:","\"I am going to be gone for a long while this time. But that... that is not all of it. The Fifth Nightmare is different from all the rest. Apotheosis is different from all other steps on the Path of Ascension. So, even if I do return... I might not be the same.\"","He felt something then. The painful sensation in his chest, grasping his heart like a vice — the undeniable reality that no matter what happened in the Nightmare, he was going to lose a part of himself. Perhaps an insignificant one... maybe a precious one, instead.","The person he had been all his life would be gone, replaced by a strange god.","Sunny inhaled deeply and looked at Rain.","‘Time really flies, doesn't it? But it also crawls like a snail.’","She wasn't the sweet toddler who used to follow him around their tiny apartment anymore. She wasn't an awkward teenager, either, or even a young woman tentatively coming to terms with her budding adulthood. Rain was in her mid-twenties now, having already become a Master. The little girl he remembered had blossomed into a real adult...","Somewhere in the middle of the apocalypse, Rain had outgrown his image of her. Having experienced both war and peace, she was now tall and strong — just like the tree behind her.","She was thriving.","Sunny smiled.","Rain didn't need to depend on him anymore. So, even if he was gone... even if he didn't return, or returned so direly changed that they would not recognize each other... she would be alright.","...That was a little painful, too.","He cradled the teacup in his hands.","\"But it has to be done. What can I do? Your brother is just too awesome. So, there's no one else who can fill my shoes.\"","Rain tried to smile, but her eyes betrayed an inner turmoil.","She looked away, remained silent for a short while, and then spoke in a tone tinged with emotion.","“We keep missing each other, don't we?\"","She took a deep breath.","\"In this life... we were meant to spend it together, but instead, we spent most of it apart. And now, we are parting again. How is this fair?\"","Sunny couldn't help but chuckle.","“There's no such thing as fair, so who knows?\"","He paused for a moment.","\"This world is so vast. It is so harsh, too. So many forces pulled us in different directions, but in the end, we still found each other, didn't we? Over and over again. To me... those times we spent together were more precious than you can ever imagine, Rain. And they always will be.\"","He took a deep breath, then exhaled slowly.","\"So, I want you to know that even if I seem odd after I return... even if I am not who I used to be or treat you differently... I will always look over you. You say that we have spent most of our lives apart, but Awakened have long lives, Rain. There are countless years ahead of us. And yes, I might not be able to spend them all by your side, but I will always be there, somewhere. Thinking of you.\"","Sunny scratched the back of his head and added awkwardly:","\"Well, unless I die, of course. But you know me — your brother is not easily killed. In fact, I pity the fool who tries to kill me.\"","Rain couldn't help but chuckle.","Afterward, she fell silent again and looked at him with a wry, bitter emotion hidden in her eyes.","She did not speak for a while, then asked:","\"So, what? This is a goodbye?\"","Sunny shook his head slightly.","“This... is a picnic. And a see you later — in a few years, hopefully. Before the world ends.\"","He reached forward and poured more tea into her cup.","His voice turned lower.","“Take care of yourself, Rain. Things are going to get worse before they get better. You are a Master now, but I know that you won't remain one for long... that means that in the years to come, you will be at the forefront of humanity's struggle to survive. I know that you will do well — that you will be exceptional. But, please, put yourself first. Remember that somewhere out there, someone is fighting to get back to you. So, for their sake as well, please put yourself above all else.\"","He looked at her and smiled.","\"Oh... and this is for you.\"","Rain frowned in confusion.","“What is?\"","Sunny gestured to the courtyard around them.","“This. The Nameless Temple — I am leaving it to you. Revel will take care of it until you become Transcendent, but it's all yours. This courtyard, this tree, the Citadel behind us. This, too, is your legacy.\"","He hesitated for a moment, then leaned forward and put a hand on her shoulder.","A spark of energy passed from his soul into hers, and the Nightmare Spell announced that he lost a Memory.","Sunny cleared his throat.","“And a small parting gift, as well.\"","Rain raised an eyebrow, then summoned the Memory and stared at it for a while.","Then, she asked in an incredulous tone:","“Your parting gift... is an ordinary rock?\"","Sunny laughed.","“Believe me, there is nothing ordinary about it. It is a Memory that can record sounds. So... I left a few recordings for you to remember me by. If you ever feel like you miss me, you can summon this Memory and listen to one or two.\"","He paused for a moment, and then added:","“Then, you'll remember how obnoxious I was, and stop missing me immediately.\"","Looking at the Extraordinary Rock, Rain let out a quiet laugh.","\"I see. Indeed. Okay then... thank you for the thoughtful gift, Brother.\"","She fell silent, stayed motionless for a while, and then gripped the rock tightly.","Raising her head, Rain looked Sunny in the eye and said:","\"You... take care of yourself too, Sunny. I don't care what happens to you or how much you change. If becoming a god gives you a big head and you forget how to be human... how to be my brother... then I'll just remind you. I'll keep reminding you until you remember, so if you want to save yourself the trouble, come back whole.\"","Sunny met her gaze, lingered for a few moments, and then nodded.","There was nothing left to say.","\"Goodbye, Rain.\"","The branches of the tree swayed above them, rustling under a lightless sky.","Just like the two of them, the tree had been born in the outskirts of NQSC. And just like the two of them, it was uprooted and thrown into a wide, perilous world. However, the tree did not perish — instead, it adapted. Now, against all odds, it was thriving in a land where there was no sun, offering its company to the ancient walls of a forgotten temple.","Its roots were robust and strong, penetrating deep into an unforgiving soil. There were three scars on its bark, left by a mischievous youth.","That youth was a man now, and he was leaving to face his Nightmare.","He was leaving many precious things behind in this pursuit, as well... things he was not willing to part with.","But he knew that he had to let them go if he wanted to protect them.","Maybe that was the difference between a youth and a man."]},{"number":3157,"title":"Chapter 3157 Shock and Awe","paragraphs":["The world had been rocked by astonishing news.","One stunning announcement followed another. Just a few years ago, Supremes had been singular beings, each no different from a cardinal direction — but now, six new Sovereigns rose to the throne of Supremacy at the same time. And they weren't just anybody, either. Each was a famed figure, either widely beloved or deeply feared, the stories of their various deeds having long become modern folklore.","The news caused a great uproar. People were stunned and rattled, feeling the foundations of the world shaking beneath them. They had many reasons to feel wary and alarmed, but strangely enough... most of all, they were elated.","In the brief period of time since the first Sovereigns revealed themselves, the very word became synonymous with strife and calamity. It wasn't long ago when most of the Supremes were known to have caused great harm to humanity — the Queen of Worms, the King of Swords, his son, the King of Nothing...","Even the Lord of Shadows, who had only lived a few minutes as a Supreme, immediately attempted to betray and kill his comrade and ally, Changing Star.","So, it would not be surprising if people were wary of the fact that six new Sovereigns were walking the earth now. However, the identity of these Sovereigns made all the difference.","Raised by Wolves and Nightingale were widely beloved. Soul Reaper Jet enjoyed the deep loyalty of all government soldiers, even if her reputation was chillingly fearsome. Nightwalker was a living legend, his image influenced by the goodwill people had towards the House of Night. And finally, there were Morgan of Valor and Song Seishan...","Even if the Song and Sword Domains were no more, countless people had lived and fought under their banners — quite recently, at that. A kingdom was more than its ruler, and while the King of Swords and the Queen of Worms were gone, their legacy remained. So, seeing Valor and Song rise from the ashes brought many people a sense of belonging, as well as an empowering feeling of stability.","Instead of being alarmed, people felt happy and more hopeful about the future because of the news of six new Sovereigns emerging. Supremes were the ultimate champions of humanity in the war against the Nightmare Creatures, after all, and in the span of a single day, their number had more than doubled.","The next news, however, was even more shocking.","Lady Nephis of Immortal Flame, the guiding star of humanity, announced that she would step down from her role as the ruler of the Human Domain and commander of its armies. Not only that, but she would also withdraw from the public entirely — going to face the Fifth Nightmare in the company of her trusted companion, Song of the Fallen.","If the previous news sent humanity into an uproar, then this one caused it to shake. Although Changing Star's reign had been brief, it had also been tectonic. The entire world had rallied around her, ignited with the passion and resolve to push back the encroaching Nightmare.","Humanity had won countless victories, broadened its territories in the Dream Realm, nurtured a great sea of new Awakened warriors, and begun migrating to a different world. It had achieved immense breakthroughs in both technology and sorcery, settling the vast expanse of untamed lands.","Its power to resist the endless tide of Nightmare Creatures had been greatly enhanced, and even with the advent of the apocalypse, humans were still fighting doggedly to survive and triumph.","It was Changing Star's conviction and leadership that had stopped the senseless bloodshed of a civil war, made all these advances possible, and preserved humanity in the early years of the apocalypse. Countless soldiers had been saved by her flames, and many more found hope and solace in her luminous light.","And now, their goddess was leaving, perhaps never to return.","Even if Nephis of Immortal Flame had made one miracle happen after another, there was no guarantee that she would survive the Fifth Nightmare. She had not spoken at length about the reason for her decision to challenge it, but people could deduce it themselves.","It was to ensure humanity's survival, since being merely Supreme — being a woman whose powers seemed deific and who was called a goddess, but wasn't a real deity — was not enough. It did not seem enough to Changing Star, at least.","People felt a wide range of emotions regarding her departure, but if there was one thing that united all of these feelings, it was that they were incredibly intense.","And while they were consumed by this emotional tempest, the next piece of news arrived.","Other things were changing, as well.","For two years, people in various parts of the Dream Realm had been expecting the return of their leaders, praying for their safety. The Steward of the West, the Steward of the East, the Steward of the South... people in Ravenheart, Bastion, and the Stormsea had grown used to their rulers, even if their reign had not been a long one.","But now that they had returned alive — and Supreme — it turned out that they would not be returning to their posts. Raised by Wolves, Nightingale, and Soul Reaper were going to take upon the duty of protecting Earth, instead, while Song Seishan, Morgan of Valor, Ananke of Weave, and Nightwalker would replace them as the rulers of the Dream Realm.","In short...","Things had been changing swiftly in the apocalypse, but now, everything seemed to have changed in an instant.","And as people were reeling, the new Supremes arrived in the Great Citadels of humanity to establish their Domains.","Nightwalker climbed onto the deck of the Night Garden, where the members of his clan were waiting at the front of a crowd of people. He flashed them a smile and then raised a fist, inhaling the salty breeze that blew from the sea with a full chest.","In Ravenheart, where the influence of the Song clan had never truly waned due to the popularity of Ki Song's daughters, a sea of people gathered on the streets, cheering as Seishan, the new queen, walked through it and across the great bridge to the gates of the Jade Palace, followed by her sisters.","Even though most members of the Valor family had been eradicated by the King of Nothing and its influence was all but gone, Morgan was met with cheers and ovations as well, a torrent of vermillion flags billowing in the wind behind her as a column of Ascended knights followed her on mighty Echo mounts. The steel of their heavy armor glistened in the sun, resembling a river of steel that flowed toward the Mirror Lake.","...Sunny, Effie, Kai, and Jet watched the procession from the shore of the Ivory Island high above, sitting leisurely on the emerald grass and sharing a bottle.","None of them could really get drunk, but the taste of good wine was still pleasant on a warm day like today.","\"Look at her go...\"","Effie clicked her tongue and took a large sip, letting out a satisfied sigh afterward.","Then, she raised the bottle and said in a bright tone:","\"To Morgan of Valor, long may she reign. Ah, say what you want about that woman... but she really knows how to throw a parade.\"","She paused for a moment, took another sip, and smiled.","\"And to us. Let's drink together again, the four of us, after this whole Fifth Nightmare business is over.\""]},{"number":3158,"title":"Chapter 3158 Greatest Fortune","paragraphs":["Sunny smiled and remained silent, taking the bottle from Effie.","He had gotten back from the Forgotten Shore only this morning, and in a few hours, he would be gone. Behind them, in the Ivory Tower, Nephis and Cassie were finishing the last of their preparation and addressing the Fire Keepers. His own farewells had already been said.","The three freshly baked Sovereigns, meanwhile, were in the strange interim period where their duties had already been decided, but did not become reality yet. An army of bureaucrats, administrators, and military officers were feverishly rearranging the whole framework of how humanity functioned at the moment. Until the logistical side of the leadership change caught up, Effie, Kai, and Jet had precious little to do.","It was all too sudden and not at all ideal, bound to cause damage across both worlds... but also a part of the process. If Sunny and Nephis wanted to ensure a flawless transition, they would have had to spend years arranging everything properly. That delay, however, would have caused even more harm.","Now that the apocalypse was in full swing, Sunny had to abandon the idea of doing things without suffering losses. Somewhere along the way, everything had become an issue of mitigating the damage, not avoiding it altogether. It was a shift in mentality that he did not want to accept, but also a necessary one.","So, this hasty transition was, in fact, a good trial run of the dire changes to come.","Once pieces of Earth started to fuse with the Dream Realm en masse and the situation worsened even further, with unexpected calamities striking without warning on a regular basis, humanity would have to learn how to function with utmost effectiveness despite the utter chaos. Taking a sip of the wine and appreciating its flavor, Sunny smiled wistfully and looked at the bottle.","This bottle, too, was a symbol of humanity's perseverance and adaptability. The grapes used to brew the wine were a strain developed in Ravenheart from Godgrave vines, then cultivated in the uniquely fertile soil of the Night Garden. The beautiful bottle itself was produced in the Glass Hell and was sturdy enough to be used as a weapon.","In fact, humanity had three superb bread baskets now. Ravenheart with its rich volcanic soil, the Night Garden with its mystical enchantments, and Effie's Domain that had been infused with a fragment of War God's own vitality. Silver Web was exceptionally productive due to Ananke's augmentation, as well. As long as these treasuries were still in human hands, people would not starve, at least.","Sunny looked at his friends and grinned.","“Wow... look at that. All three of my interns have become Supreme! That is, like, a one-hundred-percent satisfaction guarantee. Am I not the greatest mentor in history? Honestly, even I am amazed at myself.\"","The three of them looked at him wryly. Eventually, Jet chuckled.","“Yeah, way to go, genius. We conquered the Fourth Nightmare, but you still managed to make it sound like your personal achievement, somehow. That's real talent right there.\"","Effie nodded, while Kai simply smiled.","“But yes... thank you, Sunny. I don't think we would have returned if it wasn't for the experience of those three expeditions. Not all of us, at least.”","Sunny waved a hand. He passed the bottle to Jet, remained silent for a few moments, and then said:","\"Azarax, huh?\"","He looked into the distance.","\"After hearing about your Nightmare... I really want to return to the Nightmare Desert, find the bastard, and put him back on that tree.\"","After that, Sunny shivered.","“Although I'd better wait until I am Sacred. Or Divine. Let me tell you, that place is called the Nightmare Desert for a reason.\"","Effie shook her head slowly, a shadow briefly running over her eyes.","\"That guy has already received his punishment. Now, the Shadow God's curse swallowed him up... all that remains is a husk. He'll probably become a problem one day in the future, but someone else can deal with him. We don't have a monopoly on dealing with terrible crap, do we?\"","She grinned and looked at Sunny with curiosity.","“Our Nightmare is in the past, though. But yours will begin soon. So, how do you feel?\"","Sunny remained silent for a bit, then shrugged.","“Alright, I guess. If anything, I feel... unburdened. I basically got rid of all my earthly possessions, so it's all a bit weird.\"","He smiled faintly.","“Every time I entered a Nightmare before, I was wary of what awaited me in the Seed. But now, strangely enough, I am not that worried about the Nightmare itself. I am only worried about its aftermath — how much time will pass, how the world will fare without me... how much I will change.\"","Kai sighed.","“It feels strange to us, as well.\"","He looked at the procession of knights far below, which was now approaching the Mirror Lake. A sea of scarlet banners billowed in the wind, and around it, a vast city was boiling with life.","Kai's expression turned a little wistful. \"We entered the Second Nightmare together. We went into the Third one together, as well. So, except for the First, you have never challenged a Nightmare without us... I can't help but worry.\"","Sunny chuckled.","\"Now you know how I felt when you went into the Seed.\"","Jet took a sip of the wine, glanced at it, and passed the bottle to Kai.","\"I haven't been with you three in the Second Nightmare, but I did watch over this guy during his First.\"","She paused and then smiled.","Of course, that was to kill him in case he failed... but, still. Kind of makes me sentimental to remember. And look at us now. We are literally on top of the world.\"","Sunny scratched the back of his head.","“Apart from the fact that it's the wrong world, everything seemed to have turned out great. Well, except for the fact that it's the apocalypse. So, there are two facts — we are on top of the wrong world, and that world is ending. Come to think of it, I take it back. Everything seems to have turned out terribly.\"","He laughed.","Eventually, Sunny's laughter died out. He lingered for a while, then sighed.","“From before I entered the Academy until now, I had suffered both great and terrible luck. Sometimes, it threw me into situations that seemed inescapable, and sometimes, it saved me from perils that felt insurmountable. But, looking back...\"","He glanced at Effie, Kai, and Jet.","“It's clear to me now that my greatest fortune has always been somehow meeting the right people. There are so many people without whom I wouldn't have made it that far, and among them... meeting you three was truly my greatest blessing.”","Sunny smiled.","“Usually, after saying something so earnest, I would immediately follow it up with a joke to handle the aftermath. But, uh... you've just returned from your Nightmare, and I am leaving for mine. Who knows when we will get the chance to see each other again? So, I just wanted to say thank you. For tolerating me for all these years and helping me become who I am. For everything.\"","The three of them studied him for a few moments.","Then, Jet smiled and waved a hand.","\"It's me who should be thanking you, Sunny. For coming with me to Antarctica. For surviving. For helping me become a Saint. And simply for being there for me... meeting you has been a great fortune for me, as well.\"","Effie nodded.","“Mine too. There is a lot I am thankful for... besides everything, you are also the reason I got to meet my husband and become Little Ling's mom. He would have died somewhere in Antarctica without you, along with countless others. So, don't sell yourself short.\"","She paused, and then added with a mischievous grin:","“Although you are short...\"","Sunny threw a scathing glare her way.","Kai, meanwhile, simply nodded.","“I'd probably still be in that well in the Dark City if it wasn't for you. Well, my bones would be.\"","He fell silent for a moment before speaking with a smile.","“But let us stop here. This... this is starting to sound suspiciously like a goodbye. And I refuse to say goodbye to you, Sunny.\"","Kai finished the wine and shook his head.","“We will meet each other again. We will have countless years to enjoy each other's company. So, there's no need to rush... go into your Nightmare with an easy mind, Sunny. The world you are leaving behind will be fine. We'll take care of it.\"","As Sunny watched, Jet and Effie nodded. He sighed, feeling emotions swell in his chest.","This precious moment... was ending. It was already over, and now, he really had to leave.","\"Well, then. In that case...\"","Rising from the grass, Sunny dusted himself off and smiled.","\"I guess it's time to go. Knowing all of you... has been an honor and a privilege. Until we meet again.”","With that, he vanished.","He had left the world behind."]},{"number":3159,"title":"Chapter 3159 Distant Shore","paragraphs":["Sunny, Nephis, and Cassie entered the waking world together. It met them with the same kind of inhospitable pressure they had long grown accustomed to, straining to push them back into the depths of the Dream Realm — although now that Sunny's Domain was smaller, that pressure felt slightly less intense.","There was no fanfare. Everything that needed to be said had already been said, and everything that could have been done was already done. They did not need to pack anything or prepare equipment, either. Supremes did not need a lot to sustain themselves and could carry a lot in their Soul Seas. So, the three of them looked like they were going on a casual walk.","Even if they were leaving to challenge the most dire of Nightmares.","The manor of the Immortal Flame clan was quiet, since the Fire Keepers were in the Dream Realm at the moment. So was Smile of Heaven, who had long resided in the Ivory Tower — now that both Nephis and Cassie were going away, Effie was going to look after her.","It was not only Effie who would remain on the Ivory Island, either. Kai and Jet would be based there as well, taking turns watching over the waking world. The Fire Keepers would remain an independent force ready to assist any of the four Domains that spanned the Dream Realm now, while the Wolves and the Night Singers would return to Earth.","But these... these were not issues Sunny had to concern himself with anymore.","He used Shadow Step to bring Nephis and Cassie out of NQSC, into the depths of the toxic wasteland beyond. They had a long way to go and little time to waste, hurried by the need to reach their destination before the War Realm tossed them out.","Still, Sunny allowed himself a few moments of reflection while taking in the desolate landscape around them.","\"Funny.\"","His voice was quiet.","“Outside used to mean death... especially to us, people from the outskirts, who lived closer to it than anyone else. The thought of leaving the city was no different from contemplating suicide. We were so scared of it that, most of the time, we forced ourselves to forget that it even existed.\"","He inhaled deeply and then grimaced.","“But now, it's like going on a picnic. I am not sure if that is because I am much more difficult to kill now, or because I have experienced countless places that were far worse than this.\"","As if responding to his comment, a chilling howl resounded somewhere in the distance, and he sensed numerous shadows converging on their location.","They were the shadows of the new masters of Earth — the Nightmare Creatures. People liked to believe that the waking world still belonged to them, but in truth, most of its surface had been populated by abominations for a long while now. Just like humans were settling the Dream Realm, the Nightmare Creatures were settling Earth... and they were far more successful colonizers than mankind.","Nephis looked around, too.","\"This land will flourish again.\"","Her voice was even and resolute.","She bent down and picked up a handful of dry, lifeless soil. It spilled through her fingers like dust, flowing down in a dark stream.","“When it is all over, and the Nightmare Spell is no more, once we've won... there will be those who will bring it back to life.”","She paused for a moment, and then added:","“Maybe we will.\"","They moved on.","The desolate reaches of the Northern Quadrant were teeming with Nightmare Creatures, but none of them were powerful enough to cause three Supremes serious trouble. Sunny moved with startling speed, as well, carrying Nephis and Cassie through the shadows. It did not take them long to reach the edge of the continent, where a deep ocean washed over its shore.","From there, they took to the sky.","East, east...","Across the ocean.","As they flashed across the heavens, moving from the radiance of day into the dark shroud of the night, Sunny was somewhat surprised to see how swiftly they were devouring distance. He had rarely traveled this way in the waking world, and the Dream Realm was vast — far more spacious than Earth.","But then again, with how swiftly Awakened moved — especially those of higher Ranks — it had to be. The endless expanse of that alien world had seemed too daunting once, but now, it felt ordinary.","Long before the strain of remaining in the waking world became unbearable, they finally crossed the ocean and landed on an unfamiliar shore. Around them, the air was acrid with the smell of sulfur, and great pillars of smoke were rising into the sky on the horizon. Those were the volcanoes that had awakened in the aftermath of the Category Five Gate opening, blanketing the world with ash.","Sunny, Nephis, and Cassie stood on the outskirts of a dead city. The streets were empty and forlorn; the buildings had collapsed or were staring at them with empty windows. Everything was covered by ash, and rusted remains of destroyed ships protruded from the tumultuous water in the harbor.","The landscape — the vast expanse of ashen mounds, the colossal pillars of smoke supporting a dark plane of clouds that obscured the sky, the deteriorated ruins of a lifeless city — was alien and strange, as if they were still in the Dream Realm instead of on Earth.","This was America.","The first continent humanity had lost to the tide of Nightmare Creatures, as well as the place where Immortal Flame and Smile of Heaven had perished while trying to buy as many people as possible time to evacuate. Looking at the ruins, Sunny felt a dull ache in his chest.","All of it looked too familiar.","Ash replaced the snow, and the layout of the city was different. But it reminded him terribly of Falcon Scott — of the mournful devastation of Antarctica.","He sighed.","There, in the shadows of the vast ruin, something was already moving, awakening","due to their presence. Nightmare Creatures were crawling out of their lairs, attracted by the scent of human souls.","Glancing at Nephis, Sunny frowned and moved forward.","“Come. Let's not linger.\"","They had to find the Nightmare Gate that had killed this land."]},{"number":3160,"title":"Chapter 3160 Rushing Towards a Nightmare","paragraphs":["Sunny and Nephis could have eradicated the Nightmare Creatures that populated the slaughtered city. In truth, they could probably have slain every abomination in America. Even the unknown Cursed One who was presumed to dwell on this continent was not an insurmountable challenge — in fact, their track record of battling Cursed Creatures was quite spotless so far.","Perhaps Nephis wanted to avenge the destruction of her family, as well as too many other families to count.","But they had not come to America to fight this time.","Fighting a Cursed abomination on Earth could very well cause it irreparable damage. The planet itself would be fine, but billions of humans still populating it could perish.","Take America, for example... the massive volcanic eruption caused by the calamity that had happened here caused temperatures to drop across all Quadrants. The natural disasters that followed were devastating. If not for the fact that humans had caused several such cataclysmic events themselves in the past, and therefore knew how to survive them, they could have gone extinct by now.","New abominations would emerge from the Nightmare Gates eventually, anyway — if the whole continent wasn't swallowed by the Dream Realm even before that. Besides, slaying endless hordes of Nightmare Creatures and battling a Cursed One was going to take time they did not have. They had come here to find the Seed, not to hunt abominations. So, no matter how meaningful this place was to Nephis, they had to move stealthily instead of engaging in all-out slaughter.","She was looking at the ruins with a distant expression on her face, white sparks dancing in the depths of her eyes.","Sunny looked at her with concern and asked quietly:","“What are you thinking about?\"","Nephis remained silent for a while, then sighed and pulled her gaze away from the lifeless remains of the city.","\"..The price of failure.”","She paused for a moment and added in a deeper tone:","“And the merit of trying, anyway.\"","Immortal Flame and Smile of Heaven must have known that they would most likely die here. They had been mere Masters, after all. Even if no one had ever seen a Gate like the one that opened in America, they understood how terrifying the Nightmare Creatures that emerged from the apocalyptic Gate would be.","And yet, they still attempted to stall them so that more people could survive.","America still fell. Countless lives were still lost. But not quite as many as would have been without their efforts.","But would the world have been better off if Immortal Flame and Smile of Heaven had chosen to save themselves instead of helping the civilians?","There was no way to tell. Broken Sword might have been still alive. The Sovereigns might never have turned on each other. There could have been no Godgrave, no Dream Plague...","Nephis might not have grown up being hunted like an animal and watching her clan slowly wither and die.","The world would have definitely been different... unrecognizable, really. But better? Sunny was not sure.","He gripped her shoulder briefly and looked away.","“All I can say is that if I were in their place... I probably would have made the same choice.\"","The soldiers of the Evacuation Army had known that many of them — maybe most of them — would not return from Antarctica. But that did not stop them. An overwhelming enemy was nothing new in the Age of the Nightmare Spell. Humans faced insurmountable odds all the time, but they still had to continue fighting.","Cassie, who stood nearby with her hand resting on the hilt of the Quiet Dancer, turned her head slightly at that moment.","\"It's strange.\"","She hesitated for a moment, then raised a hand and briefly touched her blindfold.","“The Cursed One... I cannot sense it.\"","The Nightmare Gate was hidden in the very heart of the continent, a thousand miles away. But to someone as sensitive as Cassie, such distance was not an obstacle. Even if she could not learn anything about the Gate Guardian, she should have been able to feel an echo of its presence, at least. Sunny frowned.","Come to think of it, he did not feel anything, either. America was that thing's territory... its influence on the world should have already begun interfering with his Will, by now.","But while the atmosphere of America was oppressive, there was nothing.","The three of them were suddenly uneasy. An enemy who instilled fear with its mere presence was a dangerous foe. A being who concealed itself so utterly that even its power could not be felt, though... that was a far more frightening adversary.","An ambush predator was meant to be weaker than a true hunter, but it was also far deadlier.","“Let's proceed cautiously.\"","Leaving the ruined city and all the Nightmare Creatures that populated it behind, they rushed inland. By now, the strain of remaining in the waking world was pressing on them heavily, and as they moved closer to the source of the unimaginable devastation, the Call of Nightmare grew louder and louder, almost impossible to resist.","The Call of the apocalyptic Gate that had opened in America decades ago was unlike anything Sunny had ever endured. It was powerful, magnetic, irresistible... if not for the harrowing experience of witnessing the true Tomb of Ariel, he would have been tempted to succumb to it entirely. But everything paled in comparison to that terror.","They saw more destroyed cities on the way. They saw wreckages of military machines and signs of a desperate struggle, as well. The forces of humanity seemed to have been instantly overwhelmed, having offered little resistance — how could they, when the enemy had been of a much higher Rank?","The whole continent was like a graveyard... an empty, desecrated graveyard drowning in ash and blackened ruins. It was the sight that sent chills running down Sunny's spine, as if he was looking at an ominous depiction of what all of the world would look like one day soon.","They crossed a desert and a grand canyon that split the earth like a festering wound. They crossed a rocky mountain chain, as well. Finally, descending into vast lowlands, they moved across them with as much speed as they could muster.","And then, they finally found the Nightmare Gate that had stolen this continent from humanity.","It towered above the world like a great pillar of darkness, visible from hundreds of kilometers away. But as they drew closer, its true width was revealed. The abhorrent fissure swallowed several kilometers of the desolate plain, its seething darkness moving eerily in the absence of light.","They found the Cursed abomination that guarded the Gate, as well.","It lay on the ground in front of the vast fissure, its flesh itself like a mountain. There were countless limbs, an endless expanse of pale flesh, and a terrible maw that could swallow entire Citadels...","And blood. There was a sea of black, fetid blood surrounding the ghastly behemoth, soaking the barren land and forming a dark and motionless lake.","\"Its name was Desolation.\"","As Sunny, Nephis, and Cassie stared at the dead god in stunned silence, a voice resounded from their side.","Flinching, Sunny turned and saw a man sitting on a slab of broken concrete — even though there had not been anyone there a moment before.","The man was wiping his hands with a piece of cloth, the fabric soaked with black blood. There was a subtly revolted expression on his face, and a detached coldness in his eyes.","Sunny also saw his own reflection on their mirror-like surface.","He grimaced.","\"Look who decided to show up. How the hell did you...\"","“How did I manage to kill that thing without destroying half of the planet?\"","Mordret shrugged with seeming indifference.","“It wasn't that difficult, really. I simply lured it into my Mirror Realm and killed it there.\"","He smiled darkly and threw the cloth away. Rising, Mordret inhaled deeply and massaged his shoulder with a hint of displeasure.","\"Granted, it was merely the sparing the planet part that was easy. The killing itself was... ah, it was quite unpleasant.\"","He bowed slightly to Cassie and then turned to face Nephis.","“I would prefer it if we didn't linger. The smell is quite dreadful.”","She studied him for a moment.","“So, you've decided to join us in the Nightmare, after all?\"","Mordret remained silent for a short while, then looked around and smiled slightly.","“Well... it seems to me that I have gotten here first. So, if anything, it is you who are joining me.\"","She tilted her head slightly, then nodded.","“In that case, we shall proceed. It's... good to have you with us.\"","Mordret seemed slightly surprised to hear those words.","The rest was easy. Far easier than Sunny had expected, which hinted that everything that followed would be impossibly hard. They simply crossed the realm boundary, attempting to return to the place where their tethers had been placed. However,","instead, they were pulled toward the Seed by the Call of Nightmare.","Thrown violently off course, Sunny found himself in an unfamiliar place.","The ground was white and as hard as stone. The sky... was black and jagged. Half of it was, at least — the other was blindingly white, suffused with incandescent glow. Light poured down like a waterfall, flakes of ash dancing in it like snowflakes.","And there was something else, as well.","A suffocating, animalistic feeling of fear that suddenly grasped Sunny’s heart. The same kind of fear he had felt in the Underworld, standing on the edge of the abyss and gazing into its depths.","As if he was in the presence of an Unholy Nightmare Creature.","Feeling a suffocating heat, Sunny froze. His intuition was telling him that if he moved, he would dearly regret it.","The Call of Nightmare was deafening here.","[Stay still, Sunny.]","The four of them had been separated while crossing the realm boundary, so Sunny could only hear Cassie, not see her.","He hesitated for a moment, then asked.","[Where are we?]","But even before she answered, he already put two and two together.","The strange texture of the ground beneath him, the irregular shape of the sky, and that name, Desolation...","Sunny suppressed an unbelieving chuckle. The jagged sky... was no sky at all. It was bone — the jagged edge was where the bone had been broken, and the blinding radiance spilling into the immense breach was one he was all too familiar with.","It was the incinerating sunlight of Godgrave.","After all this time, they had returned to this cursed place. In fact, they entered a part of it that even Anvil and Ki Song had not dared to disturb.","They were inside the titanic skull of the colossal skeleton.","And the Seed they were searching for... was right at its center, in the great Hollow where the dead god's brain would have been.","They were not alone here, either.","‘Another... damn... Unholy...’","Despite the suffocating heat, cold sweat flowed down Sunny's back.","[Sunny, listen to me carefully.]","He had no other choice, since moving meant being burned to ash by the sky of Godgrave.","Cassie seemed to take a deep breath.","[You should feel by now the direction the Call is coming from. That is where the Seed is... once I tell you, run toward it as fast as you can. That is the only way we will survive — if we reach the Seed faster than the thing that dwells here reaches us.]","Sunny cursed inwardly.","[When will that be?]","Cassie did not respond immediately.","[Once the clouds close... now!]","Sunny flinched.","‘Now? Is that an example, or...’","Even while thinking that, he was already flying through the shadows.","Faster, and faster, and faster still.","Feeling something vast and ancient stirring in the darkness behind him.","Sunny did not know where Nephis, Mordret, and Cassie were. They would have entered the Dream Realm somewhere in the vicinity of the Seed, as well, but the skull of the titanic skeleton was vast. At the moment, they were probably rushing toward the Seed just like he was, knowing that only by reaching it they could survive. But would they make it?","Would he make it?","Sunny did not know.","The transition from the feeling of being powerful and all but invincible to small and defenseless was too jarring.","Sensing that something malevolent had noticed him, Sunny attempted to accelerate even further.","'Faster, damn it!'","Who would have thought that he would run toward a Seed at full speed one day, praying to dive into a Nightmare sooner?","Sunny gritted his teeth and turned into a shadow.","[Cassie, what about...]","And there, finally, he saw the Seed.","It was vast and appalling, hanging in the","darkness like a pulsating tumor. Infecting the world with an endless stream of Corruption.","The grotesque sight made Sunny's heart skip a beat. The Call washed over him like a tide, throwing his mind into disarray.","He was so close.","Witnessing the great Seed, Sunny threw himself at it...","And, without ever slowing down, plunged into its vile depths.","There, he heard a vaguely familiar voice whispering into his ear.","[Welcome, Lost from Light!]","[Prepare for your Fifth Nightmare...]","[End of volume thirteen: Prelude to Apocalypse.]"]},{"number":3161,"title":"Chapter 3161 Divine Syzygy","paragraphs":["In the beginning, the world was vast.","The day sky shining upon it was the realm of Sun God. The night sky shrouding it in darkness was the realm of Storm God. The pale moon moving across the sky was the eye of Beast God, and it illuminated the mortal realms below.","The mortal realms sprawled far and wide, populated by all manner of beasts and creatures — as well as men.","Below the red dust of the mortal world lay the peaceful darkness of Shadow God's domain.","The realm of Heart God, meanwhile, existed in the souls of living things.","And in the heart of it all, imprisoned, was the Void.","...The world was vast, but the shadow was small.","And since the world was full of horrors, the shadow was afraid.","It crawled out of the water, hid in a dark place, and shook, feeling the ground around it quake and groan under the heavy footsteps of history.","No. The Demon of Desire, Hope, had not invented writing yet, so there was no history. The world groaned under the footsteps of the gods, who walked its surface — as well as others like them, who were more terrifying than fear itself.","For they were Creatures of the Void.","In the beginning, when the world was young, the gods still fought against those few of their kin who had escaped the cage of existence during its creation. The shadow clung to the cold stones of its dark cave, terrified.","For a long time, that was all it knew. It didn't even know itself.","Outside the cave, the world was changing.","One day, a harrowing, colossal form fell from the sky, impacting the earth like a dying planet. Its death cries shattered the heavens, and its fall broke the world. The ground splintered and rose in molten waves, forming towering ridges. The being's blood flowed into the dark depths like a sea, and before it could rise again, another shape plummeted from the fractured sky to press it down.","The first being was vast and harrowing. The second was beyond the concept of horror — bestial and ferocious, it was so great as to be entirely unfathomable.","The moon served as that being's eye.","Its infinite maw was full of fearsome fangs, and with those fangs, it tore into the fallen being, rending its flesh and spirit apart. The fangs cleaved the molten earth, as well, shaping it into tall and jagged mountains.","That was Beast God slaying a great Creature of the Void.","Once the creature was dead, Beast God devoured its endless expanse and slept for a while in the molten cradle. Centuries passed, and the world slowly cooled. The Hollow Mountains took shape, and the great caverns of the Underworld were formed below them. The blood of the slain creature became true darkness, and white mist seeped into existence through the fractures in the broken fabric of reality.","Finally, Beast God stirred awake, displeased by the cold, rose from the ground, and returned into the dark embrace of the night sky.","The shadow trembled.","Another day, a horror so terrifying that it defied description — defied being cognized or conceived of, let alone comprehended — rose from the depths. All six of the great gods fought it together, and it was only when the daemons joined them that they finally managed to drive the Void Being back down.","However, they couldn't kill it.","Instead, Sun God placed a prohibition on the absolute laws of existence, eliminating the concept of warmth and movement from the waters where the terrifying being of the everlasting Void dwelled. The ocean turned to ice, imprisoning the Void Creature in its depths. A vicious cold emanated from the frozen ocean, swallowing the lands around it and turning them into a frigid, lifeless wasteland.","The cold continued to seep into the world, spreading slowly.","Many other things happened, as well.","A small sapling turned into a great tree, its roots reaching the depths of the Shadow Realm while its branches supported the heavens.","A vast forest grew around it, becoming a blissful shelter for all living things. In time, however, rot and corruption spread under its branches, and it wasn't until the Demon of Repose created the seasons that its endless hunger for growth was confined.","Humans abandoned the cradle of the primordial forest and ventured into the vast expanse of the world.","The cage of existence was almost broken by the crushing strength of the Stone Titan, who was eventually destroyed by the Demon of Dread.","All memories of Dream God were erased from existence, leaving an echoing absence.","The divine syzygy splintered into myriad realms.","A nasty bird stole Weaver's eye.","Mirage, the Demon of Imagination, built a system of artificial lakes and created the concept of reflections. Because of her, the world was able to look upon itself for the first time.","Some were enamored by their reflections; some were dismayed...","The shadow didn't look.","Reflections did not exist in the darkness, and it was reluctant to abandon its lightless shelter.","It wasn't really interested in its appearance, anyway — however, because of that disinterest...","The shadow became aware of its own existence.","It had existed for a long time, but it had never been aware of itself. Now, the thought of being indifferent to its looks made the shadow realize that it had to exist in order to look like something.","And so, the shadow asked itself a question.","‘Who am I?'","It did not know.","It did not remember.","Or, rather, it remembered too much.","The shadow vaguely remembered living myriad lives, being myriad creatures. In one life, it had been a beast hunting powerless prey. In another, a hunter slaying the beast.","In one life, it had been a king.","In another... A slave.","All of its numerous lives had been different. Some had been short, some had been long. Some had been spent in the embrace of the Flame, some drowned by the rot of Corruption.","There was only one thing uniting them all — it was death.","The shadow might have lived myriad different lives, but they all ended the same way. Death was the only constant in its strange existence, so it was what the shadow knew best.","Death felt like home.","Death was familiar, soothing, and peaceful. Life, however, was violent and full of strife. The weight of myriad lives had been arduous and overwhelming, and so the shadow was tired.","After escaping the endless cycle of rebirth, the shadow had fallen into water, sought shelter in a dark cave, and forgotten itself. It hid in the darkness while the world was in the throes of the Age of Gods.","The shadow was still tired of life, but having rested for a long while, it didn't feel as exhausted anymore. And so, as the tribes of humans spread across the mortal realms, fighting against the Creatures of Corruption that dominated the world beyond the safe haven of the Divine Realms, it asked itself a second question.","‘What am I?'","The shadow's memories were endless, impossible to encompass, and contradictory. It didn't know a lot while at the same time knowing too much. However, one thing that the shadow did understand was that a creature like it was not supposed to exist.","All beings were meant to live for a while, then find eternal peace in the embrace of death. The shadow, however, remembered dying myriad times, but it was always forced to return to the harsh embrace of life.","It vaguely remembered living — and dying — thousands upon thousands of times. Hundreds of thousands?","The shadow was not entirely sure.","It repeated the cycle of life and death over and over, over and over, over and over again... eternal, ever-changing... until it was shaped into the being it was now.","In some lives, the world was similar to how it seemed — governed by the great gods and populated in equal measure by mortals and abominations. In some, the gods were distant and indifferent, with mortals reigning over myriad realms. In some, the gods were dead, and the world was swallowed by Corruption. There were strange cities with towering buildings made from metal and people who did not know who the gods had been.","The shadow remembered the bitter smell of gunpowder drifting over a towering alloy wall, the deafening thunder of firing turrets, soldiers, and MWPs fusing into a somber litany under the light of a crimson aurora...","It also remembered staying behind as the Demon of Dread laid siege to the Realm of Death in the final battle of a world-ending war, its siblings fighting against the endless legion of shadows as gods and daemons clashed in the boundless darkness above them.","The shadow remembered Hope straining to break free of its chains. It remembered spending thousands of years being devoured by a profane vine... it also remembered being killed, kneeling, as the vine first took hold within its body.","The memories were endless, and some of them contradicted each other. Some came from the past, while many came from the future... from various futures, each more fantastical than the previous one.","It all felt like a dream.","‘Ah... a dream.'","The shadow realized that it had been asleep for a long time. And so, it felt like this world... this beautiful, harrowing world... was nothing but a dream it dreamt.","‘No, not a dream.'","It was a nightmare.","The shadow dreamt a nightmare, and in that nightmare, it had been forced to relive the lives of all the creatures it had killed. Hundreds of thousands of them...","The number was an answer that seemed to hint at what kind of being the shadow had been.","It would have been appalled and terrified, but its feelings had long been numbed by the weight of myriad lives the shadows had lived. So, it accepted it with indifference.","The shadow felt like it was forgetting something... something important. Something vital, or perhaps even precious. But even if that was true, the shadow did not really care to remember what it was, either.","Its curiosity sated and feeling no desire to explore its murderous past, the shadow settled comfortably and prepared to return to its slumber.","However, at that moment, it was disturbed. Something was moving at the mouth of the cave...","Someone was making noise in its quiet shelter.","Displeased, the shadow stirred and sighed, directing its senses to the uninvited guest. It was greatly displeased.","A strange word surfaced from the depths of its calloused being...","‘Damnation.'"]},{"number":3162,"title":"Chapter 3162 Uninvited Guests","paragraphs":["During the awe and horror of the dawn of time, the shadow had confined its senses within the cave, trying to make itself blind to the world. It wanted to become as small as possible, so that the terrifying giants that walked the earth could not see it — could not sense it watching them, and therefore become aware of its existence.","Now, however, the shadow was forced to take a look outside.","In an instant, its senses spread across hundreds of miles, encompassing the movement and texture of every creature, insect, and blade of grass swaying in the wind in the lands that surrounded its shelter.","...The world had grown small while the shadow rested.","Its cave had ended up in one of the mortal realms. The boundary of the realm felt like a moving stream to the shadow's senses — easy enough to cross, if one didn't mind getting wet.","Not that the shadow wanted to do such a thing.","Its senses encompassed a region of the primal realm that was covered by craggy mountains, green valleys, and forests. The youthful world was pure and untamed, unsullied by the devastating splendor of civilization. Myriad beasts and creatures populated its wild expanse...","And abominations, too.","They hid in the dark corners of existence, just like the shadow did. They were the beings of the Flame who had been corrupted by the Void, driven mad by the insatiable need to destroy that which they had lost, all in a futile effort to reclaim it.","They roamed the world, hunting the children of the Flame in a tortured frenzy, and infected everything around them with the appalling rot of Corruption.","Where there was life, there was Corruption. And those Corrupted were the rulers of all lands that fell beyond the cleansing fury of the gods.","The gods were great and vast... the gods themselves were beings of the Void. So what did they care about these small abominations?","The shadow did not care, either.","However, now, there was a scent of blood drifting into the cave it had chosen as its shelter. Out there near the entrance, a human was crawling across the jagged stones, leaving a trail of blood in his wake. The man was dressed in crude garments made from fur and hide, his weathered face hidden by a bushy beard. His body was covered in gruesome wounds, and his eyes were full of pain and despair.","As a hoarse groan escaped from his mouth, a grating sound came from behind him. There, a towering abomination broke through the wall of tall trees, shattering them into splinters. It was tall and imposing, blood streaming down from between its bestial fangs, its vaguely humanoid shape both gaunt and menacing.","The abomination was wounded, too, but it was nowhere near the man’s grievous state. It fell on all fours, glaring at him with murderous fury. Its powerful hind legs tensed, ready to send the creature into a deadly lunge, and its long tail whipped like a bone spear.","The man was about to perish gruesomely in the creature's hideous maw.","The shadow did not care whether he lived or died.","It had experienced hundreds of thousands of deaths, after all, so what was one more? It was not worth the effort of feeling anything. All things died, in the end. Their passions, their aspirations, their pain, their despair — none of it held meaning to the shadow. The accumulated weight of its myriad lives made everything seem fleeting, and it had lost the desire to care about small things.","All that was left was indifference.","The shadow did, however, feel a strange impulse to intervene.","It was not because the shadow felt compassion toward the man or considered his life valuable. Rather, it was because at that moment, the shadow discovered a new fact about itself.","It disliked Corruption.","In the vague recollections of its previous lives, the shadow remembered being constantly haunted by the corrupting influence of the Void. In fact, most of its lives seemed to have been spent in the throes of Corruption.","Sometimes, the shadow was born as an abomination. Sometimes, the shadow was born as a child of the Flame, lived a life full of joys and sorrows, then underwent the torturous transformation of being tainted by the Void and spent myriad years roaming the world consumed by madness and agony.","And throughout all those lives, the shadow itself — the being dreaming the nightmare of myriad lives — had to arduously resist the Corruption, preventing its seeds from taking root in its soul. That was a reason why the shadow's dream was a nightmare, as well.","Some of the seeds were small and weak, some were vast and terrifyingly virulent. The shadow seemed to possess quite a powerful means of defense, though, so it had managed to destroy them all. Still, Corruption never stopped trying to claim it, persistently sending its dark tendrils into the shadow's soul. It was unpleasant.","Corruption... was a bully.","Not only was it a bully, but it also seemed to have made its life's mission to endlessly bother the shadow.","So, even though the shadow did not feel much, it felt a strong dislike toward Corruption and those who carried it.","It was fitting, in a sense. Death was a weapon that destroyed Corruption, after all, and since the shadow felt a strange sort of closeness to death, it was only natural that it despised Corruption as well.","That was why it decided to act.","As the towering abomination prepared to lunge at the bleeding man, the shadows around it suddenly moved, as though coming alive. Tentacles of darkness surged forward, entangling its arms and legs.","The mighty being struggled, trying to break free, but it was powerless in front of the shadow. The dark tendrils dragged it back, pulling in different directions. The creature opened its maw, as if wanting to howl...","Before it could, its body ruptured, torn apart into pieces. Blood, viscera, and severed limbs fell to the ground in a torrent — wherever its yellow blood touched the soil, the soil smoked and melted, as if corroded by a strong acid.","But it didn't matter much, because the loathsome creature was dead.","Unlike Beast God, the shadow did not devour the remains of its enemy. It had better manners, and a more refined palate at that.","The shadow was displeased, though. It shivered uncomfortably.","That was because the moment the abomination died, the shadow felt something slip inside its soul, and thought that it heard an echo of a vaguely familiar voice.","It wondered if it would be forced to relive that unfortunate life, as well.","The bleeding man, meanwhile, stared at the gruesome remains of the ruptured abomination in shock. Then, he turned slowly and peered into the deep darkness suffusing the entrance to the cave.","His face paled horribly, and he took a step back, trembling.","Then, finding the strength to run, the man turned around and fled.","The shadow was relieved.","‘Good. Good riddance...’","Content that its shelter was peaceful and quiet once more, the shadow settled into its resting place. It hoped that no one would bother it again.","These hopes, however, were soon shattered into pieces.","Some time had passed — days, maybe, or perhaps years — and the shadow felt someone moving at the mouth of its cave once more.","With a heavy sigh, it directed its senses outward.","Then, its face fell.","Well, the shadow did not really have a face. But if it did, there would have been an expression of stunned dismay on it at the moment.","That day, the shadow asked itself the third question.","‘What the actual hell?’"]},{"number":3163,"title":"Chapter 3163 State of Transparency","paragraphs":["The shadow expanded its senses outward when the abomination appeared on its doorstep, so it knew where the man hunted by the creature had come from.","Out there in a valley at the foot of a hill, not too far from where the shadow's cave was, a small tribe of humans had been setting up crude tents on that day. The shadow assumed that they were merely passing by — now, however, it knew that its assumption had been wrong.","These humans were trying to settle down. The initial scattering of fur tents had grown since then, and their frames seemed more substantial. There were tools and hunting implements scattered around, wooden fences, and half-domesticated wolves gnawing on old bones.","The men were busy hunting beasts and fishing in a nearby stream. The women gathered fruit and berries, while simultaneously dedicating time to small crafts and rearing children. The children ran around and engaged in all sorts of mischief. There were not a lot of elderly around, but those few who had lived to see old age observed them from afar with grumpy discontent.","The tribe seemed like a primitive one, with only a few Awakened champions to guard them against the Creatures of Corruption that dwelled in the forest. They seemed to be at peace, but in truth, their existence was a constant war — a war against hunger, a war against the harsh elements, and most of all, a war against the loathsome rulers of this vast, untamed world.","Humans were wary of the forest. They were wary of the darkness. And so, they fought against the forest and the darkness, slowly pushing both back.","From the looks of it, the tribesmen were just barely learning the basics of agriculture, which had given their nomadic tribe the courage to settle down.","‘It means that they have nowhere else to go.'","The shadow felt a hint of interest.","It knew that agriculture was not born from progress. Rather, it was born from necessity. Nomadic tribes were far less vulnerable to the vagaries of the world, so there was only one reason why they would compromise their established way of life in favor of being tied to a land — there was not enough space for them to move to.","After all, nomads could leave in search of kinder lands in case of drought or natural disaster. They could flee if a powerful Creature of Corruption set its sights on their tribe. Once they became dependent on the land, however, there was no escaping it. Unless they wanted to starve, all they could do was stand their ground and fight — and go extinct if the enemy was too powerful.","The shadow found it mildly interesting, but its interest was aloof. It would not have paid the people any attention... if not for the fact that a group of them was currently standing near the entrance to its cave.","The man it had inadvertently saved was there as well, his wounds mostly healed. The tribesmen weren't holding spears or torches, though, and neither were they trying to enter the cave.","Instead...","They were setting up an altar.","The shadow observed them from the depths of the cave, flabbergasted.","‘For the love of gods, what the hell are they doing?'","The men dragged a large flat stone from somewhere lower down the mountain and placed it near the entrance, using smaller rocks as supports. Then, they placed strange things — fruit, meat, and some kind of beverage that smelled suspiciously like honey — on the altar and stepped back.","They were all wearing very odd garments and headdresses, as well, throwing frightened glances at the cave from time to time. Their faces were pale, but determined. The shadow was focused on something else, though.","‘...Honey?’","It recoiled.","The shadow didn't know why, but it felt a strong animosity toward honey.","The shadow distrusted it.","The humans, meanwhile, lowered themselves to their knees and then sprawled on the ground, kowtowing toward the dark entrance of the cave. Their voices rose in a strange litany, and they kept making noise for a long while.","The shadow shifted uncomfortably. It didn't like what was happening one bit.","The humans continued their ritual for some time, then left. Their pitiful presents remained lying on the altar. In time, the fruit and the meat rotted, while the vessel containing the sweet beverage was knocked over by the wind and spilled.","The shadow, obviously, did not leave its cave to lay claim to these unwanted offerings. It wasn't happy to receive them, but it was rather relieved that the noisy humans were gone.","It settled back into its half-awake state, slumbering in the darkness. Its senses still encompassed the land, so it could feel the world changing as time flowed. The trees grew taller. Two colonies of ants waged a war against each other. Deep in the forest, an eerie abomination had killed a bear, the mighty beast's body hanging limply from the creature's maw.","The realm was teeming with life, and the shadow's placid consciousness seemed to fuse with it, sensing every little facet of the boundless land through the shadows. In that state, it was difficult to differentiate where the world ended and the shadow began; it wasn't keen on making that distinction, either.","Such existence was peaceful in its own way, and while the shadow could not say that it was enjoyable, it did not find the state unpleasant. Its sense of self dissolved into the movement of shadows, and since there was close to no self in that state of inner transparency, there was no joy or discomfort either. There was only the great, endlessly changing vastness of the world. The shadow sensed the tribe of humans, as well.","The tribesmen were busy living their lives. Their settlement slowly grew, and as more of them matured and formed families, new tents were raised on its outskirts. The old tents were being slowly replaced by wooden structures. The forest was pushed back, creating space for a modest field. Some elderly surrendered to old age. Young women gave birth to children. A few of the hunters formed their soul cores and Awakened.","From time to time, the tribesmen made their way to the shadow's cave and performed their rituals, leaving new offerings on the altar. They seemed to have mistakenly decided that the creature that dwelled in the darkness was the guardian spirit of their tribe — the shadow did not care what they believed, so it wasn't going to correct them.","For what it was worth, it seemed that its presence scared away the more discerning abominations, so the tribesmen were benefiting from the shadow's existence, even if the shadow itself had no say in it. These humans were also quite lucky, since no powerful Creature of Corruption had wandered through this land in a long, long while.","They seemed to attribute that luck to the shadow, as well.","In time, the offerings the tribesmen left on their stone altar grew more lavish.","The shadow ignored them, as always. In fact, it ignored the humans entirely, enduring their noisy hymns with a mild sense of exasperation.","That was until, one day, the nature of the sacrifice they brought changed."]},{"number":3164,"title":"Chapter 3164 Precious Sacrifice","paragraphs":["The small settlement of the tribe had become a small village by then. The number of humans populating it had increased, while the tents made from fur and hide were replaced by wooden huts. The offerings brought by the villagers were more generous now — by their standards, naturally.","But perhaps, they still felt that it was not enough. Or perhaps they had grown fearful and desperate, for some reason... the shadow did not know. It did not care to know, either. All it knew was that, one day, its peaceful state of slumber was disturbed by a new noise. It wasn't the usual mumbling the tribesmen engaged in when leaving sacrifices on their altar.","Instead, the shadow heard a child crying. Displeased, it let out a heavy sigh and slowly, laboriously pulled its consciousness from the state of non-existence, creating a distinction between itself and the world once more.","‘What now?'","Its neighbors were proving to be most frustrating.","Out there, at the mouth of the cave, the shadow saw a familiar figure — it was the man it had saved once from an abomination.","The man was old now, his figure gaunt and bent. His limbs, which had been mighty once, were now thin and wiry. His thick beard had turned white, and there was a determined, mournful expression on his wrinkly face.","His shadow, on the contrary, had become darker and deeper, as if his death was drawing near.","Such was the nature of mundane humans. Their lives were fragile and fleeting — they flashed beautifully and vanished, leaving no trace of themselves in the world. One blink, and you could miss their existence entirely. The shadow frowned.","The man had grown old, but there was still strength in his limbs. He had no trouble dragging a crying child to the mouth of the cave, at least, whispering something in a somber tone.","‘What is the meaning of this?'","The shadow found its ability to ask questions much improved.","Before it could form a theory about what was happening, the old man stopped and lowered himself to one knee. Looking at the child — a girl who looked young enough to be his great-granddaughter — he said something, hugged her, and looked into the impenetrable darkness of the cave with an expression of fear, sorrow, and desperate hope.","Then, the old man pushed the girl into the darkness.","The shadow was surprised.","It was dismayed.","As the girl tumbled down sharp stones, rolling into the depths of the cave, it considered the old man, exploring a strange impulse that rose from the deepest, darkest corners of its soul.","The shadow felt compelled to kill the man. Was that so surprising, though?","It had been a consummate killer once, after all. It still was. Death was not only the shadow's home, but also the language it was most familiar with. In fact, the shadow suspected that it could very well be a living embodiment of death... its avatar, perhaps. Perhaps it was not just any shadow, but the shadow of Death itself.","Nevertheless, in the end, it allowed the old man to leave — for no other reason than that dealing with him would be bothersome. With the man gone, the shadow felt relieved.","That left it with another problem, though... The old man was gone, but the child was not.","The girl rolled to the floor of the cave and stayed there, trembling. In the darkness, her small frame looked like a heap of trash someone had left at the shadow's doorstep... in fact, using the word “doorstep” was not entirely correct.","Despite its attempts to become as small as possible, the shadow was still vast and deep. Its lightless expanse occupied most of the cave, so when the girl was pushed into the darkness, she was pushed into the vastness of the shadow.","In other words, the heap of trash had been unceremoniously left inside the shadow itself.","It hesitated, not sure what to do.","‘Should I kill her?'","The girl would be gone in the blink of an eye, anyway, like all mundane people. Killing her painlessly was the simplest solution... however, the shadow did not want to.","It felt a strong reluctance.","That was not merely because doing so would encourage more living sacrifices from the tribesmen, either.","At that moment, the shadow learned another fact about itself. It seemed that, although its nature was that of a merciless slayer... and that the number of its victims was incalculable... the shadow disliked senseless killing. The shadow abhorred it, in fact.","At the mention of the word \"slayer\", something seemed to move in its soul, but the shadow did not pay it any attention. It was preoccupied with the child.","The girl, meanwhile, seemed to find a tiny bit of courage and gathered herself from the ground, sitting up.","She looked around with an expression of fear on her small face and, unable to see anything in the dark, began to tremble even more violently.","She was trembling so much that the shadow barely made out what she said.","\"O—o—oh, D—dark One... p—please accept t —this... s—sacrifice...\"","Her voice gradually grew quieter, and then fell silent.","The shadow remained silent for a long while, then sighed inwardly.","In the end, it was forced to speak for the first time since regaining its self-awareness. The confines of the primitive human language felt alien and constricting, far inferior to the boundless expanse of its thoughts, but the shadow still forced itself to make a sound.","A cold, deep voice resounded from the darkness, making the girl freeze.","\"I refuse.\"","The girl opened her eyes wide, shocked. Her shock was so great, in fact, that it even defeated her fear.","She blinked.","\"What? W—what... do you mean?\"","Her little mind did not seem capable of comprehending the concept of a spirit — the fearsome guardian spirit of her tribe — refusing a sacrifice. That was not how the world she knew was meant to work.","The shadow did not have a head, but if it did, it would have shaken it disapprovingly.","“I never asked for such a sacrifice. Or any sacrifice, for that matter.\"","The girl drew a shaky breath.","She remained silent for a long while, and then asked in a high-pitched, tentative voice:","\"So... you... you are not going to eat me?\"","The shadow stirred.","‘Who does she think I am?'","Well... the shadow itself did not know who it was, So that was a moot question.","It answered patiently.","“No. I don't eat children.\"","Then, the shadow remembered its countless lives, and felt compelled to add:","\"...Anymore.\"","The girl did not seem convinced.","In fact, she seemed to be in disbelief.","\"Really?\"","The shadow let out a heavy sigh.","“Really.\"","The girl still appeared to have doubts.","“Really, really?\"","The shadow suppressed a groan.","It considered its words for a short while, unaware that its silence made the girl tremble even more.","Eventually, thinking that it had found a way to placate the child, the shadow spoke.","“Of course. You can trust me.\"","Then, following an impulse, it added:","\"I am the most honest shadow in the world, after all. Two worlds, even.\""]},{"number":3165,"title":"Chapter 3165 Lost Shadow","paragraphs":["The shadow's words seemed to work - to a degree, at least, because the girl eventually stopped trembling. She still seemed frightened, trying to stay as motionless as possible... but a child was a child.","Soon enough, she grew bored and restless. Looking around with an expression of curiosity - a senseless gesture, since she could not see anything in the darkness, the girl spoke in a brighter tone.","\"My name is Tatal. I'm this many years old.\" She raised a hand, proudly showing the darkness her five tiny fingers.","The shadow did not respond. What did it care what this human child was called, let alone how old she was?","The girl did not seem to understand its reluctance to engage in a conversation, though, and asked after growing uncomfortable with the silence.","\"What is your name, Dark One?\"","The shadow frowned.","It did not care what it was called, either. But since the girl asked, the shadow tried to remember.","Its names were as countless as its past lives, the sea of them vast and meaningless. Eventually, its cold voice resounded from the darkness once more:","\"I've been called by countless names in the past, in countless places. None of them have any meaning anymore, so... you can simply call me Shadow.\"","The girl turned her head this way, then another, as if trying to determine where the shadow's voice was coming from. Her attempts were futile, though, since it came from all directions.","She scrunched her face in confusion, then asked tentatively:","\"Are you... are you hiding somewhere in the darkness, Shadow?\"","The shadow was amused.","\"No\"","It paused, then added a helpful explanation.","\"I am the darkness.\"","The girl trembled again.","She remained silent for a long while, then suddenly asked in a curious tone:","\"Shadow God's name is Shadow. Aren't you afraid that he will get angry at you for stealing his name?\"","Hearing the question, the shadow felt something stir in the depths of its soul. It was an old, vague memory - a memory of a life it had lived once, a long time ago. Perhaps the very first it had been forced to endure in this cruel, never-ending nightmare.","The shadow remembered a chilling cold, the rattling of chains, and the pain of shackles biting into the tattered skin of its wrists. Step, step, another step... someone had asked something similar of it back then, all those many years ago - in the distant future.","What had it responded with?","The shadow stirred and spoke, its voice distant:","\"Why should I be afraid of a half-forgotten, weakling god?\"","Shadow God was dead, anyway.","All of them were, even if they were alive and well, terrifying the shadow with the unfathomable magnitude of their existence.","'Nothing makes sense...'","Feeling unpleasant, the shadow turned its thoughts away from the contradictory nature of its strange existence.","The girl seemed very impressed by its absent-minded statement.","\"Because gods are scary!\"","The shadow smiled in the darkness.","Of course, they were. There was nothing more terrifying than the gods, but it did not fear Shadow God's anger. If the God of Peace were to get angry over something, it wouldn't be something as trifling as the shadow using his name. The shadow was a far greater being than the tribesmen, but to one of the gods, its existence must have seemed just as fleeting and insignificant as theirs were to it.","The little girl, however, did not understand it. How could she? Even the shadow could not fathom the gods, so a mundane child - and the old man who had pushed her into the cave, as well, would not even understand what it was they were failing to imagine.","So, the tribesmen comprehended the gods in the only way they could muster, by projecting their own small and primitive way of existing on them. An unfathomable being was indescribably terrifying, but a being that was exactly like them, just far more powerful, was merely frightening.","Such a being could be reasoned with, after all, as far as the tribesmen were concerned. Ironically enough, the shadow itself had somehow ended up in the same category of beings as the gods. That was why the tribesmen had been trying to please it with presents, leaving the items they saw as desirable on the altar... fruit, meat, drinks - something that all humans would want, since all humans knew hunger and thirst.","The shadow did not quite understand the reason the old man had decided to sacrifice a small child to it. Or, rather, it did not want to understand... it had a feeling that understanding the reason would not bring it any joy.","Perhaps it was simply because the girl was precious to the old man, and so he decided that the thing he held most dear would please the shadow a great deal, as if it had an inherent value.","Or maybe he simply believed that the shadow was no different from the Creatures of Corruption and Awakened beasts populating the forests, and had a taste for human flesh.","It probably didn't occur to him that the shadow had not eaten or drunk anything since the world was created, since it simply had no need or desire to.","'What a bother.'","The shadow sighed.","It considered the girl for a while, pondering what to do with her.","Eventually, the cold voice resounded from the darkness once more, sounding a little different.","\"Why did the old man bring you to my cave?\"","The girl hesitated, then said quietly, her voice carrying a hint of both pride and sorrow that she could not quite understand yet - the sorrow of being betrayed by someone you trusted.","\"Grandpa used to be the strongest hunter of our tribe. But now, there are too few Awakened among us, and he's old. He says that his journey to the Shadow Realm is drawing near... so, he has to make sure that you'll watch over the tribe once he's gone, Dark One. Uh, I mean... Shadow\"","The shadow studied the girl with regret. One's childhood ended when they lost their trust in adults. For this human child, that moment had come far too soon.","The shadow did not know why, but it felt sad.","Eventually, it spoke from the darkness, sounding tired:","\"Go home, child.\"","Its voice was as cold as before, but now, there was a hint of emotion in it.","\"Go home and give your people my message.\"","Tatal blinked a few times.","\"W-what message?\"","The darkness around her stirred, and then the cold voice spoke again.","This time, it felt like it was resounding from somewhere closer.","\"Tell them that if they bring me a human sacrifice again...\"","Even though Tatal was sitting on cold stones, suddenly, it felt as if she was being embraced by the shadows... drowning in them.","The shadow's embrace felt peaceful.","As she sensed the world shifting around her, Tatal heard the last of its words.","\"I will kill them all.\"","In the next moment, somehow, she was not in the vast cave anymore.","Instead, she was in the heart of the village, having appeared there in the blink of an eye.","The light of day was harsh and blinding, and her visit to the dark cave seemed like a strange, frightening dream."]},{"number":3166,"title":"Chapter 3166 Color of War","paragraphs":["Having sent the child away, and hoping that the tribesmen would not disturb it again, the shadow returned to its usual state of half-slumber.","It had already thrown the little girl, as well as her grandfather, out of its mind... however, for some reason, the shadow felt restless.","The peaceful state of being one with the world was not coming.","Instead, the shadow kept returning to the moment when it remembered a fragment from one of its past lives - the life of the ignorant man who had spoken about Shadow God with contempt, only to leave for the Realm of Shadows hours later.","That man had been a child once, as well. The shadow remembered...","In that life, he had been fortunate.","He had been fortunate because he was born in the glorious Empire.","The Empire stretched across countless realms, encompassing myriad people. It did not need a name, because there had never been another one like it - and there would never be, since the Empire was eternal. It was eternal because it was not ruled by mortal monarchs or even Supreme demigods, but by the Dragon himself.","The Dragon, who was War.","From his throne at the heart of the Empire, a sea of red flowed across the mortal realms, bringing progress and prosperity to all... all who survived the death and destruction it carried.","It was an empire of war, of conquest, of life - and, most of all, glory.","Glory! Glory! Glory!","He remembered watching victorious soldiers return from war as a young child, held tightly in his mother's arms. The roar of the crowd was like a palpable force, and as it made the glass in the windows tremble, he felt his entire body vibrate with excitement.","He remembered awe.","And most of all, he remembered knowing that this awe would be directed at him one day, as well. That knowledge filled his young and inexperienced heart with an insatiable, untamed, wondrous longing.","Not all born in the Empire were equal. How could they be when there were gods walking among them? The Dragon sat on his towering throne, served by the Four Spirits - the Spirit of Victory, the Spirit of Beauty, the Spirit of Art, and the Spirit of Joy.","There used to be six Spirits watching over the Empire, but two had perished in the war against the Jade Court - the only war the Empire had ever lost - while the seventh was said to have not been born yet.","Below the pantheon of the Empire were the seven Supremes who managed its vast expanse and ruled over its provinces. Those who served the Supremes, as well as Transcendent champions of its unstoppable legions, held a noble status among the people - they were the aristocracy and priesthood of the Empire.","Below them were the citizens, among whom the warriors were the most privileged class. Those born in the outer provinces were not afforded citizenship, but still retained the lofty status of imperial subjects - and could elevate themselves with meritorious deeds.","And finally, below everyone, there were slaves.","The slaves were everywhere in the Empire, but had no rights or status - even the lowest of free men was a person, while the slaves were not.","The shadow had been born a citizen, which was already an enviable fate. More than that, his father was a soldier, just like his father's father before - as such, his family enjoyed many privileges. Of course, they were not Awakened, who were the true elites... still, theirs was a prosperous and comfortable life, full of delights and boons that only people of the Empire could enjoy. But even faced with a life of prosperity, he never felt satisfied.","That was because somewhere deep within his bones, that roar of the crowd was still echoing and reverberating, making his blood boil.","Glory! Glory! Glory!","He longed for glory.","And so, as soon as he was old enough, he followed in his father's footsteps and became a soldier.","A war soon followed, and in its bloody throes, drunk and blinded by the clangor of metal...","He stumbled on a horrifying truth.","There was no glory to war. There was no valor. There was no honor to be found, either.","There was only avarice, lust, and stagnation. There was only... plunder.","The realm he and his fellow soldiers had been sent to subjugate was a peaceful one. Its people tried to offer some resistance, but how could they resist the Empire? Their cities burned. Their temples burned as well. Their rulers - the royals and the oracles - were slaughtered.","Those who survived were sold as slaves. The riches of the peaceful realm were gathered and sent as tribute back to the heartland. The soldiers all received their share, too.","At the end of it all, he finally received what he had been dreaming of all his life. A triumph. The legions returned home and were met by a roaring crowd, the ground shaking from the deafening cheers.","But listening to it did not bring him pride or pleasure.","Instead, he only felt a bitter, scathing emptiness.","He had earned quite a sum during his long years of service, and was awarded even more after returning to the embrace of the empire and leaving the legion. It was enough to spend the rest of his life in comfort... if one lived sensibly.","But he did not, could not. He did not want to. Abandoning his devotion to the Spirit of Victory, he dedicated himself instead to pursuing the worship of the Spirit of Joy... the Spirit of Revelry.","Years passed in the haze of taverns, brothels, and gambling dens. His money slowly dwindled in the storm of debauchery, but he didn't care. He only cared about chasing the next thrill, the next pleasure, the next delight - anything at all, just to forget everything. Just to drown out the mocking call of glory that still lived there, somewhere, deep in his bones.","His pursuit of revelry continued until he had no coin left at all. In fact, he was deeply in debt, with no way to repay it.","And that was how he ended up being sold as a slave.","He was tall and broad-shouldered, and a former soldier at that. Years of debauchery had not managed to weaken his body one bit. So, his first master had a lofty goal of making him a gladiator and earning a small fortune in the arena.","He had performed well there, indeed. But while other gladiators were content with their lot in life - battle slaves led quite a privileged existence, after all, enjoying more boons and pleasures than many of the citizens - he did not care about it one bit. He did not care about himself.","So, after several fights, he beat his master black and blue, stopping short of killing the bastard only out of revulsion.","As it turned out, even slaves had somewhere lower to fall.","He changed several owners after that, acting disobediently and violently each time. In the end, that earned him the very worst fate - being sold as an imperial slave, to be used as cannon fodder in the next campaign. Only the worst of the worst, those who held no other value or had committed crimes worthy of execution, earned that gruesome fate.","He did not mind. In fact, he was a little glad, thinking that this entire farce would finally end soon.","As he was escorted across the empire in shackles, he remembered his childhood. He remembered his mother's arms, and the crowd welcoming the soldiers back with cries of glory.","He did not want glory anymore.","But, funnily enough...","Even after throwing his life away, shackled, half-dead from the cold, and being dragged to what would almost surely become his death...","He still wanted to live.","He was amused to realize that he still desperately wanted to survive. He was willing to cling to life with all his might, determined to never let go.","Perhaps that was why the Empire was eternal. Not because it was ruled by the God of War... but because the Dragon was also the god of Life.","He walked, shivering from the cold and hoping that the caravan would stop for the night somewhere protected from the wind. What were these bastards thinking, dragging the slaves onto the mountain? Every soldier worth a coin knew that marching in the cold without proper equipment was a death warrant. Did they not care how many slaves would actually make it to the destination?","As he looked ahead, at the jagged peak of a lonesome mountain that cut the sky with its sharp edges, the chain rattled. Someone suddenly shouted from behind him:","\"You little shit! I'm going to kill you!\"","He chuckled darkly.","The boy chained behind him was gaunt and weak, stumbling already. There was no need to waste air shouting at the poor waif.","He spoke, wishing for the loudmouth behind him to shut up.","\"Why bother? The weakling will be dead by sunrise anyway. The mountain will kill him.\"","A few seconds later, he added:","\"It'll kill you and me, too. Just a bit later. I really don't know what the Imperials are thinking, forcing us into this cold.\"","The loudmouth continued to spout rubbish, but a few moments later, a more composed voice resounded from behind:","\"This mountain pass is usually much warmer this time of year. We just had really bad luck. Also, I would advise you against harming this boy.\"","He turned his head, mildly curious.","\"Why is that?\"","The older slave chained behind the loudmouth gestured forward.","\"Haven't you seen the markings on his skin? He is not like us, who fell into slavery due to debts, crimes, or misfortune. He was born a slave. A temple slave, to be precise. Not long ago, the Imperials destroyed the last temple of the Shadow God. I suspect that this is how the boy ended up here.\"","Shadow God...","He hesitated, suddenly uncomfortable. There used to be a god like that... there still was, probably. People of the Empire served the greatest god of all, though - War God, so they had no reason to concern themselves with the rest of them. Especially one as weak and obscure as Shadow.","There were no temples of Shadow God left anywhere in the world, which spoke volumes about what kind of deity that god was.","He scoffed.","\"So what? Why should we be afraid of a half-forgotten, weakling god? He couldn't even save his own temples.\"","The old man was worse than the loudmouth. His voice sounded intelligent, but he spoke foolish things.","The caravan continued climbing the mountain. The cold continued to torture them and bite into their bodies. The winds continued to howl.","Eventually, they made camp. He tried to get as close to the fire as he could, finding comfort in its warmth. He ate the pitiful morsels the soldiers gave them.","He was still alive.","But then, there was a deafening sound of a crash as something gargantuan fell from the cliffs and landed in the middle of the camp. When the snow settled, he saw that thing, his eyes widening in horror...","The creature had two stumpy legs, an emaciated, hunched torso, and disproportionately long, multi-jointed hands - two of them, each ending with a set of horrifying bone claws, and another two, these ones shorter, ending with almost human-like fingers. It was covered in fur, yellowish-grey and ragged, thick enough to stop arrows and swords.","On its head, five milky, white eyes regarded the slaves with insect-like indifference. Beneath them, a terrible maw crowded with razor-sharp teeth was half-open, as though in anticipation. Viscous drool was running down the creature's chin and dripping into the snow.","And there were strange shapes endlessly moving, worm-like, under the creature's skin.","He froze.","'N-no...'","A Creature of Corruption... it was a Creature of Corruption, and a powerful one at that.","It was death.","'Move! I must move!'","He wanted to live. He still desperately wanted to live... everyone else could die, but he had to survive. There were so many things he regretted. So many things he could still do...","He tried to move away from the creature, but it was already too late.","Something flashed in the air, and suddenly, he felt lighter.","His vision grew blurry.","The snow was painted red.","Red... like the proud banners of the Empire. Like the glorious color of war.","Glory! Glory! Glory!","'Move, I must... move...'","There was no pain.","He fell down, and the dark expanse of the night sky swallowed his vision.","Growing darker and darker with each moment.","Like a vast, impossible shadow.","That was the last thing he saw.","...Deep in the cave, the shadow let out a sigh.","'Why do people love life so much?'","What was so lovable about its vicious, cruel splendor?","Perhaps it was simply in their nature. They were the Creatures of the Flame, after all... the Flame of Desire.","And the desire to be alive was the most ancient and powerful of all."]},{"number":3167,"title":"Chapter 3167 A Small Memento","paragraphs":["The boundless black sky was the last thing that the lost soldier had seen in his bitter, senseless life.","However, that was not the end of it.","The man had lived for a minute or two more... what had been the man, at least... and the shadow had lived those minutes with him. However, it did not want to remember those last moments — they were a vessel of Corruption, after all, and the shadow had no desire to feel the seeds of darkness bloom in its soul again.","Uprooting them was quite a hassle.","It remained motionless, hidden in the depths of the cave, the vivid memories of a past life still echoing in its mind. Everything about that life was so vibrant, so sharp, so stark... so different from its current peaceful existence. The shadow did not want to suffer the sharpness of life anymore.","And yet, it could not help but remember.","The lost soldier had disdained Shadow God, thinking that a deity who would allow its temples to burn was not worthy of reverence. There was no trace of the Shadow cult left in the vast and glorious Empire, after all.","However, he failed to realize that the Empire of War, while great and splendid, existed only in the world of the living... and life was nothing but a fleeting dream in the face of death.","Death was eternal, after all.","A life that spanned a scattering of years or the eternity of death... which one seemed insignificant? And why would Shadow God care about the fact that those who served War had forgotten their reverence for him, if their lives in the Empire were merely a brief stop on the way to the Realm of Shadows?","The shadow sighed.","It understood death better than the lost soldier had. And yet, it still couldn't forget the fleeting brilliance of life.","And so, uninvited, the memories of another life — one very similar to the first one, but also entirely different — surfaced from the deep ocean of its vague, fragmented memories.","In that life, he had been unfortunate. He was unfortunate because he was born at the periphery of the Empire, in one of the distant lands the legions of War had conquered.","The people who lived there were subjects of the Empire, but they were not its citizens. The glamour and splendor of the imperial heartland was like a myth to them, and they spent their lives toiling not to starve.","He came from a family of serfs. They did not own the land they farmed, and most of what they harvested was taken away by the governor of a nearby fortress. They weren't slaves, of course — they were free men and women. The distance between them and those wearing a collar was as vast as the sea.","At least that was what they told themselves, looking at the slaves tending the land of rich folks with disdain.","He did not know how vast the sea was, anyway. He had never seen the sea... in fact, he had never seen anything beyond his family's small plot of land and the nearby village.","Still, it wasn't a bad life. It might have been harsh and full of hard labor, but they rarely went hungry. He and his siblings might have all shared a small room, but at least they slept on soft mats, not on rough straw.","All of them, except for the youngest ones, woke up at dawn to help their father in the field. Their mother would already have their breakfast ready, and after eating their fill and thanking her, they left through the flimsy door of their modest home.","The door was painted red, and there was a silver bell hanging above the porch. When the wind blew, it rang beautifully.","In the moments of sweet leisure, that ringing accompanied him.","But, still...","He wanted more.","He had not even known that he wanted more, or what it meant to want anything, until he saw the soldiers march one day. Their plot was situated near the imperial road, and once in a while, the legionnaires would march past it, a river of red banners billowing above them.","He was small and weak. Toiling in the soil, he was covered in mud. His clothes were rough and colorless, threadbare, while his body was gaunt and frail. The soldiers, however...","The imperial soldiers were everything he was not.","They were tall and mighty. Their garments were painted with vibrant dye, and their armor glistened brilliantly in the sun. To a serf child like him, they were the epitome of wonder, of brilliance... of pride.","Of the Empire.","He became obsessed with everything having to do with the Empire after seeing the soldiers for the first time. Opportunities to learn were few and far between in the remote corner of the province, but there were still stories and legends. There were still wandering priests telling myths about the Spirits of the Empire.","It was from that that he learned about the valiant Spirit of Victory, the guardian deity of soldiers, who was a descendant of the Dragon and a warrior of unmatched skill.","He learned about the Spirit of Beauty, the Sacred Maiden, as well — the deity of perseverance, harvests, and motherhood.","The Spirit of Art, whose brilliance and ingenuity ensured the prosperity of the Empire, was the patron of all craftsmen and artisans.","And finally, there was the Spirit of Joy — the carefree deity of festivity and merrymaking.","He learned about the Supremes who ruled the Empire, too — the High Priests and Priestesses of the Cult of War. Each of them was a famed hero whose deeds had long become legends.","How wondrous they were, how marvelous... how dreamlike.","And, of course, there was the Dragon.","The Dragon, who dwelled atop a great tower in the heart of the Empire — a tower so tall that it scratched the sky and imposed on the realm of Sun God.","The Dragon, a living vessel of War God, had founded the Empire and oversaw it in its early years. He still watched over his subjects from his empyrean throne, his fearsome gaze scaring other deities and the Creatures of Corruption away.","Of course, War God did not rule the Empire personally anymore. The days of gods walking the earth were long over, left in the mythical Ages of Gods and Heroes.","This was a golden age — the Age of Humans.","But, of course...","Watching the glorious soldiers march past the small farm, he couldn't help but imagine that, one day... just perhaps... he could become a hero, too.","Time passed, and he grew from a boy into a young man. His family's small home seemed even smaller now, and the plot of land they toiled on seemed even more pathetic.","So, in the end, going against the wishes of his parents, he left in hopes of joining the imperial legion.","The wind was strong on the day he abandoned home. As he walked away, leaving his parents and siblings behind, the ringing of the silver bell pursued him like a sonorous song... following an impulse, he took it off the strings and placed it with his things.","He was lucky. Usually, it wasn't easy for someone like him — an untrained youth from a remote outer province — to join the great and glorious imperial army. But the Empire was gearing up for a new campaign, and so, the legions needed fresh bodies.","The competition for a spot in one of the legions was still fierce — how could it not be, when becoming a soldier promised not only riches and glory, but also a direct path to becoming a citizen? — but he performed well in front of the recruiters. His frame was tall, as well, and he was no stranger to hard work.","And so, his new life as a soldier began.","At first, he often missed home. The bell he carried in his pack reminded him of the warm days of his childhood... of his mother's touch, of his siblings laughing. Of a brighter, more innocent time. At night, he would hold it tightly and remember the past.","But as time went on, he reached for the bell less and less. Its ringing didn't sound sweet to him anymore... instead, he grew to enjoy the ringing of sharp steel.","Surviving his first war was a challenge. The second... he was seasoned by then, having become a tempered blade of the Empire. The third one was when he had proven himself and was elevated to the rank of centurion.","The army gave him what he had always felt he lacked — the right to hold his head high. To be proud of himself. To know that he was an important part of something great and fearsome.","Of something glorious.","He had left his family behind, but the Empire replaced it. The Spirits were his parents, and the fellow soldiers were his siblings. Out there on the battlefield, he never felt alone.","Sadly, there wasn't always war.","The Empire had existed for a thousand years already, and there were few places where its legions hadn't reached.","The barbarous, inferior wretches that populated them lacked the courage to offer proper resistance.","Building pathways to previously unconquered realms took time and resources.","At best, the soldiers would be sent to suppress an occasional uprising in one of the newer provinces. At worst, they were left to rot and die of boredom in the fortresses, with no opportunity to elevate themselves in battle or engage in the many pleasures of war.","His dreams of becoming a hero had been crushed, as well. Despite all the years that had passed, he wasn't even close to becoming an Awakened. And so, his career prospects grew dim.","Even though he tried to crush the dark thoughts, at times, he couldn't help but feel bitter. He couldn't help but resent who was better than him, younger than him... stronger than him.","And yet, his devotion to the Spirit of Victory and to the Dragon, as well as to the Empire itself, never wavered. In fact, it only became more fanatical.","He wasn't young by then, and had accumulated plenty of merit. If he wanted to, he could retire and live a comfortable life in the heartland of the Empire as its citizen — in fact, many of his comrades already had.","...Soon, it was most of them.","But the thought of retiring from the soldier's life had never even crossed his mind. Even when his hair turned grey, and his body began to falter, he remained stalwart in his devotion to serving the Empire.","Because the Empire was his god.","It was also because he didn't know anything except the harsh embrace of the imperial legions. The world outside his service was strange and unfamiliar. Everything had changed, at some points... the roads he marched on, the cities he encountered, the people he met. All of it was new, and it felt like the world was passing him by. Had already left him behind, lost in the dust. Only the Spirits and the Dragon remained the same, like the axis of the world.","He loved them for it.","Retiring? Living comfortably in some peaceful town? Starting a family of his own and nursing children?","He had no desire for such life. He had no interest in the softness of soil. All he desired was the harshness of steel.","Eventually, his age caught up with him, and the kind of orders he received changed. That was how he ended up leading a caravan that escorted shackled convicts — the lowest of the low, each and every one of them.","Despicable slaves...","The mission wasn't too difficult for a seasoned veteran like him. Apart from keeping the slaves in check and teaching the new recruits not to get cozy with them, there wasn't much to do. Still, he maintained his vigilance.","He always did.","He had participated in the suppression of a slave rebellion once or twice, after all. These lowlifes outnumbered him and his soldiers ten to one — he knew all too well what happened when wicked thoughts entered their bestial heads, and he knew how easily those iron shackles came off.","The real chain that bound them — the only one that could — was not made from iron. It was made from fear. It was made from surrender and submission, so he made sure to keep the slaves from thinking about anything else but his whip.","Still, even his vigilance had a limit.","The danger came from an unexpected source. It was not the disobedient slaves, road bandits, or even the elements — it came from higher up the mountain, taking the shape of a ghastly Creature of Corruption.","He knew that this would be where he died the moment he saw the beast.","The imperial legions were no strangers to fighting the Corrupted, of course, and he had participated in his fair share of battles against these insidious foes. So, he immediately knew that the beast was of a high Class... he and his mundane soldiers could have handled a Beast or two, perhaps even a Monster. But this creature?","It was death.","Still, he wasn't going to give up without a fight.","If he was to die, he was going to die while holding a sword, like he had all his life.","He was going to die hearing the clangor of steel.","The battle was short.","At the end of it all, he found himself lying in the snow. He didn't remember how he had gotten there, or what had happened to his soldiers.","There was no strength in his body. He couldn't move.","He was so cold.","He was cold and alone, surrounded by silence. All he could see was the night sky, and the snowflakes drifting slowly from the boundless darkness above.","He was dying.","It took all his remaining strength to turn his head. Out there, in the snow, he noticed the hilt of his sword. The blade was broken, but it was still a sword... his sword...","It was a sword of the Empire, just like he was.","He tried to reach for it, but his hand didn't move.","‘Must... must...’","He had to take it. He had to... he wanted to... die while holding that familiar hilt.","But it was of no use.","He grew desperate. He grew weak.","His thoughts turned slow and cold, just like the bloodied world.","He reached for the sword harder than for anything ever before...","But, still, his hand refused to move.","Angry tears moistened his eyes, growing cold in the frigid air.","Then, a shadow fell on him.","Moving his eyes, he saw a gaunt boy standing above him, his pale face expressionless. In the pale moonlight, his skin looked like pure alabaster, and his dark eyes were like two pieces of obsidian.","For a moment, he was frightened that it was Death. He was scared that Shadow God had come to take him to the lightless realm, broken and unarmed... no different from the wretched slaves that had died on the slope of the mountain while trying to run away from the beast.","No, no...","The boy was merely one of the slaves.","The wretch was still alive, having come to gloat.","He gritted his teeth, wanting to feel fury. Wanting to curse the pathetic worm.","But he was too tired. He was too cold to feel anything.","Even his despair was gone. All that was left was a sense of weakness and resignation. His life was like a candle's flame, ready to go out.","He stared at the boy, and the boy studied him silently.","Then, the boy knelt beside him and picked up the broken sword.","Reaching down, the boy raised one of his unfeeling hands, placed the hilt into it, and put it on his chest.","He found some strength to grip the hilt tightly, looking at the boy with surprise. And gratitude.","Expressionless, the boy let go of his hand and stood. Then, turning away, he disappeared into darkness.","There was silence then.","He lay in the snow, gripping his sword tightly, breathing his last breaths.","Death was coming.","‘Sword... my... sword...’","His sword was finally in his hand, but at that moment, for some reason, he didn't feel like he had missed its touch.","Instead, he remembered a different weight. The modest weight of a silver bell he had held often, a long time ago.","‘Right... the bell...‘","When had he lost it?","He didn't remember.","He had not thought about that thing for years, but now that it was gone, he suddenly felt its absence.","He could almost hear its ringing.","Its sweet ringing...","As it swayed in the wind on a sunlit porch. Now, there was only silence left.","Only darkness.","The sword fell from his motionless hand.","...The shadow surfaced from the torrent of memories, feeling like it had been drowning.","At some point, without thinking about it, it had taken a shape.","That shape was rough and vague, but still resembled a human.","The clear ringing of the silver bell echoed in his mind.","He felt like he could almost touch it...","Looking down, at his black hand, the shadow was surprised to see a small silver bell lying in his palm, having appeared there as if by magic.","‘Where did...’","He frowned in confusion, then raised the small silver bell and studied it closely. Then, following a strange impulse, the shadow rang it."]},{"number":3168,"title":"Chapter 3168 Azure Sky","paragraphs":["The clear ringing of the bell resounded in the dark cave, straining to escape it. The shadow willed it to stay within the stone walls of his shelter, sensing the sound reverberating through him.","As a peculiar vibration was born in his chest, he remembered.","The courtyard of a dark, magnificent temple that stood under a lightless sky. The rustle of leaves washing over him as a towering tree swayed gently in the wind. The laughter of a young woman who sat on the ground, enjoying a lavish picnic...","The memory came and went, leaving behind a lasting ache. The shadow did not like the feeling, so he put the silver bell down and collapsed back into his natural, formless state.","Fleeing from it.","His thoughts were heavy.","What had come over him, anyway? Taking the form of a human... who would want to be a ghastly being like that?","It was the memories of the two men who died on the slopes of the lonesome mountain, no doubt. The two of them had lived similar lives, but went down entirely different paths. By the end, the gap separating them was as wide as the abyss. And yet, they died on the same day, with only a few meters between them, their blood mixing in the snow.","The shadow remembered being those men. He remembered being the abomination who had slain them, as well.","He even remembered being the worm who had created the abomination, using the mind of a distrustful king as its chrysalis. All those lives, all those deaths... they were there, hidden in the depths of the shadow's mind.","But he did not want to recall them.","So, instead, the shadow cast his senses far and wide, so that the empty state of being fused with the world erased his thoughts. So that he could forget.","Oblivion was the only solace to those who were denied death, it seemed.","Time passed, but no matter how much the shadow tried to return to his previous peaceful non-existence, fragments of memories kept creeping into his mind.","He remembered...","Living as a soldier in a lightless land. The world was besieged by darkness, and in its cold embrace, those who still lived had to fight desperately to survive. He fought for the right to exist, as well...","He was a warrior of the Starlight Legion.","His people were led by seven great heroes who had risen to the heights of power in the endless war against the darkness... as well as the awful beings that dwelled under its tenebrous veil. Under their guidance, the humans slowly pushed the detestable creatures back, coming together to build an impregnable city in the heart of the forsaken land.","The gods were dead, so they had no one to pray to. The sun was gone, so there was nothing to illuminate their path. Even the stars had vanished from the sky, having fallen down like flaming tears.","He did not know what the sun looked like, since he had been born after the darkness devoured the world. He did not know what the stars looked like, either. But he had heard the stories... he had dreamed countless times about their distant radiance, about the sea of silver light shining brightly in the boundless black sky.","He wanted to see the stars before he died. That was the goal of the Starlight Legion.","Death was a constant companion to the soldiers of the legion. Many of them perished on the battlefield, and few survived long enough to leave a lasting mark.","He was one of the few.","He had survived many battles, slain many abominations, and buried many comrades. The longer he lived, the stronger he became. Eventually, other soldiers came to rely on him as their brother...","But death wasn't the worst fate for those who fought under the banner of the Starlight Legion. They spent their lives surrounded by darkness, after all, and the darkness seeped into them slowly, year after year, pooling in their souls.","It began from an itch. A maddening itch that came and went, but could never be entirely chased away. Peculiar thoughts soon started to enter his mind. Sometimes, he caught himself looking at his fellow soldiers or at the civilians back home, thinking how soft their bodies were. How red their blood was.","He was thirsty.","At times, no amount of water could quench his thirst. He felt like he was burning in the middle of the desert, dying in unbearable heat.","He longed to dive into the embrace of a cold, dark sea.","One day, the itch drove him mad enough to shred his forearm in a frenzy. As drops of red, vibrant, fragrant blood fell to the floor, he froze and stared at the gruesome wound in shock and revulsion.","There was something there, hidden in the bleeding flesh.","Reaching into the wound with calloused fingers, he pulled a thin, translucent plate from within his forearm.","It was scale.","There were scales and filaments growing under his skin, propagating slowly. Shuddering, he dropped the scale, took a step back, and tried to suppress the desire to sever his entire arm.","In the end, he bandaged the wound, glanced around his tent, and thought of his modest home back in the city.","He was never going to come home again, it seemed.","Following the oaths, he reported himself to the capellan of the cohort. The rest happened quickly.","He was not the first among the warriors of the Starlight Legion to succumb to the curse of the darkness, after all — far from it. Those like him, the veterans who had been infected by the darkness, were all assigned to a special unit. They lived like lepers, isolated from the rest of the soldiers and hiding their gruesome bodies under layered bandages.","However, they were not quite useless yet. On the contrary, he and the others marked by the darkness were always the ones to take on the most perilous missions, to fight where the battle was most harrowing, to die so that the others could live.","Even if the darkness had seeped into their souls and bodies, they were its most fearsome foes. If one of them died on the battlefield, they celebrated. If one was too stubborn to be killed by the claws and fangs of detestable creatures, and the curse progressed too far... then they would bring their comrade mercy with steel blades.","That blade of his, forged from azure steel, had slain numerous monsters.","It had slain plenty of his brothers, as well... Time passed, but he still failed to die. His body was a ghastly wreck by then, and his face was not worthy of showing to a mirror. He felt like the day when his siblings of the Starlight Legion would have to deliver him a final mercy was approaching soon.","That was when their hero, the Warrior, had come to meet them.","He entrusted them with one final mission... a sacred mission. A harrowing mission that only they were fit to carry out.","On a day like any other — all days were the same in the world without a sun, after all — they came to surround a vast crowd of people. There were warriors of the legion there, but there were peaceful citizens, as well. Men and women, old and young — those whom they had sworn to protect. They surrounded the crowd.","And when the ritual began — one of the seven being carried out across the lightless land — they drew their blades and turned them on the people.","They slaughtered them all in a great hecatomb. They killed until the world itself was painted red, until their arms fell limp from exhaustion, until there was no one left alive.","Until no trace of azure remained on the surface of his loyal sword.","The Warrior was there, as well. He was the last to die, sacrificing himself on the altar of his ardent mission.","Of an oath to return light into the lightless sky.","...When everything was over, he swayed and leaned heavily on his sword, looking in a daze at the corpses littering the bloodsoaked ground. He was tired. He was overcome with sorrow.","He mourned the death of his people.","He mourned himself, as well.","And, most of all, he mourned the death of his hero.","Overcome by grief, he looked up...","And saw the sun being born in the black sky.","Ever since he was a child, he had heard countless descriptions of the sun. He knew that it was round. He knew that it was so bright as to appear white — like the purest of flames. He knew that it illuminated the world, making colors vivid and all things clear.","But no description could have prepared him for how brilliant the sun was.","For how beautiful the world was in its blinding light.","Its radiance chased away the darkness, and suddenly, the black abyss above was not black anymore. It was a clear, vibrant blue. And below it, on the ground, the blood was suddenly unbearably red.","As he looked at the radiant sun, blinded by its incandescent brilliance, tears flowed down his face.","\"A star... it is a star...\"","A star was burning in the sky.","He finally saw it.","However, he did not feel joy.","He only felt shame and sorrow.","In the blinding radiance of the newborn sun, the darkness that dwelled in his soul only grew more impenetrable. All around him, his fellow soldiers suddenly convulsed and screamed.","He screamed, as well.","He fell to his knees, shrieking, his body bending and breaking.","Thick plates of chitin covered his skin, encasing him within an impenetrable carapace. Scythe-like limbs tore his flesh apart, piercing the ground like fearsome blades. His figure twisted, expanding, transforming...","Until there was nothing of him left.","The last thing he saw before the darkness swallowed him was his sword, lying in the filth on the ground, its azure blade desecrated and painted dark crimson by blood.","He knew that one day, soon, all memories of him would be erased from the world. All traces of him, and the Starlight Legion as well, would be gone, and everything they had done — both their valor and their sin — would be forgotten.","Only steel would remain.","Only steel would remember.","At the end there, he felt regret.","He thought that his poor, loyal sword deserved to forget as well..."]},{"number":3169,"title":"Chapter 3169 Dark Mosaic","paragraphs":["The shadow surfaced from the memory. But he also drowned in it.","The slave, the slave driver, the warrior of a lightless land... each of their lives was so vast, so vibrant, so intricate in its infinite complexity. Just one was enough to lose himself, and there were thousands — hundreds of thousands — of past lives crowding his tired mind.","And past deaths, as well.","The cursed legionnaire had not perished on the day the sun rose above his fallen land. An eon of Corruption followed, spent in the embrace of frenzied agony. Just as he had predicted, the civilization built on the bones of a dreadful hecatomb was eventually destroyed, and all memories of his people were erased from the world. Only Corruption remained.","But the shadow remembered.","He remembered living myriad abominable lives under the starless abyss. During the day, a radiant sun flooded the world with brilliant light. At night, a dark sea drowned it with death and destruction. Revolting creatures dwelled in that desolate hell, and the shadow had been those creatures once.","He remembered living as the cursed soldiers of the fallen legion, devouring the corpses of the creatures the sea had killed. He remembered being monstrous centipedes that hid in the coral, waiting to ambush their prey and dissolve it in virulent acid. He remembered being ghastly spiders that wove webs made of razor-sharp steel. He remembered being flesh-eating flowers that bloomed in screaming bodies and wore them as shells. harrowing vines that sprawled for hundreds of meters under the mud, ensnaring those who were unfortunate enough to step on them and dragging them into the giant maw buried deep beneath. Colonies of loathsome termites that made their nests inside the corpses of dead leviathans and slowly devoured them from within.","He remembered being a towering tree that consumed souls by luring living things with the promise of sweet fruit, then stealing their minds to force them to guard, worship, and feed it.","Each of those ghastly lives was no less vast, vibrant, and intricate than the lives of three men he had remembered. They were like a mosaic. Put together, the disjointed fragments painted an all-encompassing picture of that terrifying, starless land.","The mental picture was so detailed that the shadow felt it could encompass that hellish realm, just like his senses encompassed the land around his cave. That he could fuse with it and dissolve in its endless horror, just like he did with the mortal realm that Tatal and her people had made their home. But why would he do that?","What good would fusing with a realm devoured by Corruption do? It would only allow Corruption to swallow him, as well. The shadow did not want to remember agony.","He only wanted peace.","But those memories had a pull that was hard to resist. Once he disturbed them with his careless thoughts, they took hold of his mind and refused to let go. And so, he drowned in them... he drowned, unable to break free...","“Shadow! Shadow!\"","‘What the...'","The shadow was pulled from the ghastly sea of memories by an unreasonably loud, high-pitched voice. Dazed, he directed his gaze to the mouth of the cave and saw a familiar, tiny figure carefully making its way inside.","For a moment, he felt turned back.","‘Haven't I sent her back?'","He definitely had. And yet, here she was, demonstrably breaking the law of causality. Causality was one of the foundational laws of the universe. Not even the gods could impose on it easily... so how come the girl who was supposed to be somewhere else suddenly appeared in his cave?","There was no reasonable answer.","‘Did that old fool of a man decide to sacrifice her again?'","The only explanation the shadow could imagine was that somebody had brought the girl back. However, that didn't make much sense, either... after all, his warning was quite stark. The tribesmen would have to be complete fools to disregard it immediately.","But then again... the shadow’s sense of time was murky. He wasn't fully aware of how much of it had flown by since the moment he sent the girl back to her village. It felt like just a moment ago, but days seemed to have already passed.","\"Uh-oh!\"","Not at all aware of the inner turmoil that her appearance had caused the shadow, Tatal slid down the sloping entrance of the cave and clumsily fell to her knees.","“Ouchie...\"","She did not, however, drop the oil lamp burning in her hand.","For the first time since the birth of the world, the shadow's shelter was illuminated by the radiance of fire. He was aghast, struggling to believe that somebody would be so bold as to bring a source of light into the vast darkness of his being.","‘What... is happening?’","Tatal, meanwhile, picked herself up from the stone, dusted off her crude garments, and glanced up with a grin.","\"Shadow?\"","The shadow hesitated.","Eventually, his voice resounded from the darkness.","\"Yes?\"","The girl's smile widened, and she waved at the darkness.","\"I've come!\"","That did not dispel his confusion one bit. He remained silent for a long while, digesting her statement and getting accustomed to a candle shining within the depths of his vast and formless being.","The light of the candle was feeble, of course. If the shadow wanted to, it could extinguish it with a thought — less than that, even. But then, Tatal would stumble in the dark... making all sorts of noises...","His peace and quiet were already gone, but there were degrees to this state of unrest. Wishing to avoid having to endure even more noise, the shadow let out a mental sigh and spared the little flame.","He lingered for a moment, then spoke.","\"I see.\"","Then, after considering the situation a little more, the shadow asked:","“But why have you come?\"","Tatal blinked a couple of times, staring into the darkness with an expression of sincere surprise.","Then, her grin returned.","“Because I thought that you'd be lonely!\"","Her tone suggested that the answer should have been entirely obvious.","The shadow stared at her, utterly perplexed.","‘Aha.'","No one had brought the girl to the cave, and the law of causality had not been broken either. Instead, she was here of her own volition, having decided that the fearsome being that dwelled in the cave would be lonely there without her.","‘I shouldn't have expected a reasonable explanation. That was my mistake.'","There was some merit to Tatal's logic — he was alone in the cave, after all. It was just that her logic had nothing to do with reason...","It was little girl logic.","Since she would feel lonely living in a dark cave by herself, she assumed that Shadow would too.","Why was she concerned whether he was lonely or not, though?","The cold voice resounded from the darkness, sounding a little confused.","\"Why would you care?\"","Tatal tilted her head a little.","Then, she smiled.","“Because we're friends!\"","The shadow was flabbergasted.","‘Since when?!’","He was sure that he would have noticed making a friend.","However, the girl sounded quite confident. There was no shadow of a doubt in her voice.","So, the shadow resolved to set her straight...","Somehow, though, he failed.","That was the first time the shadow had failed at anything since the dawn of time."]},{"number":3170,"title":"Chapter 3170 Mark of Humanity","paragraphs":["\"...This is my doll! Her name is Snuggle!\"","Tatal showed the shadow the ugliest doll he had ever seen. It was made of coarse fabric and wore a crude dress that vaguely resembled Tatal's own. Two black beads served as its eyes, and its mouth seemed to be stuck in a perpetual frown.","Tatal was not the kind of girl to play with her toys gently, either. It looked like Snuggle had been torn countless times, then mended with clumsy stitches. As a result, she looked like a battle-hardened warrior covered in countless gruesome scars, not an innocent damsel's companion.","This was the first doll the shadow had ever seen — in this life, at least — and it was nearly unbearable to look at.","Still, Tatal seemed utterly in love with the ugly thing, so he kept his thoughts to himself.","\"Say hi to Snuggle, Shadow!\"","The girl grinned happily.","“What is your favorite berry, Shadow? Mine is raspberry. My second favorite is mulberry. But I like wild strawberry, blueberry, cranberry, and elderberry too! Oh, and winterberry. You'll get a tummy ache if you eat those, but they're pretty!\"","The shadow had not known that there were this many types of berries. The only ones he knew were either poisonous or twisted by Corruption. So, he did not like berries much.","The shadow remained silent for a while. When he eventually spoke, his cold voice sounded a little strained...","\"I don't like berries.\"","Tatal stared at the darkness, aghast.","She was scandalized.","\"N—not... not even raspberries?\"","The shadow had no idea what a raspberry was. Was that a berry that made your voice sound raspy if you ate it, or a berry that talked in a raspy voice? The former was strange, while the latter felt concerning.","He considered his answer for a long time...","“I can count to ten! Twenty, if I am not wearing shoes. How high can you count, Shadow?\"","The shadow was not sure what shoes had to do with counting — in fact, he could not even imagine an answer. Still, he felt obligated to answer.","“As high as I want.\"","\"Can you count to a hundred?\"","\"Yes.\"","“How about a thousand?\"","\"Yes.\"","“How about a ten thousand?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Wow!\"","Tatal looked into the darkness with admiration. Then, her little face suddenly scrunched into an expression of grave suspicion, and after staying quiet for a few moments, she said somberly:","“Prove it, then. Count to ten thousand.\"","The shadow was baffled.","\"What?\"","\"Then do it. You aren't lying to me, are you?\" The shadow felt the desire to start an earthquake.","\"I am not lying.”","\"Then do it!\"","\"I won't.\"","\"Ha! Liar!\"","\"l am not a liar... I am a very honest shadow. I haven't lied once since the dawn of time.\"","\"Then do it!\"","\"I said I won't...\"","Tatal's visits all went something like that. She came every once in a while after that first time, entirely ignoring the fact that the friend she had made was a disembodied mass of darkness that had dwelled in the ominous cave since the creation of the world.","The peace and quiet the shadow longed for were entirely obliterated. The antics of the carefree human child left him baffled, exasperated, and mentally exhausted every time. When his vast consciousness collided with Tatal's simple and impossibly straightforward worldview, unbelievably enough, it was the former that was left bruised and damaged.","The shadow had never wanted to be human, but as a result of Tatal unceremoniously invading his world, he could not help but feel more and more of her humanity leaving a mark on him.","That mark of humanity was not at all what the shadow enjoyed, let alone wanted.","But, at the same time...","He much preferred Tatal's company to that of all the other humans living in the settlement. Those who came to make offerings all wore strange garments and performed inexplicable rituals. They were full of a solemn sense of importance, fear, and reverence.","They treated the shadow as a fearsome deity... while not really understanding what a deity was.","The shadow disliked their worship much more than Tatal's complete lack of deference. In fact, her casual demeanor was not that unpleasant — unlike the veneration of the older members of her tribe.","Like that, time passed.","Seasons changed, and then changed again, killing the world and bringing it back to life once more. The shadow spent his time observing the lands surrounding his cave. He failed to reach the state of complete fusion with the world again, but it was still enough to bring his tired soul a sense of peace.","He remembered fragmented pieces of his past lives from time to time, as well, but he had never drowned in them again. His unwilling connection with Tatal prevented him from losing his sense of self too thoroughly, and as a result, it slowly grew firmer.","The human tribe, meanwhile, was developing swiftly. The forest retreated even further back, and their fields expanded. They were beginning to domesticate animals other than dogs and learning new crafts every day.","The Creatures of Corruption did not bother the tribe due to the presence of the shadow, and while they faced the hunger and fury of the beasts that populated the forest from time to time — both mundane and mythical — they had not faced anything powerful enough to wipe them out yet.","They had even established contact with several other human tribes dwelling in the neighboring lands. There was some tension between them, but overall, they all seemed to prefer trade and exchange over plundering and bloodshed.","More children were born, and the village grew.","The shadow observed the changing world indifferently.","\"Shadow! Shadow!\"","Once again, Tatal appeared at the mouth of his cave, smiling foolishly.","Only now, she wasn't a little girl anymore. In the blink of an eye, the tiny child had become a young woman on the cusp of adulthood. Her crude garments were replaced by a hunter's attire, and her ebony hair was gathered into a long braid, decorated tastefully with colorful beads and feathers.","She raised her bow triumphantly.","“Look what I caught!\"","She was dragging the carcass of a massive cave bear behind her, straining her Awakened body to pull its crushing weight. The shadow stared at the giant bear — an Ascended Beast who had been terrorizing the tribe for a few decades now — in a state of mild amusement.","“Good job. But was there really a need to drag that thing here? Are you going to eat it?\"","Dropping the paw of the cave bear, Tatal blinked a couple of times.","“Of course! The whole village will. Bear meat is not the tastiest, but you can make a stew. Its claws and teeth can be made into weapons. Its tendons will become bowstrings. The most important part is the hide, though!\"","The shadow studied the bear. It seemed that Tatal had gone an extra mile not to damage the hideous beast's hide, even though hunting an Ascended creature must have been a deadly trial for a young Awakened woman like her.","He knew it had been, of course, because he had observed every moment of her hunt carefully.","The shadow was aware of everything that happened in his land, but he rarely paid it any attention. The ruckus Tatal had created was too much to ignore, though, so this time was an exception.","\"What's so important about the hide?\"","He was not really curious, but felt like he had to ask out of politeness.","Tatal grinned.","“I'll clean it and present it as a bridal gift to my fiancé!\"","The shadow felt like his entire being froze. He did not have eyes, but if he did, one of them would have twitched.","“Your what?\"","Tatal seemed surprised. She stared at the darkness, blinked a couple of times, and then giggled.","\"What, you didn't know? I'm getting married!\"","The shadow had not, indeed, known. Perhaps he should have paid more attention."]},{"number":3171,"title":"Chapter 3171 Wedding of the Century","paragraphs":["Tatal's wedding was a grand affair...","By the standards of the nascent civilization of the Age of Gods, naturally.","The whole village participated in the preparations. The best seamstress of the tribe prepared her wedding dress; the hunters ventured deep into the forest to procure meat for the feast. A few of the daring youths robbed the nest of an Awakened queen bee and made it away with several jars of mystical honey.","The shadow had to scare the enraged creature into abandoning its plans of revenge.","The old women created an elaborate headdress, using ember, carnelian, and rubies to decorate it. An elderly craftsman carved the auspicious charm — the figurine of a ferocious wolf — from a piece of precious jade.","Special dyes were created. The shaman of a tribe spent many days preparing to officiate the ritual. The children prowled the forest, searching for sweet berries on the ground and glistening gemstones in the streams.","Usually, the tribesmen would build a home for the newlywed couple. But ever since Tatal's grandfather passed away several years ago, she had lived alone in his house — one of the largest in the village, decorated with bestial skulls and fearsome antlers.","The shadow was surprised by how much work went into ensuring that Tatal's wedding was as grand and festive as possible. Granted, she was not just any young girl — despite her youth, Tatal was special to the tribe. She was the last descendant of its most fearsome hunter, after all, and a powerful Awakened in her own right.","She had been very young when she Awakened, too — unusually so — and powerful as well. So, the elders treasured Tatal, hoping that she would grow more powerful in the future... perhaps even more powerful than her grandfather had been, and would therefore ensure the safety and prosperity of the tribe once they were gone.","And, naturally, there was the fact that she had been offered as a sacrifice to the terrifying creature that dwelled in the darkness, and was returned to the tribe alive.","So, perhaps it was no surprise that the tribe treated her wedding with such zeal. In fact, it had taken a lot to arrange the marriage itself.","By then, it was customary for the young people of neighboring tribes to marry each other. The chieftain of the tribe — its best hunter — was usually a man, while the shaman was usually a woman. The former dealt with outside threats, while the latter took care of the people, so women held more authority in the inner workings of a tribe. Therefore, the groom usually moved to live with the bride's family.","However, Tatal was not just anyone — sadly, there were no suitable young men in the neighboring tribes to become her husband. So, the elders put a lot of effort into reaching out to the far reaches of the realm, eventually finding her an outstanding groom among the youths of the Grey Wolf Tribe — a tribe of fearsome hunters that had yet to abandon its nomadic ways, wandering the vast expanse of the realm despite its many dangers.","While learning about the Grey Wolf Tribe, the shadow was also surprised to learn how Tatal's own tribe was called...","It was the Shadow Tribe.","And the reason her people were called that was none other than the shadow himself, even if he had known nothing about it.","It seemed that all tribes of humans came from a small number of great tribes who had formed a long time ago, when their ancestors left the blissful cradle of the Heart Forest.","As they spread over the mortal realms and their numbers increased, the tribes splintered — when the number of people outgrew the ability of the land to support them, someone had to leave in search of a different route in untamed wilderness. That was how humans swiftly settled most of the mortal realms, and when there was nowhere else to go, they had no choice but to settle and invent agriculture to sustain their growing population. And that, in turn, was how the shadow had ended up with his noisy, frustrating neighbors.","The ancient, great tribes were each called by the name of the guardian Spirit they worshipped. The tribe guarded by the fearsome Sacred beast, the Wolf, was called the Wolf Tribe, for example — its smaller offshoots would add an epithet to their name, one for each degree of separation from their guardian Spirit. Some of the youngest tribes would not have any name at all, having lost the connection to their deity.","That meant that the Grey Wolf tribe was old and powerful, having proven its ability to survive across dozens of generations. The Shadow Tribe, however, only had one word in its name, since there was no other group of humans protected by the shadow — it was the first of its kind.","That made its status ambiguous, so the elders had outdone themselves to secure Tatal a promising youth of the Grey Wolves. The shadow really couldn't complain.","He still wanted to, though.","‘What is she thinking about? Marriage? Too young! She's too young!’","He found himself experiencing a lot of emotions he could not quite explain. The shadow rarely felt anything that could be rightfully described as emotion, really, so it was no surprise that he could not discern his own feeling, let alone where they came from.","The greater surprise was that he felt anything at all.","Tatal... seemed happy, though, so he couldn't say anything. He wasn't entirely unhappy about whom the elders had chosen for her, either.","The Wolf. That name resonated with him, because he had been the Wolf once.","Which meant that he had killed it once, as well.","The descendants of the people who had forged a bond with the Spirit Wolf could not be terrible people. They had to be strong, at least — far stronger than Tatal's own people were.","Besides that, wolves were pack animals. They knew the value of family. So, the shadow believed that Tatal's future husband would treat her well.","And if not...","Well then, the shadow had killed the guardian Spirit of those people. Dealing with a mortal pup would be as easy as looking his way.","‘At least they had the sense to arrange a marriage with a Wolf Tribe.’","If it had been a tribe worshipping an unworthy beast, the shadow would not have stayed quiet. In fact, he would have had to put his foot down...","The shadow did not really have a foot, but the point still stood."]},{"number":3172,"title":"Chapter 3172 Little Flames","paragraphs":["The wedding came and went.","It was a splendid affair... that was what a human would have said, at least. To the shadow, it seemed like more of the strange behavior the tribesmen showcased when leaving him offerings at the mouth of the cave.","There were solemn movements. There was incoherent mumbling. The elderly shaman performed a dance... she was surprisingly energetic for a woman of her age, but somehow still retained enough stamina to offer devotions to the crude statues of the six great gods that stood in the village's small shrine.","Tatal, at least, looked beautiful in her wedding attire. With amber and carnelian sewn into the fabric and decorating her hair, she seemed like a flame... a small flame, no different from the candle she had held when visiting the shadow in his cave for the first time.","The groom... was not bad, no matter how much it pained the shadow to admit it. The youth seemed glum for a while, but after seeing Tatal for the first time, his eyes ignited with a silly kind of fervor. That mesmerized glint told the shadow that the two human children would, perhaps, be alright.","A few days after the wedding, Tatal came to his cave in high spirits.","\"Shadow!\"","She called the shadow out each time, even though his vast darkness encompassed the entire cave, and he never left.","The shadow studied the young woman for a moment. Confirming that she was in a good mood, he asked in his usual cold tone:","“What?\"","She beamed.","\"Well? Did you see him? Isn't he tall? Isn't he handsome?\"","The shadow had no sense to distinguish a handsome human from a dull one, but the boy from the Grey Wold tribe was indeed tall.","‘What's the big deal about being tall, anyway?’","The shadow was inexplicably displeased.","\"I saw.\"","He did not offer further commentary.","Tatal laughed boisterously.","“My husband is the most handsome man in the tribe! No, in the neighboring tribes as well! Even though he doesn't have a beard yet... ah, but I am sure it will grow eventually!\"","The shadow sighed.","“You humans are certainly fond of hair.\"","Tatal gave the darkness a pitying look.","“Of course. What kind of man doesn't have a beard? Let me tell you... my grandfather's beard was the thickest in the tribe. That was why he was the manliest.\"","The shadow felt like there was something wrong with that statement, but what did he know?","He didn't have a beard, either, and he wasn't really a man — he was a disembodied shadow. There was some kind of causality between the two facts, and he wasn't going to bother discerning what it was.","What he was sure of, however, was that men without beards were far more handsome and dashing. The shadow did not know where that confident opinion came from, but felt that he was right.","“I brought you hawthorn wine. Do you know what wine is, Shadow? The Grey Wolf people brought it with them. It's delicious!\"","Tatal produced a gourd and offered it to the darkness. The shadow stared at the gourd dubiously for a few moments, then answered in an indifferent tone:","\"I do know what wine is. However, I won't drink it.\"","Tatal grinned.","\"Oh, no. What a pity. We can't let this wine go to waste, though, can we?\"","With that, she retracted the ground and drank from it with a satisfied expression.","‘This vixen...'","Tatal knew perfectly well that the shadow did not eat or drink. In fact, she knew it so well that she had been secretly stuffing herself with the offerings the villagers left on his altar ever since she was a little girl. The shadow wasn't going to eat them, and the little glutton saw no reason to let all those sweet things go to waste.","Satisfied with the wine, Tatal looked around.","\"Anyway... this marriage thing. It's great!\"","She scratched the back of her head.","“Have you ever been married, Shadow?\"","As Tatal took another gulp of the wine, the shadow gave her an unamused look.","Then, he answered honestly:","“Many times.\"","He had lived hundreds of thousands of lives, after all.","Tatal spat out the wine.","\"W—what?\"","Her voice trembled.","\"What do you mean, many times? That's not allowed, Shadow! You can only marry one person, for life!\"","The shadow answered in an emotionless tone:","\"If you're human.\"","Tatal stared at the darkness, then scoffed.","\"When would you even have time to get married? You never leave your cave! You're lying again.\"","At that moment, the shadow did something he had never done before — in this lifetime, at least.","He chuckled.","His voice sounded a little amused when he spoke:","“You're right. I have no time to get married.\"","As he said that, though, he seemed to remember something.","A beautiful radiance. A reflection of white flames dancing in someone's eyes. A soothing warmth permeating his entire being...","An almost unbearable sense of longing.","The shadow was confused.","Why would a shadow like him long for light?","It didn't make any sense.","Just like Tatal and other humans never made sense.","He remained silent for a long while, then said quietly:","“Congratulations on your marriage, Tatal. I am glad that the groom is to your liking.”","She smiled.","“Thank you. I am glad too.\"","After taking another gulp of the wine, she added:","“Makes me feel like hunting that damn bear was worth it!\"","The sound of her laughter filled the cave. The shadow noticed that, somehow, he wasn't irritated by that noise anymore.","Soon, having finished the wine and gushed about her new husband enough, Tatal returned to her tribe, leaving him alone in silence.","The shadow remained motionless, quiet.","In his mind...","The reflections of the white flame were still dancing, filling his chest with an indescribable ache.","Then, however, he dispelled that strange state and settled into his usual position. Watching, waiting.","Knowing that there was nothing to wait for, and that he had already seen far too much."]},{"number":3173,"title":"Chapter 3173 Life Goes On","paragraphs":["The world moved on.","Tatal settled into her married life, and the shadow settled into his usual aloof existence. He felt the land around him change slowly. The trees reached desperately for the sky. the beasts prowled the forest, hunting those who were weaker than them while being hunted by those who were stronger.","Tatal became much busier as she matured and built her family. Her young husband proved to be a hunter of great skill and talent, effortlessly demonstrating his worth to the men of the Shadow Tribe and eventually becoming their leader. The old shaman who had officiated the wedding, meanwhile, was beginning to succumb to her age.","As a result, it was decided that Tatal would become her successor. She began her training not long after the wedding, and it consumed most of her time.","Her visits to the dark cave where the shadow dwelled slowly grew less frequent. Still, she made an effort to come at least once a month, bringing news of the outside world and chatting with him about nonsensical things that only a human could find engaging.","Then, the number of her visits reduced to once every few months or when something important happened.","That was because Tatal was with child.","Soon enough, she came to the dark cave carrying a small bundle of cloth. Nestled within the bundle was a tiny infant, its face red and wrinkly.","Tatal's own face shone with a subtle light that the shadow had not seen before, and a soft, unfamiliar smile played on her lips.","\"Look, Shadow.\"","She presented the bundle to the darkness, then gently pressed it to her chest.","\"This is my son. Isn't he lovely?\"","To the shadow, the infant looked like a strangely shaped lump of uncooked dough — ugly, to say the least. Even Snuggle had more charm than it.","However, inexplicably, he could not help but feel that the tiny human was, indeed, lovely. It was so lovely that the shadow could not express it with words.","Perhaps because the infant was a part of Tatal.","Eventually, his cold voice resounded from the darkness.","“Yes. He is beautiful.”","After becoming a mother and assuming some of the duties from the faltering old shaman, Tatal rarely had time to escape all her responsibilities and venture into the mountains to visit her reclusive friend. However, she still came once a year, every year — on the day they had first met.","The world was slowly changing. The village expanded, the forest around it replaced by fields. A master from a neighboring tribe came to build a crude stone mill. The humans learned something new every month, swiftly developing in all manner of crafts.","One year, Tatal brought with her a sharp blade. She showed it to the shadow, full of reverence.","“Look, Shadow. This is called copper. It comes from the earth, like stone... however, unlike flint, it never breaks. It never chips, never crumbles. It can pierce the toughest hide while remaining whole. Is it not a miracle?\"","Even though Tatal was performing the role of a shaman now, in her heart, she was still a hunter. So, her eyes shone with wonder as she looked at the copper knife.","Another time, Tatal brought a pile of bricks. Her voice sounded excited.","“Look, Shadow! This is called clay. I saw it when I visited the Crow Tribe — their chieftain's home is built from these things. He called them bricks. And you can get clay easily, too! My husband has been digging clay for a week now. I told him that if that haughty Crow has a brick home, then we must have one, too!\"","And yet another time, the shadow was disturbed by the sound of panicked bleating and saw Tatal dragging a skinny sheep with a red coat into the cave, holding it by the horns.","\"Shadow! Shadow, look!\"","The shadow felt the desire to palm his face, even though he had none.","‘Gods, what is it now?’","“What is that... thing?\"","Tatal smiled.","“It's called a sheep! My grandfather used to hunt these beasts for meat and hide. However... they shed their coats every year. So, if you look after them a little, you can weave as much cloth as you want. Wool, Shadow! Don't you see my dress? It's so much lighter than hide — and softer, too. No one else in the village has one yet!\"","She paused for a moment, and then laughed ominously.","“Those arrogant Crows will die of envy the next time we meet.\"","The shadow... was impressed.","Tatal's people seemed to be developing faster than he had expected. Perhaps it was because War God, the goddess of life — as well as technology and progress — was the divine patron of all humans. Maybe it was because they were descendants of the First Humans, who had wielded mythical power and had been creatures of myriad talents.","But, of course, not all of Tatal's visits were happy ones.","Life was a constant struggle, after all, and it was especially so for the ancient people who lived in the Age of Gods.","The shadow's presence might have scared off most of the Creatures of Corruption, but there were still some who failed to perceive him or were too mad to be turned away. There was no peace between humans and mystical beasts that dwelled in the untamed expanse of existence, either.","Even mundane predators were a deadly threat to them, at times, fighting desperately for ownership over the wild land.","There were other human tribes, as well. There was famine and disease. There was the unpredictable harshness of indifferent nature. The life of Tatal and her tribe was idyllic at times, while at times it was full of strife, struggle, and sorrow.","And even if Tatal did not show it, the shadow knew that she felt the harshness of the world more deeply than most. She had been orphaned at a young age, after all, and then thrown into a dark cave to die by the person whom she trusted the most. Her heart had been wounded, and so it was more sensitive to pain.","Tatal was still young when the old shaman died, and she became the new one. The responsibility over the entire tribe suddenly fell onto her shoulders, and when she appeared at the mouth of the shadow's cave — far ahead of her usual visit — there was fear and uncertainty written on her pale, tired face.","\"I don't know, Shadow... I don't know what to do. Human life is so fragile. One wrong decision — less than that, even, just a bit of bad luck — and the entire tribe will be gone. It's terrifying. The elders shield themselves from that terror with blind faith... faith in the gods, faith that tomorrow will be the same as today... but I cannot be like them. I wish that I could.\"","She looked deeply troubled. The shadow tried to console her as best he could, but he was not someone who knew solace well. His own existence was endless and endlessly arduous, after all. There was no solace to be found for him, so how could he soothe another?","Tatal came to him after her second daughter died of fever, as well. This time, she didn't say anything, and just sat silently in the darkness, tears streaming down her face. The shadow did not try to console her, since she was inconsolable. He simply stayed by her side, all around her, allowing his darkness to hide her tears from the world.","Another year, a man of her tribe killed another in a fit of jealousy. Conflict was commonplace among the people of the tribe, but crime was rare. Its people stood together against the hostile world, after all — they had to trust and support each other in order to survive. A tribe could only survive in unity, and since crime undermined it, those who broke the unspoken laws and customs were dealt with harshly.","Thieves, murderers, and people who used force to get what they want — there was no place for them among the people of the tribe.","The criminals were meant to be banished... but, actually, banishment was considered to be the cruelest of punishments. If the shaman was merciful, she would sentence the guilty to death instead.","Tatal was one such shaman. Usually, the chieftain of the tribe — the strongest of the hunters — would carry out the execution. But since Tatal was stronger than the strongest among the tribe's warriors, or perhaps for some other reason, she chose to end the murderer's life with her own hands. She came to the shadow's cave a few days after that, surrounded by a somber silence. Her face was motionless, and her gaze was distant. There was a painful, burdened ache in its depths.","After sitting silently on the stone floor for a long while, she spoke quietly.","\"I've never killed a human before, Shadow.\"","Her voice was heavy, as if pressed down by crushing weight.","Tatal took a breath, then sighed.","\"I never thought I would.\"","She smiled joylessly, then looked into the darkness.","\"Have you ever killed a person, Shadow?\"","His cold voice resounded in the cave, as calm and unaffected as it had always been.","\"Too countless to count.\"","Tatal's lips trembled.","She studied the darkness with a pained expression, and then asked in a fragile tone:","\"How do you live?\"","The shadow remained silent for a short while.","Eventually, having failed to find a better answer, he answered simply:","\"One day at a time.\"","Tatal stared at the darkness.","Slowly, her pale smile brightened a little, as if she was amused by something.","Looking down, she laughed quietly and whispered.","\"One day at a time...\"","Life went on. Tatal seemed to have found the courage to face it again, meeting its countless challenges one at a time — and overcoming them.","Her tribe overcame all the adversity that the world threw at it, as well.","They survived. They grew.","They flourished.","It was funny... the shadow had witnessed great and terrible beings fighting each other across the vast expanse of the newborn world. He had beheld gods and demons — albeit from afar. He had felt the earth trembling under their footsteps and seen them reshape all of existence with their dire feats.","But, somehow, the mundane and fleeting lives of the small, insignificant people of the tribe had become far more fascinating and meaningful to him, at some point.","Because Tatal was one of them.","Time passed, and she turned from a young girl into a woman who carried the weight of her duty and responsibility with grace. Despite the scars left on her heart, she was still full of joy and resolve. She enjoyed all the boons that life had to offer — fully and never holding anything back.","However, life had no shortage of ordeals in store for those who dared to face it with a smile.","And so, soon enough, Tatal's harshest trial yet arrived."]},{"number":3174,"title":"Chapter 3174 Tatal’s Basilisk","paragraphs":["Tatal was an Ascended by then, having lived up to the expectations of the tribe's elders and become as powerful as her grandfather had been at the peak of his power. She had learned how to be a warrior from him. The previous shaman, meanwhile, had taught her the secret of sorcery, making her a Shaper.","Most of those elders had already left for the Realm of Shadows by then, and those who still lived were too old and decrepit to manage the affairs of the tribe. So, the responsibility for its well-being lay squarely on Tatal's shoulders. She did her best to safeguard her people — but, just as she had mentioned once, disaster was always around the corner.","Sometimes, it took less than a single bad decision to doom a tribe of humans. All that stood between them and extinction was a bit of bad luck.","This time, the bad luck of Tatal's people came from far away.","North of their valley, deep in the primal forest, lived the tribe of the One-Winged Crow. And beyond that, on the shore of a wide river, lived the tribe of the Sabertooth Tiger — they were the ones who brought calamity upon the people of this distant land.","No one knew how it happened, but the people of that tribe had somehow earned the wrath of a powerful Transcendent creature that dwelled in the heart of a vast and deadly marsh. Perhaps they had offended it somehow, or perhaps they had simply disturbed its slumber...","Perhaps the creature needed no reason at all, and was simply incensed by the smell of humans.","That creature was the Basilisk, and before anyone knew it, the Sabertooth tribe was entirely wiped out.","The shadow was not just anyone, of course. He knew it all because the den of the Basilisk was well within the borders of the vast area encompassed by its senses.","But what did he care if some tribe was destroyed by an enraged Devil? The Basilisk was not a Creature of Corruption, after all, and those people had brought its wrath upon themselves.","There was no peace among humans and noble creatures that populated the world. So what if all of them had come from the Flame? They still competed for the same forests, plains, and lakes. Some creatures built a relationship with humans, but some saw them as hateful pests instead. Some simply treated them as all other living beings — the weak were prey, the strong were a threat.","That Basilisk had been slumbering in the marsh for centuries, patiently incubating a clutch of precious eggs. The crafty humans thought that they could steal the eggs without awakening the giant creature, but panicked and destroyed them instead.","So, the shadow saw no reason to intervene... he did not care to intervene even if there had been a reason. Bullying a little Transcendent wyrm was not a good look for beings like him, anyway.","The problem, however, was that the Basilisk did not stop after destroying the Sabertooth tribe. Its rampage continued unabated, as if it was determined to eradicate all humans, everywhere, and soon, the neighboring tribes had tasted its wrath as well.","News spread slowly among the ancient humans, so most of them died without knowing the reason why their lives had come to an end. Entire villages were wiped out... the forest burned.","It was only when pillars of smoke rose into the sky, and battered refugees reached the surrounding tribes, their glassy eyes full of terror, that people learned about the approaching calamity.","But, for most of them, it was already too late.","That Shadow Tribe was late to learn the news, as well. In fact, they only learned it after tragedy struck.","When a handful of surviving Crows stumbled into their village — the last of the destroyed tribe — and told their tale in quiet, trembling voices, the first thing Tatal did was turn to look at the forest.","That was because her husband had led his men on a hunt a few days ago, venturing in the exact direction where the Basilisk was prowling.","Nobody knew if the hunters would return alive.","In the end... only a few of them did.","The hunting party had encountered the giant wyrm in the depths of the forest, and despite their courage and quick reflexes, the battle was brutal and one-sided. Most of them perished in a matter of moments,","and those who survived were only alive because of their chieftain's swift thinking, composure, and personal valor.","The chieftain himself — the little Wolf who had married Tatal once — returned alive, as well. However, he was grievously wounded. Worse than that, most of his right arm had turned to stone.","It was apparent that he would never hunt again.","The loss of the hunters and the crippling wounds of its chieftain were already a terrible blow for the tribe. But that was not where their problem ended — the Basilisk was still full of wrath and bloodlust, after all, and if it had already come this close to the village, it was only a matter of time before it descended upon it.","A world-ending disaster seemed to have befallen Tatal and her people.","The survivors of the Crow tribe, who had seen the Basilisk destroy their settlement like a living calamity, had only one piece of advice — run.","Run away, and pray to the gods for mercy. However, Tatal was in no hurry to flee with her people.","Looking at the village with a somber expression, she saw what others failed or refused to see.","There were too many people in the tribe now. They could abandon their homes and their livelihoods, but not all of them would survive away from their land — many would starve or die from exposure. Perhaps even most of them.","The land was a generous mother that fed and clothed them, but it was also a trap that tied them down like an inescapable shackle.","Even if they did survive... there was nowhere else to go.","After all, there was a reason why the elders had been forced to settle down. The land was vast, but it was not boundless. Every place where humans could survive had already been claimed by older and more powerful tribes, and those tribes would not welcome a crowd of hungry strangers — life was harsh for everyone, after all, and they were struggling to sustain their own people. So, if Tatal chose to take her people and flee, they would have only two ways to survive.","One would be for the tribe to disband, its people scattering to look for new homes. A few would be accepted by this village, a few would be accepted by that one... some would not be accepted at all. Most would perish in the wilderness, trying to make their way to a human settlement, and many of those who survived would spend the rest of their lives being treated badly by the original members of their new tribes.","The other way was simpler.","It was to take the land from another tribe, slaughtering its people and taking their place.","Things like that happened often. This realm was too remote and sparsely populated, and most of the tribes populating it were young, having only settled recently. But in the places that the Shadow Tribe had come from, humans turned their weapons against each other often... that was what the elders said, at least, since the oldest of them had witnessed it personally.","But even if Tatal was willing to take another tribe's land by force, there was no point in trying. She wouldn't do it, anyway.","Looking at the people of the Crow tribe, whose faces were pale like those of corpses, she said in a dark tone:","“Run? Can you outrun a Transcendent beast? How fast are you going to run, fools?\"","If the beast was determined to eradicate all humans in the land, trying to run away would not save anyone.","The people looked at her in despair.","Several tribes were already gone. The Shadow Tribe seemed like it would follow them soon. Only gods knew how many more would be wiped out before the beast's fury was satiated, or before a more powerful creature stopped its rampage. They couldn't even flee.","Such was the fate of humans in the age when gods and daemons walked the earth. They were like ants beneath the feet of great and terrible beings... the horror of such existence could only be endured by turning yourself blind to the truth of the world.","But when the truth came knocking on your door, shutting your eyes was useless.","Tatal looked at the healer's house, where her husband was being treated. She looked at her frightened people. Then, she looked at the vast, dark forest beyond the fields.","\"So what do we do, shaman? How can we survive?\"","She remained silent for a long while, then unsheathed her precious copper knife and lowered her gaze to its sharp, polished blade.","At that point, the shadow expected her to pay his cave a visit.","But, to his surprise and dismay, Tatal went in the opposite direction instead.","Taking her bow and her spear, she changed from her beautifully embroidered wool dress into hide and leather, then left the village alone and entered the forest. She walked in the direction where the tribe's huntsmen had died.","‘What is that child doing?'","The shadow stirred, frowning mentally.","‘Has she lost her mind?’","Tatal did not seem panicked or grief-stricken. Her expression was somber, but also calm.","Her eyes were full of sorrow, but also dark and unshaken resolve.","‘Where are you going, fool?’","The shadow gnashed its teeth — he would have, rather, if he had them. The vast darkness of his being seethed restlessly. But, oblivious to his inner turmoil, Tatal continued moving toward danger.","By the morning of the next day, she reached the spot where the Basilisk had attacked the hunters. There, paling at the sight of carnage, she gritted her teeth and began tracking the beast.","It was then that the shadow did something he had not done in countless years... that he had never wanted or thought to do since the birth of the world.","He left his cave, manifesting into a vaguely human shape in Tatal's path.","His cold voice was stern when he asked, barely suppressing his irritation:","\"What do you think you're doing?\"","Tatal looked at him in confusion, then smiled faintly.","\"Shadow?\"","She hesitated for a moment, then continued walking, soon passing him.","“I'm on my way to kill the Basilisk. What else?\"","Tatal inhaled deeply, then said in a lighthearted tone:","\"My husband will be down when he comes to his senses and finds out what happened to his arm. So... I'll bring him the Basilisk's hide as a present. It won't be as soft as bear hide, but it might still lift his mood.\"","The shadow pursed his lips, then spun around and followed.","“Foolish girl, you have barely Ascended. That wyrm is a Transcendent Devil... it was one step away from becoming a Tyrant. Why are you trying to fight it? Why are you here alone?\"","Tatal shrugged.","\"You said it yourself, Shadow. The beast is Transcendent... those of my warriors that still live are no more than Awakened. Their spears won't even scratch its scales.\"","The shadow almost cursed.","\"Isn't there someone else who can help you?\"","Tatal raised an eyebrow.","\"I can pray to the gods, I guess. But the gods are too great and distant to care about a mortal woman like me. So I'd rather not waste my breath.\"","This time, the shadow did have teeth. So, he gritted them and fell silent for a short while, trying to suppress the words that struggled to escape his mouth.","But, in the end, he couldn't — even if his entire being rose against uttering them aloud.","“Me! You could have asked me! That little worm is nothing for me! I can kill it in a second!\"","Tatal continued walking, a pale smile illuminating her face.","In the end, she shook her head quietly.","“No, Shadow. I could never ask you to kill someone for me.\"","He scoffed.","“Why?\"","Tatal lowered her head.","After taking half a dozen steps, she turned to look at him, a deep emotion hidden in her eyes.","\"I think I understand now, Shadow... the reason you refused to kill me, all those years ago.\"","Tatal looked ahead.","\"I have only ever killed one person, and the burden of that death is still following me around. But you, you said that you had killed too many living things to count. That weight... it must be crushing you, Shadow. How could I ever ask you to kill more? For me?\"","She smiled sadly.","“What kind of friend would ask that?\"","The shadow stared at her, aghast.","That foolish, little human... was pitying him? Was concerned about him?","‘Humans really are the silliest of creatures!’","He exhaled slowly.","“So you'd rather put your entire tribe in danger? Your husband? You children? You'd rather risk... yourself?\"","Tatal remained silent for a long while. When she looked at the shadow again, her smile was gone, replaced by a soft expression.","\"Shadow... I'm not that selfless, Shadow.\"","She shook her head slowly.","\"It's just that even if all of them have forgotten — and you as well, perhaps — I still remember. I realized it at some point, years ago.\"","She smiled at him.","\"You are the greatest danger to my tribe, Shadow. We are alive only because you allow us to live. If you can kill the Basilisk in a second, then how long will it take you to wipe us out? How easy would it be for you to kill us all?\"","She pursed his lips.","\"This calamity has happened because the Basilisk started killing and couldn't stop. What happens if you start killing on my behalf? Will there come a day when you won't stop?\"","Her voice grew quieter.","“Will there come a day when I won't be able to stop myself from asking you to kill for me?\"","Looking down, Tatal shook her head.","“No... that man I killed. I sentenced him to death, so I took his life with my own hands, without asking someone else to bloody theirs. The Basilisk is no different. I have decided that its life must end, so I will end it!\"","With that, she hurried her steps.","The shadow fell back, watching her go in stunned silence.","At that moment, he felt something he had not felt in a long while... had never felt before, perhaps.","The familiar, biting sting of powerlessness.","...A few days later, after a long and dreadful battle, surrounded by shattered cliffs and ravaged earth, Tatal slayed a Transcendent Devil, the Basilisk, with her copper blade. She ended its life with her own hands, without asking anyone else to do it for her.","She could not take its hide to gift it to her husband, though, because it was as tough as stone — the copper knife was utterly powerless against it. So, the shadow helped her skin the dead Devil."]},{"number":3175,"title":"Chapter 3175 Gods Bearing Gifts","paragraphs":["Tatal had been gravely wounded in the battle against the Basilisk. In fact, she was barely alive.","But she was alive.","The shadow delivered her unconscious body, as well as the hide of the slain Devil, to the outskirts of the village. Then, he disappeared and returned to the comfortable, cold darkness of his cave. The tribesmen had to be full of shock and joy at the return of their shaman. After all, slaying the Basilisk was not what a mere Ascended was meant to be capable of... the battle Tatal had fought was, without a doubt, a spectacular and awesome feat — a feat worthy of becoming a song, or perhaps even a myth, one day.","The myth of a valiant shaman who faced an unstoppable calamity with a song and a copper blade.","But the shadow was in no mood to observe the tribesmen celebrating.","He was troubled... he was uneasy.","Even now that the Basilisk was dead and Tatal was out of danger, the shadow still felt strangely disturbed. It was all because of what Tatal had said, back in the depths of the forest.","‘Why did she refuse my help?’","The shadow was like a god to the people of the small human tribe. So why would Tatal turn away from her god and choose to face the Devil alone?","The shadow did not know why, but that question resonated with the depths of his dark being.","A fragment of a long-forgotten conversation surfaced from the depths of his mind, spoken by a man he did not remember in a life he did not want to recall.","‘Never trust the gods...’","Who had said it?","What did it mean?","The shadow already knew the kind of chilling horror lesser creatures felt when faced with the unfathomable vastness of Divine and Unholy beings — and of those who were Sacred or Cursed, as well. Being so small, so insignificant, so indescribably powerless... it almost made everything feel meaningless.","The only way to keep your sanity while sharing a world with such beings was not to think about their greatness at all.","However, the shadow had only ever considered the gods as a harrowing, inescapable threat. They did not even need to harbor any hostility against the shadow to destroy him. Entire realms could perish from the smallest aftershock of their actions — in front of them, even a being like him was no more than an ant, and just like an ant, he could be crushed by the careless steps of these giants.","He had only ever thought about the gods as an odd, inherently hazardous and calamitous force. He always assumed that beings that were lesser than him, like the tribesmen, would feel the same way.","But what if a god was benevolent, instead? What if a god was gentle and cared about you? What if they were willing to extend a helping hand without asking anything in return?","One would assume that having a god's favor would be an incredible boon. Who had not hoped for a miracle, after all? Who had not wished for there to be an all-powerful, kind being watching over them?","The shadow was neither kind nor all-powerful, but he could have been Tatal’s miracle.","And yet, she had refused him. It was for his benefit, yes, since she considered him a dear friend. But it was for her own benefit as well — her words hinted at that, implying something he had never considered","before...","That a benevolent god was just as terrifying as a hostile one — maybe even more so.","‘Why?’","The shadow spent a long time in the darkness, thinking.","In the end, he came to a conclusion that made him uncomfortable. That conclusion was not about what Tatal believed, but rather about what the shadow himself felt would be true... but that did not make it any less confusing.","It was that the existence of a kind god still rendered the efforts of mortals meaningless, while their benevolence was too sweet to resist — once someone tasted it, there was no going back.","If the great gods existed and were willing to pay attention to the lives of mortals, then what were mortals to do? They could strive to accomplish something for their entire lives, and in the end, everything they achieved would still be infinitely inferior to a deity's casual act. Their lives would feel fleeting and dreary, pathetic and pitiful in comparison to the glorious existence of gods.","They would only be able to look in envy at what gods could do, what gods created, and what gods possessed.","Power, freedom, abundance, immortality... Life was harsh, and mortals could endure its harshness because that was the reality that all living things had to confront. But what if they had to behold beings who were unbound by reality, who treated reality as soft and malleable instead?","That, the shadow surmised, would fill them with a heartbreaking sense of injustice.","Of maddening envy and quiet despair. Faced with the greatness of gods, mortals would only have two choices. One was to continue living their lives, heartbroken, while the other was to throw themselves on the perilous Path of Ascension in hopes of becoming a deity one day, too.","But that was just one side of the coin.","On the other side was the danger of receiving help from a deity.","Humans were small and weak, but gods were great and all-powerful. So, what if a god descended into a mortal realm to help its people?","Once a deity helped them once, wouldn't they want to receive that help once more? And if they continued to be favored by their god, wouldn't they come to expect divine assistance? Wouldn't they come to rely on it, forgetting their own efforts?","What would happen if a deity solved all their problems, protected them from all the dangers, and gave them all the things they desired?","The shadow remembered the awe Tatal had felt when she saw copper for the first time, and the joy she shared with him when the craftsmen of her tribe learned to work it. The enthusiasm she was brimming with when figuring out how to make clay bricks. The boastful pride she was full of because of her wool dress — the first one in the village.","He knew that he could have created her a blade that was a thousand times more durable than copper with a thought. He could build a city for her tribe in a matter of minutes. He could weave a fabric that was more sublime and wondrous than anything Tatal had ever worn, touched, and seen.","He could have killed the Basilisk, as well. But if he had... would Tatal ever be able to overcome the temptation of asking him for more?","Of killing more of her enemies. Of providing more for her tribe. Of making life less harsh... of overcoming the struggles of life in her stead.","And if that happened, then would her joy, enthusiasm, and pride disappear one day? Would they be extinguished, little by little, like a flame starving without fuel?","Stolen away by the generous deity.","The shadow stirred.","It did not know.","It felt like Tatal had fathomed something that even he, a being far greater and more ancient than her, had not.","That it was hazardous for mortals to be subjects of divine affection.","Countless people across history had not felt the same. The two men of the Empire he remembered were certainly comfortable serving a nation ruled directly by a god.","But then again, was the Empire really the best example? Or was it exactly the kind of malignant anomaly that Tatal was reluctant to create?","The great and glorious Empire of War,","which conquered the world with fire and sword... whose conquest could not be resisted or stopped, because it was protected by a god.","Until, one day, it was stopped. The people who stopped it simply had to kill the gods first, destroying all of existence with them. The shadow rested in the darkness, uncomfortable. He did not know why the issue of godhood concerned him so much, let alone the issue of the relationship between gods and people.","He wasn't a god, after all, and neither did he have the desire to help people.","Tatal was the singular exception to his indifferent attitude toward all humans, and since she did not want his help, the point was moot.","So, the shadow could forget all about it and rest easily, knowing that these maddening questions had nothing to do with him."]},{"number":3176,"title":"Chapter 3176 First of Her Kind","paragraphs":["Tatal eventually recovered from her wounds.","Her tribe had not been forced to abandon its land and scatter to the winds.","Instead, it absorbed the survivors of the Basilisk's rampage and grew. Its reputation had soared, as well, since people of the surrounding lands — those lucky enough to have been spared the Devil's wrath — eventually learned that it was Tatal, the shaman of the Shadow Tribe, who had slain the beast.","There were hard times, at first, because the hunters of the tribe had been decimated, and its chieftain had lost an arm. But the tribe survived and grew stronger for it. The Basilisk had given it great boons in death. Its hide, its bones, its fangs, its soul shards — all of it was used by the tribesmen to empower themselves.","Soon enough, the youths reached adulthood. Trained by Stone Hand, their former chieftain, they became skilled hunters and replaced those who had perished in the woods. The fields expanded. The craftsmen of the tribe developed their craft and reached new heights.","Tatal ruled wisely. She was both beloved and revered by her people, respected by the neighboring tribes... her name had even traveled to faraway lands, earning her a bit of renown and fame.","She still visited the shadow every year, bringing with her stories of her people. One time, not long after the Basilisk had been slain, she came to his cave in a mood that seemed both joyful and melancholic.","\"My firstborn is getting married, Shadow.\"","She smiled joyfully, tears glistening in her eyes.","\"He is going to leave the tribe. His bride is from the Otter tribe... they live so far away. When will I see him again?\"","Tatal lowered her head.","“I am so happy for him, but I am also so sad. Ah, Shadow... when did life become so complicated?\"","Another year, when Tatal came to visit him, her expression was thoughtful.","\"Do you know, Shadow? Guests came to the tribe this year. They are people who travel the land, doing nothing but exchanging things. They bartered numerous wondrous items, and they were also interested in purchasing a great deal of things from us... I never really thought about it, but many things we have or make here would seem wondrous to someone else.\"","She chuckled.","“But they also brought stories. There was a war between the Wolf Tribe and the Elk Tribe, it seems. Seven tribes have come together to build a great temple, somewhere far away, in the lands our ancestors left. The Goddess of the Moon has given birth to a human child. One of the First Humans, a man named Kanakht, is said to have defied the will of the heavens. The world is so vast, Shadow... it makes me so curious. It makes me feel happy to be alive.\"","Another year, Tatal came bearing gifts.","\"Look, Shadow!\"","The shadow looked, feeling perplexed.","\"What is it?\"","Tatal raised the item higher.","“It's called a pillow! There are goose feathers inside. My youngest daughter made it — you are supposed to put your head on it when you sleep. She also did the embroidery!\"","Nothing she said made the shadow feel less bewildered.","“I know what a pillow is. Why are you waving it around?\"","Tatal blinked a couple of times.","“Well, I just thought... there's nothing but cold stones in your cave. So, I brought you a pillow, for you to rest more comfortably...\"","The shadow had to refuse her gift.","He did, however, express his gratitude. Even if he did not have a head to rest on a pillow, the gesture itself, no matter how misguided, was quite sweet.","...He did get the impression that Tatal just wanted to brag about her youngest daughter, though.","Tatal's children grew up. After the firstborn, others had their weddings as well. Her husband retired from being the chieftain and dedicated himself to teaching the young members of the tribe. A new chieftain was selected to replace him, this one coming from a different family.","There were troubles and losses, too. Mystical beasts sometimes set their sights on the tribe's people. Creatures of Corruption — those weak enough for the shadow to ignore — prowled in the darkness. The more Tatal's tribe possessed, the more members of other tribes looked at it with envy.","She had to mediate conflicts at times. At times, she had to take up her bow and her spear, venturing into the forest to fight dangerous creatures. But no matter what happened, Tatal always managed to emerge victorious.","Her fame and reputation slowly grew.","Her power grew, as well.","This primal world was harsh and full of peril, so those who challenged it had no choice but to be tempered by its trials. And so, one day, before the shadow could even consider it, Tatal's soul tore through the boundary of her mortal body, and she became Transcendent — the first Transcendent of her tribe, as well as of all the other tribes in this remote land.","Her Transcendent form was that of a great, magnificent fox.","When Tatal became a Transcendent, there was a great celebration among her people. Beings like her were not unheard of among humans — there had been a lot of them among the mythical First Humans, and there were some among the older tribes that populated distant realms. But in this land, she was the first.","The people who lived here had only ever heard about Transcendent humans in myths and legends. So, they were full of exhilaration and awe.","The shadow, naturally, had an entirely different perspective.","But, still...","He was happy, too.","Because Transcendent beings lived longer lives. That meant that Tatal would be by his side for a bit longer, too.","The tribe was almost unrecognizable by then. What had started as a small scattering of crude tents was now a thriving village with homes built from wood and clay. The tiny pieces of land the tribesmen farmed had turned into vast fields. There were pens for cattle, chickens, and geese.","The crude flint weapons the hunters had used were replaced with copper blades. Instead of hide and fur, they now wore garments made of fabric — some woven out of plants, some out of wool.","Even the wolf-dogs who had been companions of humans for the longest time seemed different, somehow.","The shadow sighed.","‘In the blink of an eye...’","All of this had happened in the blink of an eye.","He was almost worried to imagine what would happen if he closed his eyes and took a little nap."]},{"number":3177,"title":"Chapter 3177 Parting","paragraphs":["Time passed.","The world changed, but the shadow stayed the same.","Hidden in the depths of a dark cave, he rested and experienced the changes through his senses. The trees he remembered as young saplings had become towering giants, then withered and died; new beasts were born as others grew frail and were devoured.","People changed most of all.","Out there in the vast and terrifying expanse of the world, countless humans struggled to establish a foothold against the terrifying Creatures of Corruption across numerous realms. Their tribes were wiped out one after another, only for new ones to arrive in search of a home. Humanity had no advantage in this bloody war — in fact, it was hopelessly outmatched.","But humans persisted. They hid, they learned, they endured... but most of all, they changed.","Humans were a supremely adaptable species, after all. That was what made them so deadly.","In the lands where there was snow and vicious cold, humans learned how to stay warm. In the realms covered by water, they learned how to build rafts and canoes. Their flint weapons were replaced by copper blades; their gatherers had become farmers, while their hunters had become beast tamers.","Crafts, farming, animal husbandry... they were learning it all, desperately trying to survive in a world that had no place for them. In hostile, unknown and unfathomable lands, humans were surrounded by darkness on all sides. They had to sustain themselves and push the darkness back, lest it swallow them.","But the darkness always came back to avenge itself.","The people of Tatal's tribe had an easier time than most because of the shadow. While they still had to fight the Creatures of Corruption, no abomination powerful enough to destroy the tribe without giving it a fighting chance ever appeared in their lands. They were protected by a Shaper of considerable strength, as well — great shaman Tatal, who had slain the Basilisk and became Transcendent.","Because of that, the influence of the Shadow Tribe grew, and soon, the neighboring tribes came to rely on it. Even people from the faraway lands that lay beyond the shadow's senses sometimes came to pay Tatal respect and ask for her advice or assistance.","She gave both freely.","For a long while, life was good. Tatal enjoyed the golden years of her life surrounded by people who admired and loved her. Her tribe thrived, while her family grew.","Her children married one after another. The boys went to live with other tribes, while the girls welcomed their husbands home. Soon enough, Tatal became a grandmother — and before too long, there were a dozen or more of her grandchildren running around a handful of tribes.","Despite being such a prolific grandma, Tatal still looked quite young — she was a Transcendent, after all. If one did not know better, they would have thought that she and her daughters were sisters, while her husband was their father.","The young Wolf, now known as Stone Hand, was not so young anymore. His mighty figure was still straight and imposing, but his hair and beard had long turned grey. After losing an arm to the stone curse of the Basilisk, he had surrendered his position of chieftain and became a teacher for the youths of the tribe. Many of the adult members of the tribe had been his students once, so there were few elders more respected than him.","Despite how different they looked now, Tatal and her husband still lived in perfect harmony. It was just that many things were slowly becoming difficult for him, so she had to assist her aging husband in mundane tasks from time to time — other times, their grandchildren would assist him in her place.","Their home was always full of the sound of children laughing.","When Tatal visited the shadow, there was always a bright smile on her face.","“I am so happy, Shadow. I couldn't be any happier, I think. Life is so harsh, but it is also so impossibly wonderful...\"","The shadow was content, as well. He was enjoying this measured, peaceful existence. However, time continued to pass, and things continued to change.","Nothing ever stayed the same.","Soon enough, Tatal's husband passed away from old age, surrounded by his children and grandchildren. The whole tribe mourned his death, and he was buried with the highest honors they knew how to give. Both as his wife and the shaman, Tatal performed the rituals to send his shadow off to the Realm of Death.","Standing above the grave in the ornate garment of the shaman, Tatal looked like a young woman as she buried her old husband. Her radiance was striking, and there was not a single grey hair on her head... she looked far younger than her daughters, even, as if time had no power over her.","The shadow thought that she handled the loss of her husband quite well. She still smiled warmly every time she visited, full of joy and hunger for life...","But he also noticed that her smile was never the same since that day.","There was always a tiny hint of melancholy hidden behind its radiant splendor, as if she couldn't help but feel a little sad even in her happiest moments.","In time, Tatal's village grew into a small town. The wooden and clay huts were replaced by homes built of stone. There was a watermill standing above a stream nearby, and a tall palisade with watchful sentries. Tatal's grandchildren had their own children now. Many of them married into distant tribes, so her bloodline spread far and wide, giving birth to exceptional individuals in many places. Some had even found their way to distant realms, carrying her legacy with them.","But Transcendents lived long lives. Having buried her husband, Tatal eventually buried her children as well. She had managed to maintain her composure when the old Wolf passed away... but even her stalwart heart bled when she heard the news of her firstborn son leaving for the Realm of Shadows, somewhere far away. When she lowered her daughters into the ground one after another, caressing their thin and grey hair.","One time, she cried in the shadow's embrace once again, her bitter wails echoing between the walls of the dark cave. The next time, she faced him with a faltering smile...","On that day, the shadow noticed that there were grey streaks in her own hair now, as well.","He comforted her as best he could. He did not know much about human emotions, but it seemed that his company — his mere existence — was of great comfort to Tatal, in and of itself.","But the shadow himself was uncomfortable. He was restless and worried, unable to find peace.","Time continued its merciless march. Many years passed, and in what felt like an instant, as the shadow watched, Tatal grew old. Her fiery hair had turned grey, and the lines on her face grew deeper.","One time, as she came to visit him, Tatal sat down, supporting her knees, and let out a sigh.","“Ha... climbing this mountain is not as easy as it used to be, Shadow.\"","Then, she flashed him a smile — the same unabashed, mischievous smile the little girl who had snuck into his cave once showed him. At that moment, the marks of old age covering her face seemed to disappear, and she looked just like that small, frustrating child once more. The two were indistinguishable from each other.","Despite her age, Tatal was still a Transcendent. So, no kind of mountain could strain her.","The shadow smiled in the darkness.","“Shall I make the mountain shorter? I can crush it to pieces, if you want.\"","Tatal laughed.","“No, no... please don't. I love this mountain. So many things have changed, but the mountain is still the same. We are old friends, she and I.\"","Tatal remained silent for a few moments, then smiled.","\"The world is so different now, Shadow. Sometimes, I remember how it was when I was a little girl... it's almost unrecognizable. The forest where I used to search for berries is gone. The tent where my mother nurtured me only exists in my memory. Our tribe is so large now... and it's populated by strange people. They admire me, they love me... and I love them too. But — and please don't tell anyone — I have to put in some effort to remember all their names and faces.\"","Her voice was wistful.","The shadow scoffed.","“Whom would I tell? I only ever talk to you.\"","Tatal grinned.","“That's true.\"","Her smile seemed to dim a little then, and she looked away.","After remaining silent for a while, Tatal sighed.","“Everyone I knew is gone, Shadow. None of them had the decency to stay alive a little longer.\"","Then, she looked at the darkness and smiled.","“Only you remain. Am I not lucky, to have such a loyal friend?\"","The shadow was not sure how to answer. Eventually, he shrugged mentally.","\"I guess. As far as friends go, I am quite a catch.\"","He paused for a moment, hesitating, and then added in a voice that was quieter than his usual cold tone:","“And you, as well. I must have great luck myself to have a friend such as you.\"","Tatal laughed once again.","“Naturally! You must be the luckiest shadow in the world!\"","Gradually, her laughter quieted down, and she continued to look into the darkness with a smile.","But then, a hint of wistfulness found its way into her shining eyes.","Tatal sighed and looked away, brushing her grey hair back.","She remained silent for a long while, and then said quietly, her voice full of a strange longing.","\"I wish... I never became Transcendent, Shadow. Not always, but sometimes, I do.\"","It was then that the shadow realized that their time together was running short. Tatal did not succumb to age swiftly. But to the shadow, it seemed like everything happened in the blink of an eye. Before he even knew what to say, what to do, her back became bent, and the lines on her face turned into deep wrinkles. Her grey hair turned frail and white, and her startling radiance gave place to the look of a wizened elder.","The great shaman, Tatal, was old now. She was ancient. Having become a living legend to the people of her tribe — and all the tribes in the surrounding lands — she was treated with utmost reverence by all people. Her descendants were everywhere. Some of them were pillars of the Shadow Tribe, some had scattered across faraway lands and distant realms.","Some of them had even forged legends of their own.","During the day, she was surrounded by boisterous children and people who loved her. Everywhere she went, she was met with respect and admiration. Tatal seemed to have grown comfortable with old age, having nothing but warm smiles to share with people. It looked like she had fathomed some kind of arcane wisdom that the shadow couldn't quite discern.","Otherwise, how could she remain so content and peaceful?","The closer the end of her life drew, the less peaceful the shadow became. In fact, he had forgotten the meaning of peace, spending his days in turmoil.","‘Not yet. Not yet... it must not happen yet...’","But then, a day came when Old Tatal couldn't rise from her bed anymore. It was a great shock to the people of the tribe, and they gathered around her family home in a crowd, silently praying for her recovery. Those of her descendants who lived nearby rushed back to the lands of the Shadow Tribe, many of them harboring precious memories of being cared for by their kind, wise ancestor as a child.","Tatal was never alone, her dying bed surrounded by a crowd of friends and loved ones.","But it seemed that the spark of Flame that was the source of her life had waned too much. Now, it shimmered weakly, faltering, ready to be extinguished.","As the night fell, the shadow left his cave for the second time since the dawn of existence and made his way to the room where Tatal lay in the darkness, her small figure hidden by the blankets on the bed she had shared once with the young Wolf. Her eyes had grown weak with age, and yet, she still felt his presence.","Tatal smiled.","“Shadow... you came.\"","He manifested himself into a vaguely human shape at her bedside.","Looking down, the shadow spoke:","“Of course.\"","The old woman lying on the bed laughed quietly.","“All these years, all the times I visited your home... and this is the first time you came to mine. I'm happy.\"","Her breathing was weak and strained, but her smile was relaxed and joyful.","“I am so happy to see you, my friend. One last time.\"","The shadow looked around.","Tatal's descendants and disciples slept restlessly outside. Beyond the walls of her family home, the members of the tribe were holding a vigil. It seemed like all the people in the land had gathered to see her go... But he wasn't ready.","“It doesn't have to be the last time.\"","His voice, which had always been cold, suddenly sounded ragged.","The shadow hesitated.","“If you... if you want to... I can take your shadow into my soul. You can stay there forever. At peace, unchanging. With me.\"","Tatal studied him for a long time, her smile gentle.","Then, with a sigh, she looked away and shook her head.","\"To exist forever? Never changing, never knowing anything but peace? That... sounds so terribly sad, Shadow. I don't want it. I wouldn't wish it on my enemy.\"","She paused for a moment, catching her breath, and chuckled.","“Thank you. But I am content with where I am... where I have been. I am already at peace. I'm happy.\"","Tatal turned to look at him, and even though there was contentment in her eyes... there was also a hint of regret. After staying silent for a while, she said quietly:","“I only worry about you, Shadow.\"","The shadow was bewildered.","Ever since she was a little girl, Tatal had always had a talent for leaving him confused and speechless.","Finally, he found the strength to speak:","“Me? You are about to die, and you worry about me?\"","Tatal nodded.","“Of course. I worry... that you'll be all alone without me, Shadow.”","The shadow stared at her, expressionless. He had not even known the concept of loneliness before Tatal came to his cave. So, he had never been lonely.","...But he knew that he would be, once she was gone.","Met with his silence, Tatal sighed.","Her eyes were growing unfocused.","In a weak, faltering tone, she whispered.","“Take care of yourself, my friend. And thank you. Thank you for being my companion on this long, thorny path. For... being my friend. I would have been all alone without you, too.\"","Tatal's eyes closed slowly.","“It was a... long and wondrous... life. Wasn't it? But... I'm tired now. I'm ready.\"","The shadow knelt and held her hand.","He held it until dawn broke.","By then, Tatal's breath was gone, and her shadow had left, leaving him all alone in the darkness.","The shadow let go then and rose, looking around the unfamiliar room. He noticed something on a shelf by her bedside. An old, ancient... incredibly ugly doll.","He took it, his hand trembling.","A few moments later, the shadow was back in his cave.","The mountain shook slightly, and the sky was suddenly obscured by stormy clouds, a terrible rain descending on the earth from the heavens.","Hidden in the darkness, the shadow placed the doll near a silver bell that lay on a protruding stone.","Then, he dismissed his human form, hiding himself deeper.","‘Never, never...'","He never wanted to befriend a human again.","Humans were such fragile things. They appeared and vanished in the blink of an eye.","But his memories of them, his love for them, remained forever.","At that moment, he realized something.","It was that, perhaps, the affection of mortals was just as dangerous to the gods as divine benevolence was to mortals.","But he did not care.","All he knew was that there was no Tatal in this world anymore.","And without her, the world was colder."]},{"number":3178,"title":"Chapter 3178 Promise of Blood","paragraphs":["The shadow retreated into his cave. He hid himself in the darkness.","Without Tatal, the world did not interest him anymore. And since Tatal did not come to visit him, the world did not invade his home, either.","He sensed the lands around him undergoing changes, but all of it left him indifferent.","In the darkness, the shadow glanced at the ugly doll. Then, he picked up the silver bell and shook it faintly.","He remembered...","In one of his lives, he lived in a gorgeous city that sprawled across dozens of flying islands, built of ivory stone. The city was prosperous, and his life was one of abundance. However, he was mad... everyone in the city was, and in the surrounding lands, as well.","His wife was mad, too. Theirs was a happy madness.","If there was one sorrow that darkened their blissful insanity, it was that the gods had not granted them children. They prayed, they waited, but it was all for naught... until, one day, a miracle happened.","After long years of bitter failures, his wife became pregnant.","The day his daughter was born, he was so happy that his heart was ready to jump out of his chest. His daughter was a miraculous child... a blessed child. And as she grew up, she only became more lovely.","Such a lovely child could have one fate — the most wonderful one of them all.","To be sacrificed to the Ivory Lord, the dragon.","Such honor!","On the day his daughter was chained to the blackened stone in front of the great tower, he smiled brightly. His wife was full of mirth, as well.","And when the dragon's flame swallowed their child...","Ah!","He was the happiest he had ever been. He was beyond himself, so much so that his smile had become painful.","...The shadow stirred, disgusted.","Yes, that was what he felt — disgust. He had never felt it before, but its bitter taste was familiar.","He did not want to remember such filthy, vile lives.","But the torrent of memories was merciless. In another life, the shadow was a proud and powerful warrior, a maiden from an ancient sect who venerated War God. But she was mad, as well.","All of them were.","The people from the surrounding lands brought orphaned girls to their temple, to be raised by the War Maidens and become devoted priestesses of War — especially those born with red hair.","She loved the children.","The other priestesses were harsh, and some of them were indifferent. But she cared for these girls, because she had been one of them herself — a long time ago. And so, she spent more time with them than the rest.","She was also far more motivated to make them worthy of the gorgeous, glorious legacy of their ancient sect. To make them strong enough to be beloved by War. Sadly... the children were weak and fragile. They were lazy. They failed to understand the honor of their station, and some were oblivious to their duty.","So, she taught them. Some survived her teaching, and some didn't. She mourned the latter, and redoubled her efforts to guide the former. She wanted them to succeed. She was full of desire to make them stronger. Stronger than the wicked traitor in the west, at least — strong enough to please their goddess. Desire, desire...","Desire burned her heart and blackened her gaze, turning her into something twisted. But, by then, her mind was already too far gone.","And, in the end, so were the children.","The shadow threw the silver bell away.","He had learned what disgust meant.","But now, he also knew what wrath was.","Full of disgust and anger, the shadow curled into a mass of darkness and trembled.","Cold, cold...","His cave was so cold now. It had never been that way before.","‘I want to rest.'","The shadow closed its mind and forced itself into a state of half-slumber.","And yet, even in that passive state, it could still feel the world changing.","Time was flowing swiftly on the outside. Now that Tatal was gone, the Shadow Tribe had chosen a new shaman... then another, then another. They came and went, indistinguishable from each other. They bowed in front of his cave and left offerings. No one dared to enter his cave anymore. No one dared to steal the offerings and eat them while giggling and swaying their little feet, either.","The shadow ignored it all.","Out there in the valley, the town grew. The people of the tribe learned new crafts and developed what they had already mastered. Bronze came to replace copper; mines and quarries were established in the mountains. Swift boats traveled up and down the rivers, carrying goods to and from distant tribes. The garments that the tribesmen wore changed, becoming more refined and tasteful. The interiors of their homes were decorated with items that considered beauty, not just utility. There were more Awakened among them now, as well as more Ascended. Eventually, there was even a Transcendent or two.","Soon enough, the town became a city.","By then, the Shadow Tribe was not really a tribe anymore — it was a small, young nation. Having absorbed the surrounding tribes and expanded its lands, they were swiftly approaching the point of becoming a city-state.","The shadow felt that the Age of Gods was swiftly approaching its end, ready to give way to the Age of Heroes — the age when humanity had already established a foothold in the world, and its Transcendent champions battled the Creatures of Corruption for dominion over it.","Somewhere far away, Kanakht must have already created the first human kingdom... But, strangely enough, the shadow never heard the name of Kanakht being mentioned. The former tribesmen were in contact with many other people, receiving news from countless mortal realms. And yet, there was no news of the first human Supreme expanding his Domain.","Instead of him, they only talked about a beautiful, dreadful creature called the White Abyss — a thing that was not human, and yet seemed to have established the first human kingdom... or have usurped it, at least.","The shadow was mildly surprised, since that differed from the fragmented memories of the future contained in his mind. But then again, some of the futures he remembered contradicted each other, so he simply accepted it as one of such discrepancies. He did not care, either way.","He did not even care about the flourishing city that grew near his cave.","Out there in the city, Tatal's descendants — the branches of her family that stayed in the tribe — were still prospering. However, he did not feel anything for them. These people were all strangers to him, after all. The shadow had felt some connection to her children, but they were long gone.","Now, those who called themselves the heirs of the Great Shaman did not even know what she had looked like.","If anything, the shadow disliked them.","As the fortune of the tribe improved and its life became more prosperous, its people slowly changed. The many temptations of civilization — wealth, power, vice — took root in their hearts. The descendants of Tatal wielded far more power than most... And power corrupted.","So, slowly, they became prideful and conceited, believing that they were better than the common folk.","The shadow did not care about the failings of humans, and yet he could not help but feel dismayed by these ones in particular, since they were dirtying the memory of his dear friend with their every action.","Tatal had been kind, but these people were cruel. Tatal had been selfless and generous, but these people were full of selfish avarice. Tatal had treated every person as an equal despite her great strength, but these ones glanced down at others despite being pathetic and weak.","The other people of the city were not much different.","The more the shadow looked, the more disgusted he became.","And so, not wishing to feel that way anymore, he turned his gaze away from the world.","He withdrew his senses, confining them to the darkness of his cave.","He thought that he would find peace then. But instead, he only felt lonely.","The shadow rested in the darkness, blind to the world.","He refused the call of his past lives, unwilling to remember them.","Instead, he remembered Tatal.","In his mind, he could still hear her bright voice. He could still see her and smell her scent. He could still feel her warmth.","That was a happy place.","So, for a while, the shadow indulged in dreams about the past.","A long time passed that way...","Until, one day, the shadow was disturbed by a familiar scent.","There was the scent of blood drifting into his cave. The scent of death...","Frowning, the shadow stirred, slowly shaking off his slumber, and directed his senses outward.","What he saw there made the unfathomable darkness of his being boil.","Out there, on the altar in front of his cave... There was a human body lying motionlessly, blood flowing onto the cold stone.","There were empty eyes staring at the indifferent sky.","There were other humans, as well — dressed in magnificent clothes, standing around the altar. One of them held a bloodied knife; the rest were bowing toward the cave, reciting prayers.","Some had prideful, arrogant smiles hiding behind the solemn expressions plastered across their faces.","\"For you, oh Dark One! Like the Great Shaman before us, we plead for your favor!\"","The shadow lost the ability to think for a moment.","Images flashed in his mind...","The flames of the ivory dragon.","The orphaned girls smiling tentatively on the doorstep of an old temple.","He remembered Tatal.","Kind Tatal, who had been tortured by the necessary death of a single murderer. Who refused to ask him for help in the battle against the Basilisk, knowing the price of taking a life.","The shadow remembered a gaunt man digging graves in the frozen soil on the shore of an ice-covered ocean.","And then, the shadow remembered wrath. He remembered madness.","'How DARE THEY!'","He moved.","The mountain shook when the shadow left his cave. Only, this time, he did not take the form of a human.","Instead, the shadow revealed himself in front of these people in his true form — as an endless, unfathomable, titanic torrent of darkness.","As death.","He had made Tatal a promise once, didn't he? He had sent her people a message. And he was a very honest shadow, indeed.","How short their memory was...","The shadow washed over the world.","‘Die.'","And as he willed it, everything died.","The people in front of the altar collapsed like marionettes whose strings had been cut.","The people in the city below fell, too.","The cattle in the pens, the dogs guarding the homes, the mice hidden in the walls, the ants scurrying to steal crumbs from the floor.","The wheat in the fields withered and turned into dust. The trees, the grass, the flowers — all of it died, leaving nothing but desolate emptiness in its wake.","‘Why can't they just leave me alone?’","The shadow drowned the dead city, as well as the lands that surrounded it.","He was tired of life... of the living.","He just wanted peace, so why was it so hard for these revolting things to stop bothering him?","Soon enough, the land was entirely dead, enveloped in impenetrable darkness.","The city was perfectly preserved, but it was entirely empty as well, swallowed by shadows.","It was silent.","And then, there was finally peace."]},{"number":3179,"title":"Chapter 3179 Kingdom of Peace","paragraphs":["The land was shrouded in darkness.","The world was still and silent, devoid of life. The shadow beheld the silent world and felt at peace.","'Yes... this is good. I like it better.'","There were no humans to disturb him with their noise, with their greed, with their worship... with their blazing, desperate desires. There were no trees, no grass, no beasts, no vermin. There was no chaos — there were only shadows.","The shadow had wanted to become one with the world, dissolving in its endless changes. But now, he was the world. It was a different kind of unity, but one that he found himself more fond of.","Everything was as it should be, since there was nothing to impose on his tranquility. And yet...","Somewhere deep, deep within the shadow's vast and ancient being, he felt a hint of a strange emotion.","Was it regret? Or guilt? Or perhaps horror?","The shadow did not know what guilt and regret were, so he wasn't sure.","He did not care to find out, either.","He simply wanted to enjoy his peace. Eventually, the land transformed.","The shadows surged, and countless shapes rose from them. Black trees swayed in the wind, their black leaves rustling to create a soothing melody. Black flowers bloomed beautifully in the darkness. The city was now populated by myriad shades — the shades went about their business, mimicking the mundane actions of the living.","It was just that they were silent.","The shadow was in absolute control of this dark and eerie realm. So, he could observe it without feeling disturbed, time flowing past his small island of tranquility.","‘Why did I kill them?'","At some point, he asked himself that question.","The shadow did not feel uncomfortable with his decision. The disappearance of the nascent nation had only brought him peace and relief. He had experienced countless lives, after all... he had existed for myriad years. To him, the lives of humans were brief and fleeting — a dozen generations would be born and die in a flash, devoid of meaning.","All humans died, and most of them died swiftly. He merely hastened their deaths by an instant, replacing the turmoil of their lives with eternal peace.","Just like a human would not feel much after stepping on an anthill, the shadow was not someone who concerned himself with the fate of humans.","At least he had not been, once.","The being who he had been once would not have destroyed the city, though. At most, he would have wiped out the priests and supplicants who had sacrificed a life to him — simply to avoid further annoyance.","But, at some point, something about him changed.","What was it?","After considering it for a long while, the shadow came to the conclusion that it was all because of his friend, Tatal. Tatal, who had left the mark of humanity on him. Before meeting her, the shadow did not know what loneliness was. He did not know what affection was, either... love, joy, trust, hope. He had become capable of all these emotions because of her.","But those were not the only emotions he had learned.","There was also sorrow, anger, resentment... there was hatred.","It was hatred that he had felt on that dark day.","So, in an ironic twist of fate, the shadow had not destroyed these people because he was like a deity. He had destroyed them because he had been overcome by anger...","Which was the most human thing he had ever done.","Coming to that conclusion left the shadow in low spirits. Observing his lifeless kingdom, he asked himself an old question once again.","‘What am I?'","The shadow was not quite mortal. But he wasn't a deity, either... just a forlorn being stuck somewhere in between.","Left alone in his silent kingdom, ruling it like a god, the shadow found a measure of peace.","But peace did not feel as joyous anymore. And so, for whatever reason, the shadow remembered one of his past lives.","In that life, he had been born as a prince. The nation his father ruled was small, but prosperous... it had been once, at least. By the time he was born, the kingdom was in decline, and its people were suffering.","That was because the days of its glory were long past. Once, a long time ago, valiant Transcendent heroes defeated the Creatures of Corruption that had ruled the land, allowing its people to flourish. Those heroes were dead, though, or had gone away to seek glory in distant realms. Now, only their descendants remained.","And their descendants, while not as powerful, were many times more power-hungry. Perhaps it was precisely their weakness that made them so insecure, while growing up in the shadow of their great ancestors made them greedy and ambitious.","The nobles lived in luxury, exploiting and tormenting common people. The royal family was the worst of all, while the king — his father — was a vicious, cruel tyrant.","But he... he wanted to be a hero.","He wanted to be someone who helped people, like the great heroes of the past. And yet, there was little he could do. There were different kinds of princes, after all, and he was the weakest among them. His mother wasn't a queen, and neither was she one of the favored concubines — instead, she was a lowly maid who had happened to catch the tyrant's eye.","His childhood was neither lavish nor happy. The other princes all despised and hated each other, endlessly competing for their father's favor. Even if they did not see him as a threat, they could not pass up the chance to elevate themselves by mocking and tormenting him. There was no powerful clan backing him, either, and he was frail. So, he failed every time he tried to stand up for himself.","But he still resisted.","In fact, the more they tried to crush him, the more fiercely he fought for the right to hold his head high.","In the privacy of solitude, though, he could not help but shed bitter tears.","‘Why, why? Why does Father do nothing to stop them? Am I not his son?’","If there was one gift the gods had given him, it was a sharp mind... or maybe he had simply not been given any other choice but to hone his mind, since he had no strength whatsoever to protect himself.","And so, he quickly understood that the vicious princes had become that way very much by his father's design.","A tyrant feared many things, after all... but his powerful, cruel father feared his sons the most.","His father needed the support of the noble clans, so he took their daughters as wives and concubines. However, as soon as an heir was born, he became deathly afraid that the nobles would assassinate him and put the prince of their bloodline on the throne instead.","So, he pitted the princes against each other and cultivated their viciousness, suppressing the noble clans through internal conflict. If the princes could kill each other before growing too powerful, that would be even better — then, he would be able to repeat the cycle with his grandchildren, postponing the time his bloody reign inevitably ended in a coup.","The forlorn prince, the only one of those without backing who survived, smiled bitterly.","Well, then...","Didn't that make him a perfect tool?","He was the only one of the princes whom his father could use without fearing the power of the noble clans. He could become a weapon for the king to use in order to keep the other heirs in check.","All he needed to do was help his father understand his usefulness — without appearing too capable, of course, which would only make the king feel wary of him.","But why would he?","After all, unlike his brothers, he did not want power. He did not want to become king. He just wanted to survive... he wanted to live with a measure of dignity that he believed all people deserved.","That only lasted until he happened to journey outside the castle and saw how the people of the kingdom lived, though. Their desperate plight, their suffering, the inhuman cruelties they were subjected to by the nobles and the king's men...","All of it reminded him of his mother's short and tragic life.","It left him rattled... it made him angry — angrier than he thought he could ever be.","And so, he set a new goal for himself. He decided that it wasn't just him who deserved to survive and live with dignity — it was all people of the kingdom. His people. He decided that he would set them free. And so, using his sharp mind and lack of strength, he slowly earned the attention of his father.","He became the Crown Prince, tasked with suppressing the other heirs.","But, of course, that was only the beginning...","Because all the while, he worked tirelessly to achieve his goal. He cultivated his mind, searched for reliable allies, and won the loyalty of those who wanted to save the kingdom just like he did.","A long time ago, valiant heroes had saved the people from the Creatures of Corruption. Now, he looked for heroes who would save the people from the tyranny of men.","He tried to make himself into a hero, as well. He wanted to bring everyone salvation.","...There was no doubt in his mind that he would succeed."]},{"number":3180,"title":"Chapter 3180 Slither of Doubt","paragraphs":["If there was one thing he knew, it was that great things couldn't be achieved alone. Even the great gods had banded together to fight the Void — so how could mere mortals like him hope to carry the burden of change on their own?","So, being used as a tool by his father and despised by his brothers, he endured their scorn and set out to find reliable allies in secret.","At first, he found those few among the officials who had not relinquished their honor yet. With their help, he established a small, hidden network of agents and informants. And when information from all corners of the kingdom flowed into his modest courtyard, he identified those who could help him rally the people and stop the tyrant, his father.","The people were not blind to injustice, after all, and strength was not granted exclusively to nobles. There were those among common folk who wielded great power and felt the same way he did — who wanted to help their kingdom, but were granted no recourse.","He approached them in secret, but with a sincere heart. And, perhaps moved by his sincerity, they agreed to join him.","There was a warrior who hunted the Creatures of Corruption in the mountains to protect people.","There was a beautiful and kind priestess of Heart God who soothed those who were in pain.","There was a wise scholar who lived in exile, having been dismissed from court...","And many more.","He gathered them, he won the support of the people, he did his best to protect the kingdom from the atrocities committed by the corrupt nobles.","And, when the moment was right, he rose in rebellion against the king.","The revolt was swift, but bloody — it couldn't have been peaceful, no matter how much he wished that it was. Many of his comrades and companions lost their lives, and at times, it seemed like all of them would perish. But he never lost faith in their cause. He never lost his composure, either, leading the rebels with a clear mind and a steady hand.","In the end, their despair turned to triumph. They won — not only because their cause was virtuous, but also because their adversary was corrupt. In the end, the king could only rely on the princes to suppress the rebellion, but the princes were loyal to no one but themselves. They turned on each other in secret, and in the end, even the king could not save himself from the treachery of his sons.","The weakest of them — the Crown Prince, whom everyone disregarded — was the only victor in the end. With the tyrant dead and the corrupt nobles purged, his comrades bowed as they begged him to take the throne.","Thus, he became king.","Sitting on the throne and feeling the weight of the crown pressing down on him, he felt a sense of bitter irony. He had never wanted to rule, and he had never wanted to spill blood either. But, in the end, such was his fate...","Perhaps that was the only kind of ruler who could be good — someone who did not want the crown, but was forced to put it on for the sake of others.","The rebellion, the coronation — all of it was merely a means to an end. His true goal was to alleviate the suffering of his people, and so, now was the time for his true work to begin.","Having become king, he ruled to the best of his ability. He ruled wisely and with the well-being of his subjects in mind. His former companions became the pillars of the kingdom, and for a long time, life was good.","There were problems, naturally. There were Creatures of Corruption hiding in the darkness, there were natural calamities. There were neighboring kingdoms who looked at what others possessed with greed. But with a wise ruler and powerful champions, his kingdom weathered all storms.","In time, he married his dearest companion, the blessed priestess of Heart God. The wise scholar was his most trusted advisor. The mighty warrior was his general and the leader of the kingdom's defenders. Everything seemed to be going well...","Until, one day, a worm of doubt found its way into his mind.","It began innocently enough. He used to be confident in his decisions, but at some point, he began questioning if he was doing his best. One wrong choice could doom innumerable people, after all — so, it was only natural for him to want to be as diligent as he could be.","But once he began doubting himself, it wasn't long before he began doubting others as well.","After all... if he was mistaken, if some of his decisions did not benefit the kingdom, then why did everyone remain silent?","Did he not have advisors, loyal subjects, and friends? Weren't they supposed to help him keep the kingdom on course?","He became indecisive, often wearing a troubled expression.","Doubt whispered insidiously into his ear.","‘Why has no one spoken out?’","His old comrade, the learned scholar. His wise and gentle wife. His friend, the fearless warrior... why had they ignored all his mistakes?","Was it simply because they had not noticed them? Was their faith in him too strong?","Or did they not care?","...Or was there another, more sinister reason?","That was how he began to doubt even those who were closest to him. And once he began doubting them, he saw things he had not noticed before.","Wasn't his wife laughing too eagerly when conversing with the mighty warrior? Wasn't the warrior standing too closely, and looking at her too often?","‘No, it couldn't be...’","But what if it was?","Wasn't the scholar suggesting reforms that were a little too bold, a little too vague in their implementation? Things that looked innocent in and of themselves, but painted a perilous picture when put together?","Like offering more independence to the warriors of the kingdom. Sure, it would enhance their ability to act swiftly... but wouldn't it also give their leader more control over the kingdom, while stripping authority from the crown?","‘Surely not. And what if it does? I trust my friend implicitly, so why does it matter how much control he has?’","Implicitly...","But why would he need to have independent authority?","Didn't the mighty warrior trust his friend, the king, implicitly as well?","His doubts grew deeper.","After a while, he grew quiet and withdrawn. He observed those around him, and the more he looked, the more their actions strengthened his doubt.","Until his doubt became suspicion.","He suspected that the queen harbored a secret love for the warrior.","He suspected that the warrior wanted the crown for himself.","He suspected that his advisor was cunningly trying to lead him astray.","The court officials, the maids, the soldiers, the priests...","He couldn't trust any of them.","They all wanted to see him gone.","‘How sad.’","In the throes of his suspicion, the king felt heartbroken and full of bitter regret.","He had spilled the blood of his brothers to save the kingdom from the greed of the corrupt nobility and the mad tyrant — of those whose hearts had been corrupted by power. But now that his comrades had tasted power themselves, they seemed to have succumbed to its temptation as well. So, what was he to do?","Defend the kingdom from that corruption? But how?","And so, he began doing things that he had never thought he would do. It was so alien and distasteful, in fact, that at time, he felt like he wasn't the one acting — as if his body moved on its own, his lips twisted into a smile themselves, and the words he spoke came from someone else.","From someone cunning, patient, and infinitely malevolent when it needed to be. He began by subtly manipulating those around him, like he had manipulated his father once. He instilled them with doubt, then turned them against each other, making them believe that there was intrigue and conspiracy abound.","Slowly, the atmosphere in the court changed. The previous harmony was gone, replaced by tension and hostility. He used that hostility to suppress the initiatives suggested by his old friend, the wise scholar, pulling the strings from behind the curtain to make it seem like it was the officials who rose against them, not him.","''I just don't understand.' the scholar once told him, full of frustration. 'It's like they all lost their minds!''","The king smiled soothingly, offering him a compassionate hand.","He promised to find out who was turning the court against his most loyal advisor. But, in secret, he began preparations to banish the scholar from court.","Then, he turned his gaze to the warrior.","His greatest champion wielded much more martial power than he himself possessed. So, he couldn't deal with the despicable traitor directly... instead, he used underhanded means to start a conflict with a neighboring kingdom. The battle was eventually won, and the adversary was forced to surrender a considerable tribute.","But, in the process, his general was grievously wounded, diminishing his fearsome strength.","Some soldiers had died in the process, as well as some innocent people. But what was there to do? Their lives were a necessary sacrifice for the future of the kingdom.","\"This whole story smells,\" spoke the warrior, recovering from his wounds in the palace. \"We never managed to find the bastards who burned the border village. Could it be that someone else was behind the attack?\"","The king put an expression of somber concern on his face.","“If so... then it was someone who wanted to pit our two kingdoms against each other and benefit from the strife. We must stay vigilant in case these sinister forces make another move.\"","While the warrior was recovering, the queen tended to him — she was a priestess of Heart God, after all, as well as his former comrade.","Still... was there really a need for the queen to play the role of a healer personally?","The king watched silently, a dark and vicious darkness taking root in his heart.","The queen was beloved by the people, and their love alone gave her power and influence. So, he took precautions to undermine that influence.","Dealing with her was the easiest of all — after all, despite all her virtues, the queen had a lethal weakness. It was that she had failed to give him a heir. So, he spread a rumor that the queen was barren, pushing a few court officials into demanding that he take a second wife.","He rebuked them publicly, naturally...","But the damage was already done.","The queen's influence was shaken.","''Those vicious snakes!' the queen pleaded, both angered and hurt. 'How... how dare they!''","He held her in a loving embrace.","\"Shh, my love. Don't listen to those fools. You are the only one for me — you know you are, forever...\"","Just like that, all those who threatened his position were suppressed. If he wanted to get rid of them, all he had to do was twist the mood in the court faintly. He could banish the scholar; he could dismiss the warrior from his post. He could replace the queen with a new wife, sending her to spend the rest of her life in the Heart God's temple.","He was safe... and therefore, the kingdom was safe.","But, despite that, his doubts did not disappear.","They only grew stronger.","After all... why would he send the scholar away? Why would he dismiss the warrior? Why would he let the treacherous queen go?","So that they could unite and conspire against him together, just like they had done in the past?","And what about the court officials, who hid greed and ambition behind masks of loyalty?","What about the maid, the soldiers, the priests?","All of them... all of them...","All of them conspired against him.","All of them were waiting for the moment to bring him down.","The soldiers glanced at him when they thought he could not see, hiding vicious snarls. The court officials whispered in dark corridors, discussing treacherous schemes. The maids watched him like hawks as they served him food, as if choosing which dish to poison. The priests manipulated the minds of the people, hiding their ambitions behind the names of the gods.","His former friends were the worst of them all.","They were all traitors...","They all wanted to see him gone.","So, he did what he needed to do to protect himself.","On a dark winter night, he ordered the gates of the castle to be barred. The soldiers seemed confused by the order, but followed it anyway — he killed them as soon as the gates were lowered, destroying the mechanism that would allow someone to raise them again.","Then, he made his way to his living quarters.","The queen was still awake, so she smiled when he sat on the bed near her and reached forward to hug her.","Her smile faltered when his hands wrapped around her neck.","“M-my... my king!\"","He returned the smile as he strangled the traitor, easily overpowering her attempts to break free.","It was peculiar, though... the queen was of a higher Rank than he was, so she should have been able to overpower him. However, a dire strength overcame him, turning his grip into an iron vice. No matter how she struggled, it was all for naught.","It must have been virtue that aided him, while her own strength was stolen by treachery.","“My... m—my king...\"","Once the queen was dead, he finally felt some of his doubt subsiding.","‘Ah...’","He should have done this a long time ago. He should have killed them all.","And so, he did.","His friend, the warrior, was still weak from his wounds. So, it wasn't that hard to carve him into pieces with a sharp blade.","The scholar was supposed to be wise, and yet he failed to predict the moment of his death. Once his corpse fell to the floor, his skull split open, the king smiled.","\"Traitors, traitors...\"","There were traitors everywhere.","And so, he killed them all — the soldiers, the maids, the officials, the priests.","During the darkest hours of the night, the castle was full of screams of terror. Some tried to run, some tried to resist... but they all died, in the end. That was because he was suddenly full of an awful, insurmountable power.","When everyone was dead, he stood in the middle of the throne room, covered in blood.","He was laughing... laughing in relief.","‘Oh, right. There is one more traitor left...’","There was one more person he doubted. So, he raised his blade and brought it down on his own head, splitting it open.","Blood poured from the wound.","Something else poured out of it, as well...","‘What is it?'","It was silk.","Beautiful black silk spilled to the floor, blood glistening on its fine threads like jewels. Then, something moved inside his head, and a breathtaking creature emerged. Spreading its wings and shaking the blood, the bone shards, and the brain matter off them, it leaped off his head and soared into the air.","The king watched the beautiful moth fly, his eyes full of wonder.","‘So beautiful.’","He smiled before falling down.","The last thing he saw before being blinded by the dark splendor of the moth was its graceful silhouette disappearing into the vastness of the starry sky beyond the window.","'No...'","He didn't want to be apart from it.","He wanted to pursue it... to find it again... So, as his dead body began to twist and reshape itself, the king climbed the wall and dove into the window.","He rushed toward the distant mountains.","However, even as thousands of years passed...","He had never caught sight of the beautiful moth again."]},{"number":3181,"title":"Chapter 3181 Bringer of Light","paragraphs":["The shadow remembered his life as the righteous king who had been devoured by doubt.","He remembered his life as the worm of doubt that had devoured the king, as well. He remembered being the hideous creature the king had become...","And the radiant, sinister moth that had crawled out of the king's broken skull, too. The two couldn't be more different. But, for the shadow, they were one and the same. He had lived both of their long and terrifying lives, after all, so he knew. He knew that the moth had wanted to live just as desperately as the king had.","All living things were enthralled by life, and all living things were terrified of death. Except for him.","The shadow was weary of life and denied death, so there was no escape from his endless existence. There was only the tranquil peace of his lifeless kingdom and the unwelcome torment of his memories. He remembered being the moth...","The eerie creature had been insidious, but young and weak. After gaining its dark wings in the chrysalis of the king's ravaged mind, it escaped into the vast, cruel world beyond. It wanted to live, so it wanted to become stronger... to grow. And so, it did, moving across countless realms like a calamity.","Until it became a profane deity, the sinister Spirit of Doubt.","If the shadow wanted to, he could have remembered every detail of its ghastly Apotheosis. But he turned his thoughts away from those memories — not only because a terrifying abyss of Corruption was hidden in them, but also because he had no use for such knowledge.","Even if he wanted to become a god, he wouldn't go about it the same ghastly way the moth had.","‘Still, I wonder...’","There was another memory he was wary of. An event his very being resisted remembering.","It was the day the Spirit of Doubt met the Demon of Fate.","Sprawled across his lifeless realm, encompassing it, the shadow shivered.","‘Weaver...’","Even if he did not know why, he feared the nebulous daemon more than he feared the gods and all other deities.","Perhaps it was because something moved within his soul every time he thought about Weaver, as if it was pierced by an infinite number of golden strings.","The gods were dreadful, but fate was more frightening than the gods.","The Spirit of Doubt had suffered after making a deal with Weaver.","‘Have I met Weaver once, as well?'","That would explain his pitiful fate. Unnerved, the shadow cleansed his mind of all thoughts. It was dangerous to think about gods too loudly, after all... what if they heard him?","Instead, the shadow thought back to the life of the unfortunate king.","The shadow felt like he had been plagued by doubt too, a long time ago.","But eventually, he seemed to have learned trust.","Trust was a weapon that allowed him to prevail over doubt and saved him from eventually sharing a fate similar to that of the king. It allowed him to... do what?","To be cast by another, perhaps.","The shadow did not remember.","With a sigh, he turned his attention to the simple, entertaining existence of shades populating his kingdom.","Time passed.","The shadow's existence was peaceful and empty. Nothing disturbed him — apart from weary wanderers who sometimes came to his dark land, then fled in terror.","Well, and something else.","At some point, a worm of doubt found its way into the shadow's mind.","It wasn't a sinister Creature of Corruption, but rather a mundane suspicion.","The shadow wasn't sure that he was right, or how it could even be possible...","But he began to suspect there was something still clinging to life, somehow, in the dead darkness of his peaceful kingdom.","***","Far away, in a distant realm, a magnificent city sprawled under the vast sky. At the heart of the city stood a towering pyramid, its surface clad in great plates of smooth, polished stone. The pinnacle of the pyramid was encased in sheets of purest gold, and in the brilliant light of the sun, it shone with a blinding white radiance.","It was as if the pyramid was wreathed in flame; as if there was another sun burning at its tip, reflecting the glory of its celestial sister.","That was the temple and palace of the White Abyss, from which she ruled the First Kingdom.","At the moment, an elderly priest was climbing the steps of the pyramid.","He was sweating profusely, enduring the unbearable heat. His eyes were covered by a blindfold — without it, he would have been blinded by the pristine radiance of his goddess. The pyramid was tall, and the priest was old... if not for his Rank, he would have perished on the endless steps, as countless supplicants had perished before him.","But, in the end, the old priest made it to the wide platform at the end of the great stairs. Letting out a relieved sigh, he knelt in front of the golden palace hidden inside the upper part of the pyramid.","The towering gates of the palace were open, and if one was bold enough, they could try to steal a glimpse of what lay inside. However, they wouldn't see anything — because there was nothing inside the palace except an ocean of immolating white flame.","That ocean of living flame was the true form of the White Abyss — the beautiful, dreadful queen of the First Kingdom.","The priest remained on his knees for a long while, catching his breath. Then, he pressed his forehead against the scorching stones.","\"My lady, One Who Brings Light, the Eternal Flame, the Tyrant of Compassion, oh great White Abyss... I beseech thee...\"","There was silence for a long time, disturbed","only by the roaring rustle of the dancing flames.","Then, the low roar of the flames coalesced into a clear, inhuman voice.","“What is your desire?\"","The priest trembled, overcome by awe. He remained motionless for a few moments, composing himself, then spoke in a reverent tone:","“My lady, there is news from the distant reaches of your kingdom. The realm boundary is weakened, and the influence of the Void is spreading across the border regions. We are afraid that a powerful Creature of Corruption has set its sights on your people and is soon to arrive. Please, my lady! Descend from your throne and bestow your blessing upon the unworthy! Show us the brilliance of your purifying wrath!\"","There was silence once more.","Then, the priest felt the unbearable heat abating, somewhat, and the roaring of flame growing quieter.","He heard the sound of light footsteps approaching him from the gates of the palace.","As they did, he felt his soul igniting with unbearable longing. Piety, greed, devotion, ambition, love, lust — all of his wants blazed with fiery intensity, making him grit his teeth and press himself lower harder on the stone.","\"Remove your blindfold.”","The priest hesitated, then followed the command spoken in a clear, beautiful voice with a trembling hand. He still did not dare to raise his gaze, though, knowing better. As a young neophyte, he had beheld the human form of his lady once. Her silver hair, her radiant white eyes, her graceful figure, the supple perfection of her ivory skin...","The memory alone added fuel to the raging fire burning in him, making the old priest shift awkwardly and close his eyes in shame.","His queen, the White Abyss, then spoke again:","“Lead the way.\"","Soon enough, a glorious procession departed from the city. At the head of it, the old priest walked, carrying a golden scepter. Behind him, the mortal incarnation of flame, the Immortal Queen of the First Kingdom, rode atop a magnificent Transcendent beast. Soldiers and chosen members of the priesthood followed — not to assist in the battle, but to witness the glory of their goddess.","It used to be that the White Abyss ruled the Kingdom directly, appearing in front of her people every day. But those days were long past. Now, she spent most of her time in her natural form, the vast ocean of her pristine being blazing in the depths of the great pyramid, filling it with light and immolating heat.","So, it was a rare and glorious occasion to see the great White Abyss descend from her fiery throne and grace the world with her breathtaking presence.","The old priest was full of pride and self-importance... and anxiety, as well.","He wanted everything to go flawlessly, so that his goddess wasn't dishonored by imperfection.","So that she didn't find a flaw in him.","That was why he was enraged and dismayed when, many hours later, a woman who seemed like a homeless beggar appeared in the path of the procession, blocking their way.","The woman was old, with deep lines crossing her weathered face. Her hair was grey, gathered into a messy braid. Her clothes were covered in the red dust of the road, worn and unremarkable, their edges frayed. She had set up a small campfire and was warming her hands in front of it, a simple spear lying on the ground by her side.","They were crossing the desert by then, and the sun was setting... the desert was as vast as the sky. Why couldn't she have set her fire somewhere else instead of in the path of the procession?","What was worse, the woman seemed not to have noticed their approach. She ignored them completely, looking emotionlessly into the flame — the procession would have no choice but to circle around her if they wanted to move forward... unless they were to trample her without ever slowing down. Their glorious queen having to change her path because of a nameless beggar?","A murderous fury ignited in the old priest's chest.","Stepping forward, he raised his scepter, intending to strike the insolent woman down.","\"How dare you!\"","However, before he could bring the scepter down, a soft radiance ignited under his skin.","This was the light of the White Abyss — her blessing.","A moment later, the old priest opened his mouth and let out a dreadful scream. His skin boiled and blackened, pure white flame escaping from within his body and enveloping him like a storm. His chilling wail ended just as abruptly as it started, and in a second, all that remained of him was a cloud of ash.","The ash was dispelled by the wind.","Sitting atop the towering beast, White Abyss regarded his death with an indifferent expression on her exquisitely beautiful, breathtaking face.","Then, she jumped down to the ground and walked over to the old woman, her white tunic swaying lightly with each of her graceful steps.","Reaching the small fire, she looked down and studied the weathered wanderer. Then, in a voice entirely void of emotion, she asked:","“Have you come to kill me?\"","The old woman finally tore her gaze away from the fire and looked at her with a hint of surprise.","“Why would I?\"","White Abyss lingered for a moment, then sighed and looked at the sky.","There, the sun was setting, and a scattering of stars was slowly revealing themselves in the velvet darkness of the night. Eventually, she shrugged.","\"I just assumed. After all, it is not every day that one of the great gods comes to my realm...\""]},{"number":3182,"title":"Chapter 3182 Plight of Gods","paragraphs":["White Abyss glanced at the spear lying on the ground near the old woman. It was of simple design, the wooden shaft polished by countless years of use, the sharp blade carved from glistening flint.","She remained silent for a moment.","“I welcome War.\"","The old woman smiled faintly.","Turning back to the fire, she shrugged.","\"Kill you? No. It's not time for that yet.\"","The great and terrible War God — the goddess of life, warfare, progress, craft, intellect, and humans — leaned closer to the fire.","\"I just happened to be passing by. Think nothing of it.\"","White Abyss studied her with an indifferent expression. Behind her, at a distance, her soldiers and priests were trembling in fear, startled by the cruel death of their senior. Paying them no attention, the radiant incarnation of fire took a step forward and sat across from War, with only the dancing flames separating them.","The goddess spared her a curious glance. She seemed to consider something for a moment, then asked:","“A nephilim ruling a kingdom of humans — the first human kingdom, no less. How unexpected. Tell me, nephilim... that child, Kanakht. What did you do to him?\"","White Abyss tilted her head slightly.","\"I burned him. He is still burning, somewhere within me.\"","This incarnation was only a fraction of her. Most of the endless ocean of living flames that mortals called the White Abyss were still contained within the great temple, and at the heart of that temple, a blackened corpse was still being burned by the flames. It had been burning for countless centuries,","endlessly reduced to ash and restored, kept in an immolating cage of rebirth that forbade it from crossing the threshold of life.","That corpse was Kanakht, one of the First Humans — and the first human to have ever become Supreme. He had been cursed by the God of Death, after all, so he couldn't be killed.","He could only be contained.","War chuckled.","“What a cruel fate. Hasn't he suffered enough by now? All that agony, all that pain...”","White Abyss glanced at her, emotionless. However, there seemed to be a hint of incomprehension in her gaze.","After a while, she spoke in an even tone:","\"It's just pain.”","Some said that evil stemmed from a lack of knowledge, and that those who knew pain would not visit it upon another. Therefore, pain was the source of compassion. However, White Abyss knew pain better than anyone else in the world, and yet, she was not prone to mercy.","War sighed lightly.","\"So, how is it treating you? Playing a god?\"","White Abyss frowned, then glanced away with a hint of despondency in her harrowing, radiant eyes.","She remained silent for a long while. Eventually, she said evenly:","“It hasn't been easy.\"","She glanced at War.","“At the start, I wanted to be a good ruler. I wanted to protect my people from the cruelties of the harsh world and empower them to aspire. I wanted them to pursue their passions without holding back, free and unburdened. I wanted to be kind and compassionate.\"","The white radiance of her beautiful eyes shone with pristine light.","“And so, I defended them against the Creatures of Corruption. I gave them laws and institutions. I healed their wounds and eradicated their sickness. I fed them, I educated them, I provided for them. No one went hungry in my kingdom, no one suffered the cruel tyranny of need. No one was forced to endure the hardships that they had not chosen to face.\"","White Abyss fell silent for a moment, then glanced at the fire.","“But in the end, they did not flourish. Instead of prosperity, there was only rot. They grew lazy, entitled, arrogant, and overcome by insatiable greed.They turned on each other and foamed at the mouth in the frenzy to tear their neighbors down. They were consumed by envy, avarice, sloth, depravity, and malignant pride. It is so ugly... it is so distasteful. It is so unlike what I wanted to give them, and what I wanted them to take.\"","She paused, staring into the dancing flames. After a short while, White Abyss said in an emotionless, frightening tone:","“It makes me want to burn them all.\"","As she spoke those words, the flames surged, sending a cloud of fiery sparks swirling in the black expanse of the darkening sky. The soldiers and priests who stood in the distance behind her suddenly glanced small and fragile... easily erased with a thought.","War studied the radiant nephilim, a hint of a smile on her lips.","\"Why haven't you?\"","White Abyss slowly glanced away from the flame and raised her gaze to the stars.","She remained silent for a few long moments. When she spoke, her voice carried a hint of wistful distance.","“How can I? I have lived billions of lives — all of them human. I know all about how ugly humans can be, how distasteful, how deep they can fall into depravity. How fragile their convictions are, how easily they turn on each other. But, still...\"","She raised a hand, as if wanting to grasp the stars that burned in the cold embrace of the void.","“They are so beautiful.”","War raised an eyebrow.","\"What is beautiful?\"","White Abyss smiled faintly.","“Their desires.\"","She lowered her hand and glanced at War.","\"They burn so brightly, so desperately. They are so easily extinguished, and yet pursued with such passion. They are so pure. That, to me... is beauty.”","The smile drained slowly from her face.","\"Isn't that your design? Isn't that why the Flame endlessly wanes, but is never extinguished?\"","War laughed lightly and shook her head.","“We never created humans. But, yes — that is the nature of the Flame. To endlessly burn itself and be endlessly reborn from itself, never ending, created from its own destruction.\"","White Abyss sighed.","She lingered for a while, then slowly shook her head.","\"To tell the truth, I... feel like I desired something as well, once — a long time ago. I longed for something so desperately that no amount of pain, no amount of adversity, no amount of bitter defeats and heartbreaking losses could douse my resolve to achieve it. But I don't quite remember what it was, and why I strived to accomplish it so fiercely.\"","She frowned.","“That was one of the reasons why I defeated Kanakht and usurped his throne. I pitied his people, yes... but I also thought that if I helped them achieve what they longed for, then perhaps I would remember what I desired myself.”","Her expression grew distant.","“But it's strange. The more I observe their desires and care for them, the less I remember. By now, I don't think I remember at all.”","War glanced at her with a smile.","“Maybe you should try building the First Kingdom of the Corrupted, instead. You are a nephilim, after all. Those of the Flame, those of the Void — both are your kin, even if no one wants to claim you.\"","She scrutinized White Abyss for a moment, then added:","“Although that might be difficult, with that soul of yours. Truly, you are an odd creature. Rarely have I seen anyone stranger than you.\"","She sighed and glanced away.","“But even if you are merely a half-baked god, you still seem to have stumbled into the same sad predicament we did. The more we want to help humans, these strange creatures born from the sparks of the Flame, the more we harm them. It took us a while to learn our lessons... but, by now, even the most stubborn of us are tired of hurting them. Of being hurt by them. Of suffocating the sparks of the Flame burning within them.\"","War lowered her gaze.","“That is why the Age of Gods is ending. Soon, the Age of Humans will come to replace it, instead.\"","She glanced at her spear, then brushed her calloused hand across its wooden shaft.","“I was full of pity for them once, as well. At the beginning of it all, I saw them struggling desperately to survive, to stave off hunger... and so, I gave one of those pitiful humans a spear to help him hunt.\"","A pale smile illuminated her old face.","“He took it and used it to kill another human, taking his food and his woman. I gave them fire, and they used fire to burn each other's homes. I gave them knowledge of how to work metals, hoping that they would create farming tools... but they forged weapons and tools of torture instead.\"","War shook her head lightly.","“Ever since I gave that first human a spear, I was their companion. I walked among them, living a life no different from theirs and watching them grow. The spear turned into a bow, a bow turned into a cannon. A cannon turned into cluster bombs and mustard gas. Until, eventually, I watched nuclear mushrooms rise above civilian cities, and meticulously engineered bioweapons cleanse entire continents of all life.”","White Abyss seemed to freeze, looking at War with a startled expression.","Now, for the first time, a strong emotion seemed to find its way into her voice.","“How... how do you know this? You were long dead by the time all these things happened. You couldn't have seen.\"","War simply chuckled.","Reaching forward to warm her hands by the fire, she asked:","\"What is time to a god?\""]},{"number":3183,"title":"Chapter 3183 Gift of War","paragraphs":["White Abyss seemed rattled.","Despite War's casual tone, she could not help but grow tense. A myriad of thoughts seemed to flash in her eyes.","Having experienced countless lives, myriad desires, she knew a lot... she knew too much. So much, in fact, that her own life and desire were lost in the vast sea of human passions she had endured.","But all of those lives belonged to people who would live in the distant future, in a world much different from this one. So, she was aware of what all of them knew. Eventually, she spoke:","\"So... you are not dead?\"","War simply shook her head, the same faint smile illuminating her weathered face.","\"We are.\"","Then, she shrugged.","“The real War is dead. It is only this phantom that lingers.\"","A troubled frown creased the brow of White Abyss.","“You are aware, then. You knew all along.”","War raised an eyebrow, her expression betraying a lack of understanding.","“Knew what?\"","She seemed sincere enough, even if a god lacking understanding was not something that could exist.","White Abyss leaned forward slightly.","“The war. The daemons. Weaver... you knew all along how you would die, and what would happen next.\"","A hint of sudden realization appeared on her face.","“But you did nothing to prevent it. Why?\"","Then, she leaned back, the shine of her radiant eyes shimmering restlessly.","“Was it because you feared the Forgotten God? Because that was the best of all possible outcomes?\"","Now, it was War's turn to look surprised. She studied the gorgeous nephilim in confusion, remaining silent.","Eventually, she asked:","\"Why would we fear the Forgotten God?\"","White Abyss scowled.","\"Because he is the God of Corruption. Because once he awakens, the world you created will be consumed by the Void. And you will be swallowed with it.\"","War tilted her head a little, confused. Her voice sounded incredulous:","“So what?\"","She chuckled quietly.","“Why should we fear the Void? We are of the Void, after all. For us, what you call Corruption is merely change. We have never been afraid to change; we are constantly changing.\"","She paused, and then added with a hint of amusement.","\"I thought you, of all creatures, would understand.\"","War shook her head slowly.","\"Death is also a form of change. Even if our consciousness is destroyed and our spirit dissipates, we will remain — just in a different form. Our flesh is the fabric of existence, after all. One would have to destroy all of existence to erase us, and the Void... the Void doesn't destroy. It merely changes — forever.\"","She gave White Abyss a wry smile.","\"...Of course, change can also bring ruin.\"","Then, laughing quietly at the lack of reaction, she looked at the fire with a wistful expression.","\"Do not mistake reluctance for fear, child. Do not confuse desire with unwillingness. It is not that we fear our lost sibling or are unwilling to see him awaken. It is just that this world we've created... we are fond of it. We care about all the things that inhabit it, too. So, we protect it. Not because we are afraid of destruction...\"","She smiled.","“But simply because we want to.\"","Her voice echoed in the silence of the desert night, carried away by the wind. White Abyss remained motionless, as if paralyzed by what she had heard. A strange, distant light gleamed in her eyes for a moment.","But then, it was gone.","War sighed.","“But it seems that you have mistaken my meaning. Yes, our relationship with time is different from that of most things, but we are not omniscient. We are not omnipotent, either — we have never been, and now that we have shared our Flame and become diminished, even less so.\"","She scrutinized White Abyss for a moment.","“It would be difficult for you to understand, I guess. There is time... but there is also fate. And even we are not above fate. Imagine standing at a crossroads where a thousand roads intersect — you can look ahead and explore all of them, but in the end, you'll still have to choose one. As gods, we are afforded the choice. But we still have to walk a path to its end.\"","She leaned back a little, her eyes glistening in the orange glow of the fire.","“Some paths are obscured by fog. Everything that has to do with Weaver is especially difficult to see... so while we knew a lot, we did not know all of it. We chose a path and followed it earnestly. Even if we knew that, one day, we must end... we did not surrender without a struggle. We were still fighting fiercely when we reached the end of the path — because like all living things, we too are children of the Flame. We too burn with the desire to be alive.\"","War chuckled quietly.","“Even if death is nothing more than change.”","Then, she looked at the dark sky and laughed.","“Ah, death... how I despise that cowardly shadow!\"","White Abyss regarded her in silence, the fire casting harsh shadows on her face. Then, she leaned forward slightly:","“Then why didn't you win?\"","Her voice sounded stark and severe.","\"If you were so mighty, so knowledgeable, so earnest in your desire to live... then why didn't you win the war, War? Why didn't you wipe out the daemons, or at least prevent them from opening the Void Gate? Why have you allowed this world you are so fond of to become a nightmare?\"","War looked at her silently, a hint of a wistful, distant emotion in her eyes.","Eventually, she said:","\"Because the daemons were too strong to be suppressed, and we couldn't kill them.\"","White Abyss frowned.","\"Why? Because once destroyed, they would return to their source? Because that would make the Forgotten One stronger? But you are not afraid of his return, as you've said. So why did Sun God imprison Hope instead of destroying her? Why did Shadow God lose to Repose? Why had you allowed the daemons to exist, to begin with?\"","War remained silent for a few moments. After a while, she sighed and moved closer to the fire, as if wanting to chase away the chill of the night.","“It seems you don't understand us as well as you think. Well... that is only fair. After all, even the daemons, our closest kin, did not understand us.\"","Suddenly, the old avatar of War looked even older. She seemed ancient. And yet, unexpectedly, a hint of warmth found its way onto her face.","She smiled.","“Returning to their source? Sure, that was a reason. But that wasn't the real reason. In truth, we could never kill them.\"","War looked at White Abyss.","After a few moments of silence, she said:","\"...Because we love them.\"","Her expression softened slightly.","“They are all that remains of our dearest sibling, after all.\"","White Abyss stared at her in stunned silence.","Then, her indifferent expression cracked, and she suddenly laughed while raising her face to the sky.","“Because you love them? So, all this terror... all this destruction, all this loss, all this torment... all of it happened because of something as stupid and simple as love?\"","War seemed a little offended by her remark, but in the end, she simply shrugged.","“Maybe. Ah, but you really seem to have lost your way, child. I hope that you find it before we meet again.”","With that, she picked up her spear and used it to support herself as she stood. A quiet grunt escaped from her lips.","“This body of mine... has weathered too much, it seems. I feel that my change is drawing close.\"","She lingered for a moment, then said with a hint of curiosity.","“That sword of yours... the Blessing. May I take a look?\"","White Abyss frowned, then raised a hand and summoned a torrent of brilliant flame, which then coalesced into a blade forged of pure light. Reaching for it, War grasped light in her calloused hand and raised it to her eyes. She looked into its depths keenly, then gently brushed her hand along the incinerating radiance.","“Such fine craftsmanship.\"","Her voice sounded pleased.","Returning the brilliant sword to its owner, she hesitated for a moment, and then placed her spear on the ground near White Abyss.","\"A gift of gratitude, for satisfying my curiosity.\"","The beautiful nephilim looked at the flint spear in confusion.","In the end, she asked in a flat tone:","“Aren't you wary of gifting spears to mortals, by now?\"","War laughed.","“What a fine question... I have to admit, I do feel a little trepidation. Still, I hope that you will use it better. When the time comes, I hope you'll use it well.\"","Looking down at the seated nephilim, she smiled.","\"Do you know what the saving grace of existence is, child? For us gods.\"","Not receiving an answer, she sighed.","\"It's oblivion.\"","With that, War turned away from the fire and headed into the desert. As she walked, she threw over her shoulder:","\"The next time we meet, I will be different. I might not remember this conversation, either. That will be the day when I kill you... so I hope that you'll remember it well.\"","Moments later, she was gone.","White Abyss was left alone in front of the fire.","Her soldiers and priests still stood in the distance, too afraid to move.","She remained motionless for a long while, then reached forward and picked up the spear.","A grim and chilling emotion shone in her radiant eyes.","White Abyss hesitated for a moment, then looked down and sighed.","“Then let us never meet again, War.\""]},{"number":3184,"title":"Chapter 3184 Insidious Traps","paragraphs":["Somewhere far away, in a realm being consumed by Corruption...","A blind woman fell to her knees, breathing heavily.","A slender rapier hovered over her shoulder like a stinger, its long blade slick with blood.","The woman was covered in blood as well, her garments tattered and torn. Around her, countless corpses were strewn on the ground, most killed with one swift, precise blow. Some, however, were torn apart or crushed viciously, mauled and mutilated in a myriad of ghastly ways.","There were thousands of them... tens of thousands, stretching toward the horizon like a morbid carpet.","But the land was still seething with Corruption.","Everything here had been twisted and changed, becoming a perverse parody of itself. The trees were reaching forward with branches that gaped with countless maws, their leaves as sharp as blades. The riverbeds swelled with torrents of virulent rot. The blades of grass slithered like tendrils, greedily absorbing the blood of the battle. The corpses bloomed with beautiful, harrowing flowers. The air was full of acid-like pollen.","The soil itself was seeping with black, oily liquid, long vines sprouting from it and reaching toward the blind woman like snakes.","In the distance, more abominable beasts were rushing in her direction.","The woman drew a hoarse breath and rose shakily.","“Come out, come out... I remember you...\"","Before the vines could envelop her, a deafening roar shattered the world. Then, a pillar of incandescent flame plummeted from the sky, incinerating the twisting vines, the blades of grass, the clouds of pollen, and the branches of the frenzied trees.","A radiant dragon with scales of pure ivory landed with a thunderous boom in front of the woman, shielding her from danger. Another billowing torrent of flame escaped from its maw, and it lunged forward, assaulting the world of Corruption.","He was the Ivory Lord, Sevirax — a memory of him, at least.","As the great dragon tore a path through the mass of Corruption, the woman advanced forward with unsteady steps.","She had only walked for a few minutes before her champion was brought down.","In the end, even the descendant of Sun God could not resist the hungry abundance of the abominable world. His flames were swallowed by the black liquid, his talons were shattered by the impenetrable hide of mutated beasts, his mighty body was enveloped by vines and pushed to the ground. A swarm of hideous insects crawled into his ghastly wounds, and the trapped dragon let out a chilling, haunting wail of pure agony.","He was defeated... only, unlike the rest of her champions, he did not die.","Because he was immortal.","Cassie raised a hand to grasp the hilt of the Quiet Dancer and lowered her head in exhaustion.","She dismissed the memory of Sevirax.","She was so spent, so tired... so utterly exhausted.","She was all but devoid of essence, as well. But she had not reached her goal yet.","She needed to manifest another champion, but her choices had grown limited.","So, instead, she slowly pulled her blindfold up, revealing the radiant azure depths of her sole remaining eye.","The world of Corruption reflected in it, teeming with harrowing abominations. Something else reflected in it, as well.","She sighed deeply.","“It's... time. I can't keep going any longer.\"","There was a moment of silence.","Then, the hidden reflection escaped from her eye and took the form of a tall man with raven-black hair and strange, mirror-like eyes.","He regarded the sea of Corruption surrounding them, then looked at Cassie with an indecipherable expression. Eventually, he said in an aloof tone:","\"You always bring me to the most peculiar places.\"","With that, the King of Nothing turned to face the encroaching tide of abominations and raised a hand, summoning a somber spear.","“Rest a while, Lady Cassia. And remember the deal we made. After this, I will leave you.”","***","The Fifth Nightmare was an insidious trial. It was a deadly gauntlet, and if that was not enough, it was laden with countless fatal traps.","The first of the traps was the process of the unmaking. It was the Spell's way of giving its carriers a path to attaining Apotheosis — of reaching the state of mind needed to become a god, at least.","Eurys of the Nine had said once that Apotheosis could not be achieved swiftly. There was truth to his words.","One needed to live, to experience, to expand their perspective above the mundane first if they wanted to touch upon the divine. Few ever did, and those few needed hundreds of years of gradual growth and learning — thousands of years, sometimes.","But who had thousands of years to spare in a world that teetered on the brink of apocalypse?","And so, in the Fifth Nightmare, time was folded in on itself. Time here had little meaning.","The first part of the trial, which each of the challengers had to face alone, was meant to unmake them as humans and rebuild them in the image of deities. The process was quite simple... it forced them to face their own Domain.","Cassie was not sure what the others had experienced, but she could infer it from her own unmaking. Sunny had most likely been forced to experience the lives and deaths of all the shades populating his soul. Nephis had most likely been forced to experience all the lives and desires of countless people whom she had inspired... the infinite ocean of them.","Even with the new Supremes taking control of the human territories in the Dream Realm, there were still countless souls who worshiped Changing Star in the waking world, after all.","An eternity of emotions, of aspirations, of fears, of joy, of heartbreak — all folded into a single moment.","That was enough to destroy anyone. Or to change them, at least.","The unmaking itself was a trial that hid deadly traps.","The most obvious one was the threat of one's consciousness being destroyed by eternity. Of losing oneself entirely and dissolving in the endless torrent of lives and experiences forced upon them. One had to possess an incredibly strong will, an impossibly firm sense of self, an absolute resolve to stay true to their goals in order to survive that terrifying ordeal.","Even if they did, at the end of it all, they would not be the same — so by design. They would hardly remember who they had been... who they had wanted to be. Their previous self — that of a mortal human — would be made pale and faint in the face of eternity, dwarfed by the vast immensity of accumulated experience and the great scope of consciousness worthy of a deity. For Cassie, however, that ordeal had not been too difficult to endure.","At the start of the Nightmare, she had been forced to live the lives of everyone she remembered. That was a dire test, but while it was different from her past trials — remembering something was different from truly experiencing it, after all — it was not entirely unfamiliar.","So, she managed to maintain her sense of self rather well.","There was another hidden danger in the process of the unmaking, though, at least for her.","It was the threat of Corruption.","Cassie remembered countless Nightmare Creatures, after all. So, she had to endure their appalling lives too.","She suspected that many Sovereigns had endured the same. In fact, she believed that learning how to resist Corruption — to an extent, at least — was an integral part of Apotheosis.","Cassie's own ability to resist was not that formidable, but she could cheat the process. And so, she destroyed herself countless times and rebuilt herself countless times, erasing those memories that were too dangerous for her to contain within herself. At the end of it all, she emerged relatively unscathed.","She had been tempted to erase far more of her memories, in fact, to alleviate the burden... but, in the end, she decided to keep most of them.","That was because while possessing too vast a Domain could become one's undoing in the Fifth Nightmare, completely destroying their self and obliterating them, possessing too weak a Domain was a danger in and of itself.","There was a purpose to the change, after all. Escaping the unmaking too easily would make conquering the Nightmare all but impossible.","Still. In the end, Cassie had survived.","The second part of the Fifth Nightmare was a mystery. Cassie had an inkling of what the conflict they had to resolve was, but she was not sure just yet. She did, however, have a feeling that they had not entered the final trial at the same time.","Cassie herself appeared in the young and untamed world of the shared Nightmare in the later years of the Age of Gods. It took her a long time to regain her senses, gather her shattered mind, and compose herself. By then, she learned of the first trap of this trial — the threat of being swallowed by the world.","Those whose consciousness was vast enough to become a deity, but had not undergone Apotheosis yet, faced a unique danger — the danger of allowing themselves to be enthralled by the world and fusing with it, achieving the opposite of what they strived for. Of losing their personhood and becoming elemental forces instead of Spirits.","That was an insidious peril, indeed.","But for Cassie, who had always struggled to maintain her personhood in the tide of foreign senses, that trap did not pose much danger, either.","And so, she ventured on a journey.","A journey to find something that had been long lost and did not exist in the real world anymore, but could still be found in this Nightmare."]},{"number":3185,"title":"Chapter 3185 Mundane Fortune","paragraphs":["The journey had been long, but it had not been easy.","During the dusk of the Age of Gods, the mortal realms were still ruled by the Creatures of Corruption. Humans had carved out a place for themselves under the sun, but they were still on the defensive, fighting fiercely to safeguard their settlements.","Even though humans were steadily growing stronger as time went by, they were not ready to challenge the abominations for dominion over the world just yet. That would only happen when the Age of Heroes arrived, prompted by the fall of the First Kingdom and the rise of Transcendent champions who had divine blood in their veins.","So, Cassie endured a fair share of daunting battles as she searched. Some she had escaped unscathed, while some left her wounded and battered. She sought refuge among humans while she recovered — she needed to learn what they knew to reach her goal, anyway.","News brought by merchants from distant realms, old legends, rumors of strange occurrences that happened far away... Pretending to be a wandering fortune teller, Cassie learned a lot.","She learned even more from her intuition and innate affinity to revelations and fate. However, the item she was searching for could not be discovered that way — it was as if all clues about it were hidden by fog, obscured from her senses.","She continued her search.","Sometimes, she traveled with merchant caravans and temporary companions. Sometimes, she traveled alone, accompanied only by her memories. The company of those she called upon was not unpleasant... but even if they were with her, she couldn't help but feel alone.","Time passed.","One day, Cassie found herself in a human city. It was quite large by the standards of this primitive time, perched precariously on the edge of a deep canyon. People were wary of strangers here, so she didn't want to attract attention.","She was too tired and wounded to put a lot of effort into avoiding a conflict, and she didn't want to subjugate the city if its rulers acted against her out of fear, arrogance, or greed — so, it was better to remain unnoticed.","Sitting on the ground near a fountain in the main square, wrapped in her tattered cloak, Cassie unfurled a small rug in front of her and placed a chipped bowl on it, laying a small pile of carved bones by its side.","Her hair was covered by the hood of her cloak, while her face was hidden behind a veil. Her wooden staff lay nearby. She looked unremarkable and shabby — a vagabond who made a living by fooling gullible people, no doubt, instead of a demigod powerful enough to destroy the entire city... and beautiful enough to make countless men spill blood.","Cassie's appearance had never caused her trouble in the real world, but here in the Nightmare, she had learned to hide it. She did not want to launch a thousand ships, after all.","Soon enough, the first client arrived.","“Huh. A fortune teller?\"","A copper coin fell into her bowl.","\"Come on then, tell me my fortune.\"","Cassie reached for the bones and scattered them across the carpet. There was no point in doing so, but people believed her more willingly that way.","‘A copper coin...’","She hesitated for a moment, then said:","\"Praise be! What luck. Congratulations, your home will welcome the fourth child soon. This time, it will be a son.\"","There was a moment of silence, and then an excited shout.","“A son! Finally!\"","Her client paused, then asked with suspicion:","\"No, wait. Are you blind?! The bones fell in a circular pattern. That clearly means misfortune!\"","Cassie tilted her head a little.","\"I am indeed blind.”","The man scoffed.","“What can a blind fortune teller even see?\"","Cassie smiled behind her veil.","“I can see a plump, healthy boy...\"","The man cursed a few times, then stomped away.","Before that, however, he did not fail to look at her tentatively and take the coin out of the bowl without making any noise.","Cassie did not care. What use did she have for money?","But still.","‘Bastard. I was going to tell you that your handsome young neighbor is the boy's real father, but oh well!’","It was better that way, anyway. She had learned long ago that people only got angry and confrontational when she brought them bad news, accusing them of spreading lies no matter how truthful her words were. They only believed what they wanted to hear.","There were more clients after that. Cassie easily played the role of a downtrodden fortune teller.","“What luck! Your son will be promoted by the lord soon. He will even receive precious silk as a reward...\"","“Heavens above. I can see only good omens in your future. Have you offered a sacrifice to the gods recently? The gods must have been pleased...\"","“Don't fret. Fortune smiles upon you. Your younger sister will indeed be wed before you — however, you'll meet your future husband at her wedding. And he will be the most handsome man there, by far...\"","While making predictions, she listened. And as people told her about their simple lives, she learned a great deal about the city, its citizens, and the realm.","The lord here was a mighty warrior who worshipped Beast God. There was a rivalry between him and the Transcendent Monster, a great tiger, who lived in the woods. The two often quarreled and fought, but defended the city against Creatures of Corruption side by side.","There was another city across the mountains from here, ruled by a priestess of Storm God. The priestess was old and nurturing a successor — the temple she ruled had been built many centuries ago, and its influence spread across the entire realm.","...A young shepherd had, apparently, witnessed a goddess bathing in the stream and became enamored. So enamored, in fact, that a stone he had sat upon in a daze split nine months later, revealing an infant — whose skin was so tough that no sword could pierce it.","Cassie was not sure how the locals had learned that the baby couldn't be pierced by a sword, but still made sure to file the rumor away into her endless memory. There were countless strange stories like that in there, already.","Soon enough, another client sat down in front of her, wearing a troubled expression.","“Say, fortune teller... how soon will my cow recover? No, really, I need to know! She has been taking it easy for an entire month. Does she have any shame?!\"","Cassie regarded the man quietly, tilting her head slightly.","Eventually, she spoke:","\"I didn't expect to meet you here.\"","The man blinked a few times.","“Huh? Do I know you?\"","Cassie sighed.","\"It doesn't seem that you trust my words, though.\"","The man frowned.","\"Hey! Stop stalling and tell me about my cow!\"","Cassie turned slightly.","\"I wasn't talking to you.\"","Before the man could answer, his eyes glinted strangely. In the next moment, a tall figure appeared beside him, looking down at Cassie with an inscrutable gaze.","The man flinched and reeled back, shocked and confused. Looking up, he paled and tried to crawl away.","\"A... a daemon! Gods, save me!\"","The man who had appeared out of nowhere frowned, turning his head slightly to watch him escape.","“Do I look like a daemon?\"","The retreating figure reflected in the man's mirror-like eyes. He frowned.","“That fool has never seen a daemon, so how would he even know what they look like?\"","Shaking his head, he turned back to Cassie.","“And yes, Lady Cassia. I do, indeed, doubt that you had no expectations of meeting me here. The world is vast, after all. What are the chances of us stumbling into each other by chance?\"","Cassie smiled faintly.","“Well. I might have sought you out on purpose.\"","Mordret sat down in front of her and remained silent for a few moments.","He had spent countless years in the Nightmare, already. At first, he had remained with Mirage near the Mirror Lake, where this version of him had been born. Later, he escaped the reflections and went to explore the world, hiding in people's eyes and experiencing life after life as a silent witness.","He had been the reflection of countless men and women by now, having seen the heights of virtue and the depths of depravity, having accompanied slaves and kings, soldiers and farmers — numerous faces all fusing together, slowly driving him mad.","There was a simple reason why he had chosen such a strange existence.","It was because Mordret had no Domain. His brother had built himself a mighty Domain — millions of vessels carrying the fragments of his soul, all united under the banner of the King of Nothing. But all of them had either been destroyed in the war against the Dreamspawn or consumed in an attempt to conquer Apotheosis.","This Mordret, however, had never destroyed a soul to take possession of someone else's body. He felt no desire to, and found the very idea distasteful.","He had only ever created one Reflection — and left it behind in the real world, where it was desperately needed.","There was no Citadel that he ruled, either. So, Mordret entered the Nightmare with nothing... and, as a result, he had experienced no unmaking.","Which was both a blessing and a curse.","It was a blessing because he had not been destroyed by it. It was a curse because he had not been changed by it.","Reaching the second trial of the Nightmare, Mordret had been no closer to Apotheosis than before entering it. So, having deduced what should have transpired, he endeavored to correct that.","That was why he had spent centuries submerged in the lives of countless people — experiencing all their hopes and aspirations, heartbreaks and sorrows, trials and triumphs. Observing the world through countless reflections and trying to learn what it meant to be a god.","Mordret was not sure that he had learned a lot about godhood. However, he had never experienced mundane life before... so he learned quite a lot about what it meant to be human, instead.","He wasn't sure if he liked what he had learned."]},{"number":3186,"title":"Chapter 3186 Lots of Fishes","paragraphs":["“What purpose might you have in seeking me out?\"","Mordret smiled faintly.","After countless years spent in the Nightmare, his past should have grown distant, erased from his memory by the passage of time and a torrent of new experiences — or at least eroded and chiseled away, becoming pale and faded. But he found it to be untrue.","Even now, he remembered his old life vividly. Perhaps it was because no matter how long he lived and how countless memories he accumulated, the first ones would always remain vivid and meaningful. After all, the importance of the foundation did not diminish the more floors one built — on the contrary, its nature shaped the rest of the building, no matter how towering.","His childhood spent by the Dreamspawn's side, his First Nightmare and shattering, his imprisonment and the blissful, but hollow existence in the Great Mirror... being taken away from the gorgeous mirage of his fake life and caged in his brother's soul, only to be forced to kill his brother later.","There were other memories, as well — the memories of the other part of himself he had killed.","Returning to the cold embrace of Clan Valor, being betrayed and spending long years locked in a mirror cell, the madness of the Kingdom of Hope, the ceaseless currents of the Great River, the bloodshed and violence of the war between the Sword and Song Domains, and everything that followed.","Those memories belonged to him thanks to Cassia, Song of the Fallen, so he felt indebted to her.","After all, they were all that remained of his dearest brother.","Cassie remained silent for a long while, her face obscured by the veil. Eventually, she sighed.","\"I've been searching for something for a long time. However, it is hidden from me, as if obscured by fog. You are a master of fog... there is nothing you can't find, as long as it reflects light. So, I was hoping to conscript your help.\"","Mordret studied her for a few seconds. Song of the Fallen was one of the few living beings he shared a bond with. However, he did not fool himself into believing in her benevolence. There was a reason his brother had been wary of her... every word she spoke carried a hidden meaning, and everything she did was a part of an intricate scheme that even he could not glean. Those caught in the web of her lies could end up receiving incredible boons. However, they could meet a calamitous end as well. Her attention was both a blessing and a curse.","But...","There were very few things in the world he cared about.","He had nothing to lose — except time.","And time was cheap in this Nightmare. Mordret smiled faintly.","“It warms my heart to know that the lady thought of me, of all people, in her time of trouble. Ah, but a gentleman has to have a proper reason to act. So, even at the risk of sounding uncouth, I feel obliged to ask... what's in it for me?\"","Cassie pointed to the carved bones scattered in front of her.","“How about I tell your fortune?\"","Mordret chuckled.","“I am not interested in such things.\"","She sighed, then gathered the bones and picked up her bowl, hiding the coins in the folds of her tattered cloak.","“Let's make a deal, then. Help me find what I am looking for... and when the time comes, I will help you find what you are looking for.\"","Mordret raised an eyebrow.","“What is it that you think that I want to find?\"","Cassie rose and rolled up the dusty rug. Facing him, she raised her head slightly. Then, she said:","“I don't think that even you know. So, I will help you to find out.\"","***","Years later, the two of them arrived in a realm infected by Corruption. It used to be peaceful once, with vast seas and a scattering of islands that brimmed with flowers and emerald grass. But now, peace was gone.","Far away, at the heart of the realm, its largest landmass had become a fountain of abhorrent Corruption. The waters were infected by abominations, as well. The humans who had called this land their home had either been swallowed by the spreading darkness or were forced to migrate to the edges of the realm over several generations, their lives full of hardships and constant fear.","Their champions had already perished in the battles against the endless torrent of abominations. Their kin from the neighboring realms were too busy fighting existential battles of their own to come to someone's help.","It was then that a blind oracle crossed the boundary of the infected realm, carrying a mirror wraith in her one remaining eye. Cassie put her bowl down near the well in a crowded village, hoping to hear the stories that the locals had to tell. However, people here were downtrodden and anxious, buckling under the weight of harsh life. None of them had money to spare, and even if some of them did, they only glanced at Cassie with distrust and suspicion.","Even after a few hours had passed, her bowl remained empty. She still learned a lot from encompassing the village with her senses, but it wasn't the same as becoming a foil vessel for the people to pour their worries and aspirations into.","Cassie sighed.","The goal of her search was hidden from her senses, and yet she felt that it was close. She knew that it was, in fact — Mordret had told her as much. His senses covered a vast area, after all, myriad reflections serving him as a myriad of eyes. He had been Cassie's guide for a long time, and now, they finally reached the end of the path. Suddenly, something fell into her bowl. It didn't sound like a coin, though.","Reaching forward, Cassie felt around the clay bowl and picked up a peculiar item. To her surprise, it was a piece of homemade candy wrapped in a thin cloth.","Raising her head, she faced her only client in this realm — a small boy, too young to lose even a single tooth, looking at the candy with a deep sense of regret and longing.","There was also a hint of hope hidden in the rhythm of his rapidly beating heart. He glanced at Cassie and hesitated for a moment.","\"Do you tell fortunes, grandma?\"","Cassie's face was hidden by a veil, her clothes were tattered and covered in dust, and she made a point of keeping her posture slightly bent, her steps and movements tentative and careful. She also used a wooden staff to support herself as she walked — so, it wasn't surprising that people assumed her to be an old woman. It was, in fact, an impression she meticulously created and maintained. Smiling behind the veil, she nodded. “Indeed. Are you interested in learning the secrets of fate, young man?\"","The boy nodded eagerly.","“Yes! My daddy and the other daddies can't catch any fishes! Because their boats are broken. Daddy is always sad, and my tummy hurts without the fishes. When will my daddy smile at me again?\"","Cassie remained silent for a long while, then quietly scattered the carved bones. The sea was teeming with abominations, so of course, the local fishermen had lost their boats. They were fortunate not to have lost their lives, really... but how long could they and their families survive without fishing? These people have lost their land, their roots, and the means of sustaining themselves. Even if Corruption and the abominable creatures it created did not kill them, starvation and destitution soon would.","So, the piece of candy the boy had given to the fortune teller must have been a real treasure for him.","Pretending to look at the bones, Cassie smiled behind her veil.","“Oh, my. Look at this!\"","The boy glanced at the bones, his eyes widening in wonder.","Cassie pointed to one of them.","\"Great fortune awaits, young man! Soon, there will be lots and lots of fishes. You daddy will smile all day, and your tummy won't hurt anymore. There will be a lot of candy, as well.\"","The boy smiled hesitantly.","\"Really?\"","Cassie nodded.","“Of course!\"","His smile widened slowly.","“Really, really?\"","Cassie gathered the bones.","“Really, really. Trust me — I've been telling fortunes for countless years.\"","She didn't lie to the boy. What she had told him would, most likely, come true.","Because Cassie was here. She had come to this realm pursuing selfish goals, but the sea of Corruption tormenting it stood in her way.","So, she was going to eradicate the Corruption and destroy its appalling spawn. She was going to cleanse this realm.","***","Finally, Cassie had reached her goal.","Having exhausted her power, she called upon the King of Nothing. And once the King of Nothing revealed himself, the sea of Corruption had no choice but to be destroyed.","Mordret did not command an army of vessels, and neither was he accompanied by powerful Reflections. All he had was a spear and an unbreakable will to see the adversary fall.","But he was a Supreme Titan, after all, as well as a wielder of a Divine Aspect and a descendant of War.","So, the abominations fell.","Following in his footsteps across a ravaged landscape, Cassie passed towering carcasses, splinters of obliterated trees, and pools of black blood so deep that one could drown in them. Eventually, she reached the slopes of a vast crater.","The abominable life spawned by Corruption was even thicker here, emanating waves of chilling, penetrating malevolence. It was so plentiful, in fact, that even Mordret found it difficult to cleave a path through its mass. Cassie hesitated, knowing that she had one more champion to call upon...","But hearing the echoes of his mad laughter and feeling the cold edge of a flawlessly white jade blade, she chose to keep that monster caged in her memory.","‘I'm almost there...’","In the end, Mordret fulfilled his part of the deal and guided her to the very bottom of the crater, where the source of all this Corruption was lying on the blackened soil. It was a single, radiant eye seeping with drops of golden ichor.","\"Do not look into its depths.\"","Hearing her warning, Mordret frowned and averted his gaze.","Kneeling in front of the eye, Cassie trembled slightly.","'Finally, I've found it.'","It was the torn eye of a deity...","It was Weaver's eye.","The one that had been stolen by the Thieving Bird and drove it mad, infecting its soul with Corruption.","“What a ghastly thing”","Mordret's voice was quiet.","“What are you planning to do with it?\"","Cassie hesitated for a few seconds.","“I am planning to make it mine.\"","He stared at her, a stunned expression on his face.","Then, he frowned and shook his head slightly.","“That doesn't sound like a good idea.\"","Despite the fear that held her in an iron grasp, Cassie forced out a pale smile.","“I've run out of good ideas countless years ago.\"","With that, she raised a hand and pulled her blindfold down.","Her one remaining eye was revealed, its radiant blue depths full of trepidation. The gaping wound in place where her other eye had been was revealed, as well.","Cassie remained motionless for a long while, then reached toward Weaver's eye with a trembling hand.","Picking it up between two fingers, she shuddered once more...","And then pushed the bloodied eye into her empty eye socket.","Moments later, a horrible scream shattered the sky above the deep crater."]},{"number":3187,"title":"Chapter 3187 Pursuit of Light","paragraphs":["The shadow's authority over his kingdom was absolute. There was nothing within its dark boundary that did not belong to him, so naturally, there was no one who drew breath. His land was a land of death, with only the shades under his control simulating the acts of the living.","And yet, he could not shake off the suspicion that something was hiding within the darkness, obscured even from his senses.","He could not sense any movement that could not be explained, and he could not hear any sounds that could not be traced to a predictable source. And yet, at times, he felt a faint, alien presence.","A presence that should not have existed in his dead kingdom — the presence of someone who was still alive.","‘How can this be?'","The shadow had killed everything in this land. Countless years had passed since then, and no one managed to enter the eternal darkness shrouding it. The humans who came to find out how the nation born from the Shadow Tribe had been wiped out turned back and fled in fear, while the Creatures of Corruption who dared to enter his domain were ruthlessly slain.","So, if there was a living being somewhere in his kingdom, it could only mean one of two things.","One was that someone had managed to sneak past his senses and was still hiding. The other was that someone had managed to survive his wrath and had been hiding from his gaze ever since.","Both possibilities left him displeased.","So, the shadow endeavored to find the source of the elusive presence. He explored every corner of his kingdom with special attention. He even ordered all the shades under his control to stop, wanting to eliminate the chance of their movements obscuring something he had failed to notice.","And yet, he failed to find anything.","‘Did I imagine the whole thing?’","If the shadow had a physical body, he would have frowned.","‘No, it was definitely here...'","From then on, he ordered his shades to stop for a few moments every day, hoping to sense the strange presence again.","Time passed, with nothing in particular happening. The shadow continued to rule his dead kingdom. Outside the vast expanse of his dark land, the world continued to change.","He had learned some news from the conversations of people who sometimes arrived in hopes of solving the mystery of the eerie darkness, but inevitably retreated after witnessing its frightening depths.","The Age of Gods was ending.","In fact, it was already over. Somewhere far away, the strange creature known as the White Abyss had withdrawn her grace from the people of the First Kingdom, appearing in front of them less and less. Eventually, she ceased responding to mortals altogether, becoming no more than an ocean of eternal flame burning furiously in the confines of her great temple.","The First Kingdom continued its existence for a few more generations, but eventually collapsed and splintered, thus ushering in a new age — the Age of Heroes.","All across existence, humans had become powerful enough to challenge the Creatures of Corruption openly. Instead of merely surviving in a hostile world, they were now fighting for dominion over it — led by exalted champions, of course. Strength was a question of accumulation, in most cases.","Throughout the Age of Gods, humans had been learning and accumulating knowledge — they went from hunting beasts with flint spears to forging intricate tools and weapons out of bronze. The copper knife that Tatal had treated with such awe would be seen as a common item now, an inferior and trifling blade no less.","Humans had learned how to work mystical and sublime materials, as well, which allowed them to create truly lethal weapons.","That was the deadly power of progress. They had progressed in countless other areas, as well, from sorcery to philosophy and agriculture. Being able to grow more food allowed more people to be born, which in turn allowed more champions to rise from their ranks.","A new and previously unheard-of concept, writing, was slowly spreading among some people — it was a gift from Hope, the Demon of Desire.","Humans had learned more about the Path of Ascension, as well, solving its mysteries and slowly developing essence techniques to climb it. When Tatal became a Transcendent, that had been a legendary feat — something nearly unheard of, let alone witnessed by many. But now, there were far more Transcendents around, all of them brimming with fighting spirit and resolve.","There were descendants of the gods among them, as well — humans with divine blood in their veins.","Harnessing the power of progress, humans ventured to conquer the world.","So, the world was slowly changing under their footsteps.","At the same time, the gods seemed to become more distant. While their avatars still existed, they rarely left the Divine Realms to roam the lands populated by mortals. Most of the daemons, too, had become withdrawn.","Mirage was spending more and more of her time inside her Great Mirror. Rime was exploring distant skies aboard her living ship. Ariel was rumored to have become fascinated by a beautiful monster, for whom he had built a magnificent palace from pure white jade. Nether spent his time by Storm God's side...","None of them, except Hope, seemed to be interested in humans that much.","And so, the heroes of humanity could stand tall.","No troublesome hero had grown brazen enough to try bothering the shadow, though, which he was thankful for.","Even if he felt that encountering a fool or two was only a matter of time.","Before that happened, though, he finally managed to confirm his suspicion and find the source of the strange presence.","That day, when the shades froze for a few minutes, he resorted to something he rarely did — he took a physical shape and appeared on the streets of the silent city.","All around him, shades stood motionlessly, each frozen in the middle of what they had been doing. After studying the eerie scene for a while, the shadow walked into the largest structure in the city — the temple dedicated to the six great gods — and made his way to its inner sanctum.","He had not dared to enter the temple before. Last he saw, the priests of the temple had been corrupt and greedy, hoarding riches and engaging in vices... still, nothing good could come from desecrating the home of the gods.","Even when the shadow commanded his shades to emulate the actions of living people, he had avoided sending anyone into the temple. The shades of the priests were only ever allowed to stand on its steps. Now, however, he made his way further inside. And there, in one of the treasuries hidden inside the inner sanctum, he found something that made his thoughts darken.","There, a box forged from metal lay on a pedestal — and not just any metal, at that. It was a Transcendent material akin to black silver, known for its great durability and crushing weight.","The box was wrapped in chains.","Hesitating for a moment, the shadow tore the chains and broke the lock, opening the heavy lid.","As soon as the lid opened, he hissed in displeasure. Brilliant light poured from beneath, pushing his darkness away — even if only for a moment. Then, the darkness grew deeper, and the light was suffocated, retreating to hide back inside the silver box. The source of the pure radiance... was a radiant, transparent crystal. The source of light was hidden in its depths, like a ray of sunlight trapped in clear ice.","Before the shadow could react, the crystal suddenly cracked, and the ray of light escaped from it like a brilliant arrow.","In the blink of an eye, it shot through the window and disappeared from sight.","‘How does this even make sense?'","All of the shadow’s kingdom was enveloped in darkness, and that darkness was the shadow. Even if the beam of pure light had managed to escape the temple, it would still remain within the shadow — but he could not sense it at all.","It was as if the light had hidden somewhere. And, indeed, that was the case.","A few moments later, the shadow found the light hiding inside the statue standing in the center of the city plaza. He destroyed the statue, and the ray of light escaped again.","Next, it hid inside a training dummy deep within the city barracks. The shadow destroyed the dummy, as well, but still failed to catch the annoying sprite.","That was how their game of cat and mouse began.","For the next few days, the shadow searched for the light, while the light continued to escape him. In the end, however, the shadow managed to drive the radiant thing into a corner.","Even if that corner was quite unexpected... It was a vast cave in the neighboring mountains — the very same cave the shadow had once called his home.","Taking a physical shape, he entered the familiar coldness and looked around. Everything was dark.","‘Where the hell is that damn thing?’","He walked around, and then kicked a small pile of rocks away with his foot.","Beneath it, a small figure was revealed, cowering and covering its head with both hands.","The shadow froze, staring at it with a surprised expression on his vaguely contoured face.","It was a tattered, dreadfully ugly doll. Unable to stay silent, the shadow opened his mouth and spoke for the first time in countless years.","\"...Snuggle?\"","The doll lowered its hands slightly and looked at him with its black, beady eyes. Then, unbelievably, it answered in a squeaky voice.","It said:","\"I... I'd rather not!\""]},{"number":3188,"title":"Chapter 3188 Lost Soul","paragraphs":["The shadow stared at the tattered doll in complete incomprehension.","It was all very peculiar.","Why was Snuggle suddenly moving and talking? The last time he checked, it had definitely been a mundane doll. The only unique thing about it was its unusual longevity.","Countless years had passed since Snuggle had been sewn. Entire kingdoms had been founded and collapsed, the bones of their rulers turning to dust. Humanity had endured the countless trials of prehistoric times and entered a new, enlightened era. The Age of Gods had even come to an end, but the ugly doll was still here.","Snuggle had already been close to four hundred years old by the time the shadow brought her to this cave, and more time had passed since then. At first, it had persevered because Tatal wanted it to ... and after Tatal died, it was because the shadow willed so.","But despite that, it had been a simple doll. Now, however...","Peering into the depths of the ugly thing, the shadow was blinded by the pure radiance of a brilliant soul.","Now, Snuggle seemed to have become a living being.","She was a Transcendent Beast.","The shadow frowned.","‘Since when?'","For a moment, he entertained the idea that Snuggle had somehow come to life. But, naturally, that was not the case. It was the light — the one he had been chasing for the last few days. The strange thing had turned out to be a naked soul that was somehow able to wander the world without a physical body, and now, it had hidden inside the ancient doll, using it as a vessel.","The shadow...","Was greatly displeased.","A dark feeling of dismay and anger rose from the depths of his being, and he considered ruthlessly destroying the audacious soul. What right did it have to touch that doll, after all? That doll was the only memento of Tatal he had left. Any being who touched or damaged it without the shadow's permission deserved to suffer his wrath.","But, in the end, he did not move to destroy the brilliant soul.","One reason for his inaction was that, despite having eradicated all life in this kingdom, the shadow felt a faint reluctance to kill anyone without cause.","The main reason, though, was that he was not entirely sure how to destroy the odd being without damaging Snuggle. After remaining silent for a few seconds, he reached down to pick up the doll. However, it let out a stifled squeak and dashed away, escaping his grasp.","Due to Snuggle's form, her attempts to run away looked very clumsy. The doll swayed and wobbled from side to side as she ran, raising her arms to keep her balance. Despite that, though... her speed was quite surprising. She was so quick that her hair, made out of coarse black fur, fluttered in the wind. Her crude dress rippled.","The shadow sighed.","‘Does she really think that she can outrun me?’","He took a step and appeared dozens of meters away, directly in front of the running doll. She let out another squeak and desperately tried to turn, only to slam into his shin and bounce back.","As the shadow leaned down to grab her, the doll reached for the closest thing she could find and shielded herself with it, turning her head away.","\"Please, don't eat me!\"","A clear, melodious ringing resounded in the dark cave.","The shadow froze.","In front of him, held between Snuggle's small hands, was a silver bell...","And as soon as he heard it ring, he was overwhelmed with memories.","The memories of meeting Tatal for the first time. The memories of her introducing the ugly doll to him. The memories of finding the doll in the silent room, beside Tatal's deathbed.","And many more, as well.","Tatal...","Probably wouldn't have wanted him to kill this lost soul.","Or anyone, really.","She had been kind, after all — unlike him. Suddenly, a mournful feeling welled inside the shadow's soul. He missed his friend... but, more than that, he was saddened by the understanding that Tatal would not have liked to see him the way he had become.","She probably would not have liked him at all.","So what right did he have to hold on to this doll?","‘How many children were there in the city I destroyed?’","The shadow had never once considered this before.","But now that he did, suddenly, he felt a bitter taste in his mouth.","The shadow was nauseated.","He straightened and pulled his hand back, staring at the cowering doll with a distant expression.","His heart felt heavy.","‘Since when do I have a heart?'","The shadow threw one last look at the familiar form of Snuggle, then silently turned and walked away. Soon, his figure dissolved into the darkness.","A minute or two later, Snuggle carefully lowered the bell and peeked from behind it. Then, she hesitantly rose to her feet.","\"It... left?\"","Her squeaky voice was full of surprise. Exhaling in relief, the crude doll then leaned on the bell and glanced around. After a few seconds, her voice resounded once more, full of trepidation:","“But... where am I?\"","***","The shadow dismissed his physical manifestation and returned to his usual state — passively observing his kingdom. All across it, countless shades began to move once more, simulating mundane actions of the living.","The people went about their business. The birds flew from branch to branch. The trees swayed, and the insects crawled in the mud. Shrouded by darkness, all of them were flawlessly black and silent.","However, their silence did not bring him peace anymore.","The shadow felt lost.","He did not know what to do. He did not know who he was, who he had been... which was nothing new.","He had never known that. But now, for the first time, he asked himself a new question.","‘Who do I want to be?'","There was no answer.","The shadow did not know what he would become, either. Without knowing who he had been and who he was, how could he? Letting out a sigh, he concentrated on the silent tranquility of his dark kingdom.","..Only it wasn't that silent or tranquil anymore.","A few hours after he had encountered the doll, she tentatively glanced out of the cave, turned her head this way and that, trembled, and quietly stepped out.","It was just that that silver bell she was dragging behind her caught on a stone and rang, its ringing spreading for many miles. Snuggle fell to her knees and covered her head with both hands.","The shadow grimaced.","Not knowing that the darkness surrounding her was the shadow, Snuggle gathered her courage and glanced around once more. Not noticing any movement, she sighed with relief and ventured down the mountain. She was brazen enough to make herself glow, even, illuminating her path.","The shadow had decided to ignore the strange being, but still. Wasn't she a little too bold, shining so brightly in his lightless realm?","‘Insolent...'","Despite not wanting to pay the doll any attention — the shadow only hoped that she would leave his kingdom of her own accord — he could not help but trace her every step.","The damn thing was walking around within him, after all, pouring luminous radiance everywhere she went. How was he supposed to ignore her?","Eventually, Snuggle reached the city. She seemed cautious at first, hiding in the shadows for a while and observing the shades.","Then, she seemed terrified.","Still carrying the silver bell, the small doll sneaked through the quiet streets, looking up at inky-black people who went about their business in absolute silence. Apart from the unnatural darkness and the lack of sound, the city seemed like a normal city at first glance... but once one looked closer, its eerie nature was revealed.","The inky-black people were not really alive. They did all the things that living people were supposed to do, but it was all pretend. A peddler offered his customer fruit, and the customer tasted it... but he only brought the black fruit to his mouth, never biting into it. A young couple enjoyed a stroll, holding hands — but when they glanced at each other, there was only hollow indifference in their empty, glassy eyes. A worker was repairing a cracked wall, but there was no mortar in the bucket he used — instead, the wall mended itself as soon as he pretended to move his trowel.","The doll pressed herself against a wall and squeaked in a terrified voice:","“What... what kind of hell is this?\"","Finally, the shadow's patience ran dry. Suddenly, a cold voice resounded from the darkness:","“You're quite rude, aren't you?\"","The doll shuddered and glanced around in panic, her beady eyes reflecting the soft radiance emanating from beneath the coarse fabric of her sewn body.","The shadow scoffed and added, his voice full of contempt:","“And you must not have been to many hells, either. My kingdom is very peaceful and serene. How can you compare it to hell?\"","The doll tried to back away, but there was a wall behind her. She froze for a moment, then bravely raised the silver bell and put it in front of her.","\"D—don't come near! Or I will ring it again!\"","The shadow studied her, completely baffled.","After a while, he asked in an even tone:","“And what do you think will happen if you do?\"","Snuggle hesitated, then asked in a voice","that sounded less and less confident with each word.","“Of course, it will... it will scare you away... like the last time?\"","The shadow fell into silence once more. Then, cold laughter resounded from the darkness.","“Why would the ringing of my own bell scare me?\"","He shook his head mentally.","That doll did not seem particularly bright.","'Well, what did I expect? She's a mere Beast. It is already a miracle that she knows how to speak.'","Come to think of it, why was a mere Beast speaking?","He hesitated for a moment, and then added:","“And it is my bell. So you are not only rude, but also a thief. How untoward.\"","The doll froze for a moment, then squeaked:","“At least... at least I don't harass complete strangers wanting to snuggle! Who's untoward now, huh, you creepy demon?!\"","The shadow chuckled menacingly.","“First of all... I am not a Demon. I am a Titan.\"","The doll hiccuped and fell on her backside.","\"Second of all — don't flatter yourself, little Beast. Snuggle is the name of the doll you stole.\"","The shadow fell silent for a moment.","\"It belonged to a dear friend... so treat her with care.\"","For the first time, there was a tiny hint of emotion in his voice."]},{"number":3189,"title":"Chapter 3189: Entertaining Guest","paragraphs":["Snuggle looked down at her clumsy hands and crude dress. She remained silent for a while, as if having realized something. Then, she hesitantly lowered the silver bell.","\"A...a Supreme Titan? I see.\"","Her voice trembled a little.","The shadow observed her for a while, not sure what to do.","‘A Supreme Titan...‘","Come to think of it, she was correct — he was indeed a Supreme Titan. Technically, at least. In truth, he was probably halfway to becoming Spirit... it was just that he did not know how to take the last step, and had no desire take it anyway.","The curious thing, however, was that the transient soul who had inhabited Snuggle easily identified his Rank. Unlike the humans who wandered into his kingdom from time to time, she had not confused him for a Creature of Corruption. All hints pointed to the fact that she could perceive his soul, somehow — or at least a part of it.","As for the transient soul itself...","Now that the shadow had bothered to take a closer look, he realized that it was quite unusual.","The soul belonged to a Transcendent Beast, without a doubt. However, its radiance was far too brilliant, too dazzling, as if her lustrous essence was more potent than it was meant to be — potent enough to belong to a Supreme, perhaps.","It also possessed an unusual hue.","Souls infected by Corruption brimmed with appalling darkness, while pure souls shone with pure silver light. This soul, however, burned with a beautiful golden radiance, shining like the morning sky set ablaze by the brightness of dawn.","The shadow knew that radiance well.","It was the color of divinity.","‘A wandering soul that burns with the flame of divinity.‘","Where could have a soul like that come from?","The shadow studied the ugly doll for a few moments, then took a physical shape. Soon, a vague figure made of shadows appeared in front of the Snuggle, looking down at her. Its face was a vague silhouette hidden behind layers of nebulous darkness, and the same darkness shrouded it like a mantle. Snuggle looked up at him, trembling.","“Were you... were you hiding in the darkness all this time?\"","The shadow tilted his head a little, then shook it.","\"No.\"","Then, gesturing to the silent city, he said in a cold, penetrating voice:","“Everything you see here is a part of me. The darkness, the shades of the people, the grass, the trees — all of it is my kingdom, and my kingdom is me.\"","He paused for a moment, and then smiled vaguely.","\"So, silly doll, your attempts to hide from me are meaningless. After all, you are walking around inside my soul, illuminating it carelessly with your light.\"","The doll looked around, seeming a little distraught. Then, she coughed.","“So, then, this thing in front of me... is just a physical form you took for convenience?\"","The shadow nodded.","Inwardly, he wondered why the doll was pretending to cough — she did not have a throat, after all. It seemed like a human habit.","Come to think of it, Snuggle did not even have a mouth — only an awkwardly stitched curve that served her as one. So how was she even speaking? What power moved her little body, and what gave her the strength to lift the silver bell?","He was not exactly curious... but, for a moment, he did feel a tiny pang of interest.","\"It is.\"","Snuggle hesitated for a few moments, then asked in her squeaky voice:","“Then... do you mind turning into something less creepy? With all due respect, of course!\"","After that...","She giggled awkwardly.","The shadow stared at the brazen doll, stunned for a moment.","‘The... the audacity?’","Did she not know fear?","The request to take a different shape did not bother him, but laughing in the solemn silence of his kingdom, standing directly in front of his physical manifestation...","Was it fearlessness or stupidity? Or both?","‘But probably the latter.'","He glared at the doll for a moment, then smiled pleasantly.","“I don't mind.\"","With that, the shadows swelled and billowed, surrounding him like a storm. A colossal, grotesque shape rose from them, dwarfing the buildings — the shape of a fearsome, hideous creature that seemed to have crawled out of the very depths of the Abyss.","As his myriad limbs obscured the dark heavens, Snuggle shuddered and pressed herself against the wall.","“Come to think of it, your previous form was very fitting! It was tasteful, comely, and full of grace! Ha, ha-ha... it was a joke, a joke, just a joke!\"","The shadow stared at her from the great height of his current form, then scoffed quietly and dismissed it.","‘That's better. That will teach her manners.’","Then, he fell into contemplation for a moment.","Taking a less frightening form? He did not care either way, so he could as well do it.","As if remembering an old habit, the shadow made a little effort and appeared in front of trembling Snuggle again. This time, he looked like a human.","In front of her stood a young man with porcelain skin and eyes that were like onyx, his hair as black as the darkest depths of night. He wore a simple tunic of black silk, while his expression was cold and aloof, devoid of all emotion.","“There. Are you satisfied?\"","The doll looked up cautiously, stared at him for a few moments with its beady eyes, and then nodded.","“Y—yeah... that's better! Much better!\"","The corner of his mouth rose slightly, but the faint smile never reached his tenebrous eyes.","‘What am I supposed to do now?’","The shadow had never entertained guests in his kingdom. All who came here either fled or died — so, he wasn't entirely sure what to do next.","After remaining silent for a while, he bent, picked up the silver bell, and tied it to his belt. Then, he glanced at the little doll and asked:","\"Shall I show you around my kingdom?\"","And that was how he ended up escorting Snuggle along the dark streets, describing the past of the Shadow Tribe. It felt strange and unfamiliar... but not entirely unwelcome.","Perhaps he had missed having conversations with someone.","Perhaps he had simply grown tired of his monotonous existence, and wanted to brighten it with the sound of someone else's voice.","After some time, Snuggle rubbed her forehead.","“It seems that I've been trapped for a long time.\"","He looked at her with a hint of curiosity.","“How did a wandering soul like you end up being trapped inside that crystal and locked inside a box, to begin with?\"","Snuggle let out a nervous laugh.","“Well... actually, only the box was a trap. I created the crystal myself.”","The shadow raised an eyebrow, prompting her to continue.","\"It's a... enchantment of a sorcerous item I possess. It places something into a state of stasis for as long as its master can sustain the sorcery with their essence. A very useful thing! You can remove a powerful Nightmare Creature from battle and deal with its minions first, for example. Or keep a can of be... I mean, an amphora of wine cool for a long time.\"","Snuggle sighed, her shoulders dropping.","“But, well, after spending years in this nightmarish world, I ended up in big trouble. So, in order to survive, I cast the sorcery on myself. That created a paradox — the sorcery could only be sustained for as long as I had essence, but I was placed in stasis. So, the amount of essence I had became static, as well. Therefore... I actually have no idea how may years passed since that day.\"","She looked around in confusion.","“They must have failed to destroy the crystal and decided to lock me in that box instead. The item that creates it is very powerful, so I am not even sure what could have damaged the sorcery enough for the crystal to crack... but it did crack some time ago, and little by little, I regained my senses. However, I couldn't escape the box... until you opened it.\"","The shadow remained silent.","He wasn't sure what danger the wandering soul had found itself in, and who it was that put the crystal in the box. Had it been the High Priest of the Shadow Tribe temple, or the rulers of the city? The very people who had sacrificed a living soul to him?","Or had it been someone else, who then traded the sorcerous crystal away or surrendered it to an enemy as a spoil of war? How many hands had the box passed through before ending up in the inner sanctum of that temple?","The shadow did not know.","He knew two things, though.","The first one was that, no matter who had trapped the wandering soul in the box, they must have been quite a powerful being. Runic sorcery had not spread widely yet, after all, and Shaping did not function in the absence of a sorcerer. So, creating a soul trap was not an easy task.","The second thing... he had an inkling of what had damaged the sorcery keeping the stasis crystal intact.","Looking at the small doll that waddled by his side, he said:","“I think I know what put a crack in your crystal.\"","Snuggle seemed curious.","“Oh, really? What was it?\"","Then, she waved a hand.","\"By the way... sorry for earlier! Now that I got to know you a little better, you don't seem quite as scary anymore, Lord Titan. You are actually quite nice!\"","The shadow shrugged.","Was he?","Glancing at the shades that surrounded them, he said:","“The crystal must have cracked when I swallowed this land and killed every living thing in it — the people, the beasts, the trees, the grass... I willed everything to die, but the crystal must have protected you. It is quite unexpected that something survived.","He looked down at Snuggle and smiled faintly.","“You are quite a fortunate little soul, aren't you? Oh, and thank you for saying that I am not at all scary and very nice... I agree.“","Snuggle tripped and fell down."]},{"number":3190,"title":"Chapter 3190 Freedom of Choice","paragraphs":["The shadow showed the transient soul the rest of his silent city. However, she grew much quieter after learning the nature of the shades that surrounded them. He did not have much to say, anyway — most of his memories of this place belonged to a time when the city was a makeshift settlement, and its people were no more than hunters and gatherers who barely knew how to farm land.","Tatal, Stone Hand, and their children... he remembered them well, but he knew very little about the people who had become his shades.","Of course, if he wanted to, he could peer into each of the shadows that dwelled within his soul and glean their past. The strings of their fates all ended in a single point, after all — in him. So, it was easy to learn about them. He had already glimpsed some of it when creating his kingdom, though, and had no desire to delve deeper into the mess of human lives.","Eventually, the two of them reached a solemn square with a monument towering above its center. The monument depicted a lone human figure facing a great wyrm.","The shadow studied the monument for a while, then said in an aloof tone:","“This is a statue to the Great Shaman who saved the people of this land from a terrible monster. There were no Transcendents among humans back then, so a Transcendent Devil was like a world-ending calamity. The shaman was a mere Master, but she faced the berserk creature alone. In the end, she defeated it.\"","Snuggle studied the monument for a long while.","Eventually, she asked:","“And what happened to her after that? Is she somewhere here, among these shades?\"","The shadow shook his head.","\"She lived a long and fulfilling life and eventually died of old age, surrounded by people who loved her. It was a... a good end.","The little doll remained silent for a few moments, then sighed.","\"Mere Ascended facing a world-ending calamity alone... such a familiar story. Sadly, the heroes of the story I know did not win. They did not get their happily ever after, either.\"","She paused for a moment, then glanced at the shadow. Her perpetually downturned mouth twisted into a little grin.","\"Not yet, at least!\"","He lingered for a bit, not sure what she meant, then nodded.","“This concludes the tour of my kingdom. As you can see, it is not at all a hell.”","Snuggle chuckled weakly.","“Indeed. It is more of a Limbo... or a purgatory, perhaps. If its master has any mercy.\"","She glanced at the shadow, hesitated a little, then asked:","\"Can I ask you a question?\"","The shadow stared at the tattered doll, impassive.","\"You can.\"","She turned to face the silent shades, observing their meticulous pretense of life.","\"Why did you kill all these people?\"","The shadow straightened and glanced away. He did not say anything for a long while, then uttered in a cold tone:","\"Because I was angry. Because it was easy.\"","The shadow paused, imagining what his kingdom looked like to the transient soul. Trying to see the world from a different point of view was not easy for him — it was a skill that he had seemingly possessed once, but lost somewhere along the way.","Eventually, he added:","“Even if I never wanted it, these people treated me like a deity. They prospered under my accidental protection, spared from the countless cruelties of this vast world. There was only one commandment I ever gave them — it was to never sacrifice a human life to me. I warned them that if they ever did, I would erase their tribe from existence.”","The shadow fell silent.","After a while, he spoke again, his voice sounding a little quieter:","\"But they didn't listen. Human memory is short.\"","Snuggle studied the silent shades.","After a while, she sighed.","“This is all new to me. Life has spoiled me, you see... I am used to Nightmare Creatures slaughtering innocent people, but I never really faced the malice of those who are free of Corruption. I am quite fortunate, don't you think? To have only ever fought monsters.\"","The shadow glanced at her with surprise.","“What are you talking about, silly doll? Humans are the most monstrous creatures of them all.\"","He turned his gaze to his silent kingdom, populated by the shadows of those he had slain.","“Because only humans have a choice. The Creatures of Corruption know nothing but agony and the desire to consume the Flame — they simply act according to their nature. But every human who commits an act of evil does so by choice.\"","Snuggle stared at him for a moment, then asked:","“Doesn't that make you a human, Lord Titan? After all, you committed this evil act by choice, as well.\"","The shadow tilted his head a little, feeling vague memories rise from the depths of his mind at the sound of her words.","Choice...","He felt like he had fought desperately for the right to have a choice, a long time ago. He must have won that desperate struggle... and for what?","Was he making good choices? What had he done with the privilege of being able to choose, to have chosen?","He was not sure.","The shadow smiled.","“I was human once... I was human myriad times. But it's strange — the more lives you live as a human, the less humanity you have left. You are right, however. I did make a choice. And that choice... it does seem like an act of evil.\"","Snuggle stared at him in confusion for a short while, then shook her head.","\"Well, anyway... what are you going to do with me? I, uh, I hope you are not planning to add me to your collection of dead souls?\"","The little doll shifted uncomfortably and put her hands on her hips.","“Because I—let me tell you! I have not angered you, and I won't be easy to kill. More than that, I have never sacrificed anything to you, so there's no reason to kill me, to begin with!\"","The shadow stared at her for a moment, then laughed.","“Who says that I am going to do anything to you? I have no such plans. Do what you want, little soul.\"","Snuggle stared at him some more.","\"Really?\"","He nodded.","“Really.\"","However, she did not seem convinced. After studying him some more, she asked again:","“Really, really?\"","The shadow sighed.","\"I never lie.”","The little doll hesitated for a few moments, then took a step back.","\"So... I can just leave? And you won't pursue me?\"","The shadow threw one last wistful glance at Snuggle — the last keepsake of Tatal he had left — and turned away.","\"You can, and I won't.\"","With that, he started to walk away. Soon, his figure was swallowed by darkness.","The little doll was left alone in front of the monument. She remained motionless for a short while, then dashed toward the border of the city.","The shadow sensed her departure, but didn't do anything. Instead, he returned to the steps of the temple and sat down, staring into the darkness.","He could feel the little doll reaching the end of the city and escaping into the wilderness outside. She was moving fast, as if afraid that the frightening lord of this eerie place would reconsider... however, the radiant soul did not abandon its clumsy vessel, choosing to remain a doll.","Perhaps she had felt that the shadow was attached to the ugly thing, and would hesitate to destroy it. So, she remained inside Snuggle, using it as a good luck charm.","The shadow still didn’t move.","If the transient soul wanted to leave, he had no reason to stop it. He did not want to kill it, after all, and neither did he want to imprison her and keep her within the kingdom by force.","He felt a little wistful at the thought of losing Snuggle... but he did not feel like he had the right to keep it, either. The thing he had become was not the same shadow Tatal would call a friend.","So, the shadow simply observed as the doll crossed the lands of his kingdom, feeling a little forlorn.","Soon enough, she reached the edge of the eternal darkness that shrouded the land. She dove into the light without slowing down or hesitating.","The shadow lowered his head.","‘...She could have glanced back, at least.'","After all, he had been quite hospitable to the transient soul. He had even broken the crystal and allowed it to escape the box. But, oh well. He understood her reluctance to stay in his dark kingdom any longer.","‘Good luck, little soul. I hope your travels will be...'","The shadow frowned, failing to finish the thought.","It seemed that the little doll had not made it very far.","Humans avoided the terrifying land of darkness that hid in the heart of this distant realm, so the lands surrounding it were wild and untamed.","..They were also home to countless Creatures of Corruption — some who had always dwelled there, and some who had fled here after being displaced by the swiftly spreading human civilization.","In short, the lands around his kingdom were no different from the primal hell of the world in the Age of Gods.","And the little doll... almost as soon as she left the quiet darkness and escaped into the light, she stumbled into one of the more powerful abominations that dwelled there. The shadow sighed.","‘Does she have the best luck or the worst luck?'","He couldn't tell.","One thing he did know, however, was that it was dangerous for someone whose soul shone with the golden light of divinity to exist in a world drowning in the rot of Corruption.","Somewhere outside his kingdom, a brilliant flash illuminated the sky.","The ground quaked."]},{"number":3191,"title":"Chapter 3191 There and Back Again","paragraphs":["The shadow's senses extended over a vast area... but all of that area was his kingdom. By extending himself across its lightless reach, he had turned himself all but blind to everything that happened beyond its borders.","Still, he felt compelled to watch over the small doll until she disappeared from his sight completely.","So, sitting on the steps of the temple, the shadow remained motionless as a flawless copy of him rose from the darkness.","The second incarnation, too, took the form of a human. It looked down at its human hands and slowly made them into fists.","“It feels strange, to become a human once more.\"","It was strange, but not alien. After all, the shadow remembered living countless human lives.","The incarnation tilted its head a little.","\"Don't you think?\"","The shadow smiled faintly and remained silent. He felt no desire to converse with himself.","Shaking its head, the second incarnation dissolved into the darkness. A moment later, he appeared at the very edge of his dark kingdom. Instantly, his senses spread outward, encompassing the untamed wilderness beyond.","All across the primal land of hills and forests, countless creatures shivered, as if feeling a gust of ghostly cold. All shadows seemed to grow a little deeper.","‘Ah... how blinding.’","Having spent many years in the lifeless refuge of his kingdom, the shadow was momentarily dazed by the infinitely dazzling mayhem of life. Its splendor, its multitude, its movement... the teeming revelry of it all was nothing short of violent, assaulting his tired heart.","It took him a few moments to find the little doll...","And the Nightmare Creature that had descended upon the doll, full of frenzied hunger.","The shadow frowned.","That Nightmare Creature... he knew it well. It had been a Supreme Beast once, at the dawn of time — an offspring of one of the first living beings to be created by the gods. However, somewhere along the way, its soul festered with the seeds of Corruption.","It fled to this distant realm and hid, making the depths of the forest its lair. The shadow had sensed the Great Beast prowling the edges of his senses on many occasions, but despite being driven by madness and hunger, the Nightmare Creature never dared to enter his domain. So, the shadow never bothered to eradicate it, either.","The Beast was not very talented — after all, it had failed to rise both in its Rank and its Class over the ages — but it was still one of the more powerful abominations that dwelled in this realm... among those who had survived being the shadow's neighbors, that was.","So, the transient soul had little chance of surviving an encounter with the monster.","It was wearing quite a pathetic shell, after all. Snuggle was not exactly created for battle: she had no armor, no weapons, no fangs, no claws. The shadow was not sure what kind of power allowed the radiant soul to move the tattered doll, but he knew that it did not grant her great strength.","Perhaps if it had chosen a more formidable vessel — a golem forged for battle or the body of a fearsome predator — she could have offered the Great Beast a tough fight. But, as things stood, his unexpected guest would soon be annihilated.","She was quite nimble, true, having escaped his pursuit for a few days. But that was only because the shadow had never aimed to destroy the dazzling soul — if he had wanted to kill her, there would not have been any pursuit at all.","The Great Beast had no such limitations. The shadow's frown deepened.","‘Should I intervene?’","There was no logical reason for him to interfere, and yet, he was reluctant to see the little doll be destroyed. At the same time, he had spent a long time searching for peace, finally finding it within the bounds of his tranquil kingdom. Stepping out of its silent shade felt like an imposition.","Torn, the shadow sighed.","Before he could make a decision, however, the situation suddenly changed.","There was a blinding flash of light, and the ground quaked. Far away, in the distance, the little doll had clashed with the Great Beast — and, to the surprise of the shadow, it was the Great Beast who staggered back, roaring in pain.","\"Huh?\"","The little doll did not possess weapons, tough armor, sharp claws, or vicious fangs. All it had was its blazing, radiant soul essence — soul essence that belonged to a Transcendent Beast, but was dazzling enough to be mistaken for that of a Supreme.","And, somehow, she had used that essence to make a Beast of higher Rank wail terribly, as if consumed by an unbearable agony. Looking into the distance, the shadow saw something he had never seen before. Something that made even his ancient mind stir in discomfort.","There, within the horrid soul of the Great Beast... the appalling darkness of Corruption was boiling and dissolving, dispelled by radiant streaks of dazzling golden light.","Corruption was being destroyed.","‘H—-how?'","That should not have been possible. In all his countless lives, the shadow had never seen Corruption let something that it had grasped with its claws go. It could be defeated before taking hold of a soul, but never after.","Still...","The soul of the Great Beast was being cleansed of Corruption. The golden light was too weak to purge it entirely, but it diminished the appalling darkness. And, as a result, the Nightmare Creature was weakened. But even if the Great Beast was weakened, it was still a Great Beast. It was an ancient Nightmare Creature that had survived eons of agony and divine persecution, honing its frenzy and deadly rage.","And the radiant soul was still hidden inside an old, tattered doll.","So, their battle ended in a predictable way. However, the shadow did not have to intervene — even if the little doll had failed to defeat the ancient horror, it managed to escape it, at least.","Some time later, a tattered figure flew into the darkness as if shot from a cannon, got tangled in the branches, and rolled lifelessly to the ground after breaking through the canopy.","There were a few moments of silence, and then a squeaky voice broke it weakly:","“Ouch... owie...\"","The shadow walked over to where the doll had fallen and looked down at it, unimpressed.","Snuggle had seen better days. It had always been covered in clumsy stitches, having endured countless rips and tears from rough play, but now, it looked like a victim of a particularly vicious delinquent.","Its crude dress was singed. One of its arms was barely attached to the body, and the body itself was torn almost in half. There were many smaller tears, as well, and one of the beads that served as her eyes was missing. Its hair was a tangled mess, with leaves and small branches sticking out of it like a ruined nest.","The shadow sighed.","\"Back already?\"","Snuggle turned her head and looked at him, her mouth downturned. She remained silent for a short while, then said in a trembling voice:","\"Yes, well... it suddenly struck me that I haven't thanked you properly for rescuing me from that crystal, Lord Titan! So, I thought about it and decided to return... in order to express my gratitude. After all, I would hate being seen as ungrateful!\"","The shadow studied her pathetic state for a moment.","\"Uh-huh.\"","The little doll tried to stand, but toppled after leaning on her torn leg.","A frenzied roar resounded from somewhere in the distance.","“And, uh... oh, would you look at that! It's already evening. Traveling in the dark is unwise, so I thought I'd stay until morning. Or, you know. A few days. How about that?\"","The shadow did not answer immediately. There was no morning in his kingdom, so the question was meaningless. She might as well have asked to stay indefinitely.","At the moment, however, he did not care about that. Instead, he was looking into the depths of the torn doll, feeling a hint of concern. Snuggle had suffered some damage... but it was the transient soul itself that was truly hurt. It was in tatters, having received vicious wounds.","And yet, as he looked, it was already mending itself. The radiant soul was healing with astonishing speed, recovering from the level of damage that would have destroyed almost anyone else.","That thing truly possessed mysterious powers.","With a sigh, the shadow leaned down and picked up Snuggle.","“Alright.”","She squirmed in his grasp.","\"May I ask, what...\"","He stepped into the shadows.","\"Be quiet.\"","Returning to the temple, he delivered the doll into the hands of his first incarnation and collapsed into a torrent of darkness. The doll observed in stunned silence. Holding her with one hand, the shadow outstretched the other. Soon, a needle appeared in it, and the darkness flowed, forming into a black thread.","“W—what are you doing?\"","The shadow looked at the doll with an an aloof expression.","“I am going to repair you, of course.”","With that, he began to mend the torn doll with smooth, delicate stitches. She froze, surprised.","The tears littering Snuggle's body disappeared one after another under the shadow's needle. His needlework was so precise that it seemed as if the doll had never been torn at all — soon enough, it looked better than it had ever been.","He manifested a bit of darkness into an onyx bead to replace her eye, then created some fabric to make her a new dress. Snuggle observed his actions in incredulous silence.","Eventually, she squeaked:","“What a cute little... inky-black... dress! You seem to be very good at sewing, Lord Titan. What an... unexpected talent you have.\"","The shadow smiled faintly.","“Of course. I used to be very good at weaving.\"","When was it?","He did not quite remember. His hands, however, remembered it all too well.","In no time at all, Snuggle was as good as new — better than it had ever been, really. Putting it down with a satisfied expression, the Shadow nodded.","\"That's better.\"","He considered something for a moment, then added:","“You can call me Shadow. No need to be so formal.\"","Snuggle made a few tentative steps, then waved her hands in the air and stared at them for a moment.","“Huh? That is indeed much... much better. Shadow? Alright then!\"","She stared at the needle he was still holding in his hand, which shone faintly with an ethereal golden glow.","“That is a very interesting needle you have there, Shadow. Where did you get it?\"","The shadow looked at the needle, as well. He wasn't quite sure. He had just thought about needing a needle, and it naturally appeared in his hand.","Where had he gotten it?","He tried to remember.","“This one? Hm... well, if memory serves...\"","The shadow tilted his head a little.","\"I think I stole it from Nether's tower. Yes, that should be correct.\"","The little doll trembled a little, then looked away.","\"Nether, huh? So he's on a first-name basis with a daemon.\"","Her quiet mumbling sounded dejected.","\"Gods, I'm doomed...\""]},{"number":3192,"title":"Chapter 3192 Miraculous Soul","paragraphs":["In the end, Snuggle stayed — for a few more days, according to her. She was recovering from the wounds received in the battle against the Great Beast splendidly, but somehow, she still seemed downcast.","“A Great Nightmare Creature back home. What a Nightmare!\"","The shadow could hear her grumbling from time to time.","“How many of these horrors are out there, for me to slam into one right away? Brrr. Scary!\"","Actually, a Great Beast was already a rarity in this era. The Age of Heroes was in full swing, after all. In fact, it had probably passed the halfway mark already, and the vague shape of the Golden Age — the Age of Humans — could already be seen far in the distance. The shadow wasn't quite sure, considering how rarely news of the outside world reached him.","There were still some Great abominations around, and even those who were far more powerful. But meeting one randomly was uncommon — it was just that the realm where the shadow dwelled was quite special in that regard, like a preserve for eldritch horrors.","That was because the heroes of the modern era had not gotten here yet, and the most powerful noble creature who resided in these lands — the shadow — did not feel inclined to go out of his way to battle these abominations. As long as they knew their place, he simply left them alone.","However, he did not feel the need to explain that to the downcast doll.","“What about you, Shadow? Do you clash with Great abominations often? Well... they would scare a Supreme Titan, I suppose.”","The shadow nodded.","“Not that often. And they don't scare me, indeed.\"","He remained silent for a moment, then added, wanting to appear more relatable:","\"It's not like I don't get scared, though. One time, I watched Beast God kill and devour a Void Creature. That gave me a fright.\"","Snuggle hiccuped.","Somehow, the shadow got a sense that his attempt to seem relatable had not worked. Some time later, Snuggle asked in a timid tone:","\"A—anyway. What do you do here for fun?\"","The shadow had to contemplate her question.","'What is fun?'","Was it something he enjoyed doing? Eventually, he said:","\"I like to sleep.\"","The little doll stared at him with her beady eyes. Then, she giggled.","“So we have something in common, after all!\"","Since Snuggle was going to stay... for a few days... the shadow decided that she needed a place to rest. He didn't want to return to the temple, so he led her to the largest and most opulent structure in the city — the manor where its former lord had lived.","As they entered, Snuggle looked around.","\"Is this your house?\"","The shadow shrugged.","\"All houses in this city are mine.\"","Around them, the shades of the servants and slaves were busy dusting the floors and performing other tasks needed for the upkeep of the large manor. Their presence seemed to make the little doll uncomfortable, so the shadow called them back into his soul.","\"Choose whichever room you like.\"","Seemingly satisfied, Snuggle scampered away to explore the house. The shadow, meanwhile, followed an instinct and went into the kitchen.","There, he halted in confusion.","‘Why did I come here?'","The shadow had not eaten anything since the dawn of time, and Snuggle was a doll — even if there was a Transcendent soul within it, she still couldn't consume food. Needless to say, there was no food to be cooked in the ancient manor, anyway.","The shadow frowned.","‘I guess treating a guest to some food is just a habit I picked up in my countless lives.'","Tatal used to steal the offerings from his altar, as well. So, it felt strange not to offer Snuggle anything to eat.","Shaking his head, he returned to the foyer.","“Shadow! I'll take the master bedroom!\"","A squeaky voice resounded from somewhere deeper in the manor. The shadow shrugged, indifferent to her choice. And that was how his kingdom got a second resident.","As far as residents went, Snuggle was clearly a failure — she did not pay any tax, went around brazenly illuminating the peaceful darkness, and was surprisingly loud despite her small stature.","Still, the shadow somehow found himself enjoying her company.","It was not unpleasant, at least.","So... perhaps that was fun.","Snuggle spent the first few days recovering from her wounds and replenishing her essence. Then, she went to explore the city. After that was done, she began slowly and carefully scouting out the surrounding lands, observing the Nightmare Creature that populated them from a distance.","The more she learned, the more dismayed she became.","“Another Tyrant... what the heck? Is this place really hell? No, there would be an abundance of Devils in hell, so if anything, this place is worse...\"","After a while, feeling curious, the shadow finally asked:","“That day when you fought the Great Beast. How did you do it?\"","Snuggle stared at him in confusion.","\"Did what?\"","The shadow sighed.","“I saw it. You weakened the sea of Corruption in his soul — you destroyed some of it, even. I've never seen anything like it.\"","After hesitating for a moment, he added:","“Destroying Corruption is the domain of death. It should be impossible to cleanse a living creature of Corruption without killing it.\"","He should know. After all, he was an emissary of death.","The little doll tilted her head a little.","“Oh, that? Well, it's simple. That's my Aspect.\"","The shadow frowned.","“Only humans have Aspects. You are not a human; you are a soul.\"","Snuggle raised her chin haughtily.","“So what? I'm a human soul!\"","Then, she scaled the leg of a table he was sitting at like an experienced alpinist and sat down, her legs hanging from the edge.","\"My Dormant Ability allows my soul to wander as a free spirit and animate various things. My Awakened Ability allows me to heal my own soul. My Ascended Ability allows me to infuse others with my essence to heal or empower them.\"","The shadow studied the radiant soul that shone within Snuggle.","‘The unusual potency of her essence must be the result of an Attribute, then — or even several of them, including a Divine Lineage. Quite a powerful combination.'","“What about your Transcendent Ability?\"","Snuggle coughed in embarrassment.","“Oh... my Transformation, you mean? Well, it's very beautiful and splendid! It gives me a corporeal form. A very beautiful, very magnificent form! Way more majestic and impressive than this doll. However, I can only heal souls, not flesh... so, I don't use it often in this dire place.\"","She sighed, her shoulders falling.","“Plus, I have misplaced my real body. So, I don't even know how my Transformation would work if I were whole.\"","The shadow raised an eyebrow. From the sound of it, Snuggle had misplaced her real body some time ago — before she became a Transcendent, at least.","However, that was not very important to him.","“That still doesn't explain how you were able to destroy Corruption.\"","Snuggle raised her little hands and waved them in front of her beady eyes. The shadow observed her strange antics in silence.","“What are you doing?\"","She lowered her hands.","“I'm blinking in confusion!\"","The shadow took a deep breath, suppressing the desire to palm his face.","‘Right. She doesn't have eyelids, so why not?'","\"What is so confusing about my question?\"","Snuggle beamed.","“Well, didn't I already say it? I heal souls!\"","He frowned, still unable to understand. Noticing his confusion, the little doll explained:","“Corruption infects souls, does it not? So I can heal souls from that infection, as well.\"","The shadow stared at her silently.","‘Corruption... is an infection.'","Her explanation was far too simple, but it made a strange kind of sense.","Corruption was indeed an unnatural state. It was the result of foreign influence — that of the Void — twisting and changing the souls of those who were born from the Flame. So, destroying Corruption could indeed be seen as restoring souls to their intended shape. Or, in other words, healing them.","Destruction, restoration... the words were different, but they meant the same thing.","It was a miraculous power, no doubt — especially considering how potent the essence of the radiant soul was, as well as the fact that it was infused with the Flame of Divinity. That attribute, after all, was the antithesis of the Void, and therefore of Corruption.","And since the wandering soul could heal itself, as well, she had to possess a truly fearsome resistance to being Corrupted. Which was not to say that she was completely immune to it. Even the shadow, who was far more powerful than her and a Shadow Creature to boot, was not immune to Corruption. There was no one in the world who could resist it fully — not even the gods...","No. There was one being.","Wasn't there?","“Anyway, why are you asking?\"","The shadow shifted slightly, then looked at Snuggle.","“No reason. I was just curious, since I've never seen anything like it before... and I've seen a great deal of things.\"","He remained silent for a moment, then asked:","“So what are your plans? What do you want to achieve?\"","The little doll had been cautiously exploring the outside world, so it seemed that she still harbored a desire to leave — or wanted to make sure that she had a way out, at least.","Snuggle looked away and swung her little feet a few times, in no hurry to answer. Eventually, she shrugged with a smile.","“I am not sure. All this time, I was just trying to survive. But... that's enough of a goal, I think.\"","She looked at him, her smile widening a little.","“That's because someone will come to rescue me, eventually. I just need to stay alive long enough for that person not to have wasted his time. He'd be quite disappointed to find me dead.\"","The shadow did not say anything, staring into the distance.","Somehow, an old memory surfaced from the depths of his mind.","He remembered a harrowing abyss full of impenetrable darkness, a narrow cliff, and a lantern that hung from the crossguard of a shattered sword.","And old bones illuminated by the light of the lantern, lying lonesomely amidst the darkness.","He sighed, not knowing why.","After remaining silent for a while, the shadow said:","\"I hope you won't have to wait long.\""]},{"number":3193,"title":"Chapter 3193 Regret Can","paragraphs":["Days turned into weeks, and weeks turned into months.","It didn't take the transient soul long to fully recover from her wounds. However, even after she mended herself and replenished her essence, the little doll did not seem in a hurry to leave the lightless kingdom that belonged to the shadow — she cautiously scouted its surroundings, but made no effort to venture into the wide world beyond.","That was probably because she was scared. Snuggle maintained a cheerful attitude, but the shadow could tell that there was a deep well of darker emotions hidden behind her bright surface. It was easy to understand why — she had not encased herself in an inescapable crystal without a reason, after all.","An unknown number of years had passed in the real world, but for Snuggle, those events had happened mere days ago. So, it was no surprise that she was in no hurry to embark on another traumatic adventure.","She did not have a good reason to, anyway, from what the shadow could tell. The wandering soul seemed convinced that someone would come to find her, one day in the future — she believed in that person with all her heart, not allowing even the smallest measure of doubt to creep into her thoughts.","And if that was true, then all she had to do was stay alive and wait. The shadow had frightened her at the beginning, but now, she seemed to find his company reassuring. There was no place safer than his kingdom anywhere in this realm — or any mortal realm, perhaps. So why would she leave?","The shadow did not mind her company.","His slow and uneventful existence did not change much. He was still vast and devoid of desire, his consciousness sprawled across the silent reaches of his dark kingdom — devoid of life, devoid of light, populated by no one except a legion of quiet shades.","It was just that now, there was also a little doll living among the shades as well.","The shadow maintained a human incarnation to keep her company, finding her antics a refreshing distraction from the crushing weight of eternity. He did not do much and did not speak often, but the transient soul did enough of that for both of them.","Somehow he even doubted that she knew how to keep quiet. The little doll was a constant source of noise, not to mention light.","The shadow simply kept calling her Snuggle. She did not seem to mind — and despite the nascent bond of trust between them, she did not seem in a hurry to share her true name with him either.","Names had power, after all, and especially so True Names. In the hands of a powerful sorcerer, they could become one's doom... and in the hands of a being such as the shadow, they could become a beacon for the deadly weapon of his Will.","The wandering soul did not seem aware of what the Will was, but she knew enough to keep her True Name a secret. That suited the shadow fine, since he would feel awkward calling the little doll anything but Snuggle anyway.","Snuggle, meanwhile, developed an extremely bizarre habit...","She began talking to the shades.","As the two of them walked the streets of the lifeless city, she was like a squeaky fountain of greetings.","\"Oh, hello there, Mr. Miller!\"","\"Fancy meeting you here, Madam Sash!\" \"Handsome Guard? What are you doing here? That is not your usual patrol route!\" “Lady Hairdo! How was your day?\"","The shade of a mature matron with a complicated headdress just gazed at her silently. Snuggle smiled.","“Just as usual, then! Well, I won't keep you. Let's catch up later!\"","The shadow stared at Snuggle in utter incomprehension, wondering if she had lost her mind.","Noticing his stare, she glanced in his direction and asked:","\"What?\"","The shadow lingered a few moments.","\"I just can't fathom why you would talk to them.\"","Snuggle shrugged.","“Why not? Who knows, perhaps they'll respond one day.’","The shadow frowned in confusion.","\"They won't. Even if they could, what do you think they would say?\"","Snuggle raised one of her hands and supported her chin, contemplating the answer seriously.","Then, she said:","“Something like ‘Oh, gods! A talking doll! Run for your lives!'?\"","The shadow blinked a couple of times.","He stared at the little doll, then at the shades that surrounded them.","Eventually, he nodded.","“A reasonable answer.\"","Snuggle exploded with laughter and scampered forward, forcing him to keep pace.","Eventually, it seemed like she knew everyone in the city. Snuggle spent quite some time observing the lives of the silent shades, asking the shadows questions about their actions from time to time. She was especially interested in the Transcendent shades — there were only a few of them in his kingdom, all holding important posts. The lord of the city, the high priest, the shaman...","Snuggle was fascinated by each one.","\"Transcendent humans... three of them, no less! People like them were only a theoretical existence back home. And these ones conquered Transcendence naturally. What an achievement!\"","She sighed.","“I wonder what their Aspects were...\"","The shadow studied her for a moment.","“Aren't you a Transcendent human, as well? Or a soul of one, at least.\"","Snuggle nodded.","\"Yeah. But I only became Transcendent after ending up here. It just sort of happened as I was trying to survive the collapse of the First Kingdom. Things got pretty ugly when various priests and nobles began fighting for control... being a mere Ascended did not seem like enough, so I had to step up my game.\"","The shadow looked at her with a dubious expression.","\"Countless people survived the fall of the First Kingdom, and most of them were mundane, not Ascended.”","Snuggle laughed awkwardly.","\"Yeah, but... how do I say it... most humans don't feel an overwhelming compulsion to poke their noses into other people's business, unlike me. What, did you think I would stand by and do nothing while those priests and nobles were rampaging, committing vile deeds left and right?\"","The shadow shrugged.","\"I'd think so, yes.\"","Snuggle scoffed.","“Didn't you annihilate this entire city because of one human sacrifice?\"","The shadow did not know what to answer. Eventually, he simply said:","\"I did.\"","More time passed as he and Snuggle slowly got used to each other. By now, the shadow wasn't even surprised by her conversations with the shades, seeing it as something normal.","And that, in turn, pushed him to pay more attention to the shades himself.","The more he studied the shades, the heavier his heart became...","It was the weight of what he had done, catching up with him slowly.","One day, as they took a walk along the outer edges of the city, Snuggle suddenly asked, her squeaky voice cautious:","“Hey, Shadow, don't you... don't you regret it at all?\"","Her gaze was directed at the shades of the farmers pretending to tend to the fields beyond.","The shadow hesitated.","Did he regret it? He wasn't sure. He wasn't sure that he knew what regret was, or if he was capable of feeling it still.","He saw life and death differently from mortals, as well.","Eventually, he said:","“I don't regret anything. Regret... is meaningless. It is a desire aimed at the past, and therefore doomed to stay forever unfulfilled.\"","However, after saying that, he lingered for a moment and added:","\"But... when I look at the future, I do feel reluctant to do anything similar ever again. That is the closest thing to regret I know.\"","Snuggle sighed and turned away from the fields.","\"So you do think about the future as well, sometimes.\"","The shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"Of course, I do.\"","He thought about the future all the time. Mostly, he thought about how there was always a future, for him — for someone who was denied the right to end and become a thing of the past.","The thought made him feel tired.","Snuggle looked up at him and asked, her usual bright tone returning:","\"So, is there something you want to do in the future? Something you desire?\"","The shadow smiled.","“Something I desire?\"","He lingered for a moment, then shook his head.","“Not really. I don't have any desires left, I think.\"","Snuggle shook her head.","“No, no, that's not true! You just said that you don't want to slaughter cities anymore. That's a desire, as well! So think deep. Think well! If nothing held you back, what would you want to do?\"","The shadow would prefer not to answer, but something compelled him to respond anyway.","He looked at the shades that pretended to tend the fields, contemplating.","A sense of placid melancholy slowly settled in his heart.","Eventually, he said:","“Well... actually, I guess there is one thing.”","Snuggle tugged at the hem of his tunic.","\"What is it? Come on, tell me!\"","He sighed.","“You see... I am a creature of death. All the things I kill become a part of me. So, in a sense, my existence is like a dam that blocks the entrance to the Shadow Realm. Because of me, countless shadows are doomed to never reach the Realm of Death — to stay within me forever. They are like a deep and dark lake, its surface still and unmoving.\"","The shadow fell silent for a moment.","\"A long time ago, I had a friend. She was a mortal woman, and I didn't want to part with her — so, I offered to make her a part of my soul. But she refused... she said that such an existence would be terribly sad. So, she's gone, and we will never meet again.\"","Snuggle studied him, then asked in her small, squeaky voice:","\"So you want to meet your friend?\"","The shadow shook his head.","“No. It's impossible. Even if I live forever, I will never see her again. However... I destroyed this city because I was angry, and I was angry because its people had desecrated her memory.\"","He looked at his shades, his gaze hiding a hint of despondency.","“But wasn't the act of destroying this city a desecration of her memory, as well? And wouldn't the act of keeping these countless shadows trapped within me, forever, make her terribly sad?\"","The shadow smiled wistfully.","\"I cannot meet my friend again, because she is in the past. I can't bring the city back to life, either. However... I can still set these shades free, somehow. That is the only thing I can do that belongs to the future.\"","Snuggle tilted her head a little.","\"You want to liberate your shades? Let's do it, then! What's stopping you?\"","The shadow looked down, taken aback.","He was just thinking aloud. In truth, he had never contemplated releasing his shades seriously before.","How would he even do it?","After a while, he shrugged.","“I don't really know how to set them free. I can consume them... but then they'll still be a part of me. I would have to deliver them to the Shadow Realm, I guess — let Shadow God deal with it.\"","Snuggle gulped, but then seemed to find her courage again.","“Well, so what? If that is your only desire, let's go knock on Shadow God's door! Let's come and say — here, these are your clients. Sign for delivery!\"","The shadow stared at her, baffled.","“It's... not that easy.\"","Snuggle waved her hands in the air.","“Why not?\"","He didn't know what to answer.","“Well, first of all... I don't even know how to get to the Shadow Realm. We'd need a map, or better yet, a guide. Someone who knows the mortal realms well and can lead us to the Hollow Mountains.\"","The shadow frowned.","Even if they did get to the Hollow Mountains, they would have to brave the Underworld and the Abyss. And then, they would enter the soul of Shadow God, which was not something the shadow really wanted to do.","But perhaps, maybe...","Perhaps if he met Shadow God, he could receive some answers too.","Still, the very idea was crazy.","Leaving his peaceful kingdom? Plunging into the endless chaos of the mortal realms? Braving unknown dangers and willingly entering the Shadow Realm?","Why would he ever want to do that? Looking at Snuggle, the shadow sighed.","\"Listen. You don't seem to realize, but the world out there is full of things that even I, a Supreme Titan, can't handle easily. There are powerful Creatures of Corruption, ancient deities, beings of the Flame that can rend me to shreds with a thought, and all kinds of horrors. And let's not forget people! People are the...\"","But before he could finish, a stifled hiss suddenly escaped from his mouth.","That was because some distance away, the peaceful silence of his kingdom was suddenly torn apart by a blinding explosion of pale, ethereal light.","The darkness that had shrouded this land for countless years was banished, and a small portion of the city was suddenly revealed under the night sky.","Moonlight poured from the dark heavens like a waterfall, painting the lightless landscape in pale silver.","‘What the hell?'","The shadow turned in that direction, suppressing the searing pain. He frowned.","‘Who dares?’","Snuggle spun, as well.","It was in that moment that a youthful, arrogant voice reached them from the distance.","\"Come out and face me, creature!\"","The shadow frowned, and then let out a heavy sigh.","‘Damnation.’","It seemed that the Age of Heroes had descended upon his lands, after all.","Some human fool had finally decided to come and bother him.","“Today is the day you die!\"","And that fool was an especially obnoxious one, it seemed.","‘Just what kind of idiot would attack me in my own domain?'","As the shadow grimaced and leaned down to pick up Snuggle, the wind carried the voice of the supposed hero to them once more.","\"...Because today is the day that you met me, the Crimson Beast of Twilight!\"","As if that was not enough, the uninvited fool added:","\"The greatest — and most handsome — hero in all mortal realms!\""]},{"number":3194,"title":"Chapter 3194 Fellow Wanderer","paragraphs":["Putting Snuggle into a pocket, the shadow clasped his hand behind his back and headed in the direction from which the voice was resounding. Soon enough, he reached the plaza at the edge of the city, where the northbound road turned into its main street.","There, in front of the open city gate, he saw a figure painted in shades of pale silver by the pouring moonlight.","In front of him stood a human youth. The stranger was dressed in dashing, albeit somewhat dusty, robes of pure silk — his garment must have been quite lavish once, but now, the luxurious scarlet dye had faded, and the embroidered hems were frayed. His skin was pale and smooth, and his black hair glistened in the moonlight like onyx.","There was a crescent moon mark on his forehead, and below it, two clear eyes were burning with righteous fury, imbuing his adolescent face with a hint of noble dignity. The shadow sighed inwardly.","‘Another child...’","Despite his youth, the fool who had wandered into his kingdom this time was a Transcendent Beast, no different from Snuggle. In fact, his soul gave off the scent of divinity as well — he had to be a descendant of one of the great gods, without a doubt. This was the Age of Heroes, after all, and there were plenty of them running around.","In fact...","The shadow felt that the human youth looked strangely familiar. He just couldn't quite place the young man, lost in the boundless ocean of his memories.","So, instead, the shadow simply said:","\"Greetings.\"","Hearing his voice, the youth did a double take and turned to look at him in surprise. After studying the shadow in confusion for a few moments, he suddenly beamed.","“Well met, stranger! What luck, to find a fellow wanderer in this desolate land. However, take heed — a terrifying monster is rumored to dwell in this cursed ruin. I plan to challenge and slay it, so you'd best take cover until the dust settles. We'll savor fine wine and trade stories after I return victorious!\"","The shadow stared at the youth, confused. Snuggle, meanwhile, peeked out of his pocket. Looking just as baffled, she glanced at the uninvited guest, remained silent for a moment, and then whispered:","\"Is he a fool?\"","The shadow did not respond immediately.","‘I mean... that's self-evident.'","He gave her a subtle nod, then followed an impulse and asked:","\"A terrifying monster?\"","The youth threw a tense look into the darkness, then sighed.","“Indeed! You might not know, but this land was prosperous once, populated by enlightened humans. But then, one day centuries ago, all communications with them ceased. When the merchants arrived to trade as usual, all they found was a dead city shrouded by eternal darkness. And, what's worse... something dwelled in the heart of the city.\"","He grimaced with disdain.","\"It was a vicious, ghastly abomination! The one I came here to kill.\"","The shadow tilted his head a little.","“Really? What kind of abomination?\"","The youth looked hesitant for a moment.","\"Well... no one knows for sure, and the legends people of the surrounding realms tell all differ. Some describe it as a giant beast with seven heads and the tail of a beaver, some say that it looks like a human with the head of a mountain goat. In any case, it's extremely hideous, grotesque, and unsightly! That's why it lives in darkness, afraid to see its own face.\"","He sighed.","“That creature is not only extremely abhorrent and revolting, though, it is also extremely powerful. It subjugated all the people of this land and turned them into its servants. Now, those poor souls live in the darkness, having long ceased being human. So, I — the legendary hero, Noctis — came to cleanse this land of Corruption. I came to banish the darkness and return this land to the light of the Moon!\"","The shadow studied him for a moment, then threw a furtive glance at Snuggle. Perhaps she knew what he was supposed to do.","But Snuggle just raised her hands and shook her head, similarly stumped.","The shadow sighed.","Standing at the edge of light, he said:","“Oh. I see. However, you are not entirely correct.\"","The youth raised an eyebrow.","\"I'm not? What do you mean, stranger?\"","The shadow nodded.","“You see, I never subjugated the people of this city. I merely killed them all. I killed all the beasts, insects, and Creatures of Corruption as well. So... it is not as though I have something against humans in particular. Even if they are the most bothersome bunch.\"","The youth laughed.","“Well said!\"","But then, he froze.","“Uhm... wait. What did you just say, stranger? Did you say... that you were the one who killed these people?\"","He stared at the shadow again, a clear expression of incomprehension on his face. Then, he chuckled nervously.","“Don't jest. You are clearly a human... a gentleman of refined upbringing, by the look of it. Even if you do, regrettably, suffer from a lack of taste and seem to be in the habit of wearing drab colors, that's no reason to bring yourself down!\"","The shadow blinked a couple of times.","\"I just look like a human for the sake of convenience. Would you prefer I take the shape of a giant beast with seven heads and the tail of a beaver? Or should I simply change my head for that of a mountain goat? It's no bother, really. Just say the word.\"","The youth hiccuped.","\"No, no... what are you talking about? The creature that dwells in this land is... is...\"","He had already looked pale in the moonlight, but now, his face seemed ghostly white.","The shadow shrugged.","\"Is me. Welcome to my kingdom, young Noctis... Crimson Beast of Twilight, was it? Didn't you say that I should come and face you? Since today is the day I die. So, here I am.\"","The youth studied him for a few moments, then composed himself and forced out an arrogant laugh.","“I see. So the monster who caused the ruin of this city is none other than you! You... uh... what should I call you?\"","The shadow shrugged.","\"Call me Shadow.\"","The youth scoffed.","“You vile shadow! As I was saying... I came here to slay you! So, prepare to die!\"","The shadow studied him with a dubious expression. The youth was putting on a brave face, but he clearly seemed unnerved. And why wouldn't he be? The shadow was truly an unnerving existence.","Noctis had a reason to be confident in his prowess, perhaps. He was a Transcendent — even if it looked like he had only reached Transcendence recently — and a descendant of one of the great gods to boot. He had also reached this place alone, braving the wilderness beyond.","Even if he had been lucky to avoid the most powerful abominations that dwelled there, he still had to have fought quite a few of them, and yet, he was unscathed.","However, he clearly had not expected to meet a creature that could take any form it wished, was capable of human speech, and seemed just as intelligent as a human. Beings like that were supremely dangerous. He might have already realized that his opponent was Supreme, as well. It was just that he had not realized that the shadow was a Titan.","But, really...","‘So he wants to kill me?’","He had nothing to worry about.","The shadow nodded.","“Okay.\"","Noctis stared at him in confusion.","\"Huh? What do you mean, okay?\"","The shadow shrugged.","\"Go on, kill me.”","The human youth frowned, then raised a hand.","“Don't think that I won't!\"","The shadow just stared at him.","Nothing happened for a few moments.","So, the shadow spoke with a hint of impatience in his voice:","“Alright? Come on, you may begin.\"","Noctis hesitated for a bit, then lowered his hand and glanced at the shadow with suspicion.","\"What kind of ruse is this? Are you trying to deceive me, creature? Let me tell you — I am the smartest hero in this land! Or any land! The likes of you won't ever be able to outsmart me, so you should just give up the thought right now.\"","The shadow frowned.","“There is no ruse, young human. In truth, I've longed to die for a long time now... since before the dawn of time, when the gods themselves were young. So, I decided that I might as well let you try. Go on, do your best... your worst? Anyway, strike me down with all your might. I won't resist.\"","Noctis stared at him in stunned silence. Then, he cursed.","\"You are taking all the fun out of it, knave!\"","Then, he gritted his teeth.","“But I'll take you up on that offer. So, get ready!\"","As the youth raised his hand again, Snuggle suddenly jumped out of the shadow's pocket and swiftly climbed to his shoulder. There, she raised her hands and squeaked:","\"Wait! Don't do it, please! If you do, someone is really going to die... and it won't be Shadow!\"","The young man lowered his gaze and stared at her.","Then, he somehow paled even more. Noctis opened his mouth, then closed it again.","Then, he suddenly screamed in horror:","“Oh, gods! A talking doll! Shadow, run for your life!\""]},{"number":3195,"title":"Chapter 3195 Young Hero","paragraphs":["‘How did it end up this way?’","The shadow remembered his peaceful past. The tranquil quiet of his lightless kingdom, the uneventful years he had spent slumbering in the darkness...","Now, there was bright light illuminating the vast hall, and not one, but two boisterous voices chasing away the silence.","“Thank the gods... so you're just a disembodied soul, not actually a living doll!\"","“Of course. But why are you using informal speech when addressing me?\"","\"What are you talking about? Look at you. You're so tiny and squeaky!\"","“So what?! I might be tiny, but l am a mature, respectable woman! You brat!\"","“Who are you calling a brat, pipsqueak? I am Noctis, the Crimson Beast of Twilight. l am a Transcendent hero! I am already nineteen!\"","\"See! I am... huh, wait, how old am I? Twenty-nine? Yeah, that's right!\"","\"Oh? Oh... well, sorry then. Auntie.\"","“Auntie?! Did you just call me an auntie?!\"","The shadow sighed heavily.","Currently, they were in the house of the city lord. Snuggle was seated on the table, her chin raised arrogantly. The human youth — Noctis — was sitting on a chair, tied up and unable to move. The ropes that bound him were woven out of shadows, strong enough to hold a Supreme being... so, he wasn't going to cause trouble any time soon.","Or maybe he was. Humans were unpredictable, after all — each possessed a unique Aspect, and if the shadow really wanted to contain one, a simple rope would do him no good. He would have to enchant it, somehow, and that felt like too much effort.","In any case, tying the adolescent Transcendent up was only a temporary measure. The shadow had to figure out what to do with him soon.","‘Should I just kill him?'","There was no reason to, so the shadow knew that he wouldn't. Still, a shadow could dream, right?","‘Maybe he'll just go away on his own...’","The shadow looked at Noctis.","Noctis... did not seem like a problem that would go away on its own.","What was worse, now that a Transcendent human had come to battle him, there would most likely be another, and another, and another... the sphere of human influence was expanding, and the forces of Corruption were slowly dwindling. This distant realm was not so remote anymore.","Another heavy sigh escaped from the shadow's lips.","If he would not kill the human youth, and the youth was not going to go away... then what was there to do? The shadow was a little stumped.","He was a creature of death, after all. All he knew was how to kill; if there was something that had to be resolved peacefully, he was just as powerless as a mundane person.","Luckily, Snuggle was there, and she seemed perfectly suited to solve the problem for him. In fact, even if their conversation sounded like a meaningless exchange of insults, the little doll seemed to be guiding it carefully in some mysterious direction.","“So, Noctis... why did you suddenly decide to come challenge the Shadow, anyway? Even if you are a Transcendent, that seems a little too reckless.\"","Noctis frowned, then threw a furtive glance at the shadow.","Then, he forced out an arrogant laugh.","“What's so reckless about it? Let me tell you, sister... I have slain plenty of Creatures of Corruption. Among all the heroes in the world, there is hardly anyone more fearsome than I!\"","He paused for a moment, his haughty smile dimming slightly.","Noctis remained silent for a short while, then added in a more somber tone:","\"Human life is fragile and fleeting. All across the mortal realms, countless people are fighting desperately to survive. There is not enough space for everyone, and not enough food for everyone. Scarcity gives birth to poverty and destitution — two vicious beasts that devour dreams and suffocate joy, turning good people into empty husks.\"","His expression darkened.","“I mean... have you seen the clothes that poor people wear? Those ugly things are an affront to all that is good in life! And their houses! My noble eyes were not made to look at dusty hovels. And let's not even mention the smell...\"","Noctis shuddered, a horrified grimace appearing on his face.","Snuggle stared at him with an indescribable expression.","She did not speak for a few moments, then cleared her throat.","\"So... you decided to attack Shadow, a Supreme Titan, because you don't like how poor people smell?\"","Noctis looked at the shadow, his eyes widening.","“A what now? A S—supreme... T—titan?\"","The shadow smiled politely.","\"Indeed.\"","Noctis stared at him for a moment, then raised his chin.","\"Well, so what? I must admit — even I, the great and astonishing Noctis, have not slain a Supreme Titan yet. And I might have expected to find something like a Corrupted Tyrant... perhaps a Great Beast or two... here. But! You refused to battle me, using a cunning trick to restrain me instead. So who's to say that I won't win if we fight?\"","He scoffed, then sighed and shook his head.","“But that is not what I mean. Beyond the reaches of this wild realm, humans and the Creatures of Corruption are fighting a war for dominion over the world. Transcendent heroes like me are the champions of humanity. Unlike many, I've lived a life of privilege and abundance — I've never been exposed to the bitterness of destitution, let alone to suffering and tragedy.\"","Noctis coughed and tried to scratch his nose, but failed — his hands were tied, after all.","“Truth be told, I grew up in a temple of the Moon, my grandmother. Once I came of age and Ascended, I left to wander the world... and once I saw how bitterly humans fought to live, I was rattled. It was only then that I truly understood the lessons that the priests had taught me and my siblings — all those words about duty, courage, and the Path of Ascension. About what those who wield power ought to do. So, I endeavored to distinguish myself, like other heroes had.\"","He sighed.","“Only, the thing is... as it turned out, it's actually not that easy to distinguish yourself these days. There are already plenty of heroes around, and most of them are older, wiser, and more experienced than me. Plus, the Creatures of Corruption are not endless either — with so many of them already slain, finding a worthy opponent is such a hassle! And lastly, I am a direct descendant of a god.\"","Noctis flashed them a smile.","“So, the burden of expectations piled onto me is truly great! Almost as great as I am... and I am the greatest there is, of course. As well as the most handsome, gallant, charming, and refined. Not to mention the most humble.\"","He looked at them with a self-satisfied smile.","\"If I want to have a legend or two to my name, killing just any random abomination won't do. I need to accomplish something outstanding!\"","The haughty youth cleared his throat.","\"That was why I thought to slay the mysterious creature that had been scaring people away from this realm for generations.\"","The shadow and Snuggle glanced at each other.","After a few moments of awkward silence, the shadow spoke:","“So you just went and challenged this supposedly terrifying creature without learning anything about it first? Weren't you afraid that I will slay you instead?\"","Noctis scoffed.","“Slay me? As if! Nothing has managed to slay me yet, and there is a reason for that. In truth, I know a secret heroic technique that makes me all but immortal.\"","The shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"You do?\"","The youth nodded with an expression of absolute confidence.","“Of course! It's called running away.\"","As the shadow and Snuggle stared at him silently, Noctis laughed.","“If an enemy is too strong, running away is always an option. And even if boasting is not something I do often — or ever, really, the refined gentleman that I am — let me tell you one thing. There may be heroes who are older than me, wiser than me, and more famous than me. But there's no one who is better than me at running away! If I say that I am the second most elusive man in the world, no one would dare to say that they're the first!\"","The shadow suppressed an exasperated groan.","Snuggle, meanwhile, asked in her squeaky voice:","“Aren't you sitting here tied up right now?\"","Noctis looked at the ropes binding him, then glared at the little doll for a split second, and then put on a condescending expression.","“What, these ropes? Ha! I am just tolerating them out of courtesy. If I wanted to, I could give you a slip in an instant. One blink, and I'd be out of this crumbling palace. Another blink, and I'd disappear into the darkness!\"","The shadow tilted his head.","“I don't blink, though.\"","The smile froze on the youth's face.","The shadow, meanwhile, added:","“And the darkness outside is just a part of me. So... where exactly are you going to disappear to?\"","Noctis remained silent for a while, then opened his mouth.","Then, he closed it again.","Finally, he said in a small voice:","\"Well, anyway. You wouldn't want to offend my grandmother, right? So... let's just forget I ever said anything?\"","Snuggle nodded a couple of times.","“Indeed, indeed. We should respect the elders. Oh, by the way...\"","Her beady eyes glinted.","\"Did you say that you wanted to accomplish something outstanding?\"","Her mouth twisted into a smile.","\"I have just the thing in mind!\""]},{"number":3196,"title":"Chapter 3196 Twisting Roads","paragraphs":["Snuggle had, indeed, an outstanding feat in mind.","She wanted Noctis to escort them to the Shadow Realm.","There was some merit to her idea, no doubt. After all, neither of them were familiar with the mortal realms and people who populated them — both the shadow and Snuggle were completely ignorant of their customs and traditions, let alone invisible undercurrents that ruled all human societies. They did not know what roads to take and which places to avoid, so they needed a guide.","Well... the shadow could probably find his way to the Realm of Death on his own, eventually. It was just that he would most likely leave a trail of devastation in his wake, which Snuggle wanted to avoid.","Noctis, meanwhile, was not only knowledgeable about the world outside the shadow's lightless kingdom, but also held quite a lofty status among humans — his fame and background alone could open numerous doors for them. And he would probably know where to go, as well. Traveling with a Supreme Titan to one of the Divine Realms was a journey worthy of becoming a legend, so it was in his own interest too.","There was just one problem...","Noctis glanced at the little doll with a lack of amusement on his youthful face.","\"To the Shadow Realm, you say?\"","Snuggle nodded with a grin.","\"Yeah!\"","He hesitated for a moment.","\"So you are telling me... to just go die?\"","The young man grimaced and glanced at the two of them with dismay.","\"Listen, friends, if you want to kill yourself, go ahead and have at it! But what do I have to do with any of this? Leave me out of your peculiar suicide pact, please! I am too young to die! Too gorgeous!\"","Snuggle waved a hand in front of her face weakly.","\"No, wait, I didn't mean it that way...\"","The shadow suppressed a smile.","Going to the Shadow Realm had a distinct meaning in most human languages, and that meaning was, simply put, to die. So, it was no surprise that Noctis misunderstood the little doll.","She groaned.","“I meant it literally! Walk down there! Find the Hollow Mountains, traverse the Underworld, jump into the Abyss, say hi to Shadow God! Then come back and have a party!\"","Noctis studied her intently, as if contemplating something.","Eventually, he asked, a hint of interest in his voice:","\"Party? What kind of party... wait, no! Who would want to party with you?! You're a disembodied soul! You can't even drink!\"","Snuggle scoffed.","\"You're too young to drink anyway, brat! What kind of priests raised you?!\"","With a sigh, the shadow rose and left them to it. He walked out of the hall and then exited the lord's manor, looking into the vast darkness beyond.","Of course, that dark expanse was nothing but a part of him, so peering into it was no different from peering into himself.","Even if he had left the manor, he was still there, listening to two human youths bicker.","Everything in this kingdom belonged to him, was him — the darkness, the shades crowding the streets, the dark trees swaying in the wind. The forests, the fields. Even the buildings of the ancient city had deteriorated with the passage of time, and were held up by the shadows he commanded.","If he left, all of it would disappear. Everything would simply vanish, as if it had never existed at all.","There would be only a lifeless ruin left. But even that ruin would be reclaimed by life eventually — possibly in a hundred years, or possibly in a thousand; grasses and vines would swallow the weathered stones, burying them in the depths of earth.","This land had been his home and shelter since before the world splintered into innumerable realms. Was he really ready to leave?","All of it... was a little bit too sudden.","The shadow could appear anywhere in his kingdom in the blink of an eye, but he chose to walk along the dark streets, looking around with an expression of melancholy. In truth, this city had never felt like home. There were barely any traces of what he remembered left here — everything had been rebuilt, transformed, and altered. A paved plaza lay where the huts of the nomads had once been raised; the familiar fields had long been swallowed by the city sprawl. An imposing temple towered where a humble shrine had stood, and even the old graves were gone.","So was there really anything holding him back?","From the dawn of time, the shadow had only ever wanted one thing — to exist in peace, which was the closest thing to non-existence he could achieve. And from the dawn of time, true peace had eluded him.","Maybe it was time to give up on his impossible goal.","Before the shadow knew it, his feet brought him to a familiar place. He found himself in front of the old cave where he used to reside... a long time ago.","The city was different, and the land was different as well. But the cave was still the same.","Or so it seemed.","As the shadow entered his old abode, he felt nothing. No comfort, no attachment. Just emptiness.","Tatal was not here anymore, and the sound of her voice would never echo between these stone walls again. The silver bell was not here, either.","Even Snuggle was gone, having become a vessel to a peculiar, wandering soul.","The bell and the doll were the only two things he had ever kept in the cave, so without them, there was nothing left.","‘Must I really leave?'","Turning his head faintly, the shadow observed the innumerable shades that populated his lightless kingdom. They were pretending to be alive to chase away his boredom... but they weren't alive.","He had killed them, and now, he was holding them captive within his soul. Unchanging, uncaring. Utterly quiet. Suddenly, their existence did indeed seem awfully sad.","Just like his own.","The shadow sighed.","‘Shadow God is the god of death, peace, and solace. But... he is also the god of mysteries.'","So perhaps... would he shine light on the mystery of the shadow's peculiar fate?","The shadow left the cave and stopped in front of the altar standing in front of it. There were still human remains lying atop the altar, white bones resting in the darkness, a skull staring at him with reproach in its empty eyes.","He remained in front of the altar for a long time, looking at the old bones.","That was where Snuggle found him, eventually.","“Shadow! Hey, Shadow! Where did you go?\"","The shadow let out a sigh and glanced away from the decrepit skeleton, shielding his eyes from the radiance emanating from the little doll.","She climbed the altar, gave the skeleton a wary gaze, and then raised her head to beam at the shadow.","“It's all good! I've convinced him. That kid is a bit of a wastrel, but he has a good heart. And despite how he behaves, he's clever. He'll be a good guide for us.\"","The shadow gave her a long look. Eventually, a faint smile twisted his lips.","“I never said that I would go with you.\"","Snuggle raised her chin.","“Hmmph!\"","She crossed her arms — which looked a bit comical, considering how short they were — and said:","“I never said that I would go with you, either!\"","The little doll turned away defiantly.","“Do you want me to go? Ask first! Say please, pretty please!\"","The shadow hesitated for a few seconds, then threw a glance down the mountain, where the dead city lay in the darkness. Eventually, he nodded.","“Will you go to the Shadow Realm with me, Snuggle? Please?\"","She turned around and glanced at him and smiled.","\"Okay!\"","Then, her smile slowly disappeared, and a rare serious expression settled on her crude doll face.","\"However, Shadow... I have a condition. You must agree to something first if you want me to accompany you.\"","He raised an eyebrow.","“What kind of condition?\"","Snuggle remained silent for a long while, then said solemnly:","“You must promise not to kill anyone on this journey — or any thing. For as long as we're together.\"","The shadow stared at her in confusion.","He was a little baffled.","\"l am an heir of Death. And you expect me not to kill anything?\"","Snuggle nodded seriously.","“Wouldn't things be too easy otherwise? Listen, Shadow — Sister Snuggle will teach you a valuable lesson! Only things that aren't easy are worth a damn, most of the time. So, come on! Promise.\"","The shadow remained silent for a while. Eventually, he asked with a hint of hesitation:","\"Not even Creatures of Corruption?\"","Snuggle shrugged.","“Noctis and I will kill the Creatures of Corruption. You just focus on not becoming Corrupted yourself!\"","The shadow studied her for a few long seconds, then sighed.","‘What am I getting myself into?’","Walking past the altar — and the bones lying on it — he nodded.","“Alright. I promise.\"","***","Soon enough, the three of them stood at the edge of the city. Well, Shadow and Noctis were standing, at least — Snuggle was seated comfortably on Shadow's shoulder.","\"Are you really ready?\"","Shadow closed his eyes for a moment and nodded.","Then, he opened his eyes and absorbed his kingdom into himself.","Suddenly, a terrible wind rose, and the darkness around them seemed to rush like a flood — rush into the depths of his soul, where it had come from.","All across the lightless land, innumerable shades vanished without a trace. The streets of the city were suddenly empty, devoid of the false life that had filled them just a moment ago.","The shadows he had manifested collapsed into their natural form. The trees in the forests and the stalks swaying in the fields disappeared, leaving behind only desolate soil.","The shadow holding up the ancient building vanished as well, and the entire city shuddered. Countless homes collapsed with a thunderous roar, and a billowing cloud of dust rose into the air.","And then, for the first time in innumerable years...","Rays of sunlight fell upon the broken land, shining through the dust as they illuminated the vast ruin.","Shadow studied the forlorn, lifeless scene of the devastated city before him for a long while.","Then, with a sigh, he turned his back on it.","\"Let's go.\"","The twisting roads of the mortal realms awaited...","And somewhere at the end of them, the realm of Shadow God awaited, as well."]},{"number":3197,"title":"Chapter 3197 Beauty of Life","paragraphs":["The first few days of their journey were rather uneventful. Before, when Snuggle attempted to leave Shadow's kingdom, she had to battle powerful Creatures of Corruption — but now that Noctis was with them, the path seemed clear.","That was because the young Transcendent had already scouted out the safest route to the mysterious ruins, learning how to sneak past the most fearsome beings populating the realm. He had also slain a few abominations on his way to challenge Shadow, so now they simply needed to retrace his steps.","Shadow was not worried about stumbling into some ancient horror — he was one such horror himself, after all — but even he felt that avoiding them was a better solution. He had promised Snuggle not to kill anything on their journey, after all. Since he did not know what else to do with Creatures of Corruption, the idea of fighting one made him a little bit uncomfortable.","Noctis had indeed proven to be a convenient guide... however, there was something about him that eluded Shadow's grasp. It was a faint sense of familiarity, as if he had met this human youth already, a long time ago, but couldn't quite remember when.","Well, that wasn't surprising.","First of all, Shadow could very well have met Noctis in one of his countless lives — or even several of them. In fact, he vaguely sensed that if he delved into the memories of those of his lives that had been tainted by insidious madness, he would most likely learn more about the fate of Noctis. However, Shadow didn't particularly want to remember madness, so he did not give in to curiosity.","Secondly, Noctis was a descendant of Beast God. So, the sense of familiarity Shadow sensed could simply be explained by the scent of divine blood flowing through the youth's veins.","However, there was a third reason as well. Shadow learned the last reason after finally surrendering to his curiosity and brushing his ghostly fingers across the thread of the young man's fate. He did not peer into it too deeply, unwilling to learn too much, but what he saw surprised him a great deal.","‘What are the chances?'","Shadow was truly stunned.","As it turned out, there was a connection between him and Noctis.","The young man’s father was a demigod born of a union between the avatar of Beast God and a mortal man. His mother, however, was a princess of a prosperous human kingdom — a stunning beauty with fiery red hair. People with red hair were rumored to be descendants of the Fox Tribe, and the princess was no exception. In fact, her bloodline could be traced to an obscure branch of the Fox Tribe that had vanished a long time ago — it was just that neither the princess nor her royal family knew of that connection.","The princess only knew that a distant ancestor of hers was the heroine of a popular folk song — a great shaman who had slain a powerful beast to protect her people myriad years ago.","That shaman was none other than Tatal, and the obscure branch of the Fox Tribe that had disappeared from history was the nomadic people who would eventually become the Shadow Tribe.","Noctis came from the bloodline of one of Tatal's children who had married into faraway lands.","After realizing that fact, Shadow stared at the youth for a long time.","His gaze, it seemed, made Noctis uncomfortable.","\"What?\"","Noctis raised his chin slightly and forced out a smile.","“Listen... I know that my beauty is peerless and my face is like jade, worth writing a hundred songs about, but surely an ancient being like you wouldn't be mesmerized by it, as well?\"","Shadow stared at him for a few more moments, then turned away and grumbled:","\"I wouldn't. Why do foxes always get entangled with wolves?\"","Even if that fool was Tatal's descendant, he clearly took after Stone Hand. Otherwise, Shadow couldn't explain where his personality had come from.","‘Beast of Twilight... Beast of Twilight...’","Even though Shadow pulled his consciousness away from the human youth's fate, he could still feel its thread trembling, ringing in the vast expanse of eternity.","And even if he didn't want to remember, visions of the past — of the future — still flooded his mind.","Only, this time, the life he saw was not one he had lived personally. It was also far too long, far too vast to remember it all, split between fate and fatelessness, twisted unnaturally, imbued with a strange and impossible duality...","Fragmented memories flashed past his eyes.","He saw a tranquil temple. He saw human cities drowning in the sea of Corruption. He saw Transcendent champions shining like bright flames in that darkness. He was one of these champions, as well — young, brash, full of brazen determination to reshape the world into a more beautiful form.","But he was also full of keen perception and compassion that he hid behind the mask of carefree shallowness. And the more he saw, the more he witnessed, the deeper his heart was cut by the sharp edges of the world.","He saw it all...","The suffering, the fear, the bitter plight of those who were too weak to push away the darkness on their own.","As well as a different kind of darkness that dwelled in their hearts. There was Corruption, and there was corruption — the more he lived, the less he knew which one was worse.","But he still believed in brighter things. He still had hope.","And then, one day, a shining god had asked him to become a chain that bound hope.","He agreed.","What followed next... was madness.","He was mad for a long, long time. Far longer than any mortal was supposed to live. And in his madness, he always asked himself — what was it that the shining god truly expected of him?","Was he supposed to hold hope captive?","Or had he always been meant to set hope free?","The longer he carried out his maddening duty, the better human lives in distant realms seemed to become. The world was not as harsh anymore. There was less suffering, less bitterness, and less fear. It was a different age — a golden age... an age where the darkness of Corruption did not torment humans anymore, leaving them to deal with only human darkness.","He wanted to break the chains of hope and set her — and himself — free. But he was also afraid of what would come next.","He feared that the world would come undone if he did.","But he was mad, after all.","So what did he care about all that? So, in the end, he decided to act.","And he made a deal with a daemon.","\"Really, damn it all, by the Moon! How... how did it come to this?!\"","Donning a black mantle and a black mask, he stared at his own reflection in dismay. That dastardly daemon!","Why did all these things have to be black? Did daemons have no taste?","He shook his head and groaned. The world had not even ended yet, but the worst possible things were already happening.","His face was hidden behind the mask, and he did not even have his name anymore. That was because his original fate had been discarded, replaced by another, stolen one — the fate that could allow him to die, but also demanded that he live a little bit longer.","“Alright. Let's have fun with all of this, at least...\"","He became the High Priest of the Nightmare Spell — a heretic pursued by everyone who worshipped the great gods.","It took a lot of talent and tenacity to stay alive, and it took even more to accomplish his mission. Slowly but surely, his followers spread across existence, carrying the Nightmare Spell with them. He had become Supreme, and just in time as well — before he could even blink, the Doom War was upon them, and existence trembled as countless people were destroyed.","“What a mess...\"","It was as if the madness he had kept contained for a thousand years exploded outward, consuming every realm. Hope proved to be quite dangerous, indeed...","As the fires of war consumed more and more people, spreading the faith in the Nightmare Spell became easier and easier. Desperate people were far easier to convince, after all, and he was a very convincing man.","But everything had to come to an end. Eventually, the world itself came to an end, as well.","Myriad people died, and those who survived were being swiftly consumed by Corruption. Even the gods died... even the daemons.","Even the scoundrel who had roped him into wearing all black was gone.","But, funnily enough, even though he wasn't immortal anymore, he still lived.","His spirit had sustained dreadful wounds, and his Domain had been annihilated. His followers had all scattered or perished. His body was ready to crumble, and his soul was tired...","But he was still alive, for now.","He didn't really know what to do.","There was nothing really left to do, anyway. So, out of habit, he decided to set out on one last journey. He decided to bring the Nightmare Spell to those few who were yet to perish on the ruins of the destroyed world.","His feet eventually carried him to a land that was consumed by eternal darkness. There was no sun here, no stars... there was no moon.","He missed the moon the most.","All light was gone, but people still persisted in the darkness, refusing to die. Just like him. So, he helped them fight the terrifying creatures that dwelled in the darkness, offering those who were willing to become carriers of the Nightmare Spell.","Fighting against the darkness to help humans survive...","Ah. It reminded him of his youth.","Only, in the end, the very people he had tried to save betrayed him.","Taking advantage of his weakened state, they imprisoned him in a small cell under a magnificent cathedral, bound him with powerful sorcery, and closed the door shut. He was a heretic, after all, so they did not trust him.","That was why he spent quite a long time in that cell.","It was terribly boring.","Even knowing that he would die here, he didn't mind.","He had lived a long life, after all, a glorious life.","A life full of brightness and splendor.","It was just that...","“That damn daemon... I was fooled in the end, wasn't I?\"","He had always considered himself a peerless scoundrel, but that daemon! That knave had truly been without a rival, as far as lies and deception were concerned.","Eventually, he felt seeds of Corruption blooming in his soul. Corruption was everywhere now, and all things fell to it... he was not going to be an exception. However...","\"No, no. That just won't do.\"","He had already been forced to wear all black — that horrible, drab color! — and now, even his soul would become impenetrably dark? How tasteless was that!","Sealed in the darkness, he laughed.","Then, straining his broken body, he traced a few words in the dust.","His final farewell...","Hail Weaver","Demon of Fate","Fistborn of the Forgotten God!","Looking at that final message with satisfaction, he remembered his life.","He remembered the many battles he thought... the many friends he had made along the way, then lost.","The countless pleasures of life that he had experienced.","The beauty of it all.","A sigh escaped from beneath the fearsome mask.","\"Ah... I really didn't do too bad, did I?\"","This life...","It had been everything he had hoped for.","\"Farewell.\"","With that, he shattered his spirit and extinguished his soul."]},{"number":3198,"title":"Chapter 3198 Secret Technique","paragraphs":["Eventually, they did meet an abomination that Noctis had neither slain nor knew how to avoid. It was a Corrupted Tyrant and its brood — a nest of vile creatures that looked like leaves from afar, only to turn into a cloud of grotesque locusts with razor-sharp wings that blotted out the sky, painting the world in shades of dim emerald.","The Tyrant itself was like a locust queen, its brown carapace resembling a branching reef. When the giant creature moved, it was as if a section of the forest suddenly came alive, gazing at them with chilling malice.","\"P—prepare to die, vermin!\"","Noctis seemed pale as he faced the vast cloud of abominations. Shadow was not sure why exactly, though — it would be natural to feel a measure of fear in the face of such peril, but it was just as likely that the Transcendent youth simply disliked insects a great deal.","Perhaps it was simply because Noctis seemed at his weakest when the sun was high in the sky.","In any case, Shadow did not count the youth's chances of defeating the Corrupted Tyrant and her swarm high. Dealing with vast swarms of tiny abominations was quite tricky, after all — unless one had a suitable Aspect or an enchanted weapon, the fiercest of warriors could be rendered powerless in a battle like that.","Snuggle did not seem very adept at battling swarms of abominations, either. She could ignite the soul of the Corrupted Tyrant, weakening the creature and making it not much stronger than a Fallen Tyrant would have been... but that wasn't going to help them survive.","However, the Shadow could solve the problem easily.","He could annihilate the entire swarm in an instant by simply willing it to die. Eradicating great numbers of weaker creatures was exactly what he excelled at. He could tear the giant Tyrant to shreds in no more than a few seconds, as well. After all, he excelled at slaying strong creatures too.","But...","He couldn't.","Because he had been foolish enough to promise Snuggle not to kill anything.","‘Hmm... this is a bit problematic.’","Shadow was really not sure what to do.","As he contemplated calmly, the vast cloud of abominations drew closer, the swiftest of them already rushing down from the sky. The lumbering Tyrant was slowly approaching, as well.","Snuggle squealed and hurriedly hid in his pocket. Noctis, meanwhile, trembled and backed away until he was standing directly in front of Shadow, staring at the dim emerald world with apprehension.","\"H—hey, Shadow. What do we do?\"","He paused for a moment, then forced out a few more words.","\"I can probably deal with a third... a half of these abominations! But someone will have to deal with the rest. Then, we can bring down the Tyrant together... right?\"","A squeaky voice resounded from Shadow's pocket:","\"Right! Go on, then!\"","Noctis glanced over his shoulder with a startled expression.","\"What do you mean, go on? You go on! Let's go together!\"","The locusts had almost reached them by then.","‘What to do, indeed?’","Finally, Shadow came to a conclusion.","‘Right. That is also an option...’","With that, he raised a hand and placed it on the young hero's shoulder.","And then, he pulled the three of them — himself, Noctis, and Snuggle — into the shadows.","A moment later, they stepped out of them hundreds of kilometers away, on the shore of a placid lake.","There was no sign of the swarm of locusts of their enormous queen.","Noctis staggered and looked away in stunned silence.","He blinked a couple of times.","\"Huh? Where are we?\"","Shadow shrugged.","\"Far away.\"","Noctis stared at him for a short while. Slowly, his face regained some color, and his tense body relaxed.","Then, he said in a tone of reproach.","\"Listen, Shadow... we are friends, but don't you have any shame? Stealing my special heroic technique already! I shared it with you in confidence!\"","Laughing, Noctis shook his head and let out a relieved sigh while patting his chest.","“What did I tell you? Running away is always an option!\"","Shadow nodded seriously.","\"Indeed.\"","He had never had to run away from something before, but that technique was really quite wondrous.","Noctis, meanwhile, inhaled a few times deeply, then froze for a moment.","Then, he glanced at Shadow in confusion.","“So, wait, you can just jump from one place to another in a second?\"","Shadow simply nodded.","The corner of the young man's eye twitched.","“Then why, by the Moon, did we spend these past few days walking?! You could have just brought us to where we need to go!\"","He glanced down with an aggrieved expression.","“Look at my clothes! They are so dusty! The hems are all frayed! It could all have been avoided!\"","Shadow looked at him silently for a while. Eventually, he shrugged.","“I haven't gone on a walk since before silk was invented. So, I thought I should give it a try.\"","He smiled faintly.","\"I quite liked it. I think we should continue walking everywhere.\"","Hearing his nonchalant voice, Noctis groaned.","***","It wasn't difficult to travel from one realm to another. All Ascended could do so, to a degree, and Transcendent heroes could even carry other living beings with them — not to mention Supremes, who could open towering gates in the fabric of realm boundaries.","Of course, there were always nuances. Each realm was different, for example, and their boundaries were different as well. Some were thin and easily traversed; some were all but impenetrable. The Divine Realms, for example, were almost impossible to enter unless one possessed great power or had the permission of their owners.","But there were mortal realms that were difficult to enter or leave, as well. Some were simply isolated firmly, while in some, the universal laws were twisted in a way that made traversal difficult. Some were simply special, so entering them required a special process.","There was nothing particularly special about the realm Shadow had inhabited except for its remoteness... and yet, they couldn't just leave it freely. In truth, unless one wanted to make a big commotion, they had to traverse the realm boundary in a place where it was especially thin — that was what Transcendent champions of the Age of Heroes did, at least.","Shadow could just tear through the realm boundary directly, but then his entrance would echo in the fabric of reality, attracting all kinds of unnecessary attention. So, he allowed Noctis to lead them to a suitable place.","It took them around a week to make it there. They traveled across the untamed wilderness, sometimes stopping to rest. None of them really needed to sleep, and the darkness of the night was not an obstacle either — Shadow saw perfectly well even at night, Noctis only grew stronger once the sun hid behind the horizon, and Snuggle was a walking source of radiant light.","So, they continued their journey at night as well.","As they walked, Shadow gazed at the starlit sky.","He had spent countless years hiding in his cave, and then a few more centuries in the eternal darkness of his lightless kingdom. So, he had not gazed upon the night sky for a long, long time.","Looking at the stars, Shadow felt an inexplicable wistfulness... a peculiar sense of longing he could not quite explain, but that tore at his heart with sharp edges.","‘I wonder...'","Why did he feel like he had lost something... like something so precious that it could not be described with words had been taken from him?","“Enjoying the beauty of the moon, huh?\"","Noctis pushed him with a shoulder and smiled.","Shadow looked at him, then shook his head slowly.","\"Not really.\"","The young man nodded in satisfaction.","\"Good. That's my grandma, you know. So stop ogling her!\"","Shadow stared at him, baffled by the statement. Snuggle, who sat on his shoulder, turned to look at Noctis as well.","After a while, she asked, her voice full of curiosity:","“Is Beast God really your grandmother?\"","Noctis nodded.","“Of course! Not only that, but among all her grandchildren, I am the most outstanding!\"","Snuggle lingered for a moment.","“So how does it work? Does she... uh... does the moon descend from the sky to congratulate you on your birthday and give you pocket money? Or something like that?\"","Noctis chuckled.","\"The moon doesn't descend from the sky.\"","He remained silent for a while, then sighed.","\"Gods are vast. They are too vast to be someone's parents, lovers, or friends. Gods are not something that we mortals can fathom — like the ocean, the great abyss of the night sky, or the very soil we walk upon. But the gods... they are not alien to the desire of all these bonds and emotions, either. That is what I think, at least. So, gods inhabit mortal avatars from time to time.\"","He smiled.","\"The Goddess of the Moon is no different, so she has an avatar as well. Granted, her avatar is a Divine being — and has been Divine for a long, long time. She is not exactly an attentive grandmother, but she used to visit me sometimes, when I was growing up in the temple.\"","Noctis scratched the back of his head.","“Perhaps once every few years, which must have been like a blink of an eye for her. Those nights were rare and far between, but they were also precious. I remember them fondly, at least.\"","Snuggle tilted her head a little.","\"So... what did she do when she visited? Tempered your spirit? Imparted profound wisdom?\"","Noctis looked at her solemnly for a long while, then suddenly exploded with laughter.","\"Profound wisdom? Gods, no... that grandmother of mine is more childish than I am! That is how she was with me, at least. I know that she can be terrifying and unfathomable when she wants to, but when she was visiting me in my childhood days, she wanted to be different. She wanted to be in the company of a child, I guess.\"","Sunny glanced at him, not saying anything. But, in his mind, he remembered the days he had spent with Tatal.","He had not imparted any profound wisdom to that mischievous girl, either.","He had simply enjoyed her company.","But that enjoyment returned to him tenfold as sorrow when they parted, leaving a scar on his heart.","...How many partings had Beast God endured?","How scarred was her heart?","Was that the reason why the gods were growing more and more distant, and was there more to it?","He didn't know.","What he did know, however...","Was that the Goddess of the Moon had not had to bury this grandchild of hers, in the end. Noctis would outlive the great and terrible Beast God, his grandmother.","Almost as if they were nothing but a pair of mortals, and everything happened like it was supposed to happen.","As he was contemplating that, Snuggle studied Noctis for a while, then nodded.","\"I see.\"","Then, she turned her little head and said in a deadpan voice:","“Stop ogling Noctis's grandma, Shadow.\"","He blinked.","\"I wasn't.\"","\"Uh-huh.\"","\"I said I wasn't.\"","\"Yup.","\"I really wasn't, though?\"","\"Well, good then! If you say so... continue the same way!\""]},{"number":3199,"title":"Chapter 3199 Mortal Realms","paragraphs":["Eventually, they reached a place where the realm boundary was thin. One could not see the boundary or touch it, but those who were powerful enough could sense it — and to Shadow, the boundary here felt as thin as a sheet of paper.","The three of them crossed to the other side without much effort.","Standing on the other side, Shadow inhaled deeply and looked around, feeling somewhat lost. He remembered living in countless realms... he remembered a future where only two realms remained as well, one slowly devouring the other. But, still, this was the first time he had entered an unfamiliar one in this life.","So, he felt strange.","“This one is pretty barren.\"","Noctis kicked a rock and watched it roll across the dry soil.","\"No one really lives here. There used to be some trading outposts here and there before, but after the Shadow people vanished, even those were slowly abandoned.\"","He glanced at Shadow and smiled.","\"I guess we know who's to blame.\"","Shadow did not react.","All he knew was that their journey would be a long one. Noctis had promised to guide them to the Hollow Mountains, but they would have to cross countless mortal realms to reach them — even for a creature like Shadow, that was not a task that could be accomplished swiftly. Especially because most of the lands they had to traverse were not uninhabited, and troubles could arise at any moment.","“Let's make camp.\"","They had not rested a lot while traveling across his former realm since it was populated by many powerful abominations, but now, there was no reason to keep the same unforgiving pace.","Raising a hand, Shadow manifested a flawless copy of the city lord's manor in the middle of the desert. Noctis stared at it for a moment, then grinned.","“Traveling with style! I like it!\"","This was the first time they stopped to rest for a prolonged period of time. In the end, they stayed in the manor for a few days — Shadow explored the surrounding lands, curious to see how the world had changed in the eons since the divine syzygy had splintered. There was nothing really to see here, but even then, he found the little details of the desolate realm interesting.","Soon, they continued their journey. Since Shadow was in no hurry, it took them almost a month to reach the next point where they could quietly cross to the neighboring realm — mostly because Noctis had gotten lost twice, ending up in the wrong places.","Looking aggrieved, he just shrugged.","\"Hey, why are you looking at me like that?! This whole place is one huge desert! How am I supposed to navigate it precisely without any landmarks?\"","Shadow just stared at him in confusion.","“Don't you have something like a compass?\"","Now, it was Noctis who looked confused.","“What's a compass?\"","Shadow frowned.","Indeed, what was a compass? A compass was a device that pointed to the magnetic north. However, magnetic north did not exist in all mortal realms, and many realms had features that would interfere with a compass even if it did. A compass would only be reliable in the Divine Realm of War God, really.","‘Huh.'","Shadow asked:","\"Don't you know how to navigate by stars, then?\"","Noctis scoffed.","\"Why would I? Whose grandson am I, Storm God's?\"","Shadow simply lowered his head and stared at Snuggle, who sat comfortably on his shoulder.","Snuggle hid behind his ear.","\"What? Why are you looking at me like that?!\"","Shadow sighed.","Was it not this brazen doll who had assured him that Noctis would be an excellent guide?","They continued on their way, finding the crossing eventually. In the process, Noctis and Snuggle had to fight more than a few abominations — none of them as powerful as the ones they had encountered in Shadow's own realm, though.","As he watched them fight, he had to reevaluate his opinion of the two. Noctis, despite his careless attitude, was really quite a ferocious fighter — especially at night, when his strength reached its natural peak. He was cunning and determined, as well, slaying his foes with fierce efficiency. It was Snuggle, however, who really surprised Shadow.","Even if she could not do much with her doll body, she still showed hints of being a supremely experienced and seasoned fighter — that was clear from her keen judgment, breadth of knowledge, and the ability to remain calm no matter how dire the situation seemed.","It was as if she had spent her entire life battling Creatures of Corruption, facing new foes every day. Even among people of the Age of Gods, that would have been a rarity — most people only fought deadly battles when trouble came knocking on their door, after all.","That gave Shadow a vague premonition of where the transient soul had come from, but he did not pay it much attention. Instead, he considered other things.","“Snuggle.”","During one of their rest stops, Noctis was happily feasting on the meat of an abomination they had slain, while Snuggle just sat on the sand and looked at the fire. Although her face wasn't very expressive, the little doll still looked a little wistful. Turning her head, she gave Shadow a distracted look.","“What?\"","He remained silent for a moment, then said:","“If you want, I can construct a worthy vessel for you. A battle golem built from manifested shadows and infused with Supreme essence, for example. It can have any number of blades and weapons attached to its limbs... or it can be like an abyssal beast, brimming with powerful tendrils and slaying extremities.\"","He smiled.","“That way, you can participate in the battles directly.\"","Up until now, Snuggle stayed in the back, using her powers to weaken their enemies and infusing Noctis with her essence to empower him — the young man, meanwhile, was the blade of their small formation.","But if she could join him in melee, things would be much easier.","Snuggle hesitated for a few moments, then slowly shook her head.","“No need.\"","Shadow was surprised.","\"Don't you want to...\"","However, he didn't finish the question.","He had assumed that Snuggle would want to be able to kill their enemies better, because wanting to be good at killing was natural for Shadow. However, he had forgotten that other living beings could feel differently.","Snuggle giggled.","“Do I want to be a more efficient killer?\"","Shadow just nodded.","She smiled.","“But Shadow, I am already very adept at killing abominations.\"","The little doll pointed to the carcass of the beast Noctis had dressed and was roasting pieces of.","“It's just that I know the things I'm best at well. What I am best at is scouting, healing, supporting my comrades from the back... and, most of all, staying alive. And if there's a situation where I need to clash with an enemy directly, I can do that too.\"","She shrugged.","“I just don't use vessels to fight the important battles. My strongest suit is my soul, after all, so if we really are in trouble, I'll just fight as a soul. I can heal myself as a soul, but I can't repair a vessel. So, even if receiving soul damage really hurts, that is what I will do if there's a need.”","Shadow considered her words for a moment, then nodded.","Snuggle, meanwhile, stood up and curtsied.","“Plus... I really like being a doll! Look at me! Am I not cute? Am I not precious?\"","She gave him a spin.","Shadow observed her with a dubious look. Had Snuggle... actually seen what Snuggle looked like?","It was the ugliest, crudest doll in the world! Even after Shadow personally patched it up, it still looked as if an abomination had chewed it thoroughly, but then spat it out due to how disgusting the doll tasted.","He cleared his throat.","“You... some may say that you are cute and precious, indeed.\"","Shadow nodded.","There... that wasn't technically a lie.","At that moment, though, Noctis spat out the meat he had just bitten.","\"What are you talking about? This doll is the ugliest one I have ever seen! It looks worse than an abomination. It looks like something an abomination would spit out! Honestly, I've never had nightmares about Creatures of Corruption, but I have dreamed of that thing and woke up in a cold sweat!\"","Snuggle looked at the young man with murder in her eyes.","\"Oh, really?\"","Noctis nodded.","\"I mean, why are you asking something so obvious?\"","Snuggle sighed.","\"Well, if you say so.\"","Shadow glanced at Noctis and shook his head.","‘So young, so inexperienced...'","That night, the young man's favorite pair of shoes inexplicably fell into the fire and got terribly singed. He mourned it loudly the next morning.","During their next stop, all his food somehow ended up being unbearably salty, forcing him to cough and curse as he begged for someone to bring him water.","Snuggle did, but accidentally, the water had somehow ended up being even saltier...","This continued for quite a while.","By the time they reached the crossing, Noctis looked quite miserable.","He also didn't dare to comment on Snuggle's looks anymore.","After traversing it, they finally reached a realm populated by people. After that, it only took them a few days to travel to the nearest city.","As Noctis approached the city gate with a proud bearing, some of the locals seemed to recognize him.","\"Is that... is that the Crimson Beast of Twilight?\"","Noctis nodded with satisfaction.","\"I guess my fame has spread wide enough. Indeed, it's me, the great and heroic Beast of Twilight. I've been to your city before, strangers... ah, it's good to be back!\"","The people stared at him for a few moments in silence.","Then, they turned around and screamed:","\"Noctis! It's Noctis! The scoundrel is back, hide your wives! Hide your daughters!\"","Noctis blinked a couple of times.","\"Huh?\"","\"Hide your husbands, as well!\"","Hidden in Shadow's pocket, Snuggle sighed heavily.","\"By the dead gods, this kid...\""]},{"number":3200,"title":"Chapter 3200 Human City","paragraphs":["Nocits had boasted about his fame... but by the looks of things, in this town at least, he was more infamous than famous.","Even if he and Shadow were allowed to enter the city gates — the Awakened guards would not have been able to stop a Transcendent, anyway, let alone his mysterious companion — the looks they gave the young man were less than friendly. The citizens did not seem particularly happy to see him, either.","Well... some of them. The others, on the contrary, seemed quite joyous.","“Noctis! Young master! Come inside our establishment!\"","\"No need to pay! We'll pay you instead!\"","“Aren't you tired from the road, Lord Noctis? Come rest with us!\"","Each offer was accompanied by an explosion of giggles.","Noctis grinned and wanted to say something, then glanced at Shadow. His expression dimmed.","Eventually, he forced out:","\"How... very peculiar! Why are they pretending to know me? They must have mistaken me for someone, no doubt... even though I am pretty unmistakable...\"","Shadow stared at him for a moment.","\"Uh-huh.\"","A squeaky voice resounded from his pocket at the same time:","\"Uh-huh!\"","Noctis coughed.","\"Well, anyway. Let us find a good inn. Naturally, we can trouble the local lord to host us in his stronghold... but, how do I say this? It's better that we don't. Because he is not as fond of me as one would expect.\"","Snuggle scoffed.","“No way! How fond of you is he, exactly?\"","Noctis remained silent for a while, then turned away and cleared his throat.","“Let's just say that he won't necessarily kill me if we meet... but he might.”","He paused for a moment before adding hurriedly:","“Might try, I mean! That old man killing me, the Beast of Twilight? Ptui! Impossible.\"","Shadow decided that he did not want to know the details. He just noted that it was better not to meet the local lord.","‘I mean, this city seems quite large. So what are the chances of stumbling onto its ruler?’","The chances were quite slim.","They ventured deeper into the city. The streets were lively and crowded — in fact, they were far more crowded than Shadow had expected from the look of the city. It was as if all the people from the surrounding villages had gathered behind these walls, for some reason, and were now waiting for something.","Not all of them looked lively and happy, either. Many wore anxious expressions, dark circles prominent under their eyes. Some were dressed well, some wore dirty and threadbare clothes. Some resided in pretty homes built of stone, some sheltered in makeshift tents and hovels built in narrow alleys.","Shadow was accustomed to the stark contrast of the human world... but, still, something about this city was peculiar. Noctis wore a confused expression, as well.","“That's peculiar.”","Shadow looked at him.","\"You noticed, too?\"","Noctis nodded.","“Of course!”","Then, he uttered in a baffled tone:","“Many people are staring at us... but why does it feel like more of them are looking at you than at me? That's very strange!\"","Shadow stared at Noctis with a deadpan expression for a couple of seconds, then glanced away.","“That is because I am better-looking than you.\"","Noctis chuckled.","\"Yeah...\"","Then, he turned to Shadow and blinked a couple of times.","\"Wait, are you serious?\"","When Shadow nodded calmly, Noctis let out a disbelieving laugh.","\"Come on. No way. I mean... sure, you are quite charming, with porcelain skin and exquisite features. But better-looking than me? Impossible! Inconceivable... there has to be another reason, without a doubt.”","Shadow just looked at him and shrugged. Snuggle, meanwhile, squeaked from his pocket:","“That's right! And I am better-looking than you, too! Cute and adorable, pretty as a peach!\"","Noctis scoffed again.","“Both of them are delusional.\"","He remained silent for a moment.","“They must have been blinded by my radiance. Ah, what a burden it is, to be irresistible...\"","Shadow studied him for a bit, then sighed.","“What I meant is that the streets of this city are strangely overcrowded. There is an odd tension in the air, as well. Have you not noticed that?\"","Noctis glanced around with a surprised expression, lingered for a short while, then shrugged.","“Now that you mention it, the city does indeed seem more crowded than a few months ago. I have not stayed here long enough to learn all the local customs, though... possibly they have a festival happening soon, or a fair. Possibly it's simply time for local farmers to sell their surplus grain.”","Shadow extended his senses carefully, encompassing the entire city. Some time later, he sighed and shook his head.","It didn't seem like Noctis was correct. Still, if there was something peculiar going on, they would probably hear about it at the inn, where wanderers like them had probably already discussed the same strangeness.","Soon enough, Noctis led them to a respectable inn in the wealthy part of the city — it was a tall building built of stone, its courtyard drowning in the shade cast by towering trees. There was a dining hall, rooms for clients who needed to stay the night, a stable, and even a small stage for musicians and dancers to perform in front of the inn's patrons.","Currently, however, the stage was empty, and only a few people were eating in the dining hall, conversing in whispers.","Since neither Shadow nor Snuggle had any money, Noctis was the one to pay for their accommodations, grumbling under his nose in the process. Soon enough, they descended to the dining hall to satiate the young man's hunger and listen to the gossip.","Sunny stared at the bow] in front of him with a troubled expression, while Noctis attacked his meal like a wolf. A few seconds later, he looked at Shadow and raised an eyebrow.","“What are you doing? Eat!\"","Shadow hesitated.","\"I haven't eaten anything since the dawn of time.\"","Noctis almost choked.","“What? What's the point of living for eons if you can't enjoy good food?\"","He remained silent for a moment, then asked with an expression of horror on his face.","“Wait, don't tell me... have you not drunk any wine, either? Or tea?!\"","Shadow just nodded, causing the young man to give him a look of devastation. Eventually, Noctis shook his head and returned to his meal.","\"Well, eat anyway. It would look quite strange if you just sat there and stared at perfectly good food. You don't want everyone to guess that you are an immortal monster instead of a human, do you?\"","Shadow frowned.","At the moment, he was suppressing his presence and containing his Will within himself. So, unless one had especially keen senses and glanced directly at him, he doubted that anyone would think him to be anything but a mundane person — possibly an Awakened, considering his looks.","Not wanting to be recognized as a Supreme Titan, Shadow sighed and picked up the utensils.","Then, he tasted food for the first time in this lifetime.","His eyes ignited as soon as he tasted the first spoonful of the fragrant stew.","Noctis grinned.","\"Great, isn't it?\"","Shadow lingered for a moment.","\"It's... acceptable.\"","Saying that, he was already bringing another spoonful to his mouth.","And then another, and another.","Sitting in his pocket, Snuggle sighed.","\"I miss eating food.\"","Noctis spared a glance in her direction, remained silent for a moment, then asked:","\"Can't you inhabit a living being, though? Then, you can eat again! Or do you only possess creepy dolls?\"","Snuggle did not answer for a while.","When she eventually spoke, her squeaky voice was a little solemn:","“I can inhabit living beings. But there's no place for two souls in one vessel, you know? So, I have to destroy the original soul first... which is why I don't take living vessels and only inhabit inanimate objects.\"","Noctis seemed relieved for a moment, then unnerved for a couple.","Then, he shrugged and turned his attention back to his meal.","\"More food for me, then...\"","Finally satiated, he leaned back and smiled.","“Ah... it's good to be back in a human city! Now, we can finally rest properly. Take a bath. Sleep on a soft bed. Buy new clothes! Treat our hair with fragrant oils. By the Moon, I can't wait! Let me tell you, nothing can stop me from diving into a lavish bath as soon as we're done here — nothing!\"","Shadow lowered his spoon and glanced at him with reproach.","“You just had to say that aloud, huh?\"","Noctis raised an eyebrow.","“What's wrong with what I said?\"","As soon as he spoke, the doors of the dining hall were pushed open, and a group of soldiers marched inside.","Their leader, a tall man wearing lustrous armor, stopped right in front of their table and stared at Noctis darkly.","After a few seconds of silence, he uttered through gritted teeth:","“Beast of Twilight... our lord wants to have a word. You are cordially invited to visit the stronghold.”","A dark smile twisted the man’s lips.","“I'm afraid we must insist that you come with us immediately.”"]}]);
